{"name":"Kinetic Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can make a ranged spell attack against a target within 120 feet of you. On a hit, you deal your kinetic shape die + CHA modifier damage of your chosen element's type.</p><p>The amount of the damage for both shapes increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Kinetic Shape column of the Kineticist table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":120,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"rsak","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.kineticist.kinetic-shape + @abilities.cha.mod",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/trail-streak-impact-blue.webp","_id":"s000479517ba616f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Psionics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal psychic or force damage with a wizard spell, you can add your Intelligence modifier to the damage against one of the spell's targets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s002162eba0984fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0058b3c654cef4e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unflinching Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all Saving Throws caused by the target of your Inquisitor's Gaze.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s00724bea9a26306","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vitality of the World Tree","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you activate your Rage, you regain a number of Hit Points equal to your Barbarian level. At the start of each of your turns while your Rage is active, you regain hitpoints equal to half your barbarian level (rounded down) and you can choose another creature within 10 feet of yourself to gain Temporary Hit Points. To determine the number of Temporary Hit Points, roll a number of d6s equal to your Proficiency, and add them together. If any of these Temporary Hit Points remain when your Rage ends, they vanish.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s00e68054462cce9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428323,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Echo Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can temporarily transfer your consciousness to your echo. As an Action, you can see through your echo's eyes and hear through its ears. You can sustain this effect for up to 10 minutes, and you can end it at any time (requires no action). While your echo is being used in this way, it can be up to 1,000 feet away from you without being destroyed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s00ecbcd69bfe64f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persistent Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can remain shifted for an indefinite amount of time and your Formshift does not end when you are asleep naturally. You can still end your Formshift as usual.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s00f2abee427e70f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Charisma modifier to your strength checks.</p><p>Additionally, your melee weapon attacks deal an additional 1d10 damage of the weapon's type. This extra damage increases to 2d10 at 11th level and 3d10 at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s01911c8d171e410","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel divine energy directly from the Outer Planes, using it to fuel magical effects. You start with one such effect: Divine Sense, which is described below. Other Paladin features give additional Channel Divinity effect options. Each time you use this class's Channel Divinity, you choose which effect from this class to create.</p><p>You can use this class's Channel Divinity twice. You regain one of its expended uses when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You gain an additional use when you reach Paladin level 11.</p><p>If a Channel Divinity effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals the spell save DC from this class's Spellcasting feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-smoke-yellow.webp","_id":"s01927a5b2b8476a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428435,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Drain Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now use Drain Magic as a Bonus Action. In addition, when you use Drain Magic, you can end one ongoing level 1, level 2, or level 3 spell on the target, and the target recovers one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower (the target's choice). Alternatively, you regain a number of Empower Sneak Attack uses equal to the spell's level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s01dd0be518c89e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alert Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-teal.webp","_id":"s01ea25559aa7d03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Poisoned Beauty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use a shard of the Spider Queen's alien beauty, causing other creatures to become enraptured by your appearance. As a Bonus Action, pick a creature you can see. That creature must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw or become Charmed by you. While Charmed, it also gains vulnerability to poison damage. This benefit lasts for one minute or until you or your allies damages the creature. Once you use this ability, you cannot use it again until you complete a Short or a Long Rest, unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s021e4ca720d160d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamagic (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional metamagic options.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-colllecting-energy-green.webp","_id":"s0227f8a89668bc2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drain Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can drain power from ongoing spells to recharge your allies' magic. As a Magic Action, you can touch a willing creature and end one ongoing level 1 or level 2 spell on it; the creature immediately recovers one expended spell slot of level 2 or lower (the target's choice). Alternatively, you regain a number of Empower Sneak Attack uses equal to the spell's level.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s02e4251773c0fde","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Land's Aid","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape and choose a point within 60 feet of yourself. Vitality-giving flowers and life-draining thorns appear for a moment in a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered on that point. Each creature of your choice in the Sphere must make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d6 + your Druid level Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. One creature of your choice in that area regains 2d6 + your Druid level Hit Points.</p><p>The damage and healing increase by 1d6 when you reach Druid levels 10 (3d6) and 14 (4d6).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s02f07677d3e073a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428338,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fiendish Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to fire damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s031f75d239ba6ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Implements of Mercy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Insight and Medicine skills, and you gain Proficiency with the herbalism kit.</p><p>You also gain a special mask, which you often wear when using the features of this subclass. You determine its appearance, or generate it randomly by rolling on the Merciful Mask table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Merciful Mask</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Mask Appearance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Raven</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Blank and white</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Crying visage</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Laughing visage</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Skull</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Butterfly</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s037980d1eb2f3f4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artillerist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Artillerist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Artillerist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Shield, Thunderwave</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Scorching Ray, Shatter</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fireball, Wind Wall</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Ice Storm, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s03a4a3e39579a87","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Breath of the Dragon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel destructive waves of energy, like those created by the dragons you emulate. When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of the attacks with an exhalation of draconic energy in either a 20-foot cone or a 40-foot line that is 5 feet wide (your choice). Choose a damage type: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your ki save DC, taking damage of the chosen type equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>At 11th level, the damage of this feature increases to three rolls of your Martial Arts die.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. While you have no uses available, you can spend 2 ki points to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s03f3dd6628193e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can communicate with other beasts as if you were sharing the same language.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rodent-rat-green.webp","_id":"s04816d63157d3a0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dimensional Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast Dimension Door without a verbal component. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s048b37e19904ab0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spreading Spores","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to seed an area with deadly spores. As a Bonus Action while your Symbiotic Entity feature is active, you can hurl spores up to 30 feet away, where they swirl in a 10-foot cube for 1 minute. The spores disappear early if you dismiss them as a Bonus Action, or if your Symbiotic Entity feature is no longer active.</p><p>Whenever a creature moves into the cube or starts its turn there, that creature takes your Halo of Spores damage, unless the creature succeeds on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. A creature can take this damage no more than once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s04cfdad6d0f2a2e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mask of the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attempt to hide even when you're only lightly obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist, and other natural phenomena.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-beast-eyes-green.webp","_id":"s05176d3f734b39b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Sea","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape to manifest a floating orb of water over your hand. The orb remains for 10 minutes. It ends early if you dismiss it (no action required), manifest it again, or have the Incapacitated condition.</p><p>When you manifest the orb and as a Bonus Action on your subsequent turns, you can move the orb up to 30 feet and make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes bludgeoning damage equal to a number of d6 x Proficiency.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s05291fa03bf9c6e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fiendish Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one damage type, other than Force, whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You have Resistance to that damage type until you choose a different one with this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s053441e43d6ad00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Shadow Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can draw on your Shadowfell connection to empower your teleportation. When you use your Shadow Step, you can expend 1 Ki Point to remove the requirement that you must start and end in Dim Light or Darkness for that use of the feature. As part of this Bonus Action, you can make an Unarmed Strike immediately after you teleport.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0541e712f665081","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s05790f918387b7a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Survival Instincts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>2nd-level barbarian feature (replaces Danger Sense)</p><p>You become proficient in your choice of two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, Perception, or Survival.</p><p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses either of those skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-green.webp","_id":"s057dff95df6049f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contact Patron","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>In the past, you usually contacted your patron through intermediaries. Now you can communicate directly; you always have the Contact Other Plane spell prepared. With this feature, you can cast the spell without expending a spell slot to contact your patron, and you automatically succeed on the spell's saving throw.</p><p>Once you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so in this way again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-light-fire-blue.webp","_id":"s05861cbf09e5922","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Command Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use magic to bring undead under your control, even those created by other wizards. As an Action, you can choose one undead that you can see within 60 feet of you. That creature must make a Charisma Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC. If it succeeds, you can't use this feature on it again. If it fails, it becomes friendly to you and obeys your commands until you use this feature again.</p><p>Intelligent undead are harder to control in this way. If the target has an Intelligence of 8 or higher, it has Advantage on the Saving Throw. If it fails the Saving Throw and has an Intelligence of 12 or higher, it can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of every hour until it succeeds and breaks free.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s05a28586c2e1772","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Radiant Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your link to the Celestial allows you to serve as a conduit for radiant energy. You have Resistance to radiant damage, and when you cast a spell that deals radiant or fire damage, you can add your Charisma modifier to one radiant or fire damage roll of that spell against one of its targets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s05e807ab3a7c8ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Restoration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose to recover sorcery points equal to half your sorcerer level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a short rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/orb-water-ice-pink.webp","_id":"s05eb11a32e89a4f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sentinel at Death's Door","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your Reaction to change its hit points to an amount equal to your Cleric level.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s060ef0f6be9ab31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legendary Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can choose one ally within 60 feet of you that can see or hear you. That ally gains an additional action on their next turn. Alternatively, the target can take its Reaction to use this action immediately.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-quintuple-orange.webp","_id":"s060ffff573b777c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fight as One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion gains the Multiattack feature, which allows it to make two bite attacks as part of the same Action. When you use your Action Surge, your companion can make two bite attacks instead of one or use its Breath Weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s06132c2474b8fd6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Riptide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When one or more creatures have to make a Strength Saving Throw against one of your features or spells, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on that Saving Throw.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency modifier and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s061b388109e7412","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hidden Paths","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the hidden, magical pathways that some fey use to traverse space in the blink of an eye. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, you can use your action to teleport one willing creature you touch up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s067573d76a0d62b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Item Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attune to up to six magic items at once.</p><p>Additionally, you ignore all class, race, spell, and level requirements on attuning to or using a magic item.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s068ef35a37d80b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189465,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Mobility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet. If you have a Climb Speed or Swim Speed, this increase applies to that Speed as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s06ad005e32d38af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sun Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 4 Ki Points as an Action and become wreathed in a luminous, magical aura for 10 minutes. You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. This light counts as sunlight. You can extinguish or restore the light as a Bonus Action.</p><p>If a creature hits you with a melee attack while this light shines, it takes radiant damage equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s06c115bf42a81da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Light","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Unarmed Strikes deal your choice of bludgeoning or radiant damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s06d87a000c97084","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Blows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend a use of your Second Wind when you hit with a weapon attack. If you do so, the target takes additional damage equal to 1d10 + your fighter level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s06f715811a8674e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Studied Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You masterfully study your opponents and learn from each attack you make. If you make an Attack Roll against a creature and miss, you have Advantage on your next Attack Roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strikes-sword-triple-gray.webp","_id":"s070811f45d6cef6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Living Bomb","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage dealt by your Heart of Fire feature increases to three times your Proficiency.</p><p>When a creature affected by your Heart of Fire feature that you can see is reduced to 0 hit points by fire damage, you can use your Reaction to make it explode violently. Any creature in a 20 feet radius around the target has to make a DEX Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, a creature takes fire damage equal to a number of d6 x your Proficiency and is then set aflame as per your Heart of Fire feature. On a success, it takes half as much damage and isn't set aflame.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s070c516832c7ecd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Silver Sisters Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Silver Sisters Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Shield, Zephyr Strike, Magic Weapon, Branding Smite</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Blinding Smite, Spirit Guardians</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fount of Moonlight, Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Moon Cloak, Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s07504f7b5b188fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath of the Spellguard Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of your oath ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Paladin level specified in the Oath of the Spellguard Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of the Spellguard Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Detect Magic, Shield</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>See Invisibility, Silence</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Counterspell, Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Freedom of Movement, Otiluke's Resilient Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Circle of Power, Spell Mantle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s07863a1486e568a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pack Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on an Attack Roll against a creature if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/wolf-heads-swirl-purple.webp","_id":"s0792ac63305f730","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unerring Accuracy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of weapons grants you extraordinary accuracy. If you miss with an Attack Roll using a monk weapon on your turn, you can reroll it and take the second result. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s07c339a56b3857a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with shields, simple weapons, and martial weapons.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s07e7dd03450824e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Regeneration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per rest, when you spend a hit die, you regain additional hitpoints equal to your Proficiency modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-explosion-burst-green.webp","_id":"s07f8c2490c17407","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bewitching Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron grants you the ability to weave your magic with teleportation. Immediately after you cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell using an action and a spell slot or as part of a Mystic Arcanum use, you can cast Misty Step as part of the same action and without expending a spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s07fe9245d21fefa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contagious Curse","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If the target of Bestow Curse drops to 0 hit points before the end of their duration, you can take a Bonus Action to move the curse to a new creature you can see within range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0802b74892d1f12","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenebrous Trinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Bestow Curse, its range increases to 120 feet and you can choose up to three targets instead of one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s080c36cda1a7617","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Multiattack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/death/skull-trio-badge-purple.webp","_id":"s0831b2f302fcf3f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Forestborn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Nature skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-forest-gray.webp","_id":"s0889b70533411b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0898469b9e48801","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically transform yourself into a shadowy form as a Bonus Action. In this form, you have Resistance to all damage except force and radiant damage, and you can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3. You take 5 force damage if you end your turn inside an object.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can change your hit points to three times your Sorcerer level instead. This feature does not work if the triggering damage was radiant or a critical hit. You can use this effect only once per use of Umbral form.</p><p>Once you have used this feature, you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s08f734d40eba2ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to unleash special magical effects with some of your shots. When you gain this feature, you learn two Arcane Shot options of your choice (see \"Arcane Shot Options\" below).</p><p>Once per turn, when you make a ranged weapon attack as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that attack. If the attack misses, the use is not expended.</p><p>You gain an additional Arcane Shot option of your choice when you reach certain levels in this class: 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s08fffe93739d8ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead. You can attack with your Spiritual Weapon in place of one of those attacks, if you have one summoned.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s0911acc36b71696","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Water Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict cold or bludgeoning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0971f8ff128c608","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"War Priest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can make one attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike. You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s09830eb741eff95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ascendant Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your draconic spirit reaches its peak. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Augment Breath.</strong> When you use your Breath of the Dragon, you can spend 1 ki point to augment its shape and power. The exhalation of draconic energy becomes either a 60-foot cone or a 120-foot line that is 5 feet wide (your choice), and each creature in that area takes damage equal to four rolls of your Martial Arts die on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</li><li><strong>Blindsight.</strong> You gain blindsight out to 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</li><li><strong>Explosive Fury.</strong> When you activate your Aspect of the Wyrm, draconic fury explodes from you. Choose any number of creatures you can see in your aura. Each of those creatures must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw against your ki save DC or take 3d10 acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s09b84148ca2ae61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Constitution","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 3 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class. Additionally, you can use your Constitution in place of your Dexterity for the purposes of calculating the AC of light and medium armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s09f1a0a6bd0ab2a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428338,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Turn Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you present your Holy Symbol and censure Undead creatures. Each Undead of your choice within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. If the creature fails its save, it has the Frightened and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute. For that duration, it tries to move as far from you as it can on its turns. This effect ends early on the creature if it takes any damage, if you have the Incapacitated condition, or if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":30,"width":null,"units":"ft","type":"sphere"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"self"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"wis","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-creature-skeleton.webp","_id":"s0a228ebff50d571","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-white-blue.webp","_id":"s0a2ede62fd1d5d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428450,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Geokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Mold Earth cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a3d757e73d9d9e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legion of One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to create two echoes with your Manifest Echo feature, and these echoes can coexist. If you try to create a third echo, the previous two echoes are destroyed. Anything you can do from one echo's position can be done from the other's instead.</p><p>In addition, when you roll initiative and have no uses of your Unleash Incarnation feature left, you regain one use of that feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a423f6f03a8c04","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Discerning Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against Illusions and skill checks to identify illusions.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-red.webp","_id":"s0a62dd0c5af108f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twilight Dancer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>True Hide in Plain Sight no longer carries penalties. Additionally, you now regain all uses of your Cunning Step and Slippery Escape on a Short Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a7b21de459b0ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Born Predator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a +2 bonus to initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp","_id":"s0abad6bac75976a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Theotic Conduit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to harness divine energy improves further. You regain a number of dice every time you expend a spell slot to cast a spell from the cleric spell list. The number of dice you regain is equal to the level of the expended spell slot. Additionally, the dice from your pool change to d8s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0ad88ba36e0d38f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, all attacks granted to your allies through your Concerted Attack that target the same creature are made with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0adf49e7e4b6ae7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Skill Versatility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two skills of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp","_id":"s0aedb3b5e616ac9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Viper's Arsenal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your gain Proficiency in Stealth and the Poisoner's Kit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b3f515afd70cbf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428329,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Form of Dread","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You manifest an aspect of your patron's dreadful power. As a Bonus Action, you transform for 1 minute. You gain the following benefits while transformed:</p><ul><li>You gain temporary hit points equal to 1d10 + your warlock level.</li><li>Once during each of your turns, when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll, you can force it to make a Wisdom Saving Throw, and if the Saving Throw fails, the target is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</li><li>You are Immune to the Frightened condition.</li></ul><p>You can transform a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>The appearance of your Form of Dread reflects some aspect of your patron. For example, your form could be a shroud of shadows forming the crown and robes of your lich patron, or your body might glow with glyphs from ancient funerary rites and be surrounded by desert winds, suggesting your mummy patron.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b5bd5b170f5f95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Astral Sequestration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to sequester yourself and your allies on the Astral Plane.</p><p>By performing a special ritual over the course of 5 minutes, you shift yourself and up to ten willing creatures you can see to the Astral Plane. You and those creatures gain the benefits of a Short Rest while sequestered on the Astral Plane. You then return to the spaces you all occupied when you used this ability, with no time having passed in the world.</p><p>During this Short Rest, you and the creatures you sequester can make use of any options available during a rest that affect only you and the creatures you sequester.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you cannot use it again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b975066ca12b9e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steps of Night","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can draw on the mystical power of night to rise into the air. As a Bonus Action when you are in dim light or darkness, you can magically give yourself a Fly Speed equal to your Speed for 1 minute. You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0bb1cf800db7bcb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Battle Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bonded familiar can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn. Moreover, it can use any Witchcraft options or spells it gained through your class features that require an Action in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0bc1b920ba34895","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insidious Whispers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any spell you cast ignores Immunity to and Advantage on Saving Throws against the Charmed condition unless the target also has Immunity to or Advantage on Saving Throws against the Frightened condition, respectively.</p><p>Additionally, any creature Charmed by a spell cast by you suppresses all memories of the duration. This effect is suspended if the target becomes Immune to the Frightened condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0beb19cbcb19fe1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Touch of Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The cleric can use Channel Divinity to destroy another creature's life force by touch.</p><p>When the cleric hits a creature with a weapon attack or deals necrotic damage to it with a spell, the cleric can use Channel Divinity to deal extra necrotic damage to the target. The damage equals 5 + twice his or her cleric level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0c021632ebe55c6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.</p><h5>Archery</h5><p>You gain a +2 bonus to Attack Rolls you make with ranged weapons.</p><h5>Close Quarters Shooter</h5><p>When making a ranged weapon attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. You have a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls on ranged weapon attacks.</p><h5>Defense</h5><p>While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Dueling</h5><p>When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon.</p><h5>Great Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.</p><h5>Mariner</h5><p>As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a Swim Speed and a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Protection</h5><p>When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. You must be wielding a shield.</p><h5>Two-Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.</p><h5>Superior Technique</h5><p>You learn one maneuver of your choice from among those available to the fighter archetype. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).</p><p>You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach level 10, the size of this die increases to a d8.</p><h5>Blind Fighting</h5><p>You have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</p><h5>Interception</h5><p>When a creature you can see hits a target, other than you, within 5 feet of you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by 1d10 + your Proficiency bonus (to a minimum of 0 damage). You must be wielding a shield or a simple or martial weapon to use this Reaction.</p><h5>Thrown Weapon Fighting</h5><p>You can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.</p><p>In addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll.</p><h5>Unarmed Fighting</h5><p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-daggers-orange.webp","_id":"s0c1cfb5fb7b88ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Diamond Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ki grants you Proficiency in all Saving Throws.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you make a Saving Throw and fail, you can spend 1 ki point to reroll it and take the second result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make a Saving Throw and fail"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-icecicle.webp","_id":"s0c3b2a713ad67f9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Omen Seer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Minor Prophecy Witchcraft option. If you already know it, you can choose a different Witchcraft option.</p><p>Additionally, you gain two additional uses for Minor Prophecy and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0c4803b2a23b334","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The resilience of giants flows through your body. Your hit point maximum increases by 3, and it increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, when you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 10 + your Strength modifier + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0c923cf7a98e455","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ever-Ready Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a use of Arcane Shot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0ccf262db3b94e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar of the Beyond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Arcana and Religion skills and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for these skills.</p><p>Additionally, you can cast Detect Evil and Good without expending a spell slot a number of times equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0ce6290f42f30ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast Conclave Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Beast Conclave Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Beast Bond</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Animal Messenger</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Catnap</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Charm Monster</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Awaken</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0cfd6bbfe9343a9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have formed a bond with a wildfire spirit, a primal being of creation and destruction. Your link with this spirit grants you access to some spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Circle of Wildfire Spells table.</p><p>Once you gain access to one of these spells, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day. If you gain access to a spell that doesn't appear on the druid spell list, the spell is nonetheless a druid spell for you.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Circle of Wildfire Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Cure Wounds, Flaming Sphere, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Fireball, Revivify</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Aura of Life, Fire Shield</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Flame Strike, Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-ice-teardrop.webp","_id":"s0d075e72ed36e61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cantrip","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know one cantrip of your choice from the cleric, wizard, or sorcerer spell list. Your spellcasting ability for it is INT, WIS, or CHA (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cross-circle-blue.webp","_id":"s0db7d30ec741370","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0df69ec9052bbb3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sudden Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you attack a creature that you are hidden from, you can make an additional attack as part of your attack action. On the first turn of combat, you can apply your Sneak Attack to both of these attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0dfecad39d7995b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Chemical Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:</p><ul><li>You gain Resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are Immune to the Poisoned condition.</li><li>You can cast Greater Restoration and Heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you have alchemist's supplies on your person. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a Long Rest.</li><li>Potent Healing: When you cast an Artificer spell that restores hit points, you treat the spell as two spell levels higher for the purpose of determining the amount of hit points restored.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/vials-blue-pink.webp","_id":"s0e0768e7a185665","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vivisectionist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach an Artificer level specified in the Vivisectionist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Vivisectionist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>False Life, Shocking Grasp, Witch Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Envenom, Enhance Ability</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Animate Dead, Call Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Blight, Death Ward</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Antilife Shell, Raise Dead</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0e09af6d1363db2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Duplicity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The illusion of your Invoke Duplicity has grown more powerful in the following ways.</p><ul><li><strong>Shared Distraction.</strong> When you and your allies make Attack Rolls against a creature within 5 feet of the illusion, the Attack Rolls have Advantage.</li><li><strong>Healing Illusion.</strong> When the illusion ends, you or a creature of your choice within 5 feet of it regains a number of Hit Points equal to your Cleric level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0e1d80e0f1ffa02","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword and Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Sword Mage Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Compelled Duel, Wrathful Smite, Branding Smite, Magic Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Blinding Smite, Elemental Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Staggering Smite, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Banishing Smite, Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0e5db8b3a156f40","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take a Fighting Style option more than once, even if you later get to choose again.</p><h5>Archery</h5><p>You gain a +2 bonus to Attack Rolls you make with ranged weapons.</p><h5>Close Quarters Shooter</h5><p>When making a ranged weapon attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. You have a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls on ranged weapon attacks.</p><h5>Defense</h5><p>While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Druidic Warrior</h5><p>You learn two cantrips of your choice from the druid spell list. They count as ranger spells for you, and Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them. Whenever you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip from the druid spell list.</p><h5>Dueling</h5><p>When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon.</p><h5>Great Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.</p><h5>Mariner</h5><p>As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a Swim Speed and a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Protection</h5><p>When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. You must be wielding a shield.</p><h5>Two-Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.</p><h5>Superior Technique</h5><p>You learn one maneuver of your choice from among those available to the fighter archetype. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).</p><p>You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach level 10, the size of this die increases to a d8.</p><h5>Blind Fighting</h5><p>You have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</p><h5>Interception</h5><p>When a creature you can see hits a target, other than you, within 5 feet of you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by 1d10 + your Proficiency bonus (to a minimum of 0 damage). You must be wielding a shield or a simple or martial weapon to use this Reaction.</p><h5>Thrown Weapon Fighting</h5><p>You can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.</p><p>In addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll.</p><h5>Unarmed Fighting</h5><p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-daggers-orange.webp","_id":"s0e8d1361f0f0a78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428437,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Action Surge feature, you can choose one creature within 60 feet of you that is allied with you. That creature can make one melee or ranged weapon attack with its Reaction, provided that it can see or hear you.</p><p>Starting at 18th level, you can choose two allies within 60 feet of you, rather than one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"s0f1185b34ed701a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Peerless Athlete","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in acrobatics or athletics. When you make Strength or Dexterity check, you can add your Charisma modifier to it. You can do so a number of times equal to your Proficiency and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0f14029d00cde3d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Halfling Nimbleness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move through the space of any creature that is of a size larger than yours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s0fa81d9b68e5f07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warrior of the Gods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A divine entity helps ensure you can continue the fight. You have a pool of four d12s that you can spend to heal yourself. As a Bonus Action, you can expend dice from the pool, roll them, and regain a number of Hit Points equal to the roll's total.</p><p>Your pool regains one die when you finish a Short Rest, and all expended dice when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>The pool's maximum number of dice increases by one when you reach Barbarian levels 6 (5 dice), 12 (6 dice), and 17 (7 dice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0fc55f56eba6256","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428323,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Manipulation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have discovered ways to manipulate elemental energy in dynamic ways, including adapting more nuanced kinetic shapes, either temporary or persistent.</p><p><strong>Elemental Infusions.</strong> You gain two elemental infusions of your choice. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page. When you gain certain kineticist levels, you gain additional infusions of your choice.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the infusions you know and replace it with another infusion that you could learn at that level.</p><p>If an elemental infusion has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the infusion at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.</p><p>Some infusions modify your kinetic shape. There are modifications for your kinetic blast and kinetic blade, and kinetic shape effects. You can only apply one one shape modification and one shape effect to the same use of a kinetic shape.</p><p><strong>Kinesis Points.</strong> You have 2 kinesis points, which are used to power some of your elemental infusions. You gain one additional point every time you level up, to a maximum of 20 at level 20.</p><p>You can never have more kinesis points than shown on the table for your level. You regain all spent kinesis points when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Reserves.</strong> You gain the following ways to spend your kinesis points.</p><ul><li><strong>Kinetic Enhancement.</strong> When you make an Ability Check, you can spend 1 kinesis point to gain Advantage on the check.</li><li><strong>Kinetic Shield.</strong> When you take acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, you can spend 1 kinesis point and use your Reaction to grant yourself Resistance against that instance of the damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.kineticist.kinesis-points","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/abstract-ribbons-red-orange.webp","_id":"s0fd6902f16322d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428345,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bountiful Harvest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two tools from among alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit. Your Proficiency Bonus for checks with the chosen tools is doubled.</p><p>Additionally, when you forage for food or ingredients, you can roll the die on the result column twice and take the higher result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1018dad6844153c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unsleeping","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Shadowborn require neither food nor sleep. To sustain themselves they instead harness energy from the Shadowplane, for which they need to enter a state similar to deep meditation for 4 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/moon-crescent.webp","_id":"s1040602e3f6b896","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite Improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Crimson Rite.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s104bf2ffbac07c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Maker's Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in three tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/wave-halt-stop.webp","_id":"s10d98f46e7c78b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Wanderer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Fey Wanderer Spells table. Each spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fey Wanderer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Charm Person</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Dimension Door</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Mislead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>You also possess a preternatural blessing from a fey ally or a place of fey power. Choose your blessing from the Feywild Gifts table or determine it randomly.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Feywild Gifts</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Gift</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Illusory butterflies flutter around you while you take a Short or a Long Rest.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Fresh, seasonal flowers sprout from your hair each dawn.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>You faintly smell of cinnamon, lavender, nutmeg, or another comforting herb or spice.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Your shadow dances while no one is looking directly at it.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Horns or antlers sprout from your head.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Your skin and hair change color to match the season at each dawn.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s10e0b7f6d94c074","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the nature skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/leaf-juggle-humanoid-green.webp","_id":"s1131813d0d8c6ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to chastise anyone who dares wield beguilements against you and your wards. Whenever you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you succeeds on an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to deal 2d8 + your Charisma modifier force damage to the creature that forced the Saving Throw.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s117d9b594b9b8b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Self-Restoration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sheer force of will, you can remove one of the following conditions from yourself at the end of each of your turns: Charmed, Frightened, or Poisoned.</p><p>In addition, forgoing food and drink doesn't give you levels of Exhaustion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-flared-green.webp","_id":"s11a1e633a497c96","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you choose this path, you learn to speak, read, and write Giant or one other language of your choice if you already know Giant. Additionally, you learn either the Druidcraft or Thaumaturgy cantrip (your choice). Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for this spell.</p><p>You are proficient with ranged weapon attacks you make with improvised weapons. When you make a ranged weapon attack with an improvised weapon or a thrown weapon, you do not suffer Disadvantage for attacking at long range with either.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s11a7d6c0fc4a6e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insightful","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the insight skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s11c26fd09f7c17c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Devotion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your study of psionics begins to unleash your mind's potential. When you gain this feature, choose one of the following cantrips: friends, mage hand, or message. You learn that cantrip if you don't already know it, and it doesn't count against the number of wizard cantrips you know. While your psionic focus is on your person, you can cast the chosen cantrip as a Bonus Action, requiring no components, and with the modification listed below:</p><p><strong>Friends.</strong> When the spell ends, the target doesn't become hostile to you.</p><p><strong>Mage Hand.</strong> You can make the hand Invisible when you cast the spell, and controlling the spell is a Bonus Action for you.</p><p><strong>Message.</strong> You don't need to point toward the target or whisper your message out loud.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s11e8685cdd2c67b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. It is represented by your Psionic Energy Dice, which fuel powers you have from this subclass. The Psi Warrior Energy Dice table shows the die size and number of these dice you have when you reach certain Fighter levels.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Psi Warrior Energy Dice</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Die Size</th><th scope=\"col\">Number</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>D6</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>D8</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>D8</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>D10</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>D10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>D12</td><td>12</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Any features in this subclass that use a Psionic Energy Die use only the dice from this subclass. Some of your powers expend the Psionic Energy Die, as specified in a power's description, and you can't use a power if it requires you to use a die when all your Psionic Energy Dice are expended.</p><p>You regain one of your expended Psionic Energy Dice when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all of them when you finish a Long Rest.</p><ul><li><strong>Protective Field.</strong> When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can take a Reaction to expend one Psionic Energy Die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.</li><li><strong>Psionic Strike.</strong> You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of yourself with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy Die, rolling it and dealing Force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.</li><li><strong>Telekinetic Movement.</strong> You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As a Magic action, choose one target you can see within 30 feet of yourself; the target must be a loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature other than you. You transport the target up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if the target is a Tiny object, you can transport it to or from your hand.</li><li>Once you take this action, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest unless you expend a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) to restore your use of it.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s11f961a2a64b19d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead. Moreover, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s120c8f496a2e7b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The maneuvers are presented in alphabetical order.</p><h5>Commander's Strike</h5><p>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of your attacks to direct one of your companions to strike. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you and expend one superiority die. That creature can immediately use its Reaction to make one weapon attack, adding the superiority die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Disarming Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to disarm the target, forcing it to drop one item of your choice that it's holding. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, it drops the object you choose. The object lands at its feet.</p><h5>Distracting Strike</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to distract the creature, giving your allies an opening. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll. The next Attack Roll against the target by an attacker other than you has Advantage if the attack is made before the start of your next turn.</p><h5>Evasive Footwork</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die and take the Disengage action. You also roll the die and add the number rolled to your AC until the start of your next turn.</p><h5>Feinting Attack</h5><p>When you make a melee weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to perform a feint. The target of the attack has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, you have Advantage on this attack roll against the target and you add your superiority die to the damage if the attack hits.</p><h5>Goading Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage on all Attack Rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Lunging Attack</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die and take the Dash action. If you move at least 5 feet in a straight line immediately before hitting with a melee attack as part of the Attack action on this turn, you can add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Maneuvering Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to maneuver one of your comrades into a more advantageous position. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and you choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its Reaction to move up to half its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks from the target of your attack.</p><h5>Menacing Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to frighten the target. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, it is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Parry</h5><p>When another creature damages you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction and expend one superiority die to reduce the damage by the number you roll on your superiority die + STR or DEX modifier (your choice) + fighter level.</p><h5>Precision Attack</h5><p>When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can expend one Superiority Die, roll that die, and add it to the Attack Roll, potentially causing the attack to hit.</p><h5>Pushing Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to drive the target back. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, you push the target up to 15 feet away from you.</p><h5>Rally</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die to bolster the resolve of a companion. Choose an ally of yours within 30 feet of yourself who can see or hear you. That creature gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the Superiority Die roll plus half your Fighter level (round down).</p><h5>Riposte</h5><p>When a creature misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction and expend one superiority die to make a melee weapon attack against the creature. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Staggering Strike</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock a target off-balance. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Sweeping Attack</h5><p>When you make a melee weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to perform a powerful arcing swing around you. The original target and any other creature within your reach has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failure, a target takes damage equal to one roll of your superiority die.</p><h5>Trip Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock the target down. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, you knock the target Prone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s12afb239daf24b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two of your skill proficiencies, or one of your skill proficiencies and your Proficiency with thieves' tools. Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses either of the chosen proficiencies.</p><p>At 6th level, you can choose two more of your proficiencies (in skills or with thieves' tools) to gain this benefit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"s12d1b9531fe395d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428439,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Spell Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can choose another creatue you can see within 30 feet and surround it with a protective barrier that wards against spells. For 1 hour, the target gains Resistance against the damage of spells. At level 6, it also benefits from your Aura of Protection even when outside its radius or when you're Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s12e574207485eb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flexible Casting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your sorcery points to gain additional spell slots, or sacrifice spell slots to gain additional sorcery points. You learn other ways to use your sorcery points as you reach higher levels.</p><p><strong>Creating Spell Slots.</strong> You can transform unexpended sorcery points into one spell slot on your turn (no Action required). The created spell slots vanish at the end of a Long Rest. The Creating Spell Slots table shows the cost of creating a spell slot of a given level. You can create spell slots no higher in level than 5th.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Creating Spell Slots</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Slot Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Sorcery Point Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>7</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Converting a Spell Slot to Sorcery Points.</strong> You can expend one spell slot and gain a number of sorcery points equal to the slot's level (no Action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-shock-wave-teal.webp","_id":"s13696402dc79974","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knowledge of the Ages","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the history and arcana skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-book-study-purple.webp","_id":"s13bd3878d4c233f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with the disguise kit and the poisoner's kit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s13cc23d7787f6cd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inner Light","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in persuasion. Additionally, when you use your Lay on Hands on a creature, it also gains a 1d4 bonus to the next Saving Throw it makes before the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s13cdca0c3cbfb55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428352,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Shadowborn do not breathe, cannot benefit from regular healing except for class features that can target only themselves, are Immune to Poison and Disease, and vulnerable to Radiant Damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/death/skull-energy-light-white.webp","_id":"s13d4999fc7ffb19","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mingle with the Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Levitate spell once with this trait, requiring no material components, and you regain the ability to cast it this way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-weather-snow-gusts.webp","_id":"s13ffb34474db014","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armored Hulk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter a rage, you gain the temporary hit points from your armor mastery again, which stack with any existing temporary hit points from that feature. These temporary hit points last until your rage ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s142c1c195789404","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cantrip","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know one cantrip of your choice from the bard, wizard, or sorcerer spell list. Your spellcasting ability for it is INT, WIS, or CHA (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cross-circle-blue.webp","_id":"s14d79d35e2677d1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Whirling Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Bonus Action on your turn, which you can use to make a melee weapon attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1508828442fac83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter Conclave Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hunter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Hunter's Mark</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Pass without Trace</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Barrage</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s151187f27c80d7a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in three of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Athletics, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival. You can choose to gain Proficiency with thieves' tools in place of one skill choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s1511f4b81ae78aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428344,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stalker's Instinct","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a +2 bonus to initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-roar-rush-orange.webp","_id":"s15672e8f50efc52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cleansing Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you lose Lay on Hands on a creature, you can also remove one or more of the following conditions: Blinded, Charmed, Confused, Dazed, Deafened, Dominated, Frightened, Paralyzed, or Stunned by spending 5 points per condition from your pool of healing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-teal.webp","_id":"s15c1d45bd6ef3ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sear Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use Turn Undead, you can roll a number of d8s equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1d8) and add the rolls together. Each Undead that fails its Saving Throw against that use of Turn Undead takes Radiant damage equal to the roll's total. This damage doesn't end the turn effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-impact-shock-wave.webp","_id":"s15d471ee04dc9c1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nature's Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through your magical connection to nature, you can communicate simple ideas with plants. To use this feature, you have to touch the plant you wish to communicate with.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-sproud-hands-dirt-green.webp","_id":"s15e6554315b8e74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Twisting Roots.</strong> While shifted, the ground in a 10 feet circle around you is 3 for your enemies. When a creature starts its turn in that area or enters it for the first time on a turn, you can use your Reaction to force it to make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, its Speed is reduced to 0 until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Fey Step.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 2nd Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li><li><strong>Addling Spores.</strong> As an Action, you launch a cloud of befuddling spores at a location within 30 feet of you. Each creature within a 10 feet radius sphere around that point has to make a Constitution a Saving Throw or be Confused until the end of your next turn.</li><li>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 3rd Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s15fb7d5b89776fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Smite Infidel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can mark that creature until the end of your next turn. The first attack that hits the marked creature deals additional radiant damage equal to half your warlord level (rounded down) + your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1661933877bf3ee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Retaliation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage from a creature that is within reach of your equipped melee weapon, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow.webp","_id":"s16626ebd359c44c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Touch of the Long Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your touch can channel the energy of death into a creature. As an Action, you touch one creature within 5 feet of you, and you expend 1 to 10 ki points. The target must make a Constitution Saving Throw, and it takes 2d10 necrotic damage per ki point spent on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that failed this Saving Throw has to repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turn. On a failure, it takes necrotic damage equal to your monk level. Until it succeeds, the creature cannot benefit from healing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s168da17119597fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Use Magic Device","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Attunement.</strong> You can attune to up to four magic items at once.</li><li><strong>Charges.</strong> Whenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges.</li><li><strong>Scrolls.</strong> You can use any Spell Scroll, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for the spell. If the spell is a cantrip or a level 1 spell, you can cast it reliably. If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC 10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, you cast the spell from the scroll. On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-chain.webp","_id":"s16ac2502d875026","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lucky","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll a 1 on the d20 for an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/gaming/dice-runed-brown.webp","_id":"s1754f5d0f738120","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"A Feast for Crows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when a creature fails its Saving Throw against your Unnerving Aura or when you damage a creature within its area of effect, you deal 1d10 + your Wisdom modifier necrotic damage to it and regain hit points equal to the damage dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s178321915f85835","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empower Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after a creature you can see within 30 feet of you casts a level 1+ spell, you can take a Reaction to absorb magical energy from the spell. When you do so, until the end of your next turn, the next time you hit with your Sneak Attack you deal extra Force damage. To determine the extra damage, roll a number of d6s equal to the spell's level, and add them together.</p><p>You can take this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s17d92ebe74df358","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You mantle yourself in magical serenity. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to all damage and Advantage on all Saving Throws. If you deal damage to a creature, force it to make a Saving Throw, or otherwise target it with a harmful effect, this feature stops working until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Any creature that damages or your allies you while in your Aura of Protection takes 10 radiant damage. It takes this damage only once per turn. This damage does not suspend any of your subclass features.</li><li>If you heal a target with your Lay on Hands, the amount of healing it receives per point is doubled. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s17e2fc7a7896089","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steps of the Fey","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron grants you the ability to move between the boundaries of the planes. You learn the Misty Step spell and you can cast it without expending a spell slot a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, whenever you cast that spell, you can choose one of the following additional effects.</p><p><strong>Refreshing Step.</strong> Immediately after you teleport, you or one creature you can see within 10 feet of yourself gains Temporary Hit Points equal to half your Warlock level (rounded down) + your Charisma modifier.</p><p><strong>Taunting Step.</strong> Creatures within 5 feet of the space you left must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against creatures other than you until the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s18893dc912838c7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428369,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Small Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas with Small or smaller beasts. Forest gnomes love animals and often keep squirrels, badgers, rabbits, moles, woodpeckers, and other creatures as beloved pets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rodent-rat-green.webp","_id":"s1889be4dc9d66a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Powerful Bloodline","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion grows to Large size and the reach of its bite attack increase to 10 feet, it also no longer suffers from restrictions to its flying capabilities while you are riding it as long it is at least one size larger than you.</p><p>Additionally, your companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s18990e21880462f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vengeful Ancestors","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ancestral spirits grow powerful enough to retaliate. When you use your Spirit Shield to reduce the damage of an attack, the attacker takes an amount of force damage equal to the damage that your Spirit Shield prevents.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-evil-horned-giant.webp","_id":"s19404a0ff8a335e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Hexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spread your Hexblade's Curse from a slain creature to another creature. When the creature cursed by your Hexblade's Curse dies, you can apply the curse to a different creature you can see within 30 feet of you, provided you aren't Incapacitated. When you apply the curse in this way, you don't regain hit points from the death of the previously cursed creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1958cd7a1c18e2d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose a second option from the Fighting Style class feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-purple.webp","_id":"s1995b56370f4ca4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Devious Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed yourself in new ways to use your Sneak Attack. The following effects are now among your Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Daze (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or become Dazed until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Knock Out (Cost: 6d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or drop Unconscious for 1d4 hours or until it takes damage.</li><li><strong>Obscure (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or become Blinded until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/sword-stuck-glowing-pink.webp","_id":"s1997c37e921a8ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Coil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Tentacle of the Deeps can defend you and others, interposing itself between them and harm. When you or a creature you can see takes damage while within 10 feet of the tentacle, you can use your Reaction to choose one of those creatures and reduce the damage to that creature by 1d8 + your Charisma modifier. When you reach 10th level in this class, the damage reduced by the tentacle increases to 2d8 + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s19e5c72a1c90673","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swift Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your add your Intelligence modifier to Initiative rolls.</p><p>Additionally, you can use your Cunning Action and Master of Tactics as part of the same Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s19f3d5e017a766a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. Choose one benefit for each signature spell from the list below. Whenever you cast one of your signature spells, it gains the chosen benefit. You cannot choose the same benefit for both of your signature spells.</p><p><strong>Intensified.</strong> The spell counts as 2 spell levels higher for the purpose of dealing damage.</p><p><strong>Labyrinthine.</strong> The spell cannot be counterspelled or dispelled.</p><p><strong>Focus.</strong> The spell no longer requires Concentration.</p><p><strong>Magnified.</strong> The spell's area of effect is doubled and you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your INT modifier from the effect.</p><p><strong>Overhelming.</strong> The Spell Save DC for this spell receives a +3 bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/beam-impact-purple.webp","_id":"s19f8de73e05f223","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aether Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can magically step into the veil between the planes as long as you aren't Incapacitated. Your movement doesn't provoke Attacks of Opportunity and you can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3, as well as see and affect creatures and objects on the Ethereal Plane. You take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside an object.</p><p>This feature lasts for one minute. If you are inside an object when it ends, you are immediately shunted to the nearest unoccupied space and you take force damage equal to twice the number of feet you moved.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest - or until you spend a use of your Blood Maledict to regain it. You can use Aether Walk twice between rests starting at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1a2310d76618ee5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Eldritch Knights combine the martial mastery common to all Fighters with a careful study of magic. Their spells both complement and extend their combat skills, providing additional protection to shore up their armor and also allowing them to engage many foes at once with explosive magic. The information below details how you use those rules with Wizard spells, which appear on the Wizard spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two cantrips of your choice from the Wizard spell list. Whenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the Wizard spell list.</p><p>When you reach Fighter level 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the Wizard spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Fighter levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the Wizard spell list until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Fighter, your list of prepared spells can include five Wizard spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Fighter level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Wizard spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a Spellcasting Focus for your Wizard spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s1a80ee13050dcad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Shot Options","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Arcane Shot feature lets you choose options for it at certain levels. The options are presented here in alphabetical order. They are all magical effects, and each one is associated with one of the schools of magic.</p><p>If an option requires a Saving Throw, your Arcane Shot save DC is calculated as follows:</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Arcane Shot save DC</strong> = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier + your Wisdom modifier</p><h5>Banishing Shot</h5><p>You use abjuration magic to try to temporarily banish your target to a harmless demiplane. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x Proficiency extra force damage and must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw or be banished. While banished in this way, the target is Incapacitated. At the end of its next turn, the target reappears in the space it vacated or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied.</p><h5>Beguiling Shot</h5><p>Your enchantment magic causes this projectile to temporarily beguile its target. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x Proficiency extra psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it is Charmed by the chosen ally for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><h5>Bursting Shot</h5><p>You imbue your projectile with force energy drawn from the school of evocation. The energy detonates after your attack. Immediately after the projectile hits the creature, The target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take D6 x your Proficiency force damage.</p><h5>Dimensional Shot</h5><p>You target an unoccupied space within 20 x your Proficiency ft that you can see instead of a creature. You shoot the projectile at the location and then teleport towards it. Any effect that prevents the projectile from reaching its destination also cuts short your teleport. In such a case you instead teleport to where the projectile was stopped or to the nearest unoccupied space of your choice.</p><h5>Enfeebling Shot</h5><p>You weave necromantic magic into your projectile. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><h5>Grasping Shot</h5><p>When this projectile strikes its target, transmutation magic turns it into grasping, poisonous brambles, which wrap around the target. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra poison damage, its Speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it takes D6 x your Proficiency slashing damage the first time on each turn it moves 1 foot or more without teleporting. The target or any creature that can reach it can use its action to remove the brambles with a successful Strength (Athletics) check against your Arcane Shot save DC. Otherwise, the brambles last for 1 minute or until you use this option again.</p><h5>Seeking Shot</h5><p>Using divination magic, you grant your projectile the ability to seek out a target. When you use this option, you don't make an Attack Roll for the attack. Instead, choose one creature you have seen in the past minute. The projectile flies toward that creature, moving around corners if necessary and ignoring three-quarters cover and half cover. If the target is within the weapon's range and there is a path large enough for the projectile to travel to the target, the target must make a Dexterity Saving Throw. Otherwise, the projectile disappears after traveling as far as it can. On a failed save, the target takes damage as if it were hit by the projectile, plus an extra D6 x your Proficiency force damage, and you learn the target's current location. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and you don't learn its location.</p><h5>Shadow Shot</h5><p>You weave illusion magic into your projectile, causing it to occlude your foe's vision with shadows. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra psychic damage, and it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be unable to see anything farther than 5 feet away for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1a875a08a1a7a88","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcery Incarnate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you have no uses of Innate Sorcery left, you can use it if you spend 2 Sorcery Points when you take the Bonus Action to activate it.</p><p>In addition, while your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use up to two of your Metamagic options on each spell you cast.</p><p>Additionally, you add your Charisma modifier to the damage you deal with any Sorcerer cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-teal.webp","_id":"s1acbf781235584f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rage of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Rage taps into the primal power of animals. Whenever you activate your Rage, you gain one of the following options of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1af3ab52eec75c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heroic Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Reaction to recover hitpoints equal to half your hitpoint maximum. Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you complete a Long Rest. You can spend three uses of your Indomitable feature to regain a use of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1af9d5362a6a8d4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Earth","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the earth allows you to move freely through the ground. You gain a Burrow Speed equal to your Speed and tremorsense in a radius of 60 feet around you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1b02b78cd2cb615","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Defensive Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/leaf-rune-glow-green.webp","_id":"s1b1369b20165436","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Forms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel lunar magic when you assume a Wild Shape form, granting you the benefits below.</p><ul><li><strong>Challenge Rating.</strong> The maximum Challenge Rating for the form equals your Druid level divided by 3 (round down).</li><li><strong>Armor Class.</strong> Until you leave the form, your AC equals 13 plus your Wisdom modifier if that total is higher than the Beast's AC.</li><li><strong>Temporary Hit Points.</strong> You gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to three times your Druid level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1b209c021511aad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Signature Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a 1st-level wizard spell and a 2nd-level wizard spell that are in your spellbook. You can cast those spells at their lowest level without expending a spell slot when you have them prepared. If you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.</p><p>By spending 8 hours in study, you can exchange one or both of the spells you chose for different spells of the same levels.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/projectile-wave-arrow.webp","_id":"s1b26330f2ee775a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spectral Blade Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can spend 6 ki points to and choose up to seven creatures you can see within 30 ft. Make a melee attack against each target. On a hit, a target takes 5d12 psychic damage and you can use one effect from your Psychic Slash feature against it (no additional ki required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1b38b8153cd1985","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fireheart","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to fire damage and you are acclimatized to extreme heat as per the DMG.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/elemental-fire-humanoid.webp","_id":"s1b3d61eb7f81a57","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1b4e7030b7746c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sylvan Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your creature type is both humanoid and fey.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/fae-fairy-winged-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s1b591a8ff2af47f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you are not wearing armor or wielding a shield. This bonus increases when you reach certain monk levels, as shown in the Monk table.</p><p>At 9th level, you gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling during the move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/root-vine-entangle-foot-green.webp","_id":"s1b9bfaa752fc683","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite Improvement (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Crimson Rite.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s1bc79e0f2500f14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unquenchable Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Continual Flame spell once with this trait, requiring no material components, and you regain the ability to cast it this way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-hand-orange.webp","_id":"s1bcc81290e9ec6a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Discoveries","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list or any combination thereof (see a class's section for its spell list). A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1bea6c341068eb3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Conversion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can replace the damage of any of your elemental disciplines with that of another elemental discipline you know when you use them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c0880f7751f4d4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bestial Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter your rage, the influence of your bestial spark on your form intensifies. You gain the listed benefit for your natural weapon for the duration of your rage. This effect only applies to attacks with your chosen natural weapon.</p><p><strong>Bite.</strong> When you damage a creature, you regain hitpoints equal to half your Proficiency (rounded up). This amount is doubled against creatures that have half or less of their maximum hitpoints and tripled if you reduce it to 0 hitpoints.</p><p><strong>Claws.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you attack a creature, you can immediately make another attack.</p><p><strong>Horns.</strong> Your critical range increases by 1. On your turn, when you move towards a creature in a straight line for the first time, you can add 1 damage for every 5 ft spent as part of that movement to the first melee weapon damage roll you make against that creature.</p><p><strong>Hooves.</strong> Once per turn, when you hit a creature that is no more than 1 size larger than you, you can attempt to shove the target as part of this attack. Attacks against Prone creatures deal additional damage equal to your Proficiency.</p><p><strong>Pincers.</strong> Once per turn, when you hit a creature that is no more than 1 size larger than you, you can attempt to grapple the target as part of this attack. Creatures Grappled by you have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls.</p><p><strong>Tail.</strong> Your reach increases by 5 feet and when an enemy provokes an Opportunity Attack from you, you can make the attack without spending a Reaction, but you cannot make another Opportunity Attack until the start of your next turn.</p><p>If a creature you can see within your reach hits you with an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to add your Strength modifier to your AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c368907184b225","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428321,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Storm Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Thunderwave, Witch Bolt, Shatter, Warding Wind</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Call Lightning, Wind Wall</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Storm Sphere, Thunder Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Control Winds, Destructive Wave</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c3f88c09110fc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428366,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of the Watchers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A paladin who assumes the Oath of the Watchers swears to safeguard mortal realms from otherworldly threats.</p><p><strong>Vigilance.</strong> The threats you face are cunning, powerful, and subversive. Be ever alert for their corruption.</p><p><strong>Loyalty.</strong> Never accept gifts or favors from fiends or those who truck with them. Stay true to your order, your comrades, and your duty.</p><p><strong>Discipline.</strong> You are the shield against the endless terrors that lie beyond the stars. Your blade must be forever sharp and your mind keen to survive what lies beyond.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c8713c71072194","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Ravage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at 14th level, your mastery over blood magic transcends the mere physical. You ignore Immunity to the Lacerated condition and the blood requirement (both for the target creature and for material components) for class features and spells.</p><p>Additionally, any Lacerated condition caused by your spells cannot be removed by healing and heals you for half the damage dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c91a37b89f5624","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ecclesitheurgy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two cantrips and two spells from the cleric spell list. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Wizard table. Whenever you gain a wizard level after this one, you can replace one of the wizard spells you add to your spellbook with a spell from the cleric spell list. Any of the spells gained in this manner count as wizard spells for you.</p><p>Additionally, you can copy cleric spells into your spellbook from scrolls or the spellbooks of other theurgists. If you do so, they count as wizard spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1cc25164526ab4d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Intervention","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on your deity or pantheon to intervene on your behalf. As a Magic action, choose any Cleric spell of level 5 or lower that requires an Action or a Bonus Action to cast. As part of the same action, you cast that spell without expending a spell slot or needing Material components. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue-purple.webp","_id":"s1dc04f83c7c8ab3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of the Serpent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to Gargan deepens, causing your unarmed attacks to count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>Additionally, you gain Resistance to lightning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1dc0fa6e6b16677","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with armorsmith's tools and weaponsmith's tools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s1dcf6d2b52fd97c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Overchannel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase the power of your simpler spells. When you cast a wizard spell that deals damage, you can deal maximum damage with that spell.</p><p>The first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a Long Rest, you take 2d12 necrotic damage for each level of the spell, immediately after you cast it. Each time you use this feature again before finishing a Long Rest, the necrotic damage per spell level increases by 1d12. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/projectile-faceted-glob.webp","_id":"s1e011e0e883500e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the mastery benefits for two weapons of your choice as well as an armor type (see Armor Mastery and Weapon Mastery variant rules). You must be proficient in the chosen weapons and armor. If you possess the Unarmored Defense feature, you may choose it in place of an armor type.</p><p>You can change your choices when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/maneuver-sword-katana-yellow.webp","_id":"s1e10999e1cfebf0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Necromancy Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Necromancy school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Necromancy school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e33be8271ad904","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428378,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ordained Huntsman","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in three of the following skills: Animal Handling, Nature, Perception, Stealth, Survival. You can use your Wisdom in place any ability score normally used for any of these skills, regardless of whether you obtained them through this feature.</p><p>Additionally, you can perform up to two tasks during the Travel Phase of Overland Travel.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e67e4d9f4ea521","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of the Sentinel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emit an aura of alertness while you aren't Incapacitated. When you and any creatures of your choice within 10 feet of you roll initiative, you all gain a bonus to initiative equal to your Proficiency bonus.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1ed580bb6f7e27f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Order's Demand","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to exert an intimidating presence over others.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol, and each creature of your choice that can see or hear you within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be Charmed by you until the end of your next turn or until the Charmed creature takes any damage. You can also cause any of the Charmed creatures to drop what they are holding when they fail the Saving Throw.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1f3602991f8c281","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Revelation in Flesh","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unleash the aberrant truth hidden within yourself. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 or more sorcery points to magically transform your body for 10 minutes. For each sorcery point you spend, you can gain one of the following benefits of your choice, the effects of which last until the transformation ends:</p><ul><li>You can see any Invisible creature within 60 feet of you, provided it isn't behind total cover. Your eyes also turn black or become writhing sensory tendrils.</li><li>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed, and you can hover. As you fly, your skin glistens with mucus or shines with an otherworldly light.</li><li>You gain a Swim Speed equal to twice your Speed, and you can breathe underwater. Moreover, gills grow from your neck or fan out from behind your ears, your fingers become webbed, or you grow writhing cilia that extend through your clothing.</li><li>Your body, along with any equipment you are wearing or carrying, becomes slimy and pliable. You can move through any space as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing, and you can spend 5 feet of movement to escape from nonmagical restraints or being Grappled.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1f46135cd2ca679","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Host Caller's Link","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use the Summoner's Call or Transposition class feature, you can target another creature you have summoned instead of your Eidolon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1f5a121711293e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Instinct","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your instincts are so honed that you have Advantage on initiative rolls.</p><p>Additionally, you cannot be Surprised while you are not Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/wolf-howl-moon-forest-blue.webp","_id":"s1fa63c9e1ee3391","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bolstering Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can harness your wild magic to bolster yourself or a companion. As an Action, you can touch one creature (which can be yourself) and confer one of the following benefits of your choice to that creature:</p><ul><li>For 10 minutes, the creature can roll a d3 whenever making an Attack Roll or an Ability Check and add the number rolled to the d20 roll.</li><li>Roll a d3. The creature regains one expended spell slot, the level of which equals the number rolled or lower (the creature's choice). Once a creature receives this benefit, that creature can't receive it again until after a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>You can take this action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2030058cd290e2a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nymphsong","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Performance skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/music-singing-voice-blue.webp","_id":"s205965a1b54bb55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expert Forgery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can duplicate other creatures' handwriting and craftwork. You have Advantage on all checks made to produce forgeries or duplicates of existing objects. You must have access to these objects throughout the process to benefit from this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-brown-red.webp","_id":"s2095f8fd053a818","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Illusory Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature hits you with an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to interpose an illusory duplicate of yourself between the attacker and yourself. The attack automatically misses you, then the illusion dissipates.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 2+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s20a46e54f928776","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Old Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two cantrips and three spells of your choice from the Druid spell list. A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s20b5b424cb2406d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Maneuver Options","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you have access to maneuvers, the following maneuvers are added to the list of options available to you. Maneuvers are available to Battle Masters but also to characters who have a special feature like the Superior Technique fighting style or the Martial Adept feat.</p><h5>Ambush</h5><p>When you make a Dexterity (Stealth) check or an initiative roll, you can expend one superiority die and add the die to the roll, provided you aren't Incapacitated.</p><h5>Bait and Switch</h5><p>When you're within 5 feet of a creature on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and switch places with that creature, provided you spend at least 5 feet of movement and the creature is willing and isn't Incapacitated. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p><p>Roll the superiority die. Until the start of your next turn, you or the other creature (your choice) gains a bonus to AC equal to the number rolled. This effect ends early if either of you become Incapaciated or you are more than 5 feet away from each other. The AC bonus from this maneuver does not stack with that from Evasive Footwork.</p><h5>Brace</h5><p>When a creature you can see moves into the reach you have with the melee weapon you're wielding, you can use your Reaction to expend one superiority die and make one attack against the creature, using that weapon. If the attack hits, add the superiority die to the weapon's damage roll.</p><h5>Commanding Presence</h5><p>When you make a Charisma (Intimidation), a Charisma (Performance), or a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the Ability Check.</p><h5>Grappling Strike</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to grapple the target. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must make a Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target becomes Grappled by you.</p><h5>Quick Toss</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one superiority die and make a ranged attack with a weapon that has the thrown property. You can draw the weapon as part of making this attack. If you hit, add the superiority die to the weapon's damage roll.</p><h5>Tactical Assessment</h5><p>When you make an Intelligence (Investigation), an Intelligence (History), or a Wisdom (Insight) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the Ability Check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s20d6411637b948c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Conqueror's Countenance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in Intimidation. Additionally, the bonus damage of your Divine Smite also applies to any creature that is Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s20eb94f05308a86","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Potent Cantrip","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your damaging cantrips affect even creatures that avoid the brunt of the effect. When you cast a cantrip at a creature and you miss with the Attack Roll or the target succeeds on a Saving Throw against the cantrip, the target takes half the cantrip's damage (if any) but suffers no additional effect from the cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/projectiles-fire-stone-salvo.webp","_id":"s212d63c108b092f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expert Divination","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Casting divination spells comes so easily to you that it expends only a fraction of your spellcasting efforts. When you cast a divination spell of 2nd level or higher using a spell slot, you regain spell slots with a combined level one lower than the spell cast. The slot you regain can't be higher than 5th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s212dfb9b8892dc0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giantblooded","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"s214cb32b0f15cc6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Archdruid","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The vitality of nature constantly blooms within you, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Evergreen Wild Shape.</strong> Whenever you roll Initiative and have no uses of Wild Shape left, you regain one expended use of it.</li><li><strong>Nature Magician.</strong> You can convert uses of Wild Shape into a spell slot (no action required). Choose a number of your unexpended uses of Wild Shape and convert them into a single spell slot, with each use contributing 2 spell levels. For example, if you convert two uses of Wild Shape, you produce a level 4 spell slot. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</li><li><strong>Longevity.</strong> The primal magic that you wield causes you to age more slowly. For every ten years that pass, your body ages only one year.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/beam-hand-leaves-green.webp","_id":"s214d9d45799f6e1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clinging Frost","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher that deals cold damage or it fails a save against such a spell, the magical cold you command starts clinging to it for 1 minute, reducing its Speed by 10 feet.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature can make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. Each time it fails this Saving Throw, it suffers additional effects as per below. If it succeeds three times, the effect of your Clinging Frost ends on it.</p><ul><li><strong>One failed save:</strong> The affected creature cannot take Reactions.</li><li><strong>Two failed save:</strong> The affected creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls and Ability Checks.</li><li><strong>Three failed save:</strong> The affected creature is Frozen for 1 minute but does not have Resistance against cold damage caused by your spells and the effect of your Clinging Frost ends on it.</li></ul><p>This feature has no effect on creatures that cannot be Frozen.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s214e16a78cb2c08","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal damage to a creature with Planar Warrior, you can choose to impose one of the following effects:</p><ul><li><strong>Planar Pulse.</strong> You deal the damage of Planar Warrior to all creatures of your choice within 10 ft of your target.</li><li><strong>Sealing Strike.</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it cannot teleport move to a different Plane through any means until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Teleporting Strike.</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw or be teleported 30 ft horizontally to an unoccupied space your choice that is on a solid surface.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2167cd1f58bed00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of the Ancients","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tenets of the Oath of the Ancients have been preserved for uncounted centuries. This oath emphasizes the principles of good above any concerns of law or chaos. Its four central principles are simple.</p><p><strong>Kindle the Light.</strong> Through your acts of mercy, kindness, and forgiveness, kindle the light of hope in the world, beating back despair.</p><p><strong>Shelter the Light.</strong> Where there is good, beauty, love, and laughter in the world, stand against the wickedness that would swallow it. Where life flourishes, stand against the forces that would render it barren.</p><p><strong>Preserve Your Own Light.</strong> Delight in song and laughter, in beauty and art. If you allow the light to die in your own heart, you can't preserve it in the world.</p><p><strong>Be the Light.</strong> Be a glorious beacon for all who live in despair. Let the light of your joy and courage shine forth in all your deeds.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s216dfc620150e44","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428352,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Riposte","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an attack miss with the Shield spell, reduce damage to 0 with your Arcane Deflection, or successfully prevent a spell with Counterspell, you can magically retaliate as part of the same Reaction against the originator of the attack or damage if you can see it and it is within 120 feet of you.</p><p>The target has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure it takes force damage equal to a number of D8s times your Proficiency.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also expend a level 2+ spell slot to regain a use of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s21817656dded972","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Prey","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/dissolve-bone-skull.webp","_id":"s218759ac9a70c37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion. You can use your Intelligence in place of your Charisma for these skills.</p><p>When you fail a check using these skills, you can choose to reroll it, taking either result. Once you have done so and the reroll resulted in a success, you cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s21b07b9c7995441","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battlerager Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action while you are raging.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s21dd14986016d18","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Temporal Awareness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can add your Intelligence modifier to your initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s21f8317883accf5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428379,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of the Guardian","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can shield others from harm at the cost of your own health. When a creature within 10 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to magically take that damage, instead of that creature taking it. This feature doesn't transfer any other effects that might accompany the damage, and this damage can't be reduced in any way.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s22377d0cda6129b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your quick thinking and agility allow you to move and act quickly. You can take a Bonus Action on each of your turns in combat. This action can be used only to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-watch.webp","_id":"s225d35fb16edbea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hearth of Moonlight and Shadow","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Home can be wherever you are. During a Short or a Long Rest, you can invoke the shadowy power of the Gloaming Court to help guard your respite. At the start of the rest, you touch a point in space, and an invisible, 30-foot-radius sphere of magic appears, centered on that point. Total cover blocks the sphere.</p><p>While within the sphere, you and your allies gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) and Wisdom (Perception) checks, and any light from open flames in the sphere (a campfire, torches, or the like) isn't visible outside it.</p><p>The sphere vanishes at the end of the rest or when you leave the sphere.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s22ab72369c96fde","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silver Sisters Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p>Additionally, You gain Proficiency in martial weapons with the finesse property.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s22d3edd3d037a51","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to two damage types of your choice. Whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can change the damage types you chose.</p><p>As an Action, you can temporarily give up this Resistance and transfer it to one creature you touch. The creature keeps the Resistance until the end of your next Short or a Long Rest or until you transfer it back to yourself as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s22ef13b11b46555","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ethereal Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to step through the Ethereal Plane. As a Bonus Action, you can cast the etherealness spell with this feature, without expending a spell slot, but the spell lasts only 1 minute. During that time, you can use a Bonus Action to switch from the Etheral Plane to back to the Plane you are currently on or vice versa.</p><p>You use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s23377d14e19d8d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Druidic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know Druidic, the secret language of druids. While learning this ancient tongue, you also unlocked the magic of communicating with animals; you always have the Speak with Animals spell prepared.</p><p>You can use Druidic to leave hidden messages. You and others who know Druidic automatically spot such a message. Others spot the message's presence with a successful DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check but can't decipher it without magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"s233c5dfa1867643","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Manifest Echo","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to magically manifest an echo of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 15 feet of you. This echo is a magical, translucent, gray image of you that lasts until it is destroyed, until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action, until you manifest another echo, or until you're Incapacitated.</p><p>Your echo's AC is equal to yours, has 1 hit point, and Immunity to all conditions. If it has to make a Saving Throw, it uses your Saving Throw bonus for the roll. It is the same size as you, and it occupies its space. On your turn, you can mentally command the echo to move up to 30 feet in any direction (no action required). If your echo is ever more than 30 feet from you at the end of your turn, it is destroyed.</p><p>You can use the echo in the following ways:</p><ul><li>As a Bonus Action, you can teleport, magically swapping places with your echo at a cost of 15 feet of your movement, regardless of the distance between the two of you.</li><li>When you take the Attack action on your turn, any attack you make with that action can originate from your space or the echo's space. You make this choice for each attack.</li><li>When a creature that you can see within 5 feet of your echo moves at least 5 feet away from it, you can use your Reaction to make an Opportunity Attack against that creature as if you were in the echo's space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s237447fba26bf4a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inner Alchemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can suspend the effect of one potion with a duration of more than 1 minute currently affecting you. You can resume the effect of one potion suspended in this manner at any time as a Bonus Action. Deduct the time of the potion's effect in increments of 1 minute. When you finish a Long Rest, all potion effects still suspended on you end.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2386a44e08bfd4f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (7th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 7th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-symbol-skull-grey.webp","_id":"s2399d0ff8279722","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Panache","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You also learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Disarm (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Strength or Dexterity Saving Throw (target's choice) or drop 1 item of your choice that it is holding. The target has Advantage on this Saving Throw if it is holding the item with both hands or is at least 1 size larger than you. This feature has no effect against a creature more than 2 sizes larges than you.</li><li><strong>Goad (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against targets other than you and be unable to make Opportunity Attacks against targets other than you until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Parrying Stance (Cost: 2d6).</strong> Roll 2d6. You gain a bonus to your AC equal to half the number rolled (rounded up) until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s23bddd4924073f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Cunning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can perform an esoteric rite for 1 minute. At the end of it, you regain expended Pact Magic spell slots but no more than a number equal to half your maximum (round up). Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hand-green.webp","_id":"s240826511f0c2bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persecutor's Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Brand (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or lose the ability to cast spells and turn Invisible until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Castigate (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or subtract 1d6 from its next Saving Throw before the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s241fabd801db052","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can thunderously rebuke attackers. When a creature within 10 feet of you that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to cause the creature to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. The creature takes 1d8 x your Proficiency bonus lightning or thunder damage (your choice) on a failed Saving Throw, and half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s249b7acc9a36cfa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enhanced Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The weapon attacks of any creature you summon with a conjuration spell count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s24b389b4ae418b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Living Legend","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can empower yourself with the legends—whether true or exaggerated—of your great deeds. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>If your total for a Strength, Dexterity, or Charisma check is less than your Charisma score, you can use that score in place of the total.</li><li>Your weapon attacks deal additional damage equal to half your Paladin level. The damage type is the same as the weapon's.</li><li>When you're not Incapacitated and subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail. You can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s25308f00c7f24e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spider Queen's Chosen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Spider Queen extends her protection to you while you are in her favored form. You gain Resistance to psychic and poison damage while in your spider form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s255450db49b79d2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Form of the Beast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bestial spark manifests in the form of natural weapons.</p><p>Choose one of the following options: bite, claws, horns, hooves, pincers, or tail. You permanently gain the selected option as a natural weapon. It deals 1d8 damage on a hit. You can choose whether it deals bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage when you select it. It counts as a simple weapon for you and you use your Strength modifier for attack and damage rolls with it.</p><p>You can choose how the natural weapon looks exactly. For example, the bite option might give you long fangs, mandibles, or even a beak.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2560c61d63da866","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428321,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Abeyance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell using a spell slot of 4th level or lower, you can condense the spell's magic into a mote. The spell is frozen in time at the moment of casting and held within a gray bead for 1 hour. This bead is a Tiny object with AC 15 and 1 hit point, and it is Immune to poison and psychic damage. When the duration ends, or if the bead is destroyed, it vanishes in a flash of light, and the spell is lost.</p><p>A creature holding the bead can use its action to release the spell within, whereupon the bead disappears. The spell uses your spell attack bonus and save DC, and the spell treats the creature who released it as the caster for all other purposes.</p><p>Once you create a bead with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s257b69b0002feb8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tentacle of the Deeps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically summon a spectral tentacle that strikes at your foes. As a Bonus Action, you create a 10-foot-long tentacle at a point you can see within 60 feet of you. The tentacle lasts for 1 minute or until you use this feature to create another tentacle.</p><p>When you create the tentacle, you can make a melee spell attack against one creature within 10 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 + your Charisma modifier cold damage, and its Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. When you reach 10th level in this class, the damage increases to 2d8 + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can move the tentacle up to 30 feet and repeat the attack.</p><p>You can summon the tentacle a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s25e10843e042fe7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 16)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2673ce2b0039737","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428450,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Defiance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you drop to 0 Hit Points and don't die outright, you can change your Hit Points to a number equal to double your fighter level. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind (no action required) and add its healing to the total.</p><p>You can't use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s267915c541ae2e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can imbue yourself with a primal power called Rage, a force that grants you extraordinary might and resilience. You can enter it as a Bonus Action if you aren't wearing Heavy armor.</p><p>You can enter your Rage the number of times shown for your Barbarian level in the Rages column of the Barbarian Features table. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>While active, your Rage follows the rules below.</p><p><strong>Damage Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage.</p><p><strong>Rage Damage.</strong> When you make an attack using Strength—with either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike—and deal damage to the target, you gain a bonus to the damage that increases as you gain levels as a Barbarian, as shown in the Rage Damage column of the Barbarian Features table.</p><p><strong>Strength Advantage.</strong> You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</p><p><strong>No Concentration or Spells.</strong> You can't maintain Concentration, and you can't cast spells.</p><p><strong>Duration.</strong> The Rage lasts until the end of your next turn, and it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition. If your Rage is still active on your next turn, you can extend the Rage for another round by doing one of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Duration.</strong> Make an Attack Roll against an enemy.</li><li>Force an enemy to make a Saving Throw.</li><li>Take a Bonus Action to extend your Rage.</li></ul><p>Each time the Rage is extended, it lasts until the end of your next turn. You can maintain a Rage for up to 10 minutes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":10,"units":"minute"},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":"self"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"self"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.barbarian.rages","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-human.webp","_id":"s268aea0605b7eb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428320,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Souleater","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to siphon the life energy from your fallen prey. You gain the Blood Curse of the Soul Eater for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s26beb3f3e2e2a2c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Violent Attraction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a gravity-based spell (e.g. Magnify Gravity) that deals force damage, you add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature you can see within 60 feet of you takes damage from a fall, you can use your Reaction to deal additional force damage equal to a number of D10s x your Proficiency to the creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s26d623db2b55c0a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deft Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Thanks to your travels, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Expertise.</strong> Choose one of your skill proficiencies with which you lack Expertise. You gain Expertise in that skill.</li><li><strong>Languages.</strong> You know two languages of your choice.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/settlement/bridge-stone.webp","_id":"s272e435a5e9f7b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of hemocraft suffuses your body to permanently reinforce your resilience. Your Speed increases by 5 feet, and you have a bonus to Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution Saving Throws equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-body-explode-disintegrate.webp","_id":"s2798305fdbc3909","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ibisian Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Message cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the Bless spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can also cast the Augury spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. INT, WIS, or CHA is your spellcasting ability for these spells (your choice). You can also cast them using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s27fb78067ddefa4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Searing Sunburst","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to create an orb of light that erupts into a devastating explosion. As an Action, you magically create an orb and hurl it at a point you choose within 150 feet, where it erupts into a sphere of radiant light for a brief but deadly instant.</p><p>Each creature in that 20-foot-radius sphere must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take 2d6 radiant damage. A creature doesn't need to make the save if the creature is behind total cover that is opaque.</p><p>You can increase the sphere's damage by spending ki points. Each point you spend, to a maximum of 3, increases the damage by 2d6.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s284289427417c0a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Absorb Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you successfully end or disrupt a spell with Dispel Magic or Counterspell, you regain Sorcery Points equal to half the level of the spell slot you used to cast them (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s28b0330b1abdf62","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Spellbook","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Using specially prepared inks and ancient incantations passed down by your wizardly order, you have awakened an arcane sentience within your spellbook.</p><p>While you are holding the book, it grants you the following benefits:</p><ul><li>While the book is on your person, you have Advantage on all Intelligence (Arcana) checks, as the spellbook helps you remember magical lore.</li><li>When you cast a wizard spell as a ritual, you can use the spell's normal casting time, rather than adding 10 minutes to it. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>If necessary, you can replace the book over the course of a Short Rest by using your Wizardly Quill to write arcane sigils in a blank book or a magic spellbook to which you're attuned. At the end of the rest, your spellbook's consciousness is summoned into the new book, which the consciousness transforms into your spellbook, along with all its spells. If the previous book still existed somewhere, all the spells vanish from its pages.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s291d7fe845ccacd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428380,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Frenzy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of the attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s293760913417584","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inky Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call upon your patron to escape from your foes. As a Reaction when you take damage, you can cast Darkness centered on a point within 5 ft. of you. The spell lasts until the end of your next turn, does not require concentration, and has no effect on your vision.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you cannot use it until you complete a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s29502f0bd4b1139","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wizardly Quill","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically create a Tiny quill in your free hand. The magic quill has the following properties:</p><ul><li>The quill doesn't require ink. When you write with it, it produces ink in a color of your choice on the writing surface.</li><li>The time you must spend to copy a spell into your spellbook equals 2 minutes per spell level if you use the quill for the transcription.</li><li>You can erase anything you write with the quill if you wave the feather over the text as a Bonus Action, provided the text is within 5 feet of you.</li></ul><p>This quill disappears if you create another one or if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s296620085a8b29d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428379,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nimble Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage against DEX Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp","_id":"s29727dee0808f83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Faithful Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The nature spirits you commune with protect you when you are the most defenseless. If you are reduced to 0 hit points or are Incapacitated against your will, you can immediately gain the benefits of Conjure Animals as if it were cast using a 9th-level spell slot. It summons four beasts of your choice that are challenge rating 2 or lower. The conjured beasts appear within 20 feet of you. If they receive no commands from you, they protect you from harm and attack your foes. The spell lasts for 1 hour, requiring no Concentration, or until you dismiss it (no action required).</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s298296ea6d93b3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"s29ed1bd04285cbe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Protector's Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage of the weapon's type to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn. The creature is then marked by you until the end of your next turn. While it is within 5 feet of you, the marked creature has Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you and counts as your Favored Enemy. This mark ends early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>The extra damage increases to 2d6 when you reach 11th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2a3e0df96852b24","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428359,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hoarfrost Herald","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ice grants you special abilities:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to cold damage.</li><li>You ignore 3 and movement Speed reductions caused by cold, ice, and snow, whether mundane or magical.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2a996d49d368be3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark One's Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Warlock level (minimum of 1 Temporary Hit Point). You also gain this benefit if someone else reduces an enemy within 10 feet of you to 0 Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/blood-cells-disease-green.webp","_id":"s2ab0f7da7654322","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428369,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You extend your ki into your kensei weapons, granting you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Magic Kensei Weapons.</strong> Your attacks with your kensei weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p><strong>Deft Riposte.</strong> When you spend Ki on your Deflect Attack feature, you can attack with a monk weapon you are currently wielding instead of forcing the target to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, provided the target is within your reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2afa6d66905acb2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Terrify (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it has the Frightened condition for 1 minute. The Frightened target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</li><li><strong>Torment (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or it becomes crippled with pain until the start of your next turn. For the duration, its Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on Ability Checks, Attack Rolls, and Constitution Saving Throws to maintain concentration.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b04252b3965482","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Magic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Wild Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Chaos Bolt, Color Spray, Dragon's Breath, Nathair's Mischief</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Blink, Hypnotic Pattern</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Confusion, Spell Turning</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Spell Mantle, Temporal Shunt</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b80e48e242f26f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swift Memorize","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically extract knowledge from your spellbook and replace one of the level 1+ Wizard spells you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell from the book.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-eye-brown.webp","_id":"s2b8735c0b43259f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hybrid Transformation Features","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are transformed, you gain the following benefits and drawbacks:</p><p><strong>Feral Might.</strong> You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws, and you have a +2 bonus to melee damage rolls. This bonus increases to +3 at 9th level and to +4 at 16th level.</p><p><strong>Resilient Hide.</strong> While you are not wearing heavy armor, you have a +1 bonus to AC. This bonus increases to +2 at 11th level.</p><p><strong>Predatory Strikes.</strong> You can apply your Crimson Rite feature to your Unarmed Strikes, which you treat as one weapon. You can use Dexterity instead of Strength for the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes, which deal 1d8 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage (your choice). This damage increases to 1d10 at 11th level and 1d12 at 17th level.</p><p>Additionally, when you use the Attack action to make an Unarmed Strike, you can make one additional Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b8908139013d12","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Royal Envoy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Persuasion skill. If you are already proficient in it, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Insight, Intimidation, or Performance.</p><p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses Persuasion. You receive this benefit regardless of the skill Proficiency you gain from this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b943feef83c2c7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inured to Undeath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to necrotic damage, and your hit point maximum can't be reduced. You have spent so much time dealing with undead and the forces that animate them that you have become inured to some of their worst effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2bba67f59ee60ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Concerted Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose up to two allies for your Concerted Attack. Alternatively, you can choose to make two weapon attacks instead of one with your attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/crosshair-triple-strike-orange.webp","_id":"s2bc9c602affe145","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Gathered Swarm grows mightier in the following ways:</p><ul><li>The damage of Gathered Swarm increases to 2d6.</li><li>If a creature fails its Saving Throw against being moved by Gathered Swarm, you can also cause the swarm to knock the creature Prone.</li><li>When you are moved by Gathered Swarm, it gives you half cover until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2be9e3fdb152465","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Voice of Authority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke the power of law to drive an ally to attack. If you cast a spell with a spell slot of 1st level or higher and target an ally with the spell, that ally can use their Reaction immediately after the spell to make one weapon attack against a creature of your choice that you can see.</p><p>If the spell targets more than one ally, you choose the ally who can make the attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2bf1fe547ac9502","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tough as Nails","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in Constitution Saving Throws and your hit point maximum increases by 1 for every level in this class and increases by 1 again when you gain a level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2bf29c7f02fff3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Axiom","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mutagenic hemocraft lets your Brand of Castigation reveal a foe's true nature. Any illusion or invisibility in effect on a creature when you brand it ends, and the creature can't benefit from invisibility or illusion effects while branded by you. If a creature branded by you is in an alternative form (by way of the Polymorph spell, the Change Shape action or Shapechanger trait, the Wild Shape feature, and similar effects), it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or revert to its true form and be Stunned until the end of your next turn. Whenever a branded creature attempts to alter its form, it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or have the attempt fail, and it is Stunned until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2c12f78511badda","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clairvoyant Combatant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you form a telepathic bond with a creature using your Awakened Mind, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you, and you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against that creature for the duration of the bond.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2c747bb84071d03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"War Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can cast a cantrip in place of one of your weapon attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2cc1bc4d01aafdf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elf Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the elvish spear, greatspear, shortbow, and longbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/bows/shortbow-recurve-yellow.webp","_id":"s2cf3036a878b90b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Water Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your being is altered by the power of the sea. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You no longer need to eat, drink, or sleep.</li><li>A critical hit against you becomes a normal hit.</li><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2d7df78d6c05aa1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Insight, Persuasion, or Stealth.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"s2daf58deba2e147","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428346,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Magic Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spellcasting can unleash surges of untamed magic. Immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, the DM can have you roll a d20. If you roll a 1, roll on the Wild Magic Surge table to create a random magical effect. A Wild Magic Surge can happen once per turn.</p><p>If a Wild Magic effect is a spell, it's too wild to be affected by Metamagic. If it normally requires Concentration, it doesn't require Concentration in this case; the spell lasts for its full duration.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>The Bigger, Badder Wild Magic Surge Table</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d100</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01</td><td>Roll on this table at the start of each of your turns for the next minute. If you roll a 1 on your d100 again, reroll the d100 until you get a different result.</td></tr><tr><td>02</td><td>Roll a d100. Your weight changes by a number of lbs equal to the roll. If the roll is odd, you grow lighter. If the roll is even, you grow heavier. Your physical appearance doesn't change.</td></tr><tr><td>03</td><td>You gain truesight with a range of 30 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>04</td><td>You exude a terrible odor within a radius of 15 feet for 1d4 days. Any creature that starts its turn in that radius or enters it for the first time on a turn has to make a Constitution Saving Throw, on a failure it has to spend its action retching and hacking.</td></tr><tr><td>05</td><td>An elemental chosen and controlled by the DM appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you, then disappears 1 minute later.</td></tr><tr><td>06</td><td>You cast Daylight on yourself. For the duration, the area of the spell travels with you.</td></tr><tr><td>07</td><td>You cast Fireball at the highest spell level available to you (min. 3rd level), centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>08</td><td>Your body becomes ooze-like for 1d4 hours. You gain the amorphous monster trait, allowing you to move through spaces as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing.</td></tr><tr><td>09</td><td>Roll a d10. Your height changes by a number of inches equal to the roll. If the roll is odd, you shrink. If the roll is even, you grow. If you are male, half the result of the d10 is also added to or subtracted from your genital size as inches, using the same rules.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>For the next 1d10 days, you can cast Speak with Dead at will without somatic or material components.</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>You cast Confusion at the highest spell level available to you (min. 4th level), centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>You regain your lowest-level used spell slot.</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>For the next minute, you regain an amount of hitpoints equal to your sorcery point maximum at the beginning of each of your turns.</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>Your biological gender is reversed. A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>You grow a long beard made of feathers that remains until you sneeze. When you speak more than one word at a time or cast a spell with a verbal component, roll a d6. On a 1, you sneeze and immediately roll again on this table. If you were casting a spell at the time, the casting fails, but you do not expend the spell slot.</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against spells and other magical effects for 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>You cast Grease centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>For the next minute, the first metamagic you use on a turn does not cost sorcery points.</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Creatures have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against the next spell you cast in the next minute that involves a Saving Throw.</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>You cast Insect Plague at the highest available spell level to you (min. 5th level), centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>An eye appears on your forehead for the next minute. During that time, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. Additionally, when a creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an Ability Check, Attack Roll, or Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to cause that roll to have either Advantage or Disadvantage.</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>You cast Otto's Irresistible Dance on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>For the next minute, all your spells with a casting time of 1 action have a casting time of 1 Bonus Action.</td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>You and every creature within 60 feet of you have to make a CHA Saving Throw or suffer the effects of the Slow spell.</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>You teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see.</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>You and one creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you are magically compelled into a dance-off. Both you and your target have to make a Charisma (Performance) check. A creature that is Immune to the Charmed condition can ignore this effect, but automatically loses the contest if it chooses not to dance and its opponent does. The winner of the contest gains a bardic inspiration (d12) as per the class feature. The loser has Disadvantage on the next Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw they make before the end of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>You cast Blink on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>You cast Faerie Fire, centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>Maximize the damage of the next damaging spell you cast within the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>For 1d4 days, your hands trail faint rainbows when you move them.</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>Roll a d10. Your age changes by a number of years equal to the roll. If the roll is odd, you get younger (minimum 1 year old). If the roll is even, you get older. If you are made younger, you have Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws, but Disadvantage on Wisdom Saving Throws and vice versa if you are made older instead. A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>You conjure a kitchen utensil or piece of cutlery such as a spoon or rolling pin in a space you can see within 5 ft of you and cast Animate Objects on it.</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>A beast chosen and controlled by the DM appears in unoccupied spaces within 60 feet of you. It is hostile to every creature other than you and vanishes after 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>You cast Evard's Black Tentacles, centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>Roll a number of d10 equal to your Proficiency. You regain hitpoints equal to the total.</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>For the next 1d10 days, you are under the effects of the Speak with Animals and Speak with Plants spells.</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>For the next minute, you can exchange places with a creature of your choice you can see within 20 feet as a Bonus Action on each of your turns.</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>For every time you cast a cantrip within the next minute, you find a gold coin behind one of your ears.</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>You cast Levitate on yourself. You are treated as a willing creature for the purpose of this spell. At the start of each of your turns, you float 20 feet higher into the air.</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>You cast Spider Climb on yourself, but the duration is 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>41</td><td>A djinn chosen and controlled by the DM appears within 5 feet of you. Roll a d20. On a roll of 1-10, the djinn is hostile to you. On a roll of 11-20, the djinn grants you a limited wish. You can request the effect of one spell that is 6th level or lower and has a casting time of 1 action. The spell can be from any class's spell list. If the djinn is hostile, it vanishes after 1 minute, otherwise it disappears after granting your wish or after 1 hour, whichever is earlier.</td></tr><tr><td>42</td><td>The first time you kill a creature with damage from a spell within the next minute, it explodes into fireworks and confetti, raining down {dice 1d4} sylvan candy and 5d100 gold pieces in a radius of 10 feet. For each size category above medium, increase the amount by 1d4 sylvan candy and 5d100 gold pieces.</td></tr><tr><td>43</td><td>You can't speak for the next minute. Whenever you try, you instead belch so loudly it can be heard within 300 feet and pink bubbles float out of your mouth.</td></tr><tr><td>44</td><td>You become semi-incorporeal for the next 1d4 hours. You can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. You take 5 (1d10) force damage if you end your turn inside an object. Additionally, you are Immune to the Grappled and Restrained conditions for the duration.</td></tr><tr><td>45</td><td>A spectral shield hovers near you for the next minute, granting you a +5 bonus to AC and Immunity to Magic Missile. This effect does not stack with the Shield spell.</td></tr><tr><td>46</td><td>You grow additional physical features belonging to an animal of the DM's choice (such as ears, horns, or a tail). A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>47</td><td>You are Immune to being intoxicated by alcohol for the next 5d6 days.</td></tr><tr><td>48</td><td>You cast Thunder Step at the highest spell level available to you (min. 3rd level).</td></tr><tr><td>49</td><td>Your hair falls out but grows back with a different color within 24 hours. After another 24 hours, it falls out again and the process repeats, each time with another color. A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>50</td><td>A fey chosen and controlled by the DM appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you, then disappears 1 minute later. At the start of each of its turns, you roll a d6. On a 1 to 3, the creature is hostile to you and your companions this turn. On a 4 to 6, it is friendly to you.</td></tr><tr><td>51</td><td>For the next minute, any flammable object you touch that isn't being worn or carried by another creature bursts into flame.</td></tr><tr><td>52</td><td>The first time within the next minute you cast a spell of 1st level or higher, you lose a number of hit dice equal to the spell's level.</td></tr><tr><td>53</td><td>You regain your highest-level expended spell slot.</td></tr><tr><td>54</td><td>You and all creatures within 60 feet of you have to make a Constitution Saving Throw or become drunk for 1d4 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>55</td><td>For the next minute, you must shout when you speak.</td></tr><tr><td>56</td><td>A halo of glowing letters appears around your head. For the next hour, you automatically know when someone is lying.</td></tr><tr><td>57</td><td>You cast Fog Cloud at the highest spell level available to you (min. 1st level), centered on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>58</td><td>Your tongue turns a silvery color. For the next 24 hours, you speak and understand all languages.</td></tr><tr><td>59</td><td>Roll a number of d10 equal to your Proficiency. Up to three creatures you choose within 30 feet of you take lightning damage equal to the total.</td></tr><tr><td>60</td><td>Your eyes glow with scintillating colors for 24 hours and are clearly visible up to 300 feet away. You can see normally in darkness and dim light, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet. If you have darkvision, the range of this effect increases by 60 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>61</td><td>You are Frightened by the nearest creature you can see until the end of your next turn. While Frightened in this manner, your Speed is doubled and you have to immediately spend all your movement to move away from the creature in a straight line until you are at least 60 feet away from it or no longer have line of sight of it.</td></tr><tr><td>62</td><td>A celestial chosen and controlled by the DM appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you, then disappears 1 minute later. It seeks out the creature it can see that is closest to its own alignment and protects it for the duration. If multiple creatures are equally close to its alignment, it chooses the one closest to it.</td></tr><tr><td>63</td><td>Each creature within 30 feet of you becomes Invisible for the next minute. The invisibility ends on a creature when it attacks or casts a spell.</td></tr><tr><td>64</td><td>You cast Blindness/Deafness on yourself, choosing the blind option.</td></tr><tr><td>65</td><td>You gain Resistance to all damage for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>66</td><td>You and every creature within 60 feet of you gains the effect of the Haste spell.</td></tr><tr><td>67</td><td>A random creature within 60 feet of you becomes drunk for 1d4 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>68</td><td>Your size decreases by one size category for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>69</td><td>For the next 24 hours, you replace every adjective and adverb with a form of \"nice\" when you speak. Every time you fail to do so, you take psychic damage equal to your Proficiency. If the time passes and you have not failed to do so (though must have done so successfully at least 7 times), you gain an inspiration.</td></tr><tr><td>70</td><td>You flare in an intense bright light in a 300-foot radius for a brief moment. Any creature in that radius is Blinded until the end of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>71</td><td>You cast Polymorph on yourself. If you fail the Saving Throw, you turn into a sheep for the spell's duration.</td></tr><tr><td>72</td><td>You speak with a lisp for the next 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>73</td><td>You cast the Mislead spell on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>74</td><td>A loud voice narrates your actions and thoughts for the next 24 hours. It can be heard up to 100 feet away.</td></tr><tr><td>75</td><td>You can take one additional action immediately.</td></tr><tr><td>76</td><td>You cast Stoneskin on yourself at the highest spell level available to you (min. 4th level). For the duration, your Speed becomes 10 ft.</td></tr><tr><td>77</td><td>Roll a number of {dice d10} equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down). Each creature within 30 feet of you takes necrotic damage equal to the total. You regain hit points equal to the sum of the necrotic damage dealt.</td></tr><tr><td>78</td><td>You are Immune to all conditions for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>79</td><td>You cast Mirror Image on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>80</td><td>For the next minute, your hands become incredibly slippery. You cannot hold objects. If you attempt to, they slip out of your hands and drop within 5 ft of you. If you attempt to grapple a creature, you automatically fail.</td></tr><tr><td>81</td><td>You cast Fly on a random creature within 60 feet of you.</td></tr><tr><td>82</td><td>Until the start of your next turn, every creature within 30 feet of you also has to roll on this table when they cast a spell of 1st level or higher.</td></tr><tr><td>83</td><td>You become Invisible for the next minute. During that time, other creatures can't hear you. The invisibility ends if you attack or cast a spell.</td></tr><tr><td>84</td><td>For the next 1d4 days, you can change the color of any open fire within 10 feet of you to one of your choosing. The chosen color remains until the fire is extinguished, you choose a different color, or this effect on you ends.</td></tr><tr><td>85</td><td>If you die within the next minute, you immediately come back to life as if by the Reincarnate spell.</td></tr><tr><td>86</td><td>You break your attunement with 1d3 of the magic items to which you are attuned.</td></tr><tr><td>87</td><td>Your size increases by one size category for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>88</td><td>You cast Improved Haste on a random creature within 60 feet of you.</td></tr><tr><td>89</td><td>You and all creatures within 30 feet of you gain vulnerability to all damage for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>90</td><td>You cast Freedom of Movement on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>91</td><td>Your skin turns a vibrant shade of blue and you become extremely attractive to fey creatures, who will start seeking you out from miles around. A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>92</td><td>You cast Warding Wind.</td></tr><tr><td>93</td><td>You turn into a potted plant until the start of your next turn. While a plant, you are Incapacitated and have vulnerability to all damage. If you drop to 0 hit points, you die and your form reverts.</td></tr><tr><td>94</td><td>Your spellcasting focus turns into a banana for 1 hour. It retains all its previous properties. As an Action, you can throw it at a creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The attack automatically hits and deals force damage equal to your sorcerer level + your Charisma modifier. It then immediately returns to your hands. No one expects the banana.</td></tr><tr><td>95</td><td>You become covered in thick coat of long fur that falls even over your eyes and regrows instantly when it is cut or otherwise damaged. You gain Resistance to cold damage and have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks. A Remove Curse spell can end this effect.</td></tr><tr><td>96</td><td>1d4 random pastries from within a 1 mile radius are teleported into your hands. If your hands are occupied, they are dumped on your head instead.</td></tr><tr><td>97</td><td>For the next 24 hours, you must rhyme when you speak. Every time you fail to do so, you take psychic damage equal to your Proficiency. If the time passes and you have not failed to rhyme (though must have done so successfully at least 7 times), you gain an inspiration.</td></tr><tr><td>98</td><td>You cast Flesh  to Stone on yourself. If you become Petrified as a result of this casting of the spell, you turn back to normal after 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>99</td><td>You regain all expended sorcery points.</td></tr><tr><td>100</td><td>A dragon chosen and controlled by the DM appears within 5 feet of you. It is hostile to you. Good luck.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2e030158d397b3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action: Umbral Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use your Cunning Action to shape the shadows around you into a 30-feet radius sphere around your position. The area inside the sphere counts as dim light and persists for 10 minutes. It disappears early if you become Incapacitated or if its area overlaps with light created by a spell of 3rd level or higher.</p><p>You can only have one Umbral Shroud active at a time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2e91b817a91ce5d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Epitome of Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a Sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage, you add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of the spell. If the level of the spell is higher than your Charisma modifier, you add it to the damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hand-green.webp","_id":"s2ea837c309c7880","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Divine Intervention","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are able to call on even more powerful divine intervention. When you use your Divine Intervention feature, you can select cleric spells up to 8th level. Additionally, you can select Wish when you select a spell. If you do so, you can't use Divine Intervention again until you finish 2d4 Long Rests. When you cast Wish with this feature, you are Immune to the stress caused by using Wish to do something other than casting a spell, other than the chance to lose the ability to cast the spell again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue.webp","_id":"s2ec644f0fa49238","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warding Maneuver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to fend off strikes directed at you, your mount, or other creatures nearby. If you or a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack, you can roll 1d8 as a Reaction if you're wielding a melee weapon or a shield. Roll the die, and add the number rolled to the target's AC against that attack. If the attack still hits, the target has Resistance against the attack's damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2f5ccc34d0079ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Intrigue","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with the disguise kit, the forgery kit. Additionally, you can use your Intelligence for Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Persuasion checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2f7c92c6d063653","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Runes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Carver feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2fd94d12cfb043a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two of your elemental disciplines and reduce their ki cost by 1 (minimum of 1). You change your choices whenever you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2fe7c1fcdfc7c03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Edge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of sword magic allows you to enhance your melee attacks. When you make a melee attack, the target takes extra force damage equal to half your sorcerer level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ff93cb331a432b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beacon of Leadership","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All allied creatures within 30 feet of you gain the benefits of your Favored Enemy and Greater Favored Enemy features. This feature has no effect while you are Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s301d213f5d06f96","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you gain a level of Exhaustion, you can use a Bonus Action to remove it. You can't use this ability again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage.webp","_id":"s30952ed492124e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with armorsmith's tools or weaponsmith's tools, and you learn to speak, read, and write Giant.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s30997ae6743b511","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428344,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eternal Spellguard","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can empower your Aura of Protection, granting the benefits below for 1 minute or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can restore your use of this ability by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Improved Spell-Breaking Blade.</strong> You add your Charisma modifier to the Ability Check of Counterspell and Dispel Magic when using Spell-Breaking Blade.</li><li><strong>Protection from Magic.</strong> You and your allies in the aura have Advantage on Saving Throws against spells.</li><li><strong>Spell Ward.</strong> Spell attack rolls against you and your allies in the aura have Disadvantage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s30ae9a6cec1fc92","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Performance skill if you don't already have it. Your martial arts technique mixes combat training with the precision of a dancer and the antics of a jester. You also gain Proficiency with brewer's supplies if you don't already have it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s30aef1b54de2f00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ki-Empowered Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Unarmed Strikes count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"s31009589f6f6043","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Horizon Walker Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Horizon Walker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Horizon Walker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Protection from Evil and Good</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Haste</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Teleportation Circle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s311e5cf2bcb2fd4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Body of the Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you have both your astral arms and visage summoned, you can cause the body of your astral self to appear (no action required). This spectral body covers your physical form like a suit of armor, connecting with the arms and visage. You determine its appearance.</p><p>While the spectral body is present, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Improved Deflect Attack.</strong> The damage dealt by your Deflect Attack increases to three rolls of your Martial Arts die and you can change the damage type to force damage.</p><p><strong>Empowered Arms.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a target with the Arms of the Astral Self, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s31723829d09645a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Quivering Palm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to set up lethal vibrations in someone's body. When you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike, you can expend 4 Ki Points to start these imperceptible vibrations, which last for a number of days equal to your Monk level. The vibrations are harmless unless you take an Action to end them. Alternatively, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of the attacks to end the vibrations. To end them, you and the target must be on the same plane of existence. When you end them, the target must make a Constitution Saving Throw, taking 10d12 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>You can have only one creature under the effect of this feature at a time. You can end the vibrations harmlessly (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["10d12","force"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-black-pink.webp","_id":"s31d641ce3d6cc4b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visions of the Past","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call up visions of the past that relate to an object you hold or your immediate surroundings. You spend at least 1 minute in meditation and prayer, then receive dreamlike, shadowy glimpses of recent events. You can meditate in this way for a number of minutes equal to your Wisdom score and must maintain Concentration during that time, as if you were casting a spell.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Object Reading.</strong> Holding an object as you meditate, you can see visions of the object's previous owner. After meditating for 1 minute, you learn how the owner acquired and lost the object, as well as the most recent significant event involving the object and that owner. If the object was owned by another creature in the recent past (within a number of days equal to your Wisdom score), you can spend 1 additional minute for each owner to learn the same information about that creature.</p><p><strong>Area Reading.</strong> As you meditate, you see visions of recent events in your immediate vicinity (a room, street, tunnel, clearing, or the like, up to a 50-foot cube), going back a number of days equal to your Wisdom score. For each minute you meditate, you learn about one significant event, beginning with the most recent. Significant events typically involve powerful emotions, such as battles and betrayals, marriages and murders, births and funerals. However, they might also include more mundane events that are nevertheless important in your current situation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s31de773242a6aec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Banishment Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Banishment, you can treat it as one spell level higher than the Spell Slot you expended for the purpose of determining its effects and it does not count against your Concentration limit, though the initial instance of the spell ends if you cast it again.</p><p>If you fail a Concentration Saving Throw and you are currently Concentration on more than one spell, you lose Concentration on both spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s31e2d66adb930a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Magic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at 1st level, you learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Shadow Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Arms of Hadar, Hex, Blindness/Deafness, Ray of Enfeeblement</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Speak with Dead, Summon Shadowspawn</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Shadow of Moil</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Enervation, Negative Energy Flood</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s31eed73bd41a882","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428367,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all INT, WIS, and CHA Saving Throws against magic and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/deer-antlers-glowing-blue.webp","_id":"s31fba6d70d26d09","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frozen Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you magically transform into a creature of living ice. In this form, you have Resistance to piercing, bludgeoning, and slashing damage as well as Immunity to cold damage and poison.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature hits you with a melee attack from within 10 ft or touches you while you are under the effect of your Aegis of Rime feature, it is immediately affected by your Clinging Frost feature. If it was already affected, it instead immediately makes a Constitution Saving Throw as if at the end of its turn, suffering the usual effect on a failure. Succeeding on this Saving Throw does not count towards the three successes needed to clear the effect. </p><p>Finally, creatures affected by your Clinging Frost suffer a -2 penalty to Constitution Saving Throws against your spells that deal cold damage.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest or you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s323123c770d40b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict fire damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3257374c18fa03e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Ready","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your combat training and your experiments with magic have paid off in two ways:</p><ul><li>You gain Proficiency with martial weapons.</li><li>When you attack with a magic weapon, you can use your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity modifier, for the attack and damage rolls.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/sword-engraved-glow-purple.webp","_id":"s3275e70cae2aefc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fearless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"s32a92a796189fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant's Havoc","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your rages pull strength from the primal might of giants, transforming you into a hulking force of destruction. While raging, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Crushing Hurl.</strong> When you make a ranged weapon attack with a thrown weapon or an improvised weapon, you double your rage damage bonus to the attack's damage.</li><li><strong>Giant Stature.</strong> Your reach increases by 5 feet, and if you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If there isn't enough room for you to become Large, your size doesn't change.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s32e24a72fc881a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you are in dim light or darkness, as a Bonus Action, you can magically teleport up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s32ea1653f49315f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Athletics and Nature skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"s333ade0d42766eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Holy Nimbus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can imbue your Aura of Protection with holy power, granting the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Holy Ward.</strong> You and allies in the aura have Advantage on any Saving Throw they are forced to make by a Fiend or an Undead.</li><li><strong>Radiant Damage.</strong> Whenever an enemy starts its turn in the aura, that creature takes Radiant damage equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. This damage is doubled against Fiends and Undead.</li><li><strong>Sunlight.</strong> The aura is filled with Bright Light that is sunlight.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue-purple.webp","_id":"s333fbb2fa111a8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roving","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you aren't wearing Heavy armor. You also have a Climb Speed and a Swim Speed equal to your Speed.</p><p>Additionally, you can use your Dexterity modifier in place of your Strength modifier when you make an Ability Check to swim or climb.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s337ee1b730fc242","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Your Psionic Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every member of the Psionics tradition has a story about how their psionic focus came into their life. Consider how you found yours and what form it takes.</p><p>The event that brought your psionic focus to you probably holds personal significance. Did your master give it to you upon the completion of your apprenticeship? Was it awarded to you when you graduated from your academy of wizardry? Did it call to you in a jeweler's shop? Was it associated with the moment when your psionic powers first manifested? One morning, did you wake up with it humming under your pillow?</p><p>The form your psionic focus takes is also yours to define, likely being a reflection of how your magic came into being, a symbol of your own psyche, or an item you use to focus your thoughts. It is a handheld object that has special meaning to you, but that can't be a weapon or magic item. Perhaps it's a childhood memento, the skull of an alien creature, a crystal that makes you feel a certain way, a coin that only lands on its edge, a firescarred planchette, or any other enigmatic personal relic.</p><p>However the object arrived and whatever form it takes, your psionic focus is now yours, and you decide how to handle it. Will you mount it on a wand or staff? Would you prefer to wear it on a necklace or circlet? Have you embedded it into the cover of your spellbook? Wherever you put it, you can now channel your magic through it, and it is a sign of your membership in the revered tradition of psionic wizardry.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3387e5c0d4c8c8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wind Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Immunity to lightning and thunder damage.</p><p>You also gain a magical Fly Speed of 60 feet. As an Action, you can choose a number of creatures within 30 feet of you equal to 3 + your Charisma modifier and grant them a Fly Speed of 60 feet for 1 hour. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or until you spend 5 Sorcery Points to use it again..</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s338e9b9bab71994","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oceanic Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manifest two water orbs instead of one when you use Wrath of the Sea and all features that affect one water orb, affect both.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s33937cb5298b08d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divine Energy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to harness divine energy to heal your allies or harm your foes. You have a pool of d6s equal to your wizard level. If you use a feature that uses these dice, the number of dice you expend can be no larger than half your wizard level (rounded down). You regain all expended dice when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Heal.</strong> As an Action, expend a number of d6s from your pool and roll them. Choose creatures within 30 feet of you that you can see. Each target is healed by an amount of equal to the total of the roll.</p><p><strong>Harm.</strong> As an Action, expend a number of d6s from your pool and roll them. Choose creatures within 30 feet of you that you can see. Each target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it takes an amount of damage of a type you choose when you gain this feature (cold, fire, lightning, necrotic, or radiant) equal to the total of the roll. On a success, it takes half as much damage. If the target is an undead or a fiend, it has Disadvantage on the Saving Throw, and the feature deals maximum damage to it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s33a8126e0fc6f45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raptor's Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill. Additionally, you perceive details of things you observe even at great distances and your range with ranged weapons and spell attacks increases by 5 feet times your Proficiency modifier. In the case of ranged weapons, this bonus applies only to your normal range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/eyes/lizard-single-slit-pink.webp","_id":"s33b630a20ef1d64","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soundless Steps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Pass without Trace spell once with this trait, requiring no material components, and you regain the ability to cast it this way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-spurred-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s33ce7e5b6bf60c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beautiful Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in one of animal handling, performance, and persuasion. Additionally, your pool for Lay on Hands increases by an amount equal to your paladin level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s33f0abd77affc9e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dedicated Crafter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with one tool of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/hammer-sledge-steel-grey.webp","_id":"s33f7d2c96a38e13","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Child of Night","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have darkvision out to a range of 90 feet. If you already have darkvision, you increase its range by 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s345ffb1ee2fcac7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Ambush","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you are hidden from a creature when you cast a spell on it, the creature has Disadvantage on any Saving Throw it makes against the spell this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s34aa1e6d37b989d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sylvan Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Words of the First World improve in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Sticky Misfortune.</strong> If the reroll does not turn success into failure or vice versa, the curse instead lasts 1 minute or until it changes the outcome of a roll when you activate it the next time.</li><li><strong>Gloaming Cloak.</strong> The creature affected by your Mantle of Midnight becomes Hidden instead of Invisible, ignoring all the usual restrictions for hiding in plain view.</li><li><strong>Sylvan Farstride.</strong> Tread the Unseen Path's teleport distance increases to 60 feet.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s34c53ba2290a561","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scourge of the Ancients","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to fully harness the titanic legacy of your companion. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a spell slot of any level to heighten your primeval companion's might, granting it one of the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Hulking Behemoth.</strong> The companion grows one size larger and gains temporary hit points equal to 10 times the level of the spell slot expended. If there isn't enough room for the companion to grow, it attains the maximum possible size in the space available.</li><li><strong>Mauler.</strong> On a hit, the companion's Strike deals additional damage equal to 1d8 plus the level of the spell slot expended.</li><li><strong>Titanic Stride.</strong> The companion's Speed increases by a number of feet equal to 5 times the level of the spell slot expended.</li></ul><p>For the duration, your primeval companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>These benefits last for 1 hour, until the companion vanishes, or until you expend a spell slot for this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s34d80ec0bfa52e6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can interfere with the flow of ki in an opponent's body. When you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack, you can spend 1 ki point to attempt a stunning strike. The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or be Stunned until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-blue.webp","_id":"s34e0b3d0f61ad60","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ride the Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you jump, you can use your Reaction to increase your jumping distance by half your Speed. When you take fall damage, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage by an amount equal to five times your character level. If you already have a feature that allows you to reduce fall damage as a Reaction, you gain the benefits of both features when you use your Reaction to reduce fall damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you jump or take fall damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/debuff-energy-hold-levitate-blue-yellow.webp","_id":"s34f5c045f6a12b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deep Freeze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Speed reduction from your Clinging Frost feature increases to 20 feet and subsequent failed Saving Throws against it have additional effects as per below:</p><ul><li><strong>One failed save:</strong> The affected creature has Disadvantage on its next Attack Roll.</li><li><strong>Two failed save:</strong> The affected creature's Speed is reduced to 0.</li><li><strong>Three failed save:</strong> The affected creature has vulnerability against the damage of the next spell you cast that deals cold damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s353bb14b4dc032e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack (2)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s35422960a346916","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Hex","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your alien patron grants you a powerful curse. You always have the Hex spell prepared. When you cast Hex and choose an ability, the target also has Disadvantage on Saving Throws of the chosen ability for the duration of the spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3562a24862bbfff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Disciple of the Elements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn magical disciplines that harness the power of the Four Elements. A discipline requires you to spend ki points each time you use it.</p><p>You know the Elemental Attunement discipline and two other elemental disciplines of your choice. You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice at 6th, 11th, and 17th level.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p><p>When you use an elemental discipline to cast a spell that scales with the level of the spell slot it is used with, you can spend additional ki points to treat the spell as cast at a higher level. You spend 1 ki point for each level above the original and the resulting level of the spell cannot be greater than your Proficiency bonus.</p><p>When you use an elemental discipline as an Action, you can also make one Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action.</p><p><strong>Casting Elemental Spells.</strong> Some elemental disciplines allow you to cast spells. See 10 of the Player's Handbook for the general rules of spellcasting. To cast one of these spells, you use its casting time and other rules, but you don't need to provide material components for it.</p><p>Once you reach 5th level in this class, you can spend additional ki points to increase the level of an elemental discipline spell that you cast, provided that the spell has an enhanced effect at a higher level, as Burning Hands does. The spell's level increases by 1 for each additional ki point you spend. For example, if you are a 5th-level monk and use Sweeping Cinder Strike to cast Burning Hands, you can spend 3 ki points to cast it as a 2nd-level spell (the discipline's base cost of 2 ki points plus 1).</p><p>The maximum number of ki points you can spend to cast a spell in this way (including its base ki point cost and any additional ki points you spend to increase its level) is determined by your monk level, as shown in the Spells and Ki Points table. You may spend up to 3 ki points; this increases to 4 ki points at 9th level, 5 at 13th level, and 6 at 17th level.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Spells and Ki Points</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Monk Levels</th><th scope=\"col\">Maximum Ki Points for a Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>5th-8th</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>9th-12th</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>13th-16th</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>17th-20th</td><td>6</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s359cc50d4e15626","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Necrotic Husk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to undeath and necrotic energy now saturates your body. You have Resistance to necrotic damage. If you are transformed using your Form of Dread, you instead become Immune to necrotic damage.</p><p>In addition, when you would be reduced to 0 hit points, you can use your Reaction to drop to 1 hit point instead and cause your body to erupt with deathly energy. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of you takes necrotic damage equal to 2d10 + your warlock level. Once you use this Reaction, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s35ed73ad4b80f40","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflecting Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Arcane Deflection, you can spend a spell slot to increase the amount of damage it reduces by 5 x the level of the expended spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3612a9f6500f99f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tools of the Trade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with heavy armor. You also gain Proficiency with armorsmith's tools. If you already have this tool Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/plate-steel-grey.webp","_id":"s370b76fe809b003","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wavewalker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Water Walk spell once with this trait, requiring no material components, and you regain the ability to cast it this way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast it using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/wave-water-teal.webp","_id":"s371b702a16931b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Divine power infuses you in battle. You gain one of the following options of your choice (if you get either option from a Cleric subclass in an older book, use only the option you choose for this feature).</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Strike.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll using a weapon, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice). At your DM's discretion, you can replace one of these options with a different damage type appropriate for your cleric subclass.</li><li><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Cleric cantrip.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/projectiles-blades-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s3776b6ddbda5236","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a canine aspect, granting you physical traits such as the piercing eyes, sharp nails, and elongated canines.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>Once per turn when you hit a creature that is no more than 1 size larger than you with your natural weapons, you can force the target to make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failure, the target is knocked Prone. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). If the target creature is already Prone, you grapple the creature instead if it fails the save.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, you count as 1 size larger for the purposes of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s37f2c1069313ecd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Life on the Move","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Survival skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-river-road-gray.webp","_id":"s383949382fc556d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Call to Arms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you are not incapacitated or Surprised at the start of combat, you can add your Leadership modifier to the initiative roll of all allies of your choice within 60 feet that can see or you and aren't incapacitated or Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/flags/banner-sword-blue.webp","_id":"s3878a2fac7f828b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Evocation Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Evocation school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Evocation school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/barrier-wall-explosion-orange.webp","_id":"s3883a2863a92c89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Patron","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have struck a bargain with an otherworldly being chosen from the list of available patrons. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p><p>Additionally, spells from the expanded spell list are now learned automatically and do not count against the number of warlock spells known.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/lights/candles-lit-red-evil.webp","_id":"s38be1c50c4a9c63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trance of Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to align your consciousness to the endless calculations of Mechanus. As a Bonus Action, you can enter this state for 1 minute. For the duration, Attack Rolls against you can't benefit from Advantage, and whenever you make an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can treat a roll of 9 or lower on the d20 as a 10.</p><p>Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s38d6221c940b1f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rider's Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Wyvern Companion gains a variety of benefits while it is bonded to you.</p><p>The companion obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own.</p><p>Your Wyvern Companion has abilities and game statistics determined in part by your level. Your companion uses your Proficiency bonus rather than its own. In addition to the areas where it normally uses its Proficiency bonus, a Wyvern Companion also adds its Proficiency bonus to its AC and to its damage rolls.</p><p>For each level you gain after 3rd, your Wyvern Companion gains an additional hit die and increases its hit points accordingly.</p><p>Whenever you gain the Ability Score Improvement class feature, your companion's abilities also improve. Your companion can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or it can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, your companion can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature unless its description specifies otherwise.</p><p>Whenever you use your Second Wind, your Wyvern Companion also regains hit points equal to 5 + your Fighter level.</p><p>Whenver you use Action Surge, your Wyvern Companion can also immediately make one bite attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s38ff44ff8c2dbd7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.</p><h5>Archery</h5><p>You gain a +2 bonus to Attack Rolls you make with ranged weapons.</p><h5>Close Quarters Shooter</h5><p>When making a ranged weapon attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. You have a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls on ranged weapon attacks.</p><h5>Defense</h5><p>While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Dueling</h5><p>When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon.</p><h5>Great Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.</p><h5>Mariner</h5><p>As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a Swim Speed and a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Protection</h5><p>When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. You must be wielding a shield.</p><h5>Two-Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.</p><h5>Superior Technique</h5><p>You learn one maneuver of your choice from among those available to the fighter archetype. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).</p><p>You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach level 10, the size of this die increases to a d8.</p><h5>Blind Fighting</h5><p>You have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</p><h5>Interception</h5><p>When a creature you can see hits a target, other than you, within 5 feet of you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by 1d10 + your Proficiency bonus (to a minimum of 0 damage). You must be wielding a shield or a simple or martial weapon to use this Reaction.</p><h5>Thrown Weapon Fighting</h5><p>You can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.</p><p>In addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll.</p><h5>Unarmed Fighting</h5><p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-daggers-orange.webp","_id":"s391c7e606b62ded","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ceaseless Pursuit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature within your Unnerving Aura moves away from you, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed towards it without provoking Attacks of Opportunity, then make an Attack of Opportunity against that creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s392058bef4b4aa1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Twilight Sanctuary","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to refresh your allies with soothing twilight.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol, and a sphere of twilight emanates from you. The sphere is centered on you, has a 30-foot radius, and is filled with dim light. The sphere moves with you, and it lasts for 1 minute or until you are Incapacitated or die. Whenever a creature (including you) ends its turn in the sphere, you can grant that creature one of these benefits:</p><ul><li>You grant it temporary hit points equal to 1d6 plus your cleric level.</li><li>You end one effect on it causing it to be Charmed or Frightened.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s393fe2026ad9031","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Artifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You develop a mystical connection to your magic items, which you can draw on for protection:</p><ul><li>You gain a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws per magic item you are currently attuned to.</li><li>If you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your Reaction to expend a use of Flash of Genius and change your hit points to 20 instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"20","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-beam-blue.webp","_id":"s39448dc50dc7661","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189465,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Army of One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to summon an ever-increasing number of creatures to your side. When you cast a conjuration or necromancy spell to summon a creature, you can choose to ignore the Concentration limit on that spell. But if you do so, you reduce the spell's duration to 1 minute.</p><p>If you lose Concentration, you lose it on all spells you're concentrating on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3945c847a8421cc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Blessed Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The option you chose for Blessed Strikes grows more powerful.</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Strike.</strong> The extra damage of your Divine Strike increases to 2d8.</li><li><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> When you cast a spell that deals damage, you can add your Wisdom modifier to one damage roll of that spell.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/projectile-beams-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s394fbd3e4bf2b29","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Form of the Phoenix","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You finally master the spark of fire that dances within you. When you activate your Mantle of Flame feature, you can choose to empower its effects:</p><ul><li>You have a Fly Speed of 40 feet and can hover.</li><li>You have Resistance to all damage.</li><li>If you use your Phoenix Spark, that feature deals an extra 20 fire damage to each creature.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s395644b2508dd50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dispelling Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to lace your shots with disruptive magic. Once per turn, when you hit with a ranged weapon attack, you can end any spells of 3rd level or lower on the target.</p><p>For each spell of 4th level or higher on the target, make an Ability Check using the ability score for your Arcane Shot save DC. The DC equals 10 + the caster's spellcasting ability modifier + the spell slot level of the target spell - 3. On a successful check, the spell ends.</p><p>You can use this features a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. You can also expend a use of your Arcane Shot to use this feature again (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3957b7e06234f45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Noble Scion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you gain the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover.</li><li><strong>Greater Aura of Elemental Shielding.</strong> Your Aura of Elemental Shielding now confers Immunity to the chosen element instead of Resistance.</li><li><strong>Minor Wish.</strong> As an Action, you can entreat your genie patron for the effect of one spell that is 5th level or lower and has a casting time of 1 action. The spell can be from any class's spell list, and you don't need to meet the requirements in that spell, including costly components; the spell simply takes effect as part of this Action. Once you have done so, you cannot use this feature again for this use of Noble Scion.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39778736b36bd45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mirror, Mirror","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell of up to 5th level that can only target yourself, you can choose your bonded familiar as a second target if it is within 60 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39effb054e4843f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Wings","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to manifest a pair of spectral wings from your back. While the wings are present, you have a Fly Speed of 30 feet. The wings last until you're Incapacitated, you die, or you dismiss them as a Bonus Action.</p><p>The affinity you chose for your Divine Magic feature determines the appearance of the spectral wings: eagle wings for good or law, bat wings for evil or chaos, and dragonfly wings for neutrality.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3a1c734ba4bc864","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Step through the Circle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you create a 10-feet radius circle of mushrooms at a point you can see within 30 feet. You can only have up to three of these circles at the same time. Whenever you create an additional one beyond that number, the oldest one disappears. A circle lasts for 1 year or until you trigger one of the following effects an Action:</p><p><strong>Travel Back.</strong> You and up to 8 other willing creatures of your choice within 10 feet are teleported to the circle's location.</p><p><strong>Travel Forth.</strong> You and up to 8 other willing creatures within the circle are teleported as per the effect of the Plane Shift spell.</p><p>Once you have triggered one of the above effects, you cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3a293f89a0f1c70","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Knight Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Ranger level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Ranger Knight Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Shield of Faith</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Find Steed</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Blinding Smite</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Guardian of Nature</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Circle of Power</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3a530820615583e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428359,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cryomancer Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Cryomancer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Ice Knife, Rime's Binding Ice, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm, Water Walk</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Conjure Elemental</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3a53c7e7d259387","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reckless Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can throw aside all concern for defense to attack with increased ferocity. When you make your first Attack Roll on your turn, you can decide to attack recklessly. Doing so gives you Advantage on Attack Rolls using Strength until the start of your next turn, but Attack Rolls against you have Advantage during that time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blade-tips-triple-bent-white.webp","_id":"s3a7eb1cd4584162","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heightened Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Flurry of Blows.</strong> You can expend 1 Ki Point to use Flurry of Blows and make three Unarmed Strikes with it instead of two.</li><li><strong>Patient Defense.</strong> When you expend a Ki Point to use Patient Defense, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die.</li><li><strong>Step of the Wind.</strong> When you expend a Ki Point to use Step of the Wind, you can choose a willing creature within 5 feet of yourself that is Large or smaller. You move the creature with you until the end of your turn. The creature's movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s3aa5701e436bb2f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Casting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You ignore all restrictions on casting or concentrating on spells caused by being shifted. Additionally, when you cast a spell that heals or gives the target temporary hit points, you increase the healing or temporary hit points by an amount equal to your Formshift Damage.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, this bonus doubles.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3aeaed15f4cba2f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Astral Refuge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step into an astral refuge. As an Action, you disappear from the world for a brief moment and enter the Astral Plane, taking Advantage of its timeless nature. While in your astral refuge, you can take two actions to cast spells that target only you. After using those two actions, you return to the space you occupied and your turn ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3b3485389413c5c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Victory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1) to the damage of your melee weapon attacks while your Bladesong is active.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3b766f446004355","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Restorative Reagents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:</p><ul><li>Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).</li><li>You can cast Lesser Restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you have alchemist's supplies on your person. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/bowl-herbs-green.webp","_id":"s3b991c3b6bcea59","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spiked Retribution","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are wearing spiked armor and a creature touches you (e.g. by grappling you or hitting you with a natural weapon attack) or hits you with a melee attack from within 5 ft, it takes piercing damage equal to your Proficiency bonus. If your armor has a permanent bonus to its armor class (e.g. the masterwork property), you add this bonus to the damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3be3259812e703f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You begin to take on characteristics of your patron's kind. You now have Resistance to a damage type determined by your patron's kind: bludgeoning (dao), thunder (djinni), fire (efreeti), or cold (marid).</p><p>In addition, as a Bonus Action, you can give yourself a Fly Speed of 30 feet that lasts for 10 minutes, during which you can hover. You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3c164f17001f964","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Vitality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can expend a use of your Formshift to immediately regain hit points equal to twice your Shifter level. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["2 * @classes.shifter.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/bear-roar-bite-brown-green.webp","_id":"s3c186bc530ade0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Formation Fighting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are not incapacitated, allies within 5 ft of you have half-cover against weapon attacks and you add your Leadership ability modifier to the damage roll of the first weapon attack they hit with on a turn. You can extend this benefit to allies that are farther than 5 ft away from you, as long as they are within 5 ft of an ally that already is under the effect of this feature and isn't incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3c2a417a00827d2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Elemental Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The option you chose for Elemental Fury grows more powerful:</p><p><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> When you cast a Druid spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage, you add your Wisdom modifier to one damage roll of the spell.</p><p><strong>Primal Strike.</strong> The extra damage of your Primal Strike increases to 2d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-large-teal.webp","_id":"s3c45a8e29e25c55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfect Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have developed your body and mind to new heights. Your Strength or Dexterity score (your choice) and Wisdom scores increase by 4, to a maximum of 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp","_id":"s3c547bf4bc37a31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slippery Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have acquired greater mental strength. You gain Proficiency in two out of the following Saving Throws: Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp","_id":"s3c79b0ebd19a7e3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Awakened Season","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The effect of your Awakened Season improves in the following ways:</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Affected creatures that start their turn in the area or enter it for the first time on a turn, regain hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. This effect does not receive the bonus healing from Awakened Season.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any radiant or fire damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any lightning or necrotic damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any cold damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3cb5e5da300d811","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unstable Backlash","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are imperiled during your rage, the magic within you can lash out; immediately after you take damage or fail a Saving Throw while raging, you can use your Reaction to roll on the Wild Magic table and immediately produce the effect rolled. This effect replaces your current Wild Magic effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3cbffe11a293a4d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Disciplined","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use heavy weapons despite being small.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-guard-steel-green.webp","_id":"s3cc788b16c2872f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lay on Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blessed touch can heal wounds. You have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you take a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of hit points equal to your paladin level × 5.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can touch a creature and draw power from the pool to restore a number of hit points to that creature, up to the maximum amount remaining in your pool.</p><p>Alternatively, you can expend 5 hit points from your pool of healing to cure the target of one disease or neutralize one poison affecting it. You can cure multiple diseases and neutralize multiple poisons with a single use of Lay on Hands, expending hit points separately for each one.</p><p>This feature has no effect on undead and constructs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"5 * @classes.paladin.levels","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"s3cc9b74ee453a2a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428351,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to invoke your rune magic to protect your allies. When another creature you can see within 60 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to force the attacker to reroll the d20 and use the new roll.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Additionally, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to regain one use.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3cec0dc9717d258","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slow Fall","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Reaction when you fall to reduce any falling damage you take by an amount equal to five times your monk level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you fall"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"5 * @classes.monk.levels","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/pseudopod-teal.webp","_id":"s3d0f3f5775593c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beguiling Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Charm Person and Mirror Image spells prepared.</p><p>In addition, immediately after you cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell using a spell slot, you can cause a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the target has the Charmed or Frightened condition (your choice) for 1 minute. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p>Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending one use of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3d38d32a5f60f16","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Evolution Feat","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional evolution feat for which you meet the prequisites.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3d418768035c063","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Durable Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic you channel helps ward off harm. While you maintain Concentration on a spell, you have a +2 bonus to AC and all Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3d47c6befdc2ee6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Emissary of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to diffuse violent situations. Whenever you make a Charisma check to calm violent emotions or to counsel peace, you have Advantage on the roll. You must make this entreaty in good faith; it doesn't apply if Proficiency in the Deception or Intimidation skill applies to your check.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Performance or Persuasion skill (choose one).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3d7ec86cf6f8ec1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tides of Chaos","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manipulate the forces of chance and chaos to gain Advantage on one Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw. Once you do so, you must finish a Long Rest or roll on the Wild Surge table before you can use this feature again.</p><p>Any time before you regain the use of this feature, you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher. You then regain the use of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3dd20d8cee4fdf4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Artisan's Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to create simple items.</p><p>You conduct an hour-long ritual that crafts a nonmagical item that must include some metal: a simple or martial weapon, a suit of armor, ten pieces of ammunition, a set of tools, or another metal object (see chapter 5, \"Equipment,\" in the Player's Handbook for examples of these items). The creation is completed at the end of the hour, coalescing in an unoccupied space of your choice on a surface within 5 feet of you.</p><p>The thing you create can be something that is worth no more than 1500 gp. As part of this ritual, you must lay out metal, which can include coins, with a value equal to the creation. The metal irretrievably coalesces and transforms into the creation at the ritual's end, magically forming even nonmetal parts of the creation. The ritual can create a duplicate of a nonmagical item that contains metal, such as a key, if you possess the original during the ritual.</p><p>The item you are creating automatically has the masterwork property if it can have it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3df1625759cd6b5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortified Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your half your Witch Level + spellcasting ability modifier to Saving Throws to maintain Concentration. This bonus is doubled for your Coven spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3e215327d04b1f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can expend 3 Ki Points to bolster yourself against harm for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition. During that time, you have Resistance to all damage except Force damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"at the start of your turn"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s3e3628faf73515a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Devotion Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Protection from Evil and Good, Sanctuary</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Lesser Restoration, Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Beacon of Hope, Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Freedom of Movement, Guardian of Faith</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Commune, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3e3fd830c644791","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428352,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lethality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The critical range for your weapon attacks increases by 1.</p><p>Additionally, you can apply the extra damage from your Assassinate class feature even after the first turn of combat, provided that you are hidden from the target or it is suffering from a condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3e4e8b9716bc363","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fast Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you aren't wearing any armor or wielding a shield.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s3e5eb6e2b9e7df9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428442,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura Improvements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The range of your Aura of Protection increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/barrier-wall-explosion-orange.webp","_id":"s3e75fda6c70977d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beguiling Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron teaches you how to guard your mind and body. You are immune to the Charmed condition.</p><p>In addition, immediately after a creature you can see hits you with an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage you take by half (round down), and you can force the attacker to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker takes Psychic damage equal to the damage you take. Once you use this Reaction, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3ea42f7c7b981af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Elves don't need to sleep. Instead, they meditate deeply, remaining semiconscious, for 4 hours a day. While meditating, you can dream after a fashion; such dreams are actually mental excercises that have become reflexive through years of practice. After resting in this way, you gain the same benefit that a human does from 8 hours of sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s3f0d495d5acfd63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Celestial Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain temporary hit points whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest. These temporary hit points equal your warlock level + your Charisma modifier. Additionally, choose up to five creatures you can see at the end of the rest. Those creatures each gain temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f11817685c5e38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Minor Arcana","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can expend one pact magic spell slot to gain a number of free castings for lesser spells until you finish your next Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>You can choose only warlock spells that you know and each chosen spell must not have a clause that grants it additional or enhanced effects when it is cast at a higher level. The total spell level of the chosen spells must be equal to or lower than the level of the expended pact magic slot. You can choose the same spell multiple times.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a Short or a Long Rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-eye-purple.webp","_id":"s3f21066df704f6e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artificer's Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make an INT-check related to magic items, alchemical objects, or technological devices, you have Advantage on the check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-worn-blue.webp","_id":"s3f26aa65663b951","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magical energy roiling inside you sometimes erupts from you. When you enter your rage, roll on the Wild Magic table to determine the magical effect produced.</p><p>If the effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Wild Magic</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d8</th><th scope=\"col\">Magical Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Shadowy tendrils lash around you. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take 1d12 necrotic damage. You also gain 1d12 temporary hit points.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>You teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a Bonus Action.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>An intangible spirit, which looks like a flumph or a pixie (your choice), appears within 5 feet of one creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you. At the end of the current turn, the spirit explodes, and each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or take 1d6 force damage. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again, summoning another spirit, on each of your turns as a Bonus Action.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Magic infuses one weapon of your choice that you are holding. Until your rage ends, the weapon's damage type changes to force, and it gains the light and thrown properties, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the weapon leaves your hand, the weapon reappears in your hand at the end of the current turn.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Whenever a creature hits you with an Attack Roll before your rage ends, that creature takes 1d6 force damage, as magic lashes out in retribution.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Until your rage ends, you are surrounded by multi colored, protective lights; you gain a +1 bonus to AC, and while within 10 feet of you, your allies gain the same bonus.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Flowers and vines temporarily grow around you. Until your rage ends, the ground within 15 feet of you is 3 for your enemies.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>A bolt of light shoots from your chest. Another creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take 1d6 radiant damage and be Blinded until the start of your next turn. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a Bonus Action.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f39525f6c6feaa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428323,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Watery Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to Fire and Acid damage.</p><p>You also gain the ability to defend yourself by momentarily assuming a watery form. As a Reaction when you are hit by an attack, you can reduce that damage by an amount equal to your sorcerer level plus your Charisma score, and then you can move up to 30 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, or you use 3 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3fdc70c882da532","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Illusionist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Minor Illusion cantrip. Your spellcasting ability for it is INT, WIS, or CHA (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-firefly-hand-yellow.webp","_id":"s3fdfd3b4179f435","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Coven Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Based on your chosen season, you always have the following spells prepared. You can cast each of those spells without expending a spell slot. And you cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Heal, Regenerate.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> Sunbeam, Firestorm.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Chain Lightning, Circle of Death.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> Wall of Ice, Icy Prison.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3fedfd0df73b3aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Distant Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make a ranged weapon attack, you can spend 1 ki point to prevent attacking at long range from imposing Disadvantage on your Attack Rolls until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make a ranged weapon attack at long range"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/projectile-spiral-gray.webp","_id":"s40045b9d3cea955","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the dread presence of your dragon ancestor, causing those around you to become awestruck or frightened. As a Bonus Action, you draw on this power and exude an aura of awe or fear (your choice) to a distance of 60 feet. For 1 minute, each hostile creature that starts its turn in this aura or enters it for the first time on a turn must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be Charmed (if you chose awe) or Frightened (if you chose fear) until the aura ends. A creature that succeeds on this Saving Throw is Immune to your aura for 24 hours.</p><p>Additionally, any spell that deals the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry is treated as 1 spell level higher for the purposes of its damage.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/projectile-smoke-glowing.webp","_id":"s4083742a8c8b570","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Graceful Climber","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Climb Speed of 20 feet and you may use your Dexterity modifier in place of your Strength modifier for skill checks to climb.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/root-vine-entangled-humanoid.webp","_id":"s40b3d943629f78f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Faun Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the shortbow, longbow, faunish spear, and scimitar.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/polearms/javelin-hooked.webp","_id":"s40eacfdfe6da3fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Easy Balance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Acrobatics skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/materials/feather-blue-glowing.webp","_id":"s40efea0c05496ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a number of superiority dice equal to half your maximum (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s40f9ef5fa2e4f5a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to invoke a rite of hemocraft that infuses your weapon strikes with elemental energy. As a Bonus Action, you can activate any rite you know on one weapon you're holding. The effect of the rite lasts until you finish a Short or a Long Rest. When you activate a rite, you take necrotic damage equal to one roll of your hemocraft die. This damage can't be reduced in any way.</p><p>While the rite is in effect, attacks you make with this weapon are magical, and deal extra damage equal to your hemocraft die of the type determined by the chosen rite. A weapon can hold only one active rite at a time. Other creatures can't gain the benefit of your rite.</p><p>If you have a Crimson Rite active on a weapon you're holding and a creature within 30 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points by an effect that includes the chosen damage type, you regain one Hit Die, which you can spend immediately as if you had taken a Rest. This effect cannot be triggered again until the start of your next turn.</p><p>You choose one rite from the crimson rites below when you first gain this feature. You learn an additional crimson rite at 7th level, and again at 14th level.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Flame.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is fire damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Frozen.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is cold damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Storm.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is lightning damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Dead.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is necrotic damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p><p><strong>Rite of the Oracle.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is psychic damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p><p><strong>Rite of the Roar.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is thunder damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.bloodhunter.hemocraft","necrotic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s40ffa3cbe889123","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Curving Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to direct an errant projectile toward a new target. When you make an Attack Roll with a magic projectile and miss, you can use a Bonus Action to reroll the Attack Roll against a different target within 60 feet of the original target.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s419235d05c93df2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s426c9597868306e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of the Trickster","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you can choose yourself or a willing creature within 30 feet of yourself to have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. This blessing lasts until you finish a Long Rest or you use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s427522bf9f732b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Archetype","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an archetype from the list available that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. The archetype you choose grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow.webp","_id":"s42945edbe562211","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189494,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mystical connection to the land infuses you with the ability to cast certain spells. At 3rd, 5th, 7th, and 9th level you gain access to circle spells connected to the land where you became a druid. Choose that land—arctic, coast, desert, forest, grassland, mountain, swamp, or Underdark—and consult the associated list of spells.</p><p>Once you gain access to a circle spell, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day. If you gain access to a spell that doesn't appear on the druid spell list, the spell is nonetheless a druid spell for you. You can cast these spells while in your Wildshape form.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Arid</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Blur, Burning Hands, Fire Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Wall of Stone</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Polar</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Hold Person, Ray of Frost</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Temperate</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Misty Step, Shocking Grasp, Sleep</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Tree Stride</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Tropical</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Acid Splash, Ray of Sickness, Web</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Stinking Cloud</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Polymorph</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-ice-teardrop.webp","_id":"s4299e8daffb2bb7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428338,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Copperscale Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the longbow, glaive, warspear, and greatspear.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/polearms/javelin-hooked.webp","_id":"s42f964139a7a523","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hurl Through Hell","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll, you can try to instantly transport the target through the Lower Planes. The target must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or the target disappears and hurtles through a nightmare landscape. The target takes 10d10 Psychic damage if it isn't a Fiend, and it has the Incapacitated condition until the end of your next turn, when it returns to the space it previously occupied or the nearest unoccupied space.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-fire-orange.webp","_id":"s42fbaf53688f21c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Mushroom Circles Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Mushroom Circles Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Faerie Fire, Sleep, Fortune's Favor, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hypnotic Pattern, Summon Fey</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Charm Monster, Confusion</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mislead, Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4369727913a0bf8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steel Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your tinkering has borne you a faithful companion, a steel defender. It is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See this creature's game statistics in the steel defender stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. You determine the creature's appearance and whether it has two legs or four; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.</p><p>In combat, the defender shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the defender's.</p><p>If the Mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. If it has died within the last hour, you can use your armorsmith's tools as an Action to revive it, provided you are within 5 feet of it and you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. The steel defender returns to life after 1 minute with all its hit points restored.</p><p>At the end of a Long Rest, you can create a new steel defender if you have your armorsmith's tools with you. If you already have a steel defender from this feature, the first one immediately perishes. The defender also perishes if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-golem-stone-blue.webp","_id":"s4397f2b384787e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Open Hand Technique","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manipulate your enemy's ki when you harness your own. Whenever you hit a creature with one of the attacks granted by your Flurry of Blows, you can impose one of the following effects on that target.</p><ul><li>If it is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or be knocked Prone.</li><li>It must make a Strength Saving Throw. If it fails, you can push it up to 15 feet away from you.</li><li>It must make a Constitution Saving Throw. If it fails, it can't take Reactions until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-hand-glow-pink.webp","_id":"s43d98e7cd35e88d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428348,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Intimidation, Performance, or Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"s43f8966a26a1863","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428346,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s4410bd541039acd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Druid level specified in the Circle of the Moon Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><p>In addition, you can cast the spells from this feature while you're in a Wild Shape form.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Circle of the Sea Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Cure Wounds, Moonbeam, Starry Wisp</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Conjure Animals</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fount of Moonlight</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-ice-teardrop.webp","_id":"s448a5276e1ae1b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keeper of Old","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the mighty primeval behemoths allows you new insight into the ancient world. You gain Proficiency in the History skill. When you make an Intelligence (History) check, you can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the Ability Check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s44952c9bc33fcdd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Raging Serpent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are raging you can call down your god's fury in the form of a powerful lightning bolt when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack. The target has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 8 + your Proficiency + your STR modifier. On a failure, the creature takes 12d10 lightning damage, and half as much on a successful one. Any creature that you have Grappled has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend a use of your rage to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s449cbfceafa6d09","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Savage Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 3 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you, take reduced damage from bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage while you are not Incapacitated. The reduction is equal to your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s44aa5f1c887f2fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strongheart Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with light and medium armor as well as the longsword, battleaxe, longbow, and heavy crossbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/swords-short.webp","_id":"s44e9390e233d74e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Druid level specified in the Circle of the Sea Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Circle of the Sea Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Absorb Elements, Fog Cloud, Gust of Wind, Shape Water, Water Blast</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Tidal Wave, Water Breathing</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Control Water, Watery Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Elemental, Maelstrom</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-ice-teardrop.webp","_id":"s4510d0053de9c14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Allegiance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature within 5 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to magically substitute your own health for that of the target creature, causing that creature not to take the damage. Instead, you take the damage. This damage to you can't be reduced or prevented in any way.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s45cb8795502d77c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of the Raven","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to merge with your raven spirit. As a Bonus Action when your raven is perched on your shoulder, your body merges with your raven's form. While merged, you become Tiny, you replace your Speed with the raven's, and you can use your action only to Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, or Search. During this time, you gain the benefits of your raven being perched on your shoulder. As an Action, you and the raven return to normal.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s45ce02a7545a6e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nimble Beast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>11th-level ranger Beast Conclave feature (replaces Beast's Fury)</p><p>Whenever an attacker that your companion can see hits it with an attack, it can use its Reaction to halve the attack's damage against it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4609bcd9ecf4ada","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Domain","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one domain related to your deity from the list of available domains. Each domain is detailed in their own feature, and each one provides examples of gods associated with it. Your choice grants you domain spells and other features when you choose it at 3rd level. It also grants you additional ways to use Channel Divinity when you gain that feature at 3rd level, and additional benefits at 6th, 8th, and 17th levels.</p><p><strong>Domain Spells.</strong> Each domain has a list of spells—its domain spells—that you gain at the cleric levels noted in the domain description. Once you gain a domain spell, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.</p><p>If you have a domain spell that doesn't appear on the cleric spell list, the spell is nonetheless a cleric spell for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-spirit-blue.webp","_id":"s462d8a4bfe827ec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elegant Riposte","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are currently in your parrying stance and a creature misses you with a melee weapon attack, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon against that creature, provided it is within your reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4681b1820dcb46a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Veil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can weave a veil of psychic static to mask yourself. As an Action, you can magically become Invisible, along with anything you are wearing or carrying, for 1 hour or until you dismiss this effect (no action required). This invisibility ends early immediately after you deal damage to a creature or you force a creature to make a Saving Throw.</p><p>If you expend a Psionic Energy Die, you can also affect all creatures of your choice while they are within 20 feet of you. The effect ends early on all affected creatures when any of them deal damage to a creature or force it to make a Saving Throw.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s468423ed49ef23c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Genie's Splendor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 10 + your Constitution modifier + your Charisma modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Intimidation, Performance, or Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s46ac3e6bd93c980","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hungry Darkness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Shield of Ineffable Darkness becomes more powerful. When you use it, you can select up to three additional, hostile creatures you can see within 30 feet of you. They have to make a CON Saving Throw or become Blinded until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s46fb614f8d1468a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keeper of Souls","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can seize a trace of vitality from a parting soul and use it to heal the living. When an enemy you can see dies within 60 feet of you, you or one creature of your choice that is within 60 feet of you regains hit points equal to three times your Cleric level. You can use this feature only if you aren't Incapacitated. Once you use it, you can't do so again until the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s473e852a224362f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirits of Ill Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>6th-level Sorcerer Shadow Magic feature (replaces Hound of Ill Omen)</p><p>You can cast Summon Undead without a Material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a Long Rest. Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require Concentration. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting, and the spell ends early if you cast it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s47bfff5dadf258a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Walker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Commune with Nature spell, but only as a ritual. When you do so, a spiritual version of one of the animals you chose for Totem Spirit or Aspect of the Beast appears to you to convey the information you seek.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s47d371b610d1920","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s4831f53d557988b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Back Alley Bruiser","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You don't need Advantage on the Attack Roll to use your Sneak Attack against a creature if its within your melee reach, none of its allies are within 5 feet of it, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.</p><p>Additionally, you can Sneak Attack with any melee weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s483693473fc3f07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ki","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your focus and martial training allow you to harness a well of extraordinary energy within yourself. This energy is represented by Ki Points. Your Monk level determines the amount of Ki Points you have, as shown in the Ki Points column of the Monk Features table.</p><p>You can expend these points to enhance or fuel certain Monk features. You start knowing three such features: Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind, each of which is detailed below.</p><p>When you expend Ki Points, it is unavailable until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, at the end of which you regain all your expended Ki Points.</p><p>Some features that use Ki Points require your target to make a Saving Throw. The save DC equals 8 plus your Wisdom modifier and Proficiency Bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.monk.ki-points","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s483ca21a0fdaf13","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428347,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bounding Leap","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make a jump, you can use your Dexterity score in place of your Strength score to determine the distance you can cover. Additionally, the distance for your Long Jump is increased by 10 feet and by 5 feet for your High Jump. This bonus distance is halved when you make either jump as standing jump.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/arrow-upward-blue.webp","_id":"s4889b2386ee256b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed in the Oath of Glory Spells table. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how oath spells work.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Glory Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Guiding Bolt, Heroism</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Enhance Ability, Magic Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Haste, Protection from Energy</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Compulsion, Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Legend Lore, Yolande's Regal Presence</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s48b56d01f19fd7a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cauldron Rituals","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn a number of special rituals that you can complete as part of a Short or Long Rest. You may only choose one of these rituals at a time and the effects last until you complete your next Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Bounty of the Earth.</strong> When you forage for food or ingredients, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If your Foraging check is successful, you roll an additional d4 and add it to the result of the die on the result column.</p><p><strong>Eye of Newt, Wing of Bat.</strong> Select a number of non-masterwork consumables equal to your spellcasting ability modifier that your group crafted on this Adventuring Day using alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit. The selected items receive the masterwork property.</p><p><strong>Nature's Veil.</strong> When your group makes a Prepare Campsite check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. Additionally, you and up to 8 other creatures of your choice regain additional hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch Level when you complete your next Short Rest on this Adventuring Day.</p><p><strong>Snake Stomach.</strong> If your group consumes a meal as part of this rest, the duration of the effect is increased by 1 day. The same meal can only be affected by this ritual once.</p><p><strong>Whispers of the Wild.</strong> When your group makes a Lookout check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. Additionally, you add your spellcasting ability modifier to your passive Perception and that of up to 8 other creatures of your choice.</p><p><strong>Witch Path.</strong> 3 doesn't slow your group's travel and whenever your group makes a Pathfinding check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s48f896c45aff482","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Two Minds, One Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma Saving Throws while you are in Symbiosis.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s492bee45cdef27d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of Hor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are acclimatized to hot regions as per the DMG and you have Resistance to radiant damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s493137304c5bb3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You keep your magical power and martial focus in perfect balance, allowing you to convert spell slots into Ki Points, or convert Ki Points into spell slots.</p><p><strong>Converting Spell Slots to Ki Points.</strong> You can expend a spell slot to regain a number of expended Ki Points equal to the slot's level (no action required).</p><p><strong>Recovering Spell Slots.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can transform unexpended Ki Points to recover one expended spell slot. The Recovering Spell Slots table shows the cost of recovering a spell slot of a given level, and it lists the minimum Monk level you must be to recover a slot. You can recover a spell slot no higher than level 4.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Recovering Spell Slots</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Slot Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Ki Point Cost</th><th scope=\"col\">Min. Monk Level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>19</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4943879942bd90f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428348,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Resurgence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once on each of your turns, if you have no uses of Wild Shape left, you can give yourself one use by expending a spell slot (no action required).</p><p>In addition, you can expend one use of Wild Shape (no action required) to give yourself a level 1 spell slot, but you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/spirit-deer-herd-blue.webp","_id":"s4962ee926bf80b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alchemist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Alchemist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Healing Word, Ray of Sickness</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Flaming Sphere, Melf's Acid Arrow</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Corrosion, Mass Healing Word</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Death Ward, Vitriolic Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cloudkill, Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s496415088b204c6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Cleaver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bond with the elemental might of giants and their ilk grows, and you learn to infuse weapons with primordial energy.</p><p>When you enter your rage, you can infuse one weapon of your choice that you are holding with one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, thunder, or lightning. While you wield the infused weapon during your rage, the weapon's damage type changes to the chosen type, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the chosen type when it hits, and it gains the thrown property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If you throw the weapon, it reappears in your hand the instant after it hits or misses a target. The infused weapon's benefits are suppressed while a creature other than you wields it.</p><p>While raging and holding the infused weapon, you can use a Bonus Action to change the infused weapon's current damage type to a different one from the above damage types.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s499dfcc8600ae37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fang and Claw","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal your choice of piercing or slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your fangs or claws to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blood-slash-foam-red.webp","_id":"s49b9541bc9012ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Acid Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to acid damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/dissolve-arm-flesh.webp","_id":"s49f3d4fedce9899","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Honed Technique","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, you can reroll your superiority die and take either result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s49f5277a19b871f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you regain expended uses of Bardic Inspiration until you have two if you have fewer than that.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/explosion-lava-stone-green.webp","_id":"s49f9c606f0441fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insightful Striking","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. Your magic grants you a brief vision of the target's defenses. Until the end of your next turn, you gain one of the following effects of your choice:</p><ul><li>The next time you make an Attack Roll against the target, roll a d6 and add the number rolled to the total.</li><li>The next time the target must make a Saving Throw against a spell you cast, the target must roll a d6 and subtract the number rolled from the Saving Throw.</li></ul><p>You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4a5c4bedc8047c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Way of the Long Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Monks of the Way of the Long Death are obsessed with the meaning and mechanics of dying. They capture creatures and prepare elaborate experiments to capture, record, and understand the moments of their demise. They use this knowledge to guide their understanding of martial arts, yielding a deadly fighting style.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4a697cccb4ae6aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Overcharge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast a spell gained through an elemental discipline as a 9th level spell, without expending any additional ki points.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4a9fb048e17849a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Illusion Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Illusion school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Illusion school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4aa988afdc055b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortifying Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your experience surviving harrowing environments allows you to bolster your allies in addition to yourself. When you finish a Short Rest, you can choose a number of creatures you can see equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). A chosen creature regains Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Ranger level and has Advantage on Constitution Saving Throws and Wisdom Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened condition for 24 hours.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ab268b84ea1028","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hex in the City","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Friends and Charm Person spells prepared. When you cast either spell, the target does not know that it was Charmed by you unless it directly observed you casting the spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4b2e3decedd1c47","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gatorian Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the battleaxe, greataxe, warhammer, and maul.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/axes/axe-broad-grey.webp","_id":"s4b30ed125c2dc0e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor and Shields.</p><p>In addition, you can use a Simple or Martial weapon as a Spellcasting Focus to cast spells from your Bard spell list.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4b48ec321ae02f2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gathered Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A swarm of intangible nature spirits has bonded itself to you and can assist you in battle. While you're alive, the swarm remains in your space, crawling on you or flying and skittering around you within your space. You determine its appearance, or you generate its appearance by rolling on the Swarm Appearance table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Swarm Appearance</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d4</th><th scope=\"col\">Appearance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Swarming insects</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Miniature twig blights</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fluttering birds</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Playful pixies</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Once on each of your turns, you can cause the swarm to assist you in one of the following ways, immediately after you hit a creature with an attack:</p><ul><li>The attack's target takes 1d6 piercing damage from the swarm.</li><li>The attack's target must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC or be moved by the swarm up to 15 feet horizontally in a direction of your choice.</li><li>You are moved by the swarm 15 feet horizontally in a direction of your choice.</li></ul><div><strong>It's Your Swarm</strong><p>A Swarmkeeper's swarm and spells are reflections of the character's bond with nature spirits. Take the opportunity to describe the swarm and the ranger's magic in play. For example, when your ranger casts gaseous form, they might appear to melt into the swarm, instead of a cloud of mist, or the Arcane Eye spell could create an extension of your swarm that spies for you. Such descriptions don't change the effects of spells, but they are an exciting opportunity to explore your character's narrative through their class abilities. For more guidance on customizing spells, see the \"Personalizing Spells\" section in chapter 3.</p><p>Also, remember that the swarm's appearance is yours to customize, and don't feel confined to a single appearance. Perhaps the spirits' look changes with the ranger's mood or with the seasons. You decide!</p></div","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4b81372a6981af1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Protection from Evil and Good through your Hunter's Mysticism Feature, it does not require Concentration and lasts for 7 days.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4b9be9b85973f4f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master of navigating the natural world, and you react with swift and decisive action when attacked. This grants you the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You ignore 3.</li><li>You have Advantage on initiative rolls.</li><li>On your first turn during combat, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that have not yet acted.</li></ul><p>In addition, you are skilled at navigating the wilderness. You gain the following benefits when traveling for an hour or more:</p><ul><li>Difficult terrain doesn't slow your group's travel.</li><li>Your group can't become lost except by magical means.</li><li>When performing a task during the Travelling Phase of Overland Travel, you may additionally perform the Lookout task or assist with it.</li><li>If you are traveling alone, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.</li><li>When you forage, you find twice as much food as you normally would.</li><li>While tracking other creatures, you also learn their exact number, their sizes, and how long ago they passed through the area.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s4b9c0949cd2f832","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elusive","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No Attack Roll has Advantage against you while you aren't Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-swirling-blue.webp","_id":"s4bbef3b52edb67f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Crafting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you select this school, you gain Proficiency with one tool of your choice. If you make a check to craft something, you can substitute your Intelligence for the ability score you would normally use for the crafting attempt. You can also use your arcane focus in place of the required tool.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c23ea3d115fe6c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428378,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extensive Study","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell from the wizard spell list. The spell must fulfill all the usual criteria for learning a wizard spell of 1st level or higher. You learn an additional spell in this manner at the following levels in this class: 5th, 9th, 13th, and 17th.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c39ff18216f77d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Icon of Deceit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become of an avatar of deceit and emit an aura of treacherous magic in a 30-ft emanation. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>When a creature targets you with an attack, but any of your allies are within the aura and within range of the attack, it makes the roll with Disadvantage.</li><li>As part of the Bonus Action to activate this feature and as a Bonus Action on every subsequent turn, you can give yourself Advantage on one Attack Roll.</li><li>When you use your Treacherous Strikes feature, the new target of the attack can be anywhere in the aura. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c696f13ee6b13f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Transmutation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are concentrating on a transmutation spell, your Concentration can't be broken as a result of taking damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4cba4f3ffa30db9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thieves' Cant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>During your rogue training you learned thieves' cant, a secret mix of dialect, jargon, and code that allows you to hide messages in seemingly normal conversation. Only another creature that knows thieves' cant understands such messages. It takes four times longer to convey such a message than it does to speak the same idea plainly.</p><p>In addition, you understand a set of secret signs and symbols used to convey short, simple messages, such as whether an area is dangerous or the territory of a thieves' guild, whether loot is nearby, or whether the people in an area are easy marks or will provide a safe house for thieves on the run.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"s4ccae39bd92e8c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s4ce90d0e68cbf99","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rend Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can sweep your Psychic Blades directly through a creature's mind. When you use your Psychic Blades to deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature, you can force that target to make an Intelligence Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). If the save fails, the target is Stunned for 1 minute. The Stunned target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend three Psionic Energy dice to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d1a70dfdfcdab8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Flame","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unleash the phoenix fire that blazes within you.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you magically wreathe yourself in swirling fire, as your eyes glow like hot coals. For 1 minute, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet.</li><li>Any creature takes fire damage equal to your Charisma modifier if it hits you with a melee attack from within 10 feet of you or if it touches you.</li><li>Whenever you roll fire damage on your turn, the roll gains a bonus to equal to your Charisma modifier.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 2 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d4c25deb4d4d78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Firearm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know how to turn a wand, staff, or rod into an arcane firearm, a conduit for your destructive spells. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can use woodcarver's tools to carve special sigils into a wand, staff, or rod and thereby turn it into your arcane firearm. The sigils disappear from the object if you later carve them on a different item. The sigils otherwise last indefinitely.</p><p>You can use your arcane firearm as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells. When you cast an artificer spell through the firearm, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/wands/wand-carved-fire.webp","_id":"s4d4e608f7cb2946","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rapid Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to trade accuracy for swift strikes. If you have Advantage on a weapon attack against a target on your turn, you can forgo that Advantage to immediately make an additional weapon attack against the same target as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d98cef824fc95f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428345,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empower Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to spend your own magical reserves to empower your Eidolon's attacks. As a Bonus Action, you can spend a spell slot if you can see your Eidolon within 60 feet of you. For 1 hour, you add 1d8 times the level of the spell slot expended to your Eidolon's damage rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4e366867e8c78cd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limited Flight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Fly Speed of 50 feet, but you must end your movement on a surface you can stand on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-flying-wings-purple.webp","_id":"s4eb0d1ed06b1411","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Varanu Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in three of your choice of the following skills: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, Religion, Stealth, Survival</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-symbol-leaf-green.webp","_id":"s4ec102285103b65","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Preserve Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to heal the badly injured.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol and evoke healing energy that can restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level. Choose any creatures within 30 feet of you, and divide those hit points among them. You can't use this feature on an undead or a construct.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue-purple.webp","_id":"s4ed1ebdd4f0101e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Smite Evil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage dice of your Divine Smite increase to d10s. Additionally, the bonus damage against fiends and undead now applies against all evil-aligned creatures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/projectiles-blades-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s4ee3b7b5a12a9c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ee452307acbee0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Quickened Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can spend 2 ki points and roll a Martial Arts die. You regain a number of hit points equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.monk.martial-arts","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-explosion-burst-green.webp","_id":"s4fa3587a6a8a11e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Path of Tranquility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can become an island of calm in even the most chaotic of situations. With this feature, you can cast the Sanctuary spell on yourself, no material component required, and it lasts up to 8 hours. Its Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Wisdom modifier. A creature that succeeds on the save is Immune to this effect for 1 hour.</p><p>Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again for 1 minute.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4fc6f852a5b3778","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Incalculable Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>No Attack Roll can have Advantage against you when you are under the effect of Patient Defense.</p><p>Additionally, whenever an Attack Roll misses you, you can move 10 feet in any direction without provoking Attacks of Opportunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4fdd85ee9a0907f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a student of arcane magic, you have learned to cast spells. The information below details how you use those rules with Wizard spells, which appear in the Wizard spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know three Wizard cantrips of your choice from the Wizard spell list.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Wizard cantrip of your choice.</p><p>When you reach Wizard levels 4 and 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Wizard Features table.</p><p><strong>Spellbook.</strong> Your wizardly apprenticeship culminated in the creation of a unique book: your spellbook. It is a Tiny object that weighs 3 pounds, contains 100 pages, and can be read only by you or someone casting Identify. You determine the book's appearance and materials, such as a gilt-edged tome or a collection of vellum bound with twine.</p><p>The book contains the level 1+ spells you know. It starts with six level 1 Wizard spells of your choice.</p><p>Whenever you gain a Wizard level after 1, add two Wizard spells of your choice to your spellbook. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Wizard Features table. The spells are the culmination of arcane research you do regularly.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Wizard Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To do so, choose four spells from your spellbook. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Wizard levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Wizard Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Wizard spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 3 Wizard, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination, chosen from your spellbook.</p><p>If another Wizard feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Wizard spells for you.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can change your list of prepared spells, replacing any of the spells there with spells from your spellbook.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus or your spellbook as a Spellcasting Focus for your Wizard spells.</p><div><strong>Expanding and Replacing a Spellbook</strong><p>The spells you add to your spellbook as you gain levels reflect your ongoing magical research, but you might find other spells during your adventures that you can add to the book. You could discover a Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll, for example, and then copy it into your spellbook.</p><p><strong>Copying a Spell into the Book.</strong> When you find a level 1+ Wizard spell, you can copy it into your spellbook if it's of a level you can prepare and if you have time to copy it. For each level of the spell, the transcription takes 2 hours and costs 50 GP. Afterward you can prepare the spell like the other spells in your spellbook.</p><p><strong>Copying the Book.</strong> You can copy a spell from your spellbook into another book. This is like copying a new spell into your spellbook but faster, since you already know how to cast the spell. You need spend only 1 hour and 10 GP for each level of the copied spell.</p><p>If you lose your spellbook, you can use the same procedure to transcribe the Wizard spells that you have prepared into a new spellbook. Filling out the remainder of the new book requires you to find new spells to do so. For this reason, many wizards keep a backup spellbook.</p></div","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s4fe1eb50197c4c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428451,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Universal Speech","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have gained the ability to make your speech intelligible to any creature. As an Action, choose one or more creatures within 60 feet of you, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). The chosen creatures can magically understand you, regardless of the language you speak, for 1 hour.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4fe2eb84045e3db","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Psionic Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>Whenever you gain a sorcerer level, you can replace one spell you gained from this feature with another spell of the same level. The new spell must be a divination or an enchantment spell from the sorcerer, warlock, or wizard spell list.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Psionic Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Arms of Hadar, Dissonant Whispers, Mind Sliver, Calm Emotions, Detect Thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hunger of Hadar, Sending</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Evard's Black Tentacles, Summon Aberration</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Rary's Telepathic Bond, Telekinesis</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4fe6d949ed7887d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"All-Piercing Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can supercharge a shot with arcane energy. As part of this action, you can expend up to 3 uses of your Arcane Shot. The projectile shoots forth in a line 1 foot wide and 150 feet long, before disappearing. The projectile passes harmlessly through objects and magical barriers like Wall of Force, ignoring cover. Each creature in that line must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Arcane Shot save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 6d12 force damage + 2d12 additional force damage for every use of Arcane Shot you expended as part of this action.</p><p>You can use this feature once and you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ffdc1cd89e3c47","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Rest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use soothing music or oration to help revitalize your wounded allies during a Short Rest. If you or any friendly creatures who can hear your performance regain hit points by spending Hit Dice at the end of the Short Rest, each of those creatures can roll extra d6s equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and add them to the total of hit points recovered.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s500bae2ecaed3ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clockwork Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Clockwork Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>Whenever you gain a sorcerer level, you can replace one spell you gained from this feature with another spell of the same level. The new spell must be an abjuration or a transmutation spell from the sorcerer, warlock, or wizard spell list.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Clockwork Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Alarm, Protection from Evil and Good, Aid, Lesser Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dispel Magic, Protection from Energy</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Freedom of Movement, Summon Construct</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Greater Restoration, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>In addition, consult the Manifestations of Order table and choose or randomly determine a way your connection to order manifests while you are casting any of your sorcerer spells.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Manifestations of Order</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Manifestation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Spectral cogwheels hover behind you.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>The hands of a clock spin in your eyes.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Your skin glows with a brassy sheen.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Floating equations and geometric objects overlay your body.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Your spellcasting focus temporarily takes the form of a Tiny clockwork mechanism.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>The ticking of gears or ringing of a clock can be heard by you and those affected by your magic.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5058001024b5c8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transposition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to switch positions with your Eidolon if you can see it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5060f4b9601b8cb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Patron","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You strike a bargain with an otherworldly being of your choice:</p><ul><li>The Archfey</li><li>The Dragon</li><li>The Celestial</li><li>The Fathomless</li><li>The Fiend</li><li>The Genie</li><li>The Great Old One</li><li>The Hexblade</li><li>The Kraken</li><li>The Spider Queen</li><li>The Raven Mother</li><li>The Seeker</li><li>The Undead</li><li>The Undying</li></ul><p>The choice you make augments some of your subclass features, as noted below.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/lights/candles-lit-red-evil.webp","_id":"s50dce428f53e053","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clockwork Cavalcade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You summon spirits of order to expunge disorder around you. As an Action, you summon the spirits in a 30-foot cube originating from you. The spirits look like modrons or other constructs of your choice. The spirits are intangible and invulnerable, and they create the following effects within the cube before vanishing:</p><ul><li>The spirits restore up to 100 hit points, divided as you choose among any number of creatures of your choice in the cube.</li><li>Any damaged objects entirely in the cube are repaired instantly.</li><li>Every spell of 6th level or lower ends on creatures and objects of your choice in the cube.</li></ul><p>Once you use this action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s51217eb3a2790a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead. Moreover, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s51ac433c3358719","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Strands of Fate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to see and manipulate the strands of fate that weave around other individuals. As a Bonus Action, you can enter this state for up to 1 minute or until you lose your Concentration (as if you were concentrating on a spell). For the duration, whenever another creature you can see makes an Attack Roll or an Ability Check, you can use a Reaction to give the roll Advantage or Disadvantage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s51c89d8dd39e8ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Controlled Chaos","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a modicum of control over the surges of your wild magic. Whenever you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table, you can roll twice and use either number.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s51cef1b0644e796","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wind Speaker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The arcane magic you command is infused with elemental air. You can speak, read, and write Primordial. Knowing this language allows you to understand and be understood by those who speak its dialects: Aquan, Auran, Ignan, and Terran.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s51d2fdb4c85cd86","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428366,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blazing Revival","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond with your wildfire spirit can save you from death. If the spirit is within 120 feet of you when you are reduced to 0 hit points and thereby fall Unconscious, you can cause the spirit to drop to 0 hit points. You then regain half your hit points and immediately rise to your feet.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s520fed9c9c5df83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bloodthirst","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If your Sneak Attack hits a Bloodied or Lacerated creature, the target takes extra damage of the weapon's type equal to half your Rogue level (round up). In addition, when an enemy you can see is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you can take a Reaction and move up to your Speed. You can then make one melee attack. You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice, minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s524833216d08ea9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Curse (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw or be cursed until the end of your next turn. For the duration of the effect, the target must roll a d4 every time it rolls an Attack Roll or Saving Throw and subtract the result from the total.</li><li><strong>Enfeeble (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or deal half damage with weapon attacks until the end of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Additionally, while you are in darkness, you can reduce the cost of any feature that uses your Sneak Attack dice by 2 instead of 1 (to a minimum of 0). You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5255f215c3f6ad7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Courage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you can't be Frightened while you are conscious.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s526bae9824a329b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Poison Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to make a weapon deadlier. As a Bonus Action, you touch one weapon or piece of ammunition and conjure a special poison on it. The poison lasts for 1 minute. The next time you hit a target with an attack using that weapon or ammunition, the target takes poison damage immediately after the attack. The poison damage equals 2d10 + your paladin level, or 20 + your paladin level if you had Advantage on the Attack Roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s528b500239acfd7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dragon Ancestor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose one type of dragon as your ancestor. The damage type associated with each dragon is used by features you gain later.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Ancestry</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Dragon</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>You can speak, read, and write Draconic. Additionally, whenever you make a Charisma check when interacting with dragons, your Proficiency bonus is doubled if it applies to the check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-fire-breath-orange.webp","_id":"s52993014dcede7d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limitless Metamagic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Metamagic, you can combine any of the options you know for the same spell, paying the sorcery point cost for each.</p><p>Additionally, when an ally you can see within 120 feet casts a spell, you can use your Reaction to use your Metamagic on their spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s52ae586bd6a1214","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Pack Tactics.</strong> You have Advantage on Attack Rolls with your natural weapons against a creature if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't Incapacitated.</li><li><strong>A Friend in Deed.</strong> You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action and with a range of 30 feet. You can always use the Help action to give someone Advantage on a skill check, even if you are not proficient in the relevant skill yourself.</li><li><strong>Thick Hide.</strong> The temporary hit points gained through your Martial Mastery (Unarmored Defense) increase by half (rounded down). Additionally, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against becoming Poisoned or Lacerated.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s52c94c0d06d7723","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oceanic Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are now even more at home in the depths. You gain Resistance to cold damage. In addition, when you are fully submerged, any creature that is also fully submerged can understand your speech, and you can understand theirs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s53229b5e1bdfa93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Glorious Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can turn defense into a sudden strike. When you or another creature you can see within 10 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to grant a bonus to the target's AC against that attack, potentially causing it to miss. The bonus equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of +1). If the attack misses, you can make one weapon attack against the attacker as part of this Reaction, provided the attacker is within your weapon's range.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain one expended use on a Short Rest and all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s533ac5802c905bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You embody the power of the wilds. Your Strength and Constitution scores increase by 4. Your maximum for those scores is now 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"s53bcdca96c463bc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of the Ancients Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Ensnaring Strike, Speak with Animals</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Moonbeam, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Plant Growth, Protection from Energy</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Commune with Nature, Tree Stride</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s542d356dfb4f124","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Leadership Ability Score","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Some of your features reference your Leadership ability score. It represents how you command the respect and loyalty of those around you, as well as how you lead them in battle. Perhaps you are an experienced veteran, survivor of dozens of military conflicts both large and small, a cunning tactician with an academic background in the study of warfare, or a driven idealist with a larger-than-life personality.</p><p>Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. The chosen ability score becomes your Leadership ability score.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/charge.webp","_id":"s5434a4d7262b9ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Faithful Steed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on the aid of an otherworldly steed. You always have the Find Steed spell prepared.</p><p>You can also cast the spell once without expending a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":10,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/creatures/horse-white.webp","_id":"s5454377ca9096dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Breath Weapon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, your companion can exhale destructive energy in a 30 feet cone. The damage type is that of its Draconic Blood feature. Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your companion's Save DC, which is equal to 8 + your proficiency + its Constitution modifier, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>Your companion cannot use this feature again until it has finished a Short or Long Rest, or until you expend a use of your Second Wind to allow it use it again (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["(4+floor(((@details.level)-1)/5))d6",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/beam-jet-stream-trails-orange.webp","_id":"s54b3446e7a9a253","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Zephyr Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are hit by an attack, you can use your Reaction to make a Dexterity (Acrobatics) check and subtract the result of the roll from the damage taken.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Dexterity modifier and you can regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s54e701b0ec73cec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Piercing Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Initiative rolls and to Investigation and Intimidation checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s54e7f7b50bd9b43","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Student of War","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Deception, History, Insight, Intimidation, Investigation, Stealth. You can choose to gain Proficiency with an artisan's tools of your choice in place of any of these skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s557d19a014eeec7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animal Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Nature, Perception, Stealth, Survival.</p><p>Additionally, you add your Formshift Damage to the chosen skills and to your initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/humanoid-wolf-dog-blue.webp","_id":"s55a05b207c78c46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Radiant Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to cloak your allies in radiant armor.</p><p>As an Action, you channel blessed energy into an ally that you can see within 30 feet of you. The first time that ally is hit by an attack before you complete a Short or a Long Rest, the attacker takes radiant damage equal to 2d10 + your cleric level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55a77133e497686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you are in dim light or darkness, as a Bonus Action you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness. You then have Advantage on the first melee attack you make before the end of the turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55b8b23cfb30c6c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tigori Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the warspear, longbow, scimitar, and greatspear.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/scimitar-guard-brown.webp","_id":"s560ca6e1c12e085","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Adder's Kiss","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the Blood Curse of the Adder's Kiss for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s56503871216d231","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aquatic Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can breathe underwater and you gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s56cbca1fb6dcfdf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battlerager Armor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in heavy armor and ignore all restrictions for Barbarian class features while wearing heavy armor. You also gain the ability to modify your armor with spikes, blades, and other hazardous materials and turn it into a weapon: spiked armor.</p><p>Every time you finish a Short Rest, you can use this feature to remove these materials from your current spiked armor and attach them to another armor of your choice.</p><p>Spiked armor has the same properties as the original armor. Additionally, it counts as a heavy martial melee weapon with a reach of 5 ft that you are proficient in. On a hit, it deals 1d4 piercing damage. You use your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls. If spiked your armor has a permanent bonus to its armor class (e.g. the masterwork property), you add this bonus to your attack and damage rolls with it.</p><p>When you are raging and wearing spiked armor, you can make one attack with your spiked armor as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Additionally, when you successfully grapple a creature or shove it Prone, the creature also takes damage equal to your Strength modifier. If you are raging, you add your rage damage bonus to this damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5740f6583a343e1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428321,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Acolyte of Strength","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one druid cantrip of your choice. You also gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Athletics, Nature, or Survival.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s578a9e309e9ecaa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armorer Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Armorer Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Armorer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Magic Missile, Shield</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Mirror Image, Shatter</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Hypnotic Pattern, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Fire Shield, Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Passwall, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s5796a013995b4cf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rapid Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to trade accuracy for swift strikes. If you take the Attack action on your turn and have Advantage on an Attack Roll against one of the targets, you can forgo the Advantage for that roll to make an additional weapon attack against that target, as part of the same action. You can do so no more than once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57b1d5b1b67fef9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Night Flyer.</strong> You gain a darkvision range of 120 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 120 ft to its range.</li><li><strong>Agile Flyer.</strong> Your Speed increases by 10 feet and you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks when you fly out of an enemy's reach.</li><li><strong>Diving Raptor.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce, you can move up to double your Speed if your target is below you. If you moved at least 20 feet in this manner, the attack adds your Natural Weapons die to the damage again once.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57fbb9b55a47cf1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 2 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s58002d4ad1ae840","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rat Father's Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now target other creatures beside your bonded familiar for the purposes of your Mirror, Mirror feature.</p><p>You and any other creature that are currently Invisible through a spell or feature of yours have their speed doubled and can Hide as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s582246c5f3092de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Timeless Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ki sustains you so that you suffer none of the frailty of old age, and you can't be aged magically. You can still die of old age, however. In addition, you no longer need food or water.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/clock-stopwatch-white-blue.webp","_id":"s582a5359def94d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Winter's Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Frostbite cantrip. Additionally, you can start to use your control over cold to hamper your foes. Once per turn, when you damage one or more creatures with a weapon attack or a spell that does cold damage, you can use your Reaction to reduce the movement Speed of any of those creatures by 10 feet until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s585a8d2acad5028","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Seasonal Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain the following benefits based on your chosen season:</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> You are Immune to poison and disease.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> You are Resistance to fire and radiant damage, and you are acclimatized to extreme heat.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> You are Resistance to necrotic and lightning damage, and your maximum hit points cannot be reduced.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> You are Resistance to cold damage and you are acclimatized to extreme cold. Any temporary hit points that you gain are increased by an amount equal to your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s586ed24455f1dd2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Juggernaut","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation. As a result, the extra damage you deal with the Giant's Might feature increases to 1d10. Moreover, when you use that feature, your size can increase to Huge, and while you are that size, your reach increases by 5 feet.</p><p>Additionally, you now regain the use of your Giant's Might feature on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5874409e15fc66f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can direct your magic to absorb damage while your bladesong is active. When you take damage, you can use your Reaction to expend one spell slot and reduce that damage to you by an amount equal to five times the spell's slot level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s588fd4e576ecac8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Smite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one spell slot to deal radiant damage to the target, in addition to the weapon's damage. The extra damage is 2d8 for a 1st-level spell slot, plus 1d8 for each spell level higher than 1st, to a maximum of 6d8. The damage increases by 1d8 if the target is an undead or a fiend, to a maximum of 7d8.</p><p>You can use this feature without expending a spell slot a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"floor(@attributes.prof/2)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow-teal.webp","_id":"s589d176e445c6f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Wildkeepers Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a Wild Domain. At each indicated Witch level, add the corresponding listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Dunes Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Earth Tremor, Silent Image, Dust Devil, Mirror Image</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Haste, Wall of Sand</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Hallucinatory Terrain</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Maelstrom, Mislead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Marshes Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Grease, Ray of Sickness, Envenom, Ray of Enfeeblement</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Corrosion, Water Walk</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Evard's Black Tentacles, Vitriolic Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Acid Pit, Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Peaks Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Feather Fall, Witch Bolt, Earthbind, Darkvision</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Erupting Earth, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Stoneskin, Wall of Stone</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Blindsense, Transmute Rock</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Tundras Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Ice Knife, Blindness/Deafness, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Slow, Glacial Spike</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Control Winds</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Waves Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Charm Person, Fog Cloud, Enthrall, Water Blast</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Tidal Wave, Water Breathing</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Control Water, Watery Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dominate Person, Maelstrom</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Wealds Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Animal Friendship, Beast Bond, Barkskin, Pass without Trace</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Conjure Animals, Speak with Plants</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Conjure Nature Spirits, Guardian of Nature</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Tree Stride, Wrath of Nature</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s58a3b020c4c6f66","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tranquil Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As long as you have at least 1 hit point, you regain hit points equal to half your paladin level + your Charisma modifier at the start of every one of your turns.</p><p>If you deal damage to a creature, force it to make a Saving Throw, or otherwise target it with a harmful effect, this feature stops working until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s59174298214c8c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Implement of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Insight, Performance, or Persuasion skill (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s596fe95f32298b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rite of Dawn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Rite of the Dawn as part of your Crimson Rite feature. When you activate the Rite of the Dawn, the extra damage dealt by your rite is radiant damage. Additionally, while that rite is active on your weapon, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your weapon sheds bright light out to a range of 20 feet. This light counts as sunlight when you reach lvl 11 in this class.</li><li>You have Resistance to necrotic damage.</li><li>When you hit an undead creature with a weapon for which the Rite of the Dawn is active, you roll an additional hemocraft die when determining the extra damage from the rite.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s598200abe3342ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428327,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are shifted, any hostile creature that starts its turn within 60 feet of you or enters that area for the first time on a turn, must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier) or be Frightened or Charmed by you (your choice) until the end of your next turn. Any affected creature also has Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your breath weapon.</p><p>Once a creature succeeds on this save, it is Immune against this feature for the next 24 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5990dea6092d9b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Purity of Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are always under the effects of a Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/toxins/poison-bottle-corked-fire-green.webp","_id":"s59d470ecd5e5db0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Bane","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have survived the Hunter's Bane—a dangerous, long-guarded ritual that alters your life's blood, forever binding you to the darkness and honing your senses against it. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. The chosen ability score is your Hemocraft ability score, which represents how you make use of your dark gift. You can use this ability score in place of the usual one when you make Arcana, Religion, or Survival checks.</p><p>The Hunter's Bane also empowers your body to control and shape hemocraft magic, using your own blood and life essence to fuel your abilities. Some of your features require your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the feature's effects. The Saving Throw DC is calculated as follows:</p><p><b>Hemocraft save DC</b> = 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Hemocraft modifier (your choice between Intelligence or Wisdom)</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hand-claw-glow-orange.webp","_id":"s59e46b8c9231cca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Sabotage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Spell Susceptibility (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes against a spell until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Steal Resistance (Cost: 2d6).</strong> Choose one kind of damage. If the target has Resistance to that kind of damage, until the start of your next turn, the target loses that Resistance and you gain Resistance to that damage type.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5a14cc73dbee827","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Health","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine magic flowing through you makes you Immune to disease.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s5a5b76c4d9e1b18","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slippery Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you may use your Reaction to immediately teleport 30 feet to a place that you can see and attempt to hide.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5a72f03dd08dca4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ties That Bind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can temporarily tie your fate to others. As an Action, you can touch one object or creature and magically tie a strand of fate from yourself to it for 1 hour or until you use this feature again. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC to resist this effect. While the target is bound to you and on the same plane of existence as you, you can sense the direction to the target's location, and you know the direction of its movement if it is in motion.</p><p>In addition, once per turn when you cast a spell using a spell slot to deal damage or restore hit points to the target, roll a d6, and the target receives extra damage or healing, respectively, equal to the number rolled.</p><p>You can use this feature's action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5a8629f3983b0f9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Iron Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed your ability to resist the mind-altering powers of your prey. You gain Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws. If you already have this Proficiency, you instead gain Proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma Saving Throws (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5aa9712d17753c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Durability","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your toughness allows you to shrug off assaults that would devastate others.</p><p>Whenever you make a Saving Throw, roll 1d6 and add the die to your Saving Throw total. If applying this bonus to a death Saving Throw increases the total to 20 or higher, you gain the benefits of rolling a 20 on the d20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5aaddab47d61a9d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your animal-like swiftness or thick skin makes it more difficult to land a hit on you.</p><p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice when you get this feature) and your Constitution modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-green.webp","_id":"s5ae0b016e990fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animal Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use your magic to create a powerful bond with a creature of the natural world.</p><p>With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 50 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth an animal from the wilderness to serve as your faithful companion. You can select any beast of CR 1/2 or lower as your companion. However, your choices may be restricted depending on the area you currently find yourself in. Your DM determines if any such restrictions apply.</p><p>At the end of the 8 hours, your animal companion appears and gains all the benefits of your Companion's Bond ability. You can have only one animal companion at a time.</p><p>If your animal companion is ever slain, the magical bond you share allows you to return it to life. With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 25 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth your companion's spirit and use your magic to create a new body for it. You can return an animal companion to life in this manner even if you do not possess any part of its body.</p><p>If you use this ability to return a former animal companion to life while you have a current animal companion, your current companion leaves you and is replaced by the restored companion.</p><p>If you are small enough to ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can any of its actions during your turn or immediately after.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5ae939bc00260da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Champion's Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a second Reaction. Additionally, you make Initiative checks with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5b204660dbe2b1b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Smith Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Battle Smith Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Battle Smith Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Shield</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Branding Smite, Warding Bond</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Aura of Vitality, Conjure Barrage</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Aura of Purity, Fire Shield</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Banishing Smite, Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s5b3006fd2c40c1a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tooth and Tail","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal your choice of piercing or slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your fangs or tail to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/tail-swipe-green.webp","_id":"s5b3a2f96eaa84a3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Transmuter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to consume the reserve of transmutation magic stored within your transmuter's stone in a single burst. Once per Long Rest when you do so, choose one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>Major Transformation.</strong> You can transmute one nonmagical object—no larger than a 5-foot cube—into another nonmagical object of similar size and mass and of equal or lesser value. You must spend 10 minutes handling the object to transform it.</p><p><strong>Panacea.</strong> You remove all curses, diseases, and poisons affecting a creature that you touch with the transmuter's stone. The creature also regains all its hit points.</p><p><strong>Restore Life.</strong> You cast the Raise Dead spell on a creature you touch with the transmuter's stone, without expending a spell slot and without providing any components.</p><p><strong>Restore Youth.</strong> You touch the transmuter's stone to a willing creature, and that creature's apparent age is reduced by 3d10 years, to a minimum of 13 years. This effect doesn't extend the creature's lifespan and can be used no more than once on the same creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5bc9a5df543033c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Incarnate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Battle Tyrant.</strong> You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against any creature with the Frightened condition.</li><li><strong>Murderous Intent.</strong> When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for your Sneak Attack, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5be737cc70a613c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Conjuration Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Conjuration school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Conjuration school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5bf163dc124ea5d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428376,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s5c785258b91df52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Patient Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Disengage action as a Bonus Action. Alternatively, you can expend 1 Ki Point to take both the Disengage and the Dodge actions as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-glowing-blue.webp","_id":"s5cabc37e591bc42","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Erudite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your continued studies broaden your areas of expertise. Choose another skill as per your Scholar feature. Alternatively, you can choose to learn a new language.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-purple-glyph.webp","_id":"s5cbaa3817ee1417","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use yourself as a Spellcasting Focus and you can ignore verbal components for your wizard spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d00a2da7bcc77a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fool's Insight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to gather stories and lore gains a supernatural edge. You can cast detect thoughts up to a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier. You regain any expended uses of this ability after completing a Long Rest.</p><p>If a creature resists your attempt to probe deeper and succeeds at its Saving Throw against your detect thoughts, it immediately suffers an embarrassing social gaffe. It might loudly pass gas, unleash a thunderous burp, trip and fall, or be compelled to tell a tasteless joke.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d3609f22fcb77a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drakewarden Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Drakewarden Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Cause Fear</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dragon's Breath</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Elemental Bane</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Summon Dragon</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Any of these spells can be cast as if you were in the space of your drake companion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d3748f1d6bb166","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Among the Dead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Spare the Dying cantrip, which counts as a warlock cantrip for you. You also have Advantage on Saving Throws against any disease and poison.</p><p>Additionally, undead have difficulty harming you. If an undead targets you directly with an attack or a harmful spell, that creature must make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC (an undead needn't make the save when it includes you in an area effect, such as the explosion of Fireball). On a failed save, the creature must choose a new target or forfeit targeting someone instead of you, potentially wasting the attack or spell. On a successful save, the creature is Immune to this effect for 24 hours. An undead is also Immune to this effect for 24 hours if you target it with an attack or a harmful spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d5eaef0db1bc49","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sylvan Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your creature type is both humanoid and fey.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/fae-fairy-winged-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s5d73a0603b8d34b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Eldritch Invocation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d757e0fd9b29c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Devotion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Though the exact words and strictures of the Oath of Devotion vary, paladins of this oath share these tenets.</p><p><strong>Honesty.</strong> Don't lie or cheat. Let your word be your promise.</p><p><strong>Courage.</strong> Never fear to act, though caution is wise.</p><p><strong>Compassion.</strong> Aid others, protect the weak, and punish those who threaten them. Show mercy to your foes, but temper it with wisdom.</p><p><strong>Honor.</strong> Treat others with fairness, and let your honorable deeds be an example to them. Do as much good as possible while causing the least amount of harm.</p><p><strong>Duty.</strong> Be responsible for your actions and their consequences, protect those entrusted to your care, and obey those who have just authority over you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5df3319820a4b64","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428352,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Harvest's Scythe","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to unravel and harvest the life energy of other creatures. You can augment your spells to drain the life force from creatures. You have a pool of energy represented by a number of d10s equal to your druid level.</p><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can increase that damage by spending dice from the pool. You can spend a number of dice equal to half your druid level or less. Roll the spent dice and add them to the damage as necrotic damage. If you kill one or more hostile creatures with a spell augmented in this way, you or an ally of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you regains 5 hit points per die spent to increase the spell's damage.</p><p>You regain the expended dice when you finish a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Wildshape as an Action to regain a number of dice equal to half your Proficiency (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e161d9ce75c530","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Words of the First World","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to invoke primordial fey magic and direct it with your voice, be that song, poetry, or a recital of an ancient tale. You learn Sylvan. In addition, you gain the following options:</p><ul><li><strong>Curse of Ill Fortune.</strong> You can expend one of your Bardic Inspirations as a Bonus Action to curse a creature you can see within 60 feet with bad luck. The curse lasts until the start of your next turn or until you activate its effect as a Reaction.</li><li>Whenever the creature succeeds on a D20 Test, you can choose to force it to reroll the D20 and take the lower result.</li><li>Alternatively, if the creature is missed by an Attack Roll, you can immediately have the attacker reroll the D20 and take the higher result.</li><li><strong>Mantle of Midnight.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration to turn an ally you can see within 60 feet of yourself Invisible until the start of your next turn. The invisibility ends early if it attacks, casts a spell, or otherwise performs a hostile action.</li><li><strong>Tread the Unseen Path.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration and teleport yourself or an ally you can see within 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of the original position.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e419db54e0566e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Alleyways Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Alleyways Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Disguise Self, Expeditious Retreat, Detect Thoughts, Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Meld into Stone, Tongues</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Greater Invisibility, Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mislead, Passwall</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e51de237c6545f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189562,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutal Beating","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action and use your Sneak Attack, you can immediately make another attack. If the target is suffering from a condition, you can add half your Sneak Attack dice (rounded down) to that attack.</p><p>You also learn the following new way to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Stun (Cost: 6d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or become Stunned until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e5bbff36397729","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gather Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your expended elemental energy through focused meditation.</p><p>Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose to regain a number of kinesis points equal to half your kineticist level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a short rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"1","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/portal-vortex-orange.webp","_id":"s5e66fb4e04312dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lionhearted","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/lion-roar-yellow.webp","_id":"s5e8e5863ebaea93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Touch of Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your study of death allows you to extract vitality from another creature as it nears its demise. When you reduce a creature within 10 feet of you to 0 hit points, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier + your monk level (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5eabbe48aefde81","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428348,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swift as the Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your base walking increases to 35 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-swirl-gray-blue.webp","_id":"s5ead33c44765bd0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a draconic aspect, granting you physical traits such as scaled skin, vertical pupils, and sharp nails.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>As an Action, you can exhale destructive energy. All creatues in the area of effect take damage equal to a number of rolls of your Natural Weapons die equal to your Proficiency. The shape, Saving Throw, and damage type of your breath weapon is determined by your draconic form, which you choose when you gain this feature. You can find all available options in the table below. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Constitution modifier. Once you have used your breath weapon, you have to roll a d6 at the start of each of your turns. On a roll of 5 or 6, you regain your use of this feature.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, the size of your breath weapon doubles.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Character Advancement</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Dragon</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon Shape (Saving Throw)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Jabberwock</td><td>Fire</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Night</td><td>Force</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Shadow</td><td>Necrotic</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td><td>60x5 ft line (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Sylvan</td><td>Poison</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5eeb0b5aa7ca41a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Exorcist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You hone your hemocraft to tear corruption from the minds and bodies of your allies—and to punish those responsible for it. You gain the Blood Curse of the Exorcist for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["3d6","psychic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"wis","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/fear-fright-monster-grin-red-orange.webp","_id":"s5eeb527d5c7e69c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Defy Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If an ally that is currently affected by your Warcry is reduced to 0 hitpoints but not killed outright, it can spend hit dice up to a number equal to your Leadership ability modifier as if it had taken a rest. Any excess damage from the instance of damage that reduced the ally to 0 hitpoints is then subtracted from the regained hitpoints.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5eed99fb84ba644","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor Modifications","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your artificer infusions to specially modify your Arcane Armor. That armor now counts as separate items for the purposes of your Infuse Items feature: armor (the chest piece), boots, helmet, and the armor's special weapon. Each of those items can bear one of your infusions, and the infusions transfer over if you change your armor's model with the Armor Model feature. In addition, the maximum number of items you can infuse at once increases by 2, but those extra items must be part of your Arcane Armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/feet/boots-armored-banded-steel.webp","_id":"s5f056d520cc43f3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transmuter's Stone","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spend 8 hours creating a transmuter's stone that stores transmutation magic. You can benefit from the stone yourself or give it to another creature. A creature gains a benefit of your choice as long as the stone is in the creature's possession. When you create the stone, choose the benefit from the following options:</p><ul><li>Darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If the holder already has darkvision, its range increases by 60 feet.</li><li>An increase to Speed of 10 feet while the creature is unencumbered.</li><li>Proficiency in Constitution Saving Throws.</li><li>Resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (your choice whenever you choose this benefit).</li></ul><p>Each time you cast a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher, you can change the effect of your stone if the stone is on your person.</p><p>If you create a new transmuter's stone, the previous one ceases to function.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5f326c90c89058a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Druid Circle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose to identify with a circle of druids from the list of available circles. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s5f3846f48285260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Beauty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become an avatar of unearthly beauty. Your enemies attack with uncertainty, fearful of damaging the wondrous being they behold, while your magic draws upon your presence to augment its power.</p><p>As a Reaction, you can impose a penalty on a creature's attacks against you or on its Saving Throws against your spells and abilities. This benefit lasts until the end of the current turn The penalty equals your Charisma modifier (minimum 1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5f914329b605195","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fate's Right Hand","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the Raven Mother's power to curse a creature. You can cast Pale Knight's Portentous Premonition. After you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5f9f0b5294e8de8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can spend one use of your Wild Shape to empower your body with the might of the elements. Choose one of the following elements (air, earth, fire, water). Depending on your choice, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You gain a bonus to any Constitution Saving Throws you make to maintain Concentration on a spell. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</li><li>Once per turn when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can force the target creature and creatures of your choice within 10 feet of the target to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. A target takes damage equal to a number of D6 x 1/2 your proficiency (rounded down) on a failure, and half as much on a success. The damage type is determined by your chosen element, as per the table below. The number of damage dice are doubled on all affected targets if the original attack was a critical hit.</li><li>You gain one damage Resistance and an additional benefit based on your chosen element for the duration, as per the table below.</li></ul><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Element-specific Benefits</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Elemental</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Additional Benefit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Air</td><td>Lightning</td><td>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>Earth</td><td>Thunder</td><td>You reduce any bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage you take by an amount equal to your Proficiency.</td></tr><tr><td>Fire</td><td>Fire</td><td>The damage dice of your Elemental Might become D8s.</td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td>Cold</td><td>All space within a 10-feet Emanation is 3 for hostile creatures.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5fc0cd2cd4c0144","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428338,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frenzy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are raging, you can make one additional attack as part of your Attack action when you are using your Reckless attack class feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/anatomy-organ-heart-red.webp","_id":"s5fca8e04a75a140","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428321,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Sundering Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to channel destructive energy.</p><p>As an Action, you touch a creature or a an unattended object within reach. A creature must make a Constitution Saving Throw, taking 5 times your cleric level force damage on a failed Saving Throw and half as much on a successful one. An unattended object takes 5 times your cleric level force damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5fe09c16360ea44","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s5fe161a3af96494","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice) + your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"s604c4d58654b312","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428432,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Be like Water","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to embody the evershifting, ungraspable nature of your element.</p><p>When you are Grappled or Restrained on your turn, you can spend 5 feet of movement to no longer be Grappled or Restrained. You also gain blindsight in a 30 feet radius.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60660f645e854f8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s60794c4e8e8248c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hybrid Transformation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to control the lycanthropic curse that courses through your veins. As a Bonus Action, you transform into a special hybrid form for up to 1 hour. You can speak, use equipment, and wear armor while in this form, and can revert to your normal form as a Bonus Action. You automatically revert to your normal form if you fall unconscious or die.</p><p>This feature replaces the rules for lycanthropy in the Monster Manual. You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can expend a use of your Blood Maledict feature to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60884fe9f3b2c3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Formshift Damage to your weapon damage rolls even when not currently shifted. If you are shifted, this damage bonus is doubled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/tail-strike-bone-orange.webp","_id":"s60abd2d7ccf4829","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Leontari Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the battleaxe, longsword, greataxe, and greatsword.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/axes/axe-broad-grey.webp","_id":"s60e914fa0105f60","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Killing Bite.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can immediately make another attack with them as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Stronger Together.</strong> Allies within 20 feet of you also benefit from your Feral Resilience while you are not Unconscious.</li><li><strong>Feral Defiance.</strong> Your Ferocious Vitality recharges on a Short or a Long Rest and heals for 1x Shifter level additional hit points.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60f2dc44dc4517c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speech Beyond the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to reach beyond death's veil in search of knowledge. Using this feature, you can cast Speak with Dead without material components, and you understand what the target of this casting says. It can understand your questions, even if you don't share a language or it is not intelligent enough to speak.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6105ac5a64f429c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"s6132054d79bdf40","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428344,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Manifest Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can conjure forth the mind of your Awakened Spellbook. As a Bonus Action while the book is on your person, you can cause the mind to manifest as a Tiny spectral object, hovering in an unoccupied space of your choice within 60 feet of you. The spectral mind is intangible and doesn't occupy its space, and it sheds dim light in a 10-foot radius. It looks like a ghostly tome, a cascade of text, or a scholar from the past (your choice).</p><p>While manifested, the spectral mind can hear and see, and it has darkvision with a range of 60 feet. The mind can telepathically share with you what it sees and hears (no action required).</p><p>Whenever you use a spell scroll on your turn, you can cast it as if you were in the spectral mind's space, instead of your own, using its senses. To do so, you must have placed the scroll in your awakened spellbook.</p><p>The spectral mind stops manifesting if it is ever more than 300 feet away from you, if someone casts Dispel Magic on it, if the Awakened Spellbook is destroyed, if you die, or if you dismiss the spectral mind as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you conjure the mind, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of any level to conjure it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6181d40f42d0f83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two of your skill proficiencies, or one of your skill proficiencies and your Proficiency with thieves' tools. Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses either of the chosen proficiencies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"s61845395450cf08","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Terror of the Skies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion grows to Huge size and the reach of its bite attack increases to 15 feet, its Strength and Constitution also increase by 2, to a maximum of 22.</p><p>Additionally, the damage of its Breath Weapon increases to 10d6 and the cone size increases to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s61d49b1d64d3cca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Totem","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call forth nature spirits to influence the world around you. As a Bonus Action, you can magically summon an incorporeal spirit to a point you can see within 60 feet of you. The spirit creates an aura in a 30-foot radius around that point. It counts as neither a creature nor an object, though it has the spectral appearance of the creature it represents.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move the spirit up to 60 feet to a point you can see.</p><p>The spirit persists for 1 minute or until you're Incapacitated. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Wildshape (no action required) to regain a use of this feature. But you can not have more than one spirit totem active at the same time.</p><p>The effect of the spirit's aura depends on the type of spirit you summon from the options below.</p><p><strong>Bear Spirit.</strong> The bear spirit grants you and your allies its might and endurance. Each creature of your choice in the aura when the spirit appears gains temporary hit points equal to 5 + your druid level. In addition, you and your allies gain Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws while in the aura.</p><p><strong>Hawk Spirit.</strong> The hawk spirit is a consummate hunter, aiding you and your allies with its keen sight. When a creature makes an Attack Roll against a target in the spirit's aura, you can use your Reaction to grant Advantage to that Attack Roll. In addition, you and your allies have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks while in the aura.</p><p><strong>Unicorn Spirit.</strong> The unicorn spirit lends its protection to those nearby. You and your allies gain Advantage on all Ability Checks made to detect creatures in the spirit's aura. In addition, if you cast a spell using a spell slot that restores hit points to any creature inside or outside the aura, each creature of your choice in the aura also regains hit points equal to your druid level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s61d9adc85f78bce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nourishing Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your fire spells soothe and restore you. When you expend a spell slot to cast a spell that includes a fire damage roll, you regain hit points equal to the slot's level + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s61e8da3ac2e2317","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elder Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can imbue your Aura of Protection with primal power, granting the benefits below for 1 minute or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Diminish Defiance.</strong> Enemies in the aura have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your spells and Channel Divinity options.</li><li><strong>Regeneration.</strong> At the start of each of your turns, you regain 10 Hit Points.</li><li><strong>Swift Spells.</strong> Whenever you cast a spell that has a casting time of an Action, you can cast it using a Bonus Action instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62127d41aba8bae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supreme Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12.</p><p>If the healing formula of the spell involves a static number (beside your spellcasting ability modifier), you increase that number by half, rounded down.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s6240983ab9e7885","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Dancer's Fervor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spend one use of your Channel Divinity as part of the same Bonus Action you use to enter your Crescent Dance to enhance it further. Choose one of the following benefits. You gain the chosen benefit for the duration of your Crescent Dance.</p><p><strong>Dance Partner.</strong> You can cast Spiritual Weapon as part of the same Bonus Action if you know it, expending a spell slot as normal. If you do so, its damage die becomes a d12 and it critically hits on a 19 or 20.</p><p><strong>Grace.</strong> You add your Wisdom modifier to Dexterity Saving Throws and when you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half damage if you fail.</p><p><strong>Swiftness.</strong> Your Speed increases by an additional 10 feet and you don't provoke attacks of opportunity when you move out of an enemy's reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6262ee1d39eca4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Curse Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Bestow Curse spell prepared and it does not count against your Concentration limit, though the initial instance of the spell ends if you cast it again. If you fail a Concentration Saving Throw and you are currently concentrating on more than one spell, you lose concentration on both spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s627254a4f33bc9e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can form a telepathic connection between your mind and the mind of another. As a Bonus Action, choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. You and the chosen creature can communicate telepathically with each other while the two of you are within a number of miles of each other equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). To understand each other, you must both know at least one language.</p><p>The telepathic connection lasts for a number of minutes equal to your Warlock level. It ends early if you use this feature to connect with a different creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s627a59a2d018768","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428369,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undying Sentinel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points and not killed outright, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead, and you regain a number of Hit Points equal to three times your Paladin level. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Additionally, you can't be aged magically, and you cease visibly aging.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62a94a7896f4657","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Durable Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any creature that you summon or create with a conjuration spell has temporary hit points equal to twice your Wizard level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62b84d5ece31fc6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reveler","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Performance skill and one musical instrument of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/instruments/harp-gold-glowing.webp","_id":"s62e321cf89d39ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Animal Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You cannot be Surprised unless you are Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/humanoid-wolf-dog-blue.webp","_id":"s62f412ae934d571","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s638a3825f8e8809","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Hit Dice to regain hit points, you roll two D12s for each Hit Die and add them together. Any healing you regain through Hit Dice cannot be reduced in any way.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you score a critical hit with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you regain one expended use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-evil-horned-giant.webp","_id":"s63b4d9e5d602574","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Master's Odem","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you open a small portal and call upon the raw energy of your patron's powerful breath weapon.</p><p>Every creature in the area of effect, which originates from your position, has to make a Saving Throw against your spell save DC. A target takes 15d10 damage on a failed save, and half as much on a successful one. The shape, Saving Throw, and damage type of the breath weapon depends on your draconic patron.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Master's Odem</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Draconic Patron</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Jabberwock</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Night</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Shadow</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Sylvan</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s63f0d9b74c9a3f0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your familiar gains 1 additional hit point for each of your Witch levels and its AC increases by 2. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus in place of its own attack bonus and your spellcasting save DC in place of any DC for its features.</p><p>Your familiar's weapon attacks deal an additional 1d4 damage of a type determined by your chosen Wild Domain, as seen in the table below. This additional damage increases at 5th level (1d6), 11th level (1d8), and 17th level (1d10) in this class.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Familiar Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>Radiant</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s641b410cd9167f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shielding Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use your mastery of the storm to protect others. Each creature of your choice has the damage Resistance you gained from the Storm Soul feature while the creature is in your Storm Aura.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6452c0257dba7cd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silver Tongue","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master at saying the right thing at the right time. When you make a Charisma (Persuasion) or Charisma (Deception) check, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s647a40b64c867e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Jolt","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn new ways to channel arcane energy to harm or heal. When either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:</p><ul><li>The target takes an extra 2d6 force damage.</li><li>Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 hit points to it.</li></ul><p>You can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once on a turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"2d6","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-impact-shock-wave.webp","_id":"s64972774c469e93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428319,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Waves","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You no longer have need for weapons. You learn to throw your weight around with the might of the waves and your hands become instruments of Gargan's will - and with that, his crushing, inescapable grasp. You can roll a d8 in place of the normal damage of your Unarmed Strike. If you have both hands free or are attacking a target that you have Grappled, this die changes to a d12.</p><p>Additionally, you gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s64b403ca077df47","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Restore Balance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the plane of absolute order allows you to equalize chaotic moments. When a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself is about to roll a d20 with Advantage or Disadvantage, you can take a Reaction to prevent the roll from being affected by Advantage and Disadvantage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s64ba887548109a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Flesh of Stone","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can harden your body like stone, dampening the impact of most attacks until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Constitution modifier + your Charisma modifier and any bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing you take is reduced by an amount equal to half your kineticist level (rounded down), this reduction applies before any other effect.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s651381c6cbed14f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Second-Story Work","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've trained to get into especially hard-to-reach places, granting you these benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Climber.</strong> You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</li><li><strong>Jumper.</strong> You can determine your jump distance using your Dexterity rather than your Strength.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/settlement/stone-stairs.webp","_id":"s653a80d60bf6081","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You respond to danger with extraordinary vigilance. In combat, you get a special Reaction that you can take once on every creature's turn, except your turn. You can use this special Reaction only to make an Opportunity Attack, and you can't use it on the same turn that you take your normal Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s653a8d6c9d363ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transposition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to switch positions with your Eidolon if you can see it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6556482212efd89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Spirit Claw.</strong> When you are hidden, you ignore Immunity to the Lacerated condition and healing does not remove the Lacerated condition if it was applied by you unless the target was healed back to its hitpoint maximum. Additionally, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that are Lacerated.</li><li><strong>Feline Grace.</strong> No Attack Roll has Advantage against you and you cannot have Disadvantage on Dexterity Saving Throws and Ability Checks. You lose these benefits when you are Incapacitated or your Speed is 0.</li><li><strong>Killing Bite.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can immediately make another attack with them as a Bonus Action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s656bc1b214323c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Imposing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Intimidation skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"s65714314055574a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Predator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception and Stealth skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp","_id":"s6586fcaefd7f697","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Alchemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with the Alchemist's Supplies and you can use your hemocraft ability score to make ability checks with them. Additionally, you add your hemocraft modifier to the maximum number of potions you can have imbibed at the same time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s65a27b7c4cf8fc8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swim Speed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp","_id":"s663245f45cd26a6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Cycle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When Initiative is rolled, you enter one of the below Lunar Phases of your choice, as long as you are not wearing any armor or shield.</p><p>Each Lunar Phase has a passive and an active effect. You can trigger the active effect at the start of your turn (no action required). After you do so, you automatically enter the next Lunar Phase on the start of your next turn.</p><p>The order of Lunar Phases is New Moon -> Crescent Moon -> Full Moon, after which the cycle repeats.</p><p><strong>New Moon.</strong> You gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. If you activate this effect, you gain additional temporary hit points equal to twice your Witch level.</p><p><strong>Crescent Moon.</strong> Your Speed increases by 10 feet. If you activate this effect, your speed is doubled and you cannot be targeted by Attacks of Opportunity.</p><p><strong>Full Moon.</strong> Your melee weapon attacks deal additional 1d4 radiant damage. If you activate this effect, the radiant damage increases to 2d4.</p><p>The additional damage increases at 5th level (1d6/2d6), 11th level (1d8/2d8), and 17th level (1d10/2d10) in this class.</p><p>You lose the benefits of any Lunar Phase when you don armor or a shield.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s664649f01ff7dfe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Calm before the Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s66570ebb89dcaa3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unsettling Words","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spin words laced with magic that unsettle a creature and cause it to doubt itself. As a Bonus Action, you can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration and choose one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. Roll the Bardic Inspiration die. The creature must subtract the number rolled from the next Saving Throw it makes before the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s665e7a83399cbe7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nature's Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to diseases and the Poisoned condition, and you have Resistance to a damage type associated with your current land choice in the Circle Spells feature, as shown in the Nature's Ward table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Nature's Ward</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Land Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Arid</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Polar</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Temperate</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Tropical</td><td>Poison</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/flowers/lotus-pink.webp","_id":"s666dc882ff6798e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Illusions","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast Illusion spells without providing Verbal components, and if an Illusion spell you cast has a range of 10+ feet, the range increases by 60 feet.</p><p>You also know the Minor Illusion cantrip. If you already know it, you learn a different Wizard cantrip of your choice. The cantrip doesn't count against your number of cantrips known. You can create both a sound and an image with a single casting of Minor Illusion, and you can cast it as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6670c790a520698","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mindless Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can't be Charmed or Frightened while raging. If you are Charmed or Frightened when you enter your rage, the effect ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/toxins/cup-goblet-poisoned-spilled.webp","_id":"s66b0d9760619b45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes of the Dark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can see normally in darkness and dim light, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet.</p><p>You learn the Darkness spell, which doesn't count against your number of sorcerer spells known. In addition, you can cast it by spending 2 sorcery points or by expending a spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s67297a1fc70839c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428367,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fang and Claw","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal your choice of piercing or slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your fangs or claws to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blood-slash-foam-red.webp","_id":"s677bea89722bbeb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monastic Tradition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You commit yourself to a monastic tradition, chosen from the list of available traditions. Your tradition grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 11th, and 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s6780d225c0d26e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deadly Whispers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to lace your mind-affecting magic and weapons with deadly psychic energy.</p><p>When you deal psychic damage to a creature with a spell or hit it with a weapon attack, you can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration to deal an extra 2d6 psychic damage to that target. You can do so only once per turn.</p><p>The psychic damage increases when you reach certain levels in this class, increasing to 3d6 at 5th level, 5d6 at 10th level, and 8d6 at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6808b634b99ca04","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Companion's Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your animal companion gains a variety of benefits while it is linked to you.</p><p>The animal companion loses its Multiattack action, if it has one.</p><p>The companion obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own.</p><p>When using your Natural Explorer feature, you and your animal companion can both move stealthily at a normal pace.</p><p>Your animal companion has abilities and game statistics determined in part by your level. Your companion uses your Proficiency bonus rather than its own. In addition to the areas where it normally uses its Proficiency bonus, an animal companion also adds its Proficiency bonus to its AC and to its damage rolls.</p><p>Your animal companion gains Proficiency in two skills of your choice. It also becomes proficient with all Saving Throws.</p><p>For each level you gain after 3rd, your animal companion gains an additional hit die and increases its hit points accordingly.</p><p>Whenever you gain the Ability Score Improvement class feature, your companion's abilities also improve. Your companion can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or it can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, your companion can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature unless its description specifies otherwise.</p><p>Your companion shares your alignment, and has a personality trait and a flaw that you can roll for or select from the tables below. Your companion shares your ideal, and its bond is always, \"The ranger who travels with me is a beloved companion for whom I would gladly give my life.\"</p><p>Your animal companion gains the benefits of your Favored Enemy feature, and of your Improved Favored Enemy feature when you gain that feature at 6th level. It uses the favored enemies you selected for those features.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Companion Trait</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Trait</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>I'm dauntless in the face of adversity.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Threaten my friends, threaten me.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>I stay on alert so others can rest.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>People see an animal and underestimate me.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>I have a knack for showing up in the nick of time.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>I put my friends' needs before my own in all things.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Companion Flaw</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Flaw</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>If there's food left unattended, I'll eat it.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>I growl at strangers, and all people except my ranger are strangers to me.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Any time is a good time for a belly rub.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>I'm deathly afraid of water.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>My idea of hello is a flurry of licks to the face.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>I jump on creatures to tell them how much I love them.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6896efe39d19e72","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wyvern Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have undergone specialized training that allows you to bond with and ride a wyvern.</p><p>With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 50 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth a wyvern from the wilderness to serve as your faithful companion. See its game statistics in the accompanying Wyvern Companion stat block. You choose the damage type for its Draconic Blood feature.</p><p>At the end of the 8 hours, your Wyvern Companion appears and gains all the benefits of your Rider's Bond ability. You can have only one Wyvern Companion at a time.</p><p>If your Wyvern Companion is ever slain, the life bond you share allows you to return it to life. To do so you have to spend 1 hour, 25 gp worth of ingredients, and a use of your Second Wind or 2 of your Hit Dice to return it to life with a special ritual.</p><p>You can return your Wyvern Companion to life in this manner even if you do not possess any part of its body, but to do so you have spend double the required resources and the ritual instead requires 8 hours.</p><p>If you use this ability to return a former Wyvern Companion to life while you have a current Wyvern Companion, your current companion leaves you and is replaced by the restored companion.</p><p>You can mount your companion even if you are the same size. If you ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can use any of its actions during your turn or immediately after. While you ride it, your companion's flying speed is halved and it has to end its flying movement on the ground.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68aedca10f3e0b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 6)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68b2bc75f7af7c3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pyrokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Control Flames cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68ba40dbd62b5a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Dark Sisters Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Dark Sisters Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Bane, Dissonant Whispers, Arcane Rend, Blindness/Deafness</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dark Orb, Hunger of Hadar</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Doomtide, Greater Malison</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dominate Person, Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68bf1b80eddc0d0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Coordinated Takedown.</strong> When a creature within reach of your natural weapons is hit by a melee attack from one of your allies, you can use your Reaction to immediately force that creature to make a Strength Saving Throw as per your Fanged Aspect feature.</li><li><strong>Bolstering Barks.</strong> Whenever you use the Help action on one of your allies, they gain temporary hit points equal to half your Shifter level.</li><li><strong>Fierce Protector.</strong> When you hit a creature with your natural weapons, it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against creatures other than you until the end of your next turn while it is within your reach. If it makes an attack against a target other than you during that time, you have Advantage on your next Attack Roll against it and add half your Shifter level to the damage roll (rounded down).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68f0ef9a1466549","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Burning Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill and you can see in darkness as if it were bright light.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-eye.webp","_id":"s68fde9642bfac74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Exceptional Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Bonus Action to give magically allow your companion to act more swiftly. On its next turn, it can use its Bonus Action to use the Dash, Disengage, Dodge, or Help action (your choice).</p><p>Additionally, your companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6923d5bb60a98ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Thief","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Empower Sneak Attack, you can try to steal the knowledge of how to cast a spell from the caster. The DC equals 8 + your proficiency + your Intelligence. On a failed save, you negate the spell's effect, and you steal the knowledge of the spell. You can cast this spell once without expending a spell slot and without material components during the next 7 days. You can also cast it again by expending a number of uses of your Empower Sneak Attack equal to the spell's level. The original caster can't cast it until the 7 days have passed.</p><p>Once you have stolen a spell with this feature, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s693e8440045cd54","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reclaim Potential","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned to absorb the fleeting magic of your echo. When an echo of yours is destroyed by taking damage, you can gain a number of temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Constitution modifier.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s695a731e8dbf65d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Harm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use your ki to inflict wounds. When you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike, you can spend 1 ki point to deal extra necrotic damage equal to one roll of your Martial Arts die + your Wisdom modifier. You can use this feature only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6971d8f85f31cea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Radiant Sun Bolt","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hurl searing bolts of magical radiance.</p><p>When you make an Unarmed Strike, you can replace it with a ranged weapon attack with a range of 60 feet, which deals radiant damage equal to your Unarmed Strike.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s69820facf5ee804","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following two Channel Divinity options. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how Channel Divinity works.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-smoke-yellow.webp","_id":"s698b0d938436416","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you share with your drake creates a connection to dragonkind, granting you understanding and empowering your presence. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Thaumaturgy.</strong> You learn the Thaumaturgy cantrip, which is a ranger spell for you.</li><li><strong>Tongue of Dragons.</strong> You learn to speak, read, and write Draconic or one other language of your choice.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s69b3cf2f352f87f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sculpt Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can create pockets of relative safety within the effects of your evocations. When you cast an Evocation spell that affects other creatures that you can see, you can choose a number of them equal to 1 plus the spell's level. The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their saving throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-dripping-pseudopods-green.webp","_id":"s69c108c5c2fc97c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Duelist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you use your Sneak Attack, you can make another attack against the same target with a melee weapon you are holding, provided the target is within your reach and no other creatures are within 5 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s69c3a36788b8ba3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Peerless Skill","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Ability Check or Attack Roll and fail, you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration; roll the Bardic Inspiration die, and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning a failure into a success. On a failure, the Bardic Inspiration isn't expended.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s69e436fe74bca7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cauterizing Flames","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to turn death into magical flames that can heal or incinerate. When a Small or larger creature dies within 30 feet of you or your wildfire spirit, a harmless spectral flame springs forth in the dead creature's space and flickers there for 1 minute. When a creature you can see enters that space, you can use your Reaction to extinguish the spectral flame there and either heal the creature or deal fire damage to it. The healing or damage equals 2d10 + your Druid level.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6a2241a7423e33a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Ascendance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action you transform into an apparition of pure magic for 1 minute, gaining the following benefits. The transformation ends early if you die, you are Incapacitated, or if you end it as a Bonus Action. Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you spend 7 Sorcery Points (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p><ul><li><strong>Arcane Wellspring.</strong> During your turn, you can trade any number of your Hit Dice for the same number of Sorcery Points (no Action required).</li><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You gain a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover.</li><li><strong>Spell Avoidance.</strong> When you're subjected to a spell or magical effect that allows you to make a Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6a6cf519945eee7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Impel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to giant strength now allows you to hurl both allies and enemies on the battlefield. As a Bonus Action while raging, you can choose one Medium or smaller creature within your reach and move it to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) to avoid the effect.</p><p>If, at the end of this movement, the thrown creature isn't on a surface or liquid that can support it, the creature falls, taking damage as normal and landing Prone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6aaccd9c26d29ac","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Genie's Vessel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron gifts you a magical vessel that grants you a measure of the genie's power. The vessel is a Tiny object, and you can use it as a spellcasting focus for your warlock spells. You decide what the object is, or you can determine what it is randomly by rolling on the Genie's Vessel table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Genie's Vessel</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Vessel</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Oil lamp</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Urn</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Ring with a compartment</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Stoppered bottle</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Hollow statuette</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Ornate lantern</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>While you are touching the vessel, you can use it in the following ways:</p><p>The vessel's AC equals your spell save DC. Its hit points equal your warlock level plus your Proficiency bonus, and it is Immune to poison and psychic damage.</p><p>If the vessel is destroyed or you lose it, you can perform a 1-hour ceremony to receive a replacement from your patron. This ceremony can be performed during a Short or a Long Rest, and the previous vessel is destroyed if it still exists. The vessel vanishes in a flare of elemental power when you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6ab0b47a5a5b7c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Concentration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your aura of protection fosters mental focus. You and your allies have Advantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain Concentration while in your Aura of Protection.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6abea2f288b1438","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mimicry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can mimic sounds you have heard, including voices. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful Wisdom (Insight) check opposed by your Charisma (Deception) check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-call-sound-blue.webp","_id":"s6ad1da92db96751","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can weave magic around yourself for protection. When you cast an abjuration spell with a spell slot, you can simultaneously use a strand of the spell's magic to create a magical ward on yourself that lasts until you finish a Long Rest. The ward has a hit point maximum equal to twice your Wizard level plus your Intelligence modifier. Whenever you take damage, the ward takes the damage instead, and if you have any Resistances or Vulnerabilities, apply them before reducing the ward's hit points. If the damage reduces the ward to 0 Hit Points, you take any remaining damage. While the ward has 0 Hit Points, it can't absorb damage, but its magic remains.</p><p>Whenever you cast an Abjuration spell with a spell slot, the ward regains a number of Hit Points equal to twice the level of the spell slot. Alternatively, as a Bonus Action, you can expend a spell slot, and the ward regains a number of Hit Points equal to twice the level of the spell slot expended. Additionally, the ward regains hit points equal to your Proficiency every time you finish a Short Rest.</p><p>Once you create the ward, you can't create it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6ad32f28a8fe417","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428376,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your symbiotic link to fungus and your ability to tap into the cycle of life and death grants you access to certain spells. You learn the Chill Touch cantrip. At 3rd, 5th, 7th, and 9th level you gain access to the spells listed for that level in the Circle of Spores Spells table.</p><p>Once you gain access to one of these spells, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day. If you gain access to a spell that doesn't appear on the druid spell list, the spell is nonetheless a druid spell for you.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Circle of Spores Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Circle Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Blindness/Deafness, Gentle Repose</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Animate Dead, Gaseous Form</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Confusion</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cloudkill, Contagion</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-ice-teardrop.webp","_id":"s6ae01152a1989d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bonded familiar can now also use the special actions gained through your Witchcraft. This does not change the number of uses a given feature has or how many times it can affect the same creature.</p><p>Additionally, your bonded familiar now also adds your Proficiency to its AC.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6af1f1ecc488df4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battering Roots","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Tendrils of the World Tree extend from your melee weapons. While you wield any melee weapon, your reach with that weapon increases by 10 feet.</p><p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack while raging, you can use the Shove action against that same creature. You can count as Huge for the purpose of this Shove.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b01a11d8206a91","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Mystic Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack Action or use your Flurry of Blows, you can cast a spell in place of two of your Unarmed Weapon attacks. You can use this feature only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b2931f9139db28","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jungle Stalker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Survival skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-eyes-pink.webp","_id":"s6b4c6a25245b062","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutal Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you use Reckless Attack, you can forgo any Advantage on one Strength-based Attack Roll of your choice on your turn. The chosen Attack Roll mustn't have Disadvantage. If the chosen Attack Roll hits, the target takes an extra 1d10 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon or Unarmed Strike, and you can cause one Brutal Strike effect of your choice. You have the following effect options.</p><ul><li><strong>Forceful Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a STR Saving Throw or be pushed 15 feet straight away from you. You can then move up to half your Speed straight toward the target without provoking Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Hamstring Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a DEX Saving Throw or have its Speed reduced by 15 feet until the start of your next turn. A target can be affected by only one Hamstring Blow at a time—the most recent one.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"s6b5f040fe2e845b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Moonlight Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically transport yourself, reappearing amid a burst of moonlight. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, and you have Advantage on the next Attack Roll you make before the end of this turn.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also regain uses by expending a level 2+ spell slot for each use you want to restore (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b66c11fca8042c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortifying Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>15th-level ranger Beast Conclave feature (replaces Share Spells)</p><p>While your companion can see you, it has Advantage on all Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b780cf4e185c53","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Shape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of nature allows you to assume the form of an animal. As a Bonus Action, you shape-shift into a Beast form that you have learned for this feature (see \"Known Forms\" below). You stay in that form for a number of hours equal to half your Druid level or until you use Wild Shape again, have the Incapacitated condition, or die. You can also leave the form early as a Bonus Action.</p><ul><li><strong>Number of Uses.</strong> You can use Wild Shape twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li><li>You gain additional uses when you reach certain Druid levels, as shown in the Wild Shape column of the Druid Features table.</li><li><strong>Known Forms.</strong> You know four Beast forms for this feature, chosen from among Beast stat blocks that have a maximum Challenge Rating of 1/4 and that lack a Fly Speed (see appendix B for stat block options). The Rat, Riding Horse, Spider, and Wolf are recommended. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can replace one of your known forms with another eligible form.</li><li>When you reach certain Druid levels, your number of known forms and the maximum Challenge Rating for those forms increases, as shown in the Beast Shapes table. In addition, starting at level 8, you can adopt a form that has a Fly Speed.</li><li>When choosing known forms, you may look in the Monster Manual or elsewhere for eligible Beasts if the Dungeon Master permits you to do so.</li><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Beast Shapes</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Known Forms</th><th scope=\"col\">Max. CR</th><th scope=\"col\">Fly Speed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>1/4</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>1/2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>8</td><td>1</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><li><strong>Rules While Transformed.</strong> While in a form, you retain your personality, memories, and ability to speak, and the following rules apply:</li><ul><li><strong>Temporary Hit Points.</strong> When you assume a Wild Shape form, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to your Druid level.</li><li><strong>Game Statistics.</strong> Your game statistics are replaced by the Beast's stat block, but you retain your creature type; Hit Points; Hit Point Dice; Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; class features; languages; and feats. You also retain your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies and use your Proficiency Bonus for them, in addition to gaining the proficiencies of the creature. If a skill or Saving Throw modifier in the Beast's stat block is higher than yours, use the one in the stat block.</li><li>If you attack in this form, you can use your spell attack bonus instead of the form's attack bonus if it is higher. If the form has a special ability that requires a Saving Throw, you can use your spell save DC in place of the form's DC.</li><li><strong>No Spellcasting.</strong> You can't cast spells, but shape-shifting doesn't break your Concentration or otherwise interfere with a spell you've already cast.</li><li><strong>Objects.</strong> Your ability to handle objects is determined by the form's limbs rather than your own. In addition, you choose whether your equipment falls in your space, merges into your new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it's practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment based on the creature's size and shape. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with the form. Equipment that merges with the form has no effect while you're in that form.</li></ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.druid.wildshape","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s6b8077cd5422a0f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tempestuous Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>On your turn, you can cause whirling gusts of elemental air to briefly surround you, immediately before or after you cast a spell of 1st level or higher. Doing so allows you to Fly up to 30 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.</p><p>The Fly distance granted by this feature increases to 60 feet at 11th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6bea80143bfe436","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428366,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of the Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to lightning and thunder damage.</p><p>In addition, whenever you start casting a spell of 1st level or higher that deals lightning or thunder damage, stormy magic erupts from you. This eruption causes creatures of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of you to take lightning or thunder damage (choose each time this ability activates) equal to half your sorcerer level. You can deal this damage before, during, or after the movement granted by your Tempestuous Magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6bfce7a78052538","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rite Revival","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to protect your fading life by reabsorbing the energy you feed to your weapons. If you have one or more crimson rites active and you are reduced to 0 hit points but don't die outright, you can choose to have all your active crimson rites end and immediately regain hit points equal to twice your blood hunter level. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6c1d77a22a1538d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Prodigious Memory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The number of spells you can prepare is increased by half your wizard level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6c62ecd4eff7be4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swim Speed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp","_id":"s6c7c8babb30cfed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6c8d2bb62a3cb07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The information below details how you use those rules with Druid spells, which appear on the Druid spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two cantrips of your choice from the Druid spell list. Whenever you gain a Shifter level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the Druid spell list.</p><p>When you reach Shifter level 10, you learn another Druid cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Spring's Branch Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the Druid spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Shifter levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Spring's Branch Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the Druid spell list until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Shifter, your list of prepared spells can include five Druid spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Shifter level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Druid spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for your Druid spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use a Druidic Focus as a Spellcasting Focus for your Druid spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s6cb40251561ef1e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"High Elf Education","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Arcana skill and one more INT-based skill of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-purple-glyph.webp","_id":"s6cdd029a12fb315","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death's Friend","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your association with death has become so close that you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>When you use your Wails from the Grave, you can deal the necrotic damage to both the first and the second creature.</li><li>When you roll initiative, you regain one soul trinket.</li><li>You also ignore Resistance to necrotic damage from your Wails from the Grave feature and treat Immunity to it as Resistance instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d3bf013e969b45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Counter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to counterattack when your prey tries to sabotage you. If the target of your Slayer's Prey forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to make one weapon attack against the quarry. You make this attack immediately before making the Saving Throw. If your attack hits, your save automatically succeeds, in addition to the attack's normal effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d4b94304268788","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heir of Ruin","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are acclimatized to very hot regions as per the DMG.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-shield-barrier-steel.webp","_id":"s6d7f102e9f5b9a0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Knowledge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in another skill of your choice from the skill list available to Barbarians at level 1.</p><p>In addition, while your Rage is active, you can channel primal power when you attempt certain tasks; whenever you make an Ability Check using one of the following skills, you can make it as a Strength check even if it normally uses a different ability: Acrobatics, Intimidation, Perception, Stealth, or Survival. When you use this ability, your Strength represents primal power coursing through you, honing your agility, bearing, and senses.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/bull-head-horns-glowing.webp","_id":"s6d8f7dd72c06b19","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d93908f1193aca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead. Moreover, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s6dc6146742601c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
