{"name":"Hammering Blows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, if you hit a creature no more than one size larger than you with a melee weapon attack, you can use your Reaction or Bonus Action to use the shove action against that same creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-hammer-destructive-blue.webp","_id":"s6e041c09b3cd3c9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Warrior","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to draw on the energy of the multiverse to augment your attacks.</p><p>Once on your turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, all damage dealt by the attack becomes force damage, and the creature takes an extra 1d8 force damage from the attack. When you reach 11th level in this class, the extra damage increases to 2d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6e058540dc6c375","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Advanced Transformation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to unleash and control more of the beast within. Your hybrid form also gains the following additional benefit.</p><p><strong>Lycan Regeneration.</strong> At the start of each of your turns in your hybrid form when you have at least 1 hit point, you regain hit points equal to your hemocraft die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6e2fe78191d5407","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ritual Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast any spell as a Ritual if that spell has the Ritual tag and the spell is in your spellbook. You needn't have the spell prepared, but you must read from the book to cast a spell in this way.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/star-yellow.webp","_id":"s6e473ffc9846072","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s6e80bb333c67ed3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unleash Incarnation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can heighten your echo's fury. Whenever you take the Attack action, you can make one additional melee attack from the echo's position.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6eb78f6a51b89eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice.</p><p><strong>Superiority Dice.</strong> You have four superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a superiority die (no action required).</p><p><strong>Using Superiority Dice.</strong> You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Precision Attack.</strong> When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can expend one Superiority Die, roll that die, and add it to the Attack Roll, potentially causing the attack to hit.</li><li><strong>Monster's Bane.</strong> When you damage a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the damage roll. You can use this ability after rolling damage. If the attack causes the target to make a Constitution Saving Throw to maintain Concentration, it has Disadvantage on that save.</li><li><strong>Hunter's Resilience.</strong> When you fail an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma Saving Throw, you can expend one superiority die to add it to the roll, possibly turning the failure into a success.</li><li><strong>Hunter's Knowledge.</strong> When you make a check that allows you to apply your Proficiency in Arcana, Insight, Religion, Perception, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add the number rolled on the superiority die to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6ecd3a75643498b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428343,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wails from the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As you nudge someone closer to the grave, you can channel the power of death to push them over the threshold or harm someone else as well. When you deal your Sneak Attack damage to a creature on your turn, you can cause that creature to take additional damage. Alternatively, you can target a second creature that you can see within 30 feet of the first creature. Roll half the number of Sneak Attack dice for your level (round up), the original target or the second creature takes necrotic damage equal to the roll's total, as wails of the dead sound around them for a moment.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6f20008a79338ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Knight Conclave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6f356c177933672","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Favored Enemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become more adept at fighting your favored foes. Choose a second creature type as favored enemy. Your damage bonus against all your favored enemies increases to +4. Additionally, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against the spells and abilities used by a favored enemy.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp","_id":"s6f3d969b366fe10","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Whispers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you cloak yourself in dark magic that preys upon the instinctual fears of your foes. When you use this feature, you can designate any number of creatures to be unaffected by it. The effect lasts for 1 hour or until you are Incapacitated or dismiss this effect as a Bonus Action.</p><p>When a creature sees you while you are under this effect, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a success, the creature becomes Immune to this feature for the next 24 hours. A creature that is Immune to the Frightened condition is unaffected by this feature.</p><p>On a failure, the creature's enchanted subconscious forces it to ignore you, to the point it denies your existence altogether. You are automatically treated as Hidden from the creature for the duration. All memories of you while affected by this feature are likewise suppressed, even after the effect ends.</p><p>If the creature is in Combat with you, it can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6f48f093a742c78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack Action on your turn, you can replace one of the attacks with a casting of one of your Sorcerer cantrips that has a casting time of an Action.</p><p>Any feature that increases the damage die size of your Unarmed Attack also increases the size of one of your damaging cantrips' dice by the same number of steps. For the purposes of this feature, the initial effect of your Martial Arts feature counts as one step, as do any further increments acquired through Monk levels. This feature has no effect when you are wielding a weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6f7ac5b6add76cc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Sister's Scorn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 60 feet hits you or your bonded familiar with an attack or forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to curse that creature. The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it is subject to one of the effects of the Bestow Curse spell until the start of its next turn.</p><p>If the target is already under the effect of Bestow Curse, it stacks with this feature as long as you choose a different curse effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6fff004298e9681","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tempered Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to sword magic gives you extra fortitude. Your hit point maximum increases by 1, and it increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>As an Action, you can gain a base AC of 10 + your Constitution modifier + your Charisma modifier if you aren't wearing armor. This effect lasts until you end it as a Bonus Action or you don armor other than a shield.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7031382cf191543","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Backalley Education","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are proficient in your choice of two of the following skills: Acrobatics, Deception, Stealth, and Sleight of Hand. Alternatively, you can replace one of these choices with Proficiency with thieves' tools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/shadow-stealth-eyes-purple.webp","_id":"s70f4bab58d336eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Intimidation or Persuasion skill (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s71010bcd9030197","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weakening Hex","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you apply your Hexblade's Curse to a creature, it also has Disadvantage its next Saving Throw before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7133b79c9bb5827","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Omens and Portents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can perceive signs of the future in everyday objects and events, such as flights of birds or ripples made in water by a thrown stone. You can cast the Augury spell without expending a spell slot and, when you cast the spell in this way, the spell has no verbal, somatic, or material components. Once you cast the spell in this way, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, until you finish a Long Rest, when you cast a divination spell that includes a chance the DM gives you no answer or a random reading—such as augury, commune, or divination—reduce that chance by 25 percent.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s71d0964155ba5ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Phenomenon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your lunar phase magic bursts. As a Bonus Action, you can tap into a special power of the lunar phase you are currently in. Alternatively, as part of the Bonus Action you take to change your lunar phase using your Waxing and Waning feature, you can immediately use the power of the lunar phase you are entering:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon:</strong> You radiate intense moonlight for a moment. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC or be Blinded until the end of its next turn. In addition, one creature of your choice in that area regains 3d8 hit points.</li><li><strong>New Moon:</strong> You momentarily emanate an oppressive gloom. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take 3d10 psychic damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. In addition, you become Invisible until the end of your next turn, or until you make an attack or cast a spell.</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon:</strong> You slip through light and darkness. You can magically teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet of yourself. In addition, you also gain Resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Once you use a phase's Bonus Action, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s71fbfb3138a5883","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement (Level 13)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature four times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"s723db0e3f058861","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summoner's Guardian","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your improved connection with your Eidolon allows it to defend you more effectively. You can use your Bonus Action to command your Eidolon to take a guarding stance while it is within 5 feet of you.</p><p>The stance lasts until the start of your next turn. It ends early if your Eidolon is no longer within 5 feet of you or it is Incapacitated.</p><p>While the stance is active, all Attack Rolls that target you have Disadvantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-golem-stone-blue.webp","_id":"s7247809f3c9b162","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two ability scores from Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution. The chosen ability scores and their maximums increase by 2.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"s726dd8063020011","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sea Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Sea Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Create Or Destroy Water, Fog Cloud, Mirror Image, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Wall of Water, Tidal Wave</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Control Water, Watery Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Elemental Spirit, Maelstrom</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s729e94937bfe7b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You augment your martial prowess with the ability to cast spells. The information below details how you use those rules with Cleric spells, which appear on the Cleric spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two cantrips of your choice from the Cleric spell list. Whenever you gain a Warlord level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the Cleric spell list.</p><p>When you reach Warlord level 10, you learn another Cleric cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Crusader Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the Cleric spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Warlord levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Crusader Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the Cleric spell list until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Warlord, your list of prepared spells can include five Cleric spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Warlord level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Cleric spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Your Leadership ability is your spellcasting ability for your Cleric spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Holy Symbol as a Spellcasting Focus for your Cleric spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s730a2846667b9d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Eidolon can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s731444e5bfddb3c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428445,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to harness sunlight, banishing darkness and dealing radiant damage to your foes.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol, and any magical darkness within 30 feet of you is dispelled. Additionally, each hostile creature within 30 feet of you must make a Constitution Saving Throw. A creature takes radiant damage equal to 2d10 + your cleric level on a failed Saving Throw, and half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that has total cover from you is not affected.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7316f3091ceb9a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grave Touched","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron's powers have a profound effect on your body and magic, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Arcane Necrosis.</strong> Whenever you cast a spell or hit a creature with an attack roll and deal Necrotic damage, the damage dealt ignores Resistance to Necrotic damage.</li><li>Additionally, once per turn when you cast a spell that deals damage while using your Form of Dread, you can change that spell's damage type to Necrotic.</li><li><strong>Undead Endurance.</strong> You don't gain Exhaustion levels from dehydration, malnutrition, or suffocation. In addition, you don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s73364be9c50ed7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Leadership ability modifier to your initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d10","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-spiral.webp","_id":"s733f9dfa90405f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428448,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Infusion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Intelligence or Charisma modifier (your choice) to your Eidolon's damage rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/tail-strike-bone-orange.webp","_id":"s7355dde054b5fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Charm Animals and Plants","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to charm animals and plants.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol and invoke the name of your deity. Each beast or plant creature that can see you within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. If the creature fails its Saving Throw, it is Charmed by you for 1 minute or until it takes damage. While it is Charmed by you, it is friendly to you and other creatures you designate.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7475c56d96b1685","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dedicated Crafter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in one tool of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/hammer-sledge-steel-grey.webp","_id":"s74b17b1413ee078","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Harness Divine Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend a use of your Channel Divinity to fuel your spells. As a Bonus Action, you touch your holy symbol, utter a prayer, and regain one expended spell slot, the level of which can be no higher than half your Proficiency bonus (rounded up). The number of times you can use this feature is based on the level you've reached in this class: 3rd level, once; 7th level, twice; and 15th level, thrice. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"s74cff080ed57e77","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428435,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rune Carver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a Long Rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Runes Known</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Number of Runes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>10th</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>15th</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The following runes are available to you when you learn a rune. If a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a Saving Throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.</p><h5>Cloud Rune</h5><p>This rune emulates the deceptive magic used by some cloud giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks and Charisma (Deception) checks.</p><p>In addition, when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to invoke the rune and choose a different creature within 30 feet of you, other than the attacker. The chosen creature becomes the target of the attack, using the same roll. This magic can transfer the attack's effects regardless of the attack's range. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Fire Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic channels the masterful craftsmanship of great smiths. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses your Proficiency with a tool.</p><p>In addition, when you hit a creature with an attack using a weapon, you can invoke the rune to summon fiery shackles: the target takes an extra 2d6 fire damage, and it must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw or be Restrained for 1 minute. While Restrained by the shackles, the target takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, banishing the shackles on a success. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Frost Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic evokes the might of those who survive in the wintry wilderness, such as frost giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Animal Handling) checks and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action to increase your sturdiness. For 10 minutes, you gain a +2 bonus to all Ability Checks and Saving Throws that use Strength or Constitution. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Stone Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic channels the judiciousness associated with stone giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks, and you have darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.</p><p>In addition, when a creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to invoke the rune and force the creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. Unless the save succeeds, the creature is Charmed by you for 1 minute. While Charmed in this way, the creature has a Speed of 0 and is Incapacitated, descending into a dreamy stupor. The creature repeats the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Hill Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic bestows a resilience reminiscent of a hill giant. While wearing or carrying an object that bears this rune, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Poisoned, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action, gaining Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage for 1 minute. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Storm Rune</h5><p>Using this rune, you can glimpse the future like a storm giant seer. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks, and you can't be Surprised as long as you aren't Incapacitated.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action to enter a prophetic state for 1 minute or until you're Incapacitated. Until the state ends, when you or another creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to cause the roll to have Advantage or Disadvantage. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s74f92bb2d4f4d67","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slow Metabolism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A day's worth of food or rations lasts you twice as long and you retain the benefits of full meals for an additional day.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/arrows-circling-pink.webp","_id":"s7542cc9106d4255","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blade-tip-chipped-blood-red.webp","_id":"s7570d60cf42bd73","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Conquest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A paladin who takes this oath has the tenets of conquest seared on the upper arm.</p><p><strong>Douse the Flame of Hope.</strong> It is not enough to merely defeat an enemy in battle. Your victory must be so overwhelming that your enemies' will to fight is shattered forever. A blade can end a life. Fear can end an empire.</p><p><strong>Rule with an Iron Fist.</strong> Once you have conquered, tolerate no dissent. Your word is law. Those who obey it shall be favored. Those who defy it shall be punished as an example to all who might follow.</p><p><strong>Strength Above All.</strong> You shall rule until a stronger one arises. Then you must grow mightier and meet the challenge, or fall to your own ruin.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7575f69d388feec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 4 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75772701056ca6a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with three skills of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s75b42dbe5ad5339","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wind Walker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the wind allows you to move freely through the air. You gain a Fly Speed equal to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s76bb572c12e2187","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expanded Spell List","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron lets you choose from an expanded list of spells. When you gain access to a new pact magic spell level, you can select one of the options listed for your patron. You learn that spell and it does not count against the number of warlock spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Archfey Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Faerie Fire, Sleep</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Calm Emotions, Phantasmal Force</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Blink, Plant Growth</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Dominate Beast, Greater Invisibility</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Celestial Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Cure Wounds, Guiding Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Flaming Sphere, Lesser Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Daylight, Revivify</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Guardian of Faith, Wall of Fire</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Dragon Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Cause Fear, Command</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Darkvision, Dragon's Breath</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Counterspell, Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Elemental Bane, Spell Turning</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fathomless Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Create Or Destroy Water, Thunderwave</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Gust of Wind, Silence</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Lightning Bolt, Sleet Storm</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Control Water, Summon Elemental (Water only)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fiend Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Burning Hands, Command</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Blindness/Deafness, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fireball, Stinking Cloud</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Fire Shield, Wall of Fire</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Genie Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Detect Evil and Good, Sanctuary (Dao), Thunderwave (Djinni), Burning Hands (Efreeti), Fog Cloud (Marid)</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Phantasmal Force, Spike Growth (Dao), Gust of Wind (Djinni), Scorching Ray (Efreeti), Blur (Marid)</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Create Food and Water, Meld into Stone (Dao), Wind Wall (Djinni), Fireball (Efreeti), Sleet Storm (Marid)</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Phantasmal Killer, Stone Shape (Dao), Greater Invisibility (Djinni), Fire Shield (Efreeti), Control Water (Marid)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Great Old One Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Dissonant Whispers, Tasha's Hideous Laughter</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Detect Thoughts, Phantasmal Force</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Clairvoyance, Sending</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Dominate Beast, Evard's Black Tentacles</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hexblade Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Shield, Wrathful Smite</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Blur, Branding Smite</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Blink, Elemental Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Phantasmal Killer, Staggering Smite</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Kraken Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Thunderwave, Create Or Destroy Water</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Augury, Gust of Wind</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Call Lightning, Water Breathing</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Evard's Black Tentacles, Control Water</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Spider Queen Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Faerie Fire, Jump</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Darkness, Web</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fear, Vampiric Touch</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Dimension Door, Giant Insect</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Raven Mother Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>False Life, Sanctuary</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Silence, Spiritual Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Feign Death, Speak with Dead</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Ice Storm, Death Ward</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Seeker Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Feather Fall, Jump</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Levitate, Locate Object</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Clairvoyance, Sending</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Arcane Eye, Locate Creature</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Undead Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>Bane, False Life</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Blindness/Deafness, Phantasmal Force</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Phantom Steed, Speak with Dead</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Death Ward, Greater Invisibility</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Undying Expanded Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>False Life, Ray of Sickness</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Blindness/Deafness, Silence</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Feign Death, Speak with Dead</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Aura of Life, Death Ward</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/encase-creature-monster-hold.webp","_id":"s76dd35dd803f77b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Cannon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to create a magical cannon. Using woodcarver's tools or weaponsmith's tools, you can take an Action to magically create a Small or Tiny eldritch cannon in an unoccupied space on a horizontal surface within 5 feet of you. A Small eldritch cannon occupies its space, and a Tiny one can be held in one hand.</p><p>Once you create a cannon, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or until you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. You can have only one cannon at a time and can't create one while your cannon is present.</p><p>The cannon is a magical object. Regardless of size, the cannon has an AC of 18 and a number of hit points equal to five times your artificer level. It is Immune to poison damage and psychic damage, and all conditions. If it is forced to make an Ability Check or a Saving Throw, treat all its ability scores as 10 (+0). If the Mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. It disappears if it is reduced to 0 hit points or after 1 hour. You can dismiss it early as an Action.</p><p>When you create the cannon, you determine its appearance and whether it has legs. You also decide which type it is, choosing from the options on the Eldritch Cannons table. On each of your turns, when you take your Action, you can cause the cannon to activate if you are within 60 feet of it and fire at the closest hostile creature. Alternatively, you can use your Bonus Action to designate the target creature manually. As part of the same Bonus Action, you can direct the cannon to walk or climb up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space, provided it has legs.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Eldritch Cannons</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cannon</th><th scope=\"col\">Activation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Flamethrower</td><td>The cannon exhales fire in an adjacent 15-foot cone that you designate. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d8 fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.</td></tr><tr><td>Force Ballista</td><td>Make a ranged spell attack, originating from the cannon, at one creature or object within 120 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 force damage, and if the target is a creature, it is pushed up to 5 feet away from the cannon.</td></tr><tr><td>Protector</td><td>The cannon emits a burst of positive energy that grants itself and each creature of your choice within 10 feet of it a number of temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/artillery/cannon-engraved.webp","_id":"s76f83a6b6e3c2db","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Strength and Constitution scores increase by 2, up to a maximum of 22.</p><p>In addition, you can now use Jotun Rage twice between rests, but no more than once on a turn. If you use that feature while under its effects, its increases to your size, hit points, reach, and Speed are cumulative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s775da004c8679dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher that deals fire damage or it fails a save against such a spell, you also set it aflame.</p><p>A creature that is aflame takes fire damage equal to twice your Proficiency at the start of each of its turns and sheds bright light in a radius of 10 feet and dim light light in a radius of 10 feet beyond that for 1 minute.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature can make a DEX Saving Throw against your spell save DC to end the effect on itself. Alternatively, it or another creature can spend an Action to put out the flames.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s77674ffd6f34101","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Savage Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you score a critical hit with a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice (and only the weapon's own damage dice) again and add the result to the total.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-purple.webp","_id":"s779dc5e43a82edb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (6th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 6th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p><p>At higher levels, you gain more warlock spells of your choice that can be cast in this way: one 7th-level spell at 13th level, one 8th-level spell at 15th level, and one 9th-level spell at 17th level. You regain all uses of your Mystic Arcanum when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-black-grey.webp","_id":"s77b307447d2e113","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inescapable End","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The cleric's ability to channel negative energy becomes more potent. Necrotic damage dealt by the character ignores Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s77de93e4d9f3f61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Charger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can run down your foes, whether you're mounted or not. If you move at least 10 feet in a straight line right before attacking a creature no more than 1 size larger than you (or your mount if you're mounted) and you hit it with the attack, that target takes additional damage equal to half your fighter level and must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be knocked Prone. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s77f60483beabb3e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tinker's Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Mending cantrip.</p><p>As a Magic action while holding Tinker's Tools, you can create one item in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of yourself, choosing the item from the following list:</p><ul><li>Ball Bearings</li><li>Basket</li><li>Bedroll</li><li>Bell</li><li>Blanket</li><li>Block and Tackle</li><li>Bottle, Glass</li><li>Bucket</li><li>Caltrops</li><li>Candle</li><li>Crowbar</li><li>Flask</li><li>Grappling Hook</li><li>Hunting Trap</li><li>Jug</li><li>Lamp</li><li>Manacles</li><li>Net</li><li>Oil</li><li>Paper</li><li>Parchment</li><li>Pole</li><li>Pouch</li><li>Rope</li><li>Sack</li><li>Shovel</li><li>Spikes, Iron</li><li>String</li><li>Tinderbox</li><li>Torch</li><li>Vial</li></ul><p>The item lasts until you finish a Long Rest, at which point it vanishes.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"you must be holding Tinker's Tools"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-offering-ritual.webp","_id":"s781bfdfac57f9fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frigid Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Frost Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Cold damage.</li><li><strong>Hunter's Rime.</strong> When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d6 Cold damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn. This extra damage ignores Resistance to Cold damage. When you reach Ranger level 11, this extra damage increases to 2d6.</li><li>A creature that took damage from this feature cannot use the Dash or Disengange Actions until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s782664a2139e17d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Power of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a magical benefit based on a totem animal of your choice. You can choose the same animal you selected previously or a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7840b5230df5ad6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Close-Quarters Shooting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to handle yourself in close combat. Making a ranged Attack Roll while within 5 feet of an enemy doesn't impose Disadvantage on your roll.</p><p>In addition, if you hit a creature within 5 feet of you with a ranged attack on your turn, that creature can't take Reactions until the end of this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78458abbf72fe8a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed when you are shifted, but you have to end your flying movement on the ground.</p><p>Additionally, you gain Resistance to the damage type associated with your Draconic Form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s784ba41e87088a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gravity Well","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to manipulate gravity around a living being: whenever you cast a spell on a creature, you can move the target up to 10 feet to an unoccupied space of your choice if the target is willing to move, the spell hits it with an attack, or it fails a Saving Throw against the spell.</p><p>Upon reaching 10th level in this class, the maximum distance you can move a creature in this manner increases to 20 ft.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s785582ea7fc2f87","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes of Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your eyes begin to glow with your inner fire, giving you a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, your darkvision instead increases by 60 feet.</p><p>In addition, fire and smoke caused by fire cannot obscure your vision.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78d6f5b6287ca98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an enemy you can see ends its turn within 5 feet of you, you can take a Reaction and expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration to move up to half your Speed. Then one ally of your choice within 30 feet of you can also Speed up to half their Speed using their Reaction.</p><p>None of this feature's movement provokes Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78e845b0aa7f095","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scion of the Depths","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron accepts you into his inner court of servitors. You gain the ability to breathe water, and a Swim Speed equal to your normal Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>You gain Immunity to lightning damage. When your Immunity reduces damage from an effect to 0, as a Reaction you can cause creatures of your choice that you can see within 30 ft. of you to take lightning damage equal to your Charisma modifier + your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7952ebdcca4a1ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bond of Fang and Scale","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you share with your drake intensifies, protecting you and stoking the drake's fury. When you summon your drake, it grows wings on its back and gains a Fly Speed equal to its Speed.</p><p>In addition, while your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Drake Mount.</strong> The drake grows to Large size. Its Hit Points increase by 1 for each of your levels in this class.</li><li><strong>Elemental Infusion.</strong> The drake's Bite and Elemental Bolt attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence and counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> You gain Resistance to the damage type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7953d62ea28a075","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Noble Bearing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-peace-alliance.webp","_id":"s7978f1a701e5e01","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kensai Kai","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to infuse your monk weapons with some of your Ki, making them even more deadly. Your critical range with your monk weapons increases by 1.</p><p>Additionally, when you deal damage with a monk weapon, you can spend 1 Ki Point to deal additional damage equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s797f5677f3ea957","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 8)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s79832867357169c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428450,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mark of the Ordning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class. These spells depend on your chosen giant heritage, as shown in the tables below. The spells count as sorcerer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Cloud Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Silent Image, Invisibility, Warding Wind</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Gaseous Form, Major Image</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Greater Invisibility, Hallucinatory Terrain</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Control Winds, Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fire Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Catapult, Enhance Ability, Heat Metal</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Elemental Weapon, Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fabricate, Fire Shield</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Creation, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Frost Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Frost Fingers, Hold Person, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm, Summon Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fire Shield, Ice Storm</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Bigby's Hand, Cone of Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hill Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Longstrider, Earthbind, Protection from Poison</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Create Food and Water, Erupting Earth</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Locate Creature, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Destructive Wave, Tree Stride</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Stone Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Id Insinuation, Sleep, Calm Emotions, Suggestion</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Enemies Abound, Meld into Stone</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Stoneskin, Stone Shape</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Modify Memory, Wall of Stone</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Storm Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Identify, Witch Bolt, Detect Thoughts, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Clairvoyance, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Divination, Storm Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Scrying, Legend Lore</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7994916243cae89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Light Steps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You make any stealth check that is contingent on not being heard rather than not being seen with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-sandals-tan.webp","_id":"s79a97d95448c3d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-axe-blood-red.webp","_id":"s79afd7928f7862c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a number of superiority dice equal to half your maximum (rounded down)</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a03fded292adf3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428343,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rite Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your weapon becomes a conduit for the power of your pact with your chosen patron. While you have an active crimson rite, you can use your weapon as a spellcasting focus for your warlock spells, and you gain a specific benefit based on your chosen pact.</p><p><strong>The Archfey.</strong> Once on your turn, when you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you can expend one use of your Blood Maledict to force the creature to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your hemocraft save DC. On a failure, the creature casts dim light in a 10 feet radius and cannot benefit from being Invisible until the end of your next turn. Additionally, Attack Rolls against the creature have Advantage for the duration.</p><p><strong>The Dragon.</strong> When you activate your Crimson Rite, you can change the damage type of your rite to that associated with your draconic patron (as per the warlord dragon patron's Draconic Arcana feature). Additionally, you gain blindsight out to a range of 10 ft. </p><p><strong>The Celestial.</strong> As a Bonus Action or as part of the same Bonus Action used to activate your Crimson Rite, you expend one use of your Blood Maledict feature to heal one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. That creature regains a number of hit points equal to one roll of your hemocraft die + your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p><strong>The Fathomless.</strong> You can breathe underwater. Additionally, you suffer no Disadvantage on melee weapon attacks for fighting underwater and, once per turn when you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you can reduce that creature's Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>The Fiend.</strong> While using the Rite of the Flame, your hemocraft die increases by 1 step for the purposes of dealing damage with your weapon. Additionally, the damage from this rite ignores Resistance to fire damage.</p><p><strong>The Genie.</strong> As a Bonus Action or as part of the same Bonus Action used to activate your Crimson Rite, you expend a use of your Blood Maledict feature to give yourself a Fly Speed of 30 feet, which lasts for a number of rounds equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of 1 round).</p><p><strong>The Great Old One.</strong> When you score a critical hit against a creature, that creature and any other creatures of your choice within 10 feet of it are Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>The Hexblade.</strong> When you attack a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite and the target is under a curse effect (such as the Hex or Bane spell or a blood curse), your crit range against that target increases by 1 step.</p><p><strong>The Kraken.</strong> You can breathe underwater and suffer no Disadvantage on melee weapon attacks for fighting underwater. Additionally, you gain darkvision with a range of 30 feet. If you already have darkvision, its range increases by 30 feet.</p><p><strong>The Spider Queen.</strong> Once on your turn, when you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you can expend one use of your Blood Maledict to force the creature to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your hemocraft save DC. On a failure, the creature is Poisoned until the end of your next turn. This feature ignores Immunity to the poisoned condition.</p><p><strong>The Raven Mother.</strong> A shadowy spirit appears on your shoulder. The spirit assumes the form and game statistics of a raven, and it always obeys your commands, which you can give telepathically. The spirit disappears if it is more than 100 feet from you, but can be resummoned onto your shoulder as a Bonus Action as long as your Crimson Rite is active. The spirit is incorporeal and cannot physically interact with anything except you. It is Immune to all damage and conditions.</p><p>While the raven is perched on your shoulder, you gain darkvision with a range of 30 feet and a bonus to your passive Wisdom (Perception) score and to Wisdom (Perception) checks. The bonus equals your Hemocraft modifier.</p><p><strong>The Seeker.</strong> When a creature you can see within 10 feet damages you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to expend one use of your Blood Maledict to deal radiant damage to the attacker. The damage equals one roll of your hemocraft die + your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p><strong>The Undead.</strong> When you take necrotic damage, you can use your Reaction to halve that damage. In addition, your appearance changes to reflect some aspect of your patron while you have any crimson rite active.</p><p><strong>The Undying.</strong> When you reduce a hostile creature to 0 hit points, you regain a number of hit points equal to one roll of your hemocraft die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a0695f2bf268c3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428329,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Battle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to the Frightened condition and you gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a26eef20f439aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline (Level 11)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 3 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a29b9be0fd4b68","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Season","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you or your bonded familiar awaken the power of your chosen season in a 30-feet radius sphere around a point you can see within 60 feet, affecting creatures of your choice in the area in the following ways for 1 minute.</p><p>Either of you can dismiss this effect as a Bonus Action and only one instance of the effect can be active at a time.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> An affected creature regains additional hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier when healed.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> An affected creature that starts its turn in the area or enters it for the first time on turn, its Speed is increased by 10 feet. Additionally, the area is brightly lit. This light counts as sunlight.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Healing on affected creatures is halved.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> The area is 3 for affected creatures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a55d3a9ec295bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Blades","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manifest your psionic power as shimmering blades of psychic energy. Whenever you make a weapon attack, you can manifest a psychic blade from your free hand and make the attack with that blade. This magic blade is a simple melee weapon with the finesse and thrown properties. It has a normal range of 60 feet and no long range, and on a hit, it deals psychic damage equal to your Psionic Energy Die plus the ability modifier you used for the Attack Roll. The blade vanishes immediately after it hits or misses its target, and it leaves no mark on its target if it deals damage.</p><p>After you attack with the blade, you can make a melee or ranged weapon attack with a second psychic blade as a Bonus Action on the same turn, provided your other hand is free to create it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a9a5de0cd1c612","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Meditation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the power granted by the Hunter's Bane to rapidly heal your wounds. If you spend 10 uninterrupted minutes in meditation, you can spend a number of Hit Dice up to your Proficiency as if you had taken a Rest. You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7aa6336054d9465","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Argent Conjunction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can choose to gain the effects of all Lunar Phases at the same time (no action required). If you choose to activate the effect of a Lunar Phase, you likewise trigger the active effects of all Lunar Phases.</p><p>You can use this feature twice and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ab3cc689856806","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel the souls of your ancestors into your physical form. When you start casting a sorcerer spell on your turn and expend a spell slot, you can increase your size by one category—from Medium to Large, for example.</p><p>This increase lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you die or are Incapacitated. Until it ends, you enjoy the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your current hit points and your hit point maximum both increase by 1 per sorcerer level.</li><li>Your reach increases by 5 feet.</li><li>Your Speed increases by 5 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</li><li>If you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can shove or grapple that creature as part of the same attack.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you spend 4 sorcery points to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ab7aaafaf73fae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to psychic damage and your features ignore Resistance to psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ac1cfbe67ecac7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through the vagaries of fate, your own study of the supernatural, or other circumstances you have come into contact with a mystical force or great entity whom you are sworn to serve. As a proxy and teacher, you are provided with a constant companion in the form of a bonded familiar.</p><p>This familiar takes the form of a beast, celestial, elemental, fiend, plant, or undead of CR 0, which you choose. It uses the corresponding statblock of the creature, but uses your proficiency bonus and mental ability scores in place of its own. In addition to its own, it also shares your saving throw proficiencies and any of your skill proficiencies that use Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. For each level in this class, it also gains 4 additional hit points. When you finish a Short or Long Rest, your bonded familiar regains all its hit points.</p><p>Your bonded familiar can understand and speak all languages you speak. While it is on the same plane of existence as you, you can communicate with it telepathically.</p><p>Your bonded familiar acts independently of you, but it always obeys your commands. In combat, it rolls its own initiative and acts on its own turn.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can shunt your bonded familiar into a safe pocket dimension. You can recall it to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you in the same manner.</p><p>Should your bonded familiar die, you can resummon it with a special ritual that takes 10 minutes. Alternatively, you can resummon it as an Action by spending a spell slot of 1st level or higher.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ac2d9ec6141ea7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gnome Cunning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all INT, WIS, and CHA Saving Throws against magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s7ad8dd53d6ad12b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lore Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Arcana, Deception, History, Insight, Intimidation, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Performance, Persuasion, Religion, Survival.</p><p>Alternatively, you may replace a chosen skill with one of the following tools: Alchemist's Supplies, Cook's Utensils, Enchanter's Supplies, Herbalist's Kit, Poisoner's Kit, or Tinkerer's Tools.</p><p>If you are already proficient in a chosen skill or tool, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p><p>Additionally, you can use Intelligence for skill checks with a chosen skill or tool if it normally uses a different ability score.</p><p>You can choose two additional skills or tools for this feature when you reach 10th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7af346d5f395d11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add Symbol to your spellbook and it doesn't count against the number of prepared spells for you. When you cast the spell, you can choose a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier. The chosen creatures are exempt from the spell's effect when it is triggered.</p><p>Additionally, you can cast the spell without a spell slot and without material components. You cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7b1317904ec3538","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Stalker's Ambush.</strong> Any attack with your natural weapons against a creature that is Surprised has Advantage and adds an additional roll of your Natural Weapons die to the damage.</li><li><strong>Swift Climber.</strong> You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and when you take fall damage, you can use your Reaction to decrease that damage by an amount equal to five times your Shifter level.</li><li><strong>Feral Pounce.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and your attack hits, you can force the target to make a Strength Saving Throw if it is no more than one size larger than you. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target is knocked Prone.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7b86b7ecacb7788","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If a creature has a Bardic Inspiration die from you and casts a spell that restores hit points or deals damage, the creature can roll that die and choose a target affected by the spell. Add the number rolled as a bonus to the hit points regained or the damage dealt. The Bardic Inspiration die is then lost.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-firefly-hand-yellow.webp","_id":"s7b9c930422454d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar of the Extraplanar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain expertise in Arcana and two additional languages.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"s7bb72f3282e840e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thrill of Victory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally that you can see within 60 ft of you and that can see or hear you, reduces a creature to 0 hitpoints, it can immediately regain a hit die. This feature has no effect if you're incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7c5e135d190cc1b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The study of runes has enabled you to wield primordial magic. Your knowledge of these runes is stored in your spellbook, though you determine the runes' cosmetic appearance. You can invoke these runes in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Rune of Renewal.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature regains hit points equal to your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier and you removal all poisons and diseases affecting it.</li><li><strong>Rune of Destruction.</strong> When you cast a spell that deals damage, you can add your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of that spell and change its damage type to force.</li><li><strong>Rune of Protection.</strong> When a creature you can see within 60 feet has to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to give it a bonus to that roll equal to your Intelligence modifier.</li><li><strong>Rune of Clarity.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature is under the effect of the Detect Magic and Comprehend Languages spells for the next 24 hours.</li></ul><p>You can invoke each rune once. When you finish a Short Rest, you can choose one rune and regain its use. When you finish a Long Rest, you regain the use of all runes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7c8c1806de4c709","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Resilience of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every time you cast a Witch spell of 1st level or higher, your bonded familiar gains temporary hit points equal to four times the spell's level.</p><p>Additionally, you and your bonded familiar gain Resistance to the same damage type gained through the Battle Familiar feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7c9858491908077","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aerokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Gust cantrip, which you can cast using only its somatic component.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ca4852b2c07da1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Warrior Scholar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in Arcana. When you use your Lay on Hands, the target also can immediately repeat a Saving Throw against one on-going spell effect on it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7d195ac5e7012a9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thunderbolt Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal lightning or thunder damage to a Large or smaller creature, you can also push it up to 10 feet away from you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7e8ccc42ad62215","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summoner's Call","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to call your Eidolon to your side. It appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you that you can see.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7eb3eaa41afcf23","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earthen Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your connection to earth to meld slightly into stone and earthen surfaces, granting you a Climb Speed equal to your Speed when climbing such surfaces.</p><p>Additionally, when you have to make a Strength Saving Throw or check, you can make a Charisma Saving Throw or check instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7eb91ff1e4ace4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes of the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to occasionally sense the presence of the undead, whose existence is an insult to the natural cycle of life. As an Action, you can open your awareness to magically detect undead. Until the end of your next turn, you know the location of any undead within 60 feet of you that isn't behind total cover and that isn't protected from divination magic. This sense doesn't tell you anything about a creature's capabilities or identity.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ebe2e2372989f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Feat of Strength","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to enhance your physical might. When you fail an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw using Strength, you can use your Channel Divinity to gain a +10 bonus to the roll. Alternatively, when a creature within 30 feet of you fails an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw using Strength, you can use your Reaction to grant that creature a +10 bonus to the roll, using your Channel Divinity. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the roll succeeds or fail.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ec02abf33bf93b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Foreknowledge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you magically expand your mind to the possibilities of the future. For 1 hour, you have Advantage on D20 Tests. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of this feature by expending a level 7+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ece644507c2879","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (d10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d10s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7f0434c7d8dca25","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Treachery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A paladin who embraces the Oath of Treachery owes allegiance to no one. There are no tenets of this oath, for it lacks any substance. Those who are unfortunate enough to have close contact with blackguards have observed that a blackguard's overwhelming concern is power and safety, especially if both can be obtained at the expense of others.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7f463be4be6b89a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divination Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Divination school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Divination school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7f5ed0b4bc11bb7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428376,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Friendly Face","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/commoner.webp","_id":"s7fa36c0a4884bcc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Student of the Divine","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Religion skill. If you are already proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7fd797edaa51c9f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You radiate a soothing, unseeable aura in a 30-foot Emanation that originates from you. The aura is inactive while you have the Incapacitated condition.</p><p>All allied creatures in the aura are Immune to the Frightened condition. If a Frightened ally enters the aura, that condition has no effect on that ally while there.</p><p>Any hostile creature in the aura that targets you or your allies with an attack or other harmful effect takes psychic damage equal to half your cleric level (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7fdd188fa077afd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"There and Back Again","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to speak, read, and write Sylvan. You make Pathfinding checks in the Feywild with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ffa0baea54bebf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bounding Leap","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make a jump, you can use your Dexterity score in place of your Strength score to determine the distance you can cover. Additionally, the distance for your Long Jump is increased by 10 feet and by 5 feet for your High Jump. This bonus distance is halved when you make either jump as standing jump.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/arrow-upward-blue.webp","_id":"s802c77738b15250","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hydrosophic Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to summon up your water-based defenses at a split-second's notice.</p><p>When you are hit by an attack or subject to an effect that forces you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to create a shield of water around you, granting yourself half-cover until the start of your next turn.</p><p>This cover applies even when against effects that normally ignore cover.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8041468fd0cdeec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dazzling Footwork","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Dance Virtuoso.</strong> You have Advantage on any Charisma (Performance) check you make that involves you dancing.</li><li><strong>Unarmored Defense.</strong> Your base Armor Class equals 10 plus your Dexterity and Charisma modifiers.</li><li><strong>Agile Strikes.</strong> When you expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration as part of an Action, a Bonus Action, or a Reaction, you can make one Unarmed Strike as part of that action, Bonus Action, or Reaction.</li><li><strong>Bardic Damage.</strong> You can use Dexterity instead of Strength for the Attack Rolls of your Unarmed Strikes. When you deal damage with an Unarmed Strike, you can deal Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Dexterity modifier, instead of the strike's normal damage. This roll doesn't expend the die.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8044aa1a445de3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Viper's Venom","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you damage a creature with a weapon affected by your Rite of the Viper, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Hemocraft save DC. You can force a creature to make this Saving Throw only once per turn.</p><p>On a failure, a target is Poisoned for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turn, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s80532eb3516b3f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a special kind of Blindsight with a radius of 120 feet. This Blindsight only functions against creatures with blood.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s806786e6927607b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Menacing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Intimidation skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/water-elemental-blue-teeth.webp","_id":"s80ca50b21f64fc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to cast spells. The information below details how you use those rules as an Arcane Trickster. The information below details how you use those rules with Wizard spells, which appear on the Wizard spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know three cantrips: Mage Hand and two other cantrips of your choice from the Wizard spell list.</p><p>Whenever you gain a Rogue level, you can replace one of your cantrips, except Mage Hand, with another Wizard cantrip of your choice.</p><p>When you reach Rogue level 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Arcane Trickster Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of 1st+ Level.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 Wizard spells.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Rogue levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Arcane Trickster Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Wizard spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the Arcane Trickster Spellcasting table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Rogue, your list of prepared spells can include five Wizard spells of level 1 or 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Rogue level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Wizard spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for your wizard spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a Spellcasting Focus for your Wizard spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s80d60a1efc7661c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shield of the Faithful","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Shield of Faith spell prepared.</p><p>You can cast it without Concentration and without expending a spell slot. You can do so a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and regain all expended uses on Long Rest. You can also restore a use by expending a level 2+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s80f8d92e343a7ac","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mote of Potential","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you give a creature a Bardic Inspiration die, you can utter a note from the Song of Creation to create a Tiny mote of potential, which orbits within 5 feet of that creature. The mote is intangible and invulnerable, and it lasts until the Bardic Inspiration die is lost. The mote looks like a musical note, a star, a flower, or another symbol of art or life that you choose.</p><p>When the creature uses the Bardic Inspiration die, the mote provides an additional effect based on whether the die benefits an Ability Check, an Attack Roll, or a Saving Throw, as detailed below:</p><ul><li><strong>Ability Check.</strong> When the creature rolls the Bardic Inspiration die to add it to an Ability Check, the creature can roll the Bardic Inspiration die again and choose which roll to use, as the mote pops and emits colorful, harmless sparks for a moment.</li><li><strong>Attack Roll.</strong> Immediately after the creature rolls the Bardic Inspiration die to add it to an Attack Roll against a target, the mote thunderously shatters. The target and each creature of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take thunder damage equal to the number rolled on the Bardic Inspiration die.</li><li><strong>Saving Throw.</strong> Immediately after the creature rolls the Bardic Inspiration die and adds it to a Saving Throw, the mote vanishes with the sound of soft music, causing the creature to gain temporary hit points equal to the number rolled on the Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s810908e9061d274","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature three times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"s810fad0302fd904","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Aura","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emanate a stormy, magical aura while you rage. The aura extends 10 feet from you in every direction, but not through total cover.</p><p>Your aura has an effect that is active for the duration of your rage, and an additional empowered effect.</p><p>You can empower your aura only once per rage.</p><p>Choose blaze, thunderstorm, or blizzard. Your aura's effect depends on your choice, as detailed below. You can change this choice whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>If your aura's effects require a Saving Throw, the DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8142071a84fab6c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rite of the Viper","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Rite of the Viper as part of your Crimson Rite feature. When you activate the Rite of the Viper, the extra damage dealt by your rite is poison damage and weapons affected by it have their crit range increased by 1 and their reach increased by 5 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8149f91142c07d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428329,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twinkling Constellations","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The constellations of your Starry Form improve. The 1d8 of the Archer and the Chalice becomes 2d8, and while the Dragon is active, you have a Fly Speed of 20 feet and can hover.</p><p>Moreover, at the start of each of your turns while in your Starry Form, you can change which constellation glimmers on your body.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s816b25fff8c9c5b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits while shifted:</p><ul><li>Your can increase your size to Huge and your Natural Weapons die is tripled for calculating your base weapon damage. If you lack the room to become Huge, your size doesn't change.</li><li>You can't be Charmed or Frightened. If you are Charmed or Frightened when you use Formshift, the effect is suspended for the duration of the shift.</li><li>The healing gained from your Ferocious Vitality feature is increased to 5x your Shifter level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"s816bedfba59ca9b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swarmkeeper Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Mage Hand cantrip if you don't already know it. When you cast it, the hand takes the form of your swarming nature spirits.</p><p>You also learn an additional spell of 1st level or higher when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Swarmkeeper Spells table. Each spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Swarmkeeper Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Faerie Fire</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Web</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Gaseous Form</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Arcane Eye</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s81bcb0c200376ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dragon Wings","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to sprout a pair of dragon wings from your back, gaining a Fly Speed equal to your current Speed. You can create these wings as a Bonus Action on your turn. They last until you dismiss them as a Bonus Action on your turn.</p><p>You can't manifest your wings while wearing armor unless the armor is made to accommodate them, and clothing not made to accommodate your wings might be destroyed when you manifest them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/wing-batlike-white-blue.webp","_id":"s81be58b16e99940","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tumbling Fool","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master a variety of acrobatic techniques that allow you to evade danger. As a Bonus Action, you can tumble. When you tumble, you gain the following benefits for the rest of your turn:</p><ul><li>You gain the benefits of taking the Dash and Disengage actions.</li><li>You gain a Climb Speed equal to your current Speed.</li><li>You take half damage from falling.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s81deb92d271090b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roguish Archetype","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an archetype that you emulate in the exercise of your rogue abilities from the list of available archetypes. Your archetype choice grants you features at 3rd level and then again at 9th, 13th, and 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-robe-evil-power.webp","_id":"s81ec1acf81c29ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Elemental Smite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose the patron of your oath from Dao, Djinni, Efreeti, or Marid. Whenever you use Divine Smite, you can invoke the effect corresponding to your patron.</p><ul><li><strong>Dao's Crush.</strong> The target has to make a Strength Saving Throw or be Restrained for 1 minute. On its turn, the target can make a Strength check against your Spell Save DC to end the effect.</li><li><strong>Djinni's Escape.</strong> You teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself and take on a mist-like form, which lasts until the end of your next turn. While in this form, you have Immunity to the Grappled, Prone, and Restrained conditions.</li><li><strong>Efreeti's Fury.</strong> The target takes additional fire damage equal to a number of D8s x 1/2 your Proficiency (rounded down). Any die size increment to your Divine Smite also affects this feature. The target is then set ablaze for 1 minute. While under this effect, the target takes fire damage equal to 2 x your Proficiency at the start of each of its turns. At the end of any of its turns, it can make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC to end the effect.</li><li><strong>Marid's Surge.</strong> The target and each creature of your choice in a 10-foot Emanation originating from you makes a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature is pushed 15 feet straight away from you and has the Prone condition.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8201b5d9ddf62eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic-User's Nemesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to thwart someone else's magic. When you see a creature casting a spell or teleporting within 60 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to try to magically foil it. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or its spell or teleport fails and is wasted. If the target is also the quarry of your Slayer's Prey, then you subtract a d6 from its Saving Throw.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you spend a 3rd-level slot or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8225366503f0069","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to become the centerpiece of a fighting unit and direct others to fight more effectively. Choose an ally within 60 feet that can see or hear you and isn't incapacitated and select one of the options below. You can use any number of the listed options on the same ally or divide them up between multiple allies.</p><ul><li>On your turn, you can use your Bonus Action to give the target an additional Bonus Action on their next turn. Alternatively, the target can use its Reaction to use this Bonus Action immediately.</li><li>You can use your Reaction to give the target an additional Reaction until the start of your next turn. This Reaction cannot be used on the same turn as their normal Reaction.</li><li>On your turn, you can subtract a multiple of 5 from your Speed and add the amount to the target's Speed for its next turn. The amount of Speed the target gains in this manner cannot be higher than its base Speed. This feature has no effect on a target whose Speed is currently 0. You can choose multiple targets. If you do so, you have to divide the amount you subtract among the targets in multiples of 5. Any one of the targets can choose to use their Reaction to move up to the Speed gained in this manner immediately. This movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks. If it does not use up all Speed gained in this manner, it loses the rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/infantry-army.webp","_id":"s8229c310e283d23","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Occult Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can cast the Nondetection spell, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability. When you do so, you can target only yourself, and the duration increases to 7 days.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s822b9e7aeb1a656","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s824bb6e597a10c7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visions of the Future","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your knowledge of the future allows you to guide an individual to achieve their greatest possible success. You can cast the Foresight spell once without expending a spell slot. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s827b944c48beb26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animal Speaker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At 3rd level when you adopt this path, you can cast the Beast Sense and Speak with Animals spells, but only as rituals. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s828e07077c85ab4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Watcher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in arcana, insight, or perception. When you use your Lay on Hands, the target also has half cover until the start of your next turn while it is within 5 feet of you and you aren't Incapacitated. Starting at 7th level, it gains this benefit while within your Aura of Protection.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s82badb9aaa0c657","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428357,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Resilient Survivor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a bonus to your Constitution Saving Throws equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s82d40e12651ae0f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hold Breath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hold your breath for up to 10 minutes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/water-iceberg-bubbles.webp","_id":"s83a15feb86afff7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Elf Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All Dark Elves enjoy the protection of their patron goddess. Excepting the cantrip, you can cast the following spells once per Long Rest without expending material components. Your spellcasting ability for these spells is WIS or CHA (your choice). You can also cast them using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p><p>Dancing Lights, Sanctuary, Healing Spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s83a26390cbfaaba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic in the Blood","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Arcana check, you can use your Charisma in place of your Intelligence for it.</p><p>Additionally, you learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the Sorcerer or Wizard spell list. A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Sorcerer Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s83b0ffee2341175","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with alchemist's supplies. If you already have this Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"s83c8511f8ea9c05","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189465,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mystical touch can mend wounds. As an Action, you can spend 1 ki point to touch a creature and restore a number of hit points equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die + your Wisdom modifier.</p><p>When you use your Flurry of Blows, you can replace one of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of this feature without spending a ki point for the healing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s842a80ecf9f8005","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supernatural Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain extra resilience against your prey's assaults on your mind and body. Whenever the target of your Slayer's Prey forces you to make a Saving Throw or Ability Check, add 1d6 to your roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s842e5f641c33ea5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Phoenix Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Phoenix Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Cure Wounds, Lesser Restoration, Aganazzar's Scorcher</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Revivify, Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fire Shield, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Greater Restoration, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8450674564f216b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Like a Fish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your attunement to the element of water allows you to move within it just as easily as on land. You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed and you can breathe underwater. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>Additionally, you make any Athletics checks and Saving Throws related to swimming or resisting water-based effects using your Charisma modifier instead of your Strength modifer.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8455e9ccfcbeb46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fancy Footwork","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to land a strike and then slip away without reprisal. During your turn, if you make a melee attack against a creature, that creature can't make Opportunity Attacks against you for the rest of your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s845f91e73e1aa8b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Explosive Cannon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every Eldritch Cannon you create is now more destructive. You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Detonate.</strong> When your cannon takes damage, you can take a Reaction to command the cannon to detonate if you are within 60 feet of it. Doing so destroys the cannon and forces each creature within 20 feet of it to make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 3d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p><strong>Firepower.</strong> The cannon's damage rolls and the number of Temporary Hit Points granted by Protector increase by 1d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":20,"width":null,"units":"ft","type":"sphere"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["3d10","force"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"dex","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/explosion-fireball-large-red-orange.webp","_id":"s8499178ee4b99ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expanded Element","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use another element or expand your understanding of your own element. You learn the damage types, cantrip, and elemental defense of that elemental school and you quality for all elemental infusions that have that elemental school as prerequisite.</p><p>This also allows you access to powerful composite kinetic shape, by either combining two different elements or focusing on a single one. You gain another element at 14th level, but you can't choose the same element a third time.</p><p>Using a composite shape requires a great deal of energy and costs 2 kinesis points each time. If you do so, increase the number of dice for that kinetic shape by half (rounded up).</p><p>If your composite shape features two of the same element, you double your Charisma modifier when determining the kinetic shape damage and the cost for using a composite shape is reduced to 1 kinesis point.</p><p>You also gain access to whatever infusion any of the included elements normally would allow, but you do pay their kinesis point cost as normal.</p><p>When you do combine elements with different damage types, half of the total damage is dealt as either damage type. For example, if you use a composite shape of the water and fire elements and roll for a total of 20 damage, 10 damage will be dealt as bludgeoning and 10 as fire.</p><p>If the damage number is uneven, you determine which damage type deals the higher amount.</p><p>You can find a table with the resulting composite elements below:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Composite Elements</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">\\</th><th scope=\"col\">Air</th><th scope=\"col\">Earth</th><th scope=\"col\">Fire</th><th scope=\"col\">Water</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Air</td><td>Storm</td><td>Sand</td><td>Plasma</td><td>Blizzard</td></tr><tr><td>Earth</td><td>Sand</td><td>Metal</td><td>Magma</td><td>Mud</td></tr><tr><td>Fire</td><td>Plasma</td><td>Magma</td><td>Blue Fire</td><td>Steam</td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td>Blizzard</td><td>Mud</td><td>Steam</td><td>Frost</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-smoke-pink.webp","_id":"s84b24e05edb8438","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aspect of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a magical benefit based on the totem animal of your choice. You can choose the same animal you selected at 3rd level or a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s84b58fbdc69ed93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s84b6e1c9b53dc71","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animating Performance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can animate one Large or smaller nonmagical item within 30 feet of you that isn't being worn or carried.. The animate item uses the Dancing Item stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB). The item is friendly to you and your companions and obeys your commands. It lives for 1 hour, until it is reduced to 0 hit points, or until you die.</p><p>In combat, the animated item shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the animated item's.</p><p>When you use your Bardic Inspiration feature, you can command the item as part of the same Bonus Action you use for Bardic Inspiration.</p><p>Once you animate an item with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use this feature again. You can have only one item animated by this feature at a time; if you use this action and already have a dancing item from this feature, the first one immediately becomes inanimate.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s853bd47a3cc193a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Cantrips","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Sacred Flame and Light cantrips. They count as warlock cantrips for you, but they don't count against your number of cantrips known.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s854ce5b03608b91","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Boons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Lunar phases influence your metamagic. Each lunar phase is associated with spells of the following schools of magic:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon.</strong> Abjuration and conjuration spells</li><li><strong>New Moon.</strong> Evocation and necromancy spells</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon.</strong> Divination and transmutation spells</li></ul><p>Whenever you use Metamagic on a spell from the Lunar Spells table or a spell of a school of magic associated with the lunar phase you are in, you can reduce the sorcery points spent by 1 (minimum 0). You can reduce the sorcery points spent for your Metamagic a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s857512c469ffd59","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fleet Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take a Bonus Action other than Step of the Wind, you can also use Step of the Wind immediately after that Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s857fef239aaa90a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Conclave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose to emulate the ideals and training of a ranger conclave from the list of available conclaves. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 5th, 7th, 11th, and 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8590206aaefdd9b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Plane Charter Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach an Artificer level specified in the Plane Charter Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Plane Charter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>Faerie Fire, Guiding Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Locate Object, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Blink, Clairvoyance</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Dimension Door, Locate Creature</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Scrying, Teleportation Circle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s85b3eb06cc223e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Seasons Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a season. At each indicated Witch level, add the corresponding listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Spring Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Goodberry, Healing Word, Healing Spirit, Lesser Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Mass Healing Word, Plant Growth</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Aura of Purity, Conjure Woodland Beings</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Greater Restoration, Raise Dead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Summer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Color Spray, Entangle, Heat Metal, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Fireball, Haste</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Aura of Life, Death Ward</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dawn, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Autumn Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Witch Bolt, Death Armor, Warding Wind</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Call Lightning, Thunder Step</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Storm Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Enervation, Jallarzi's Storm of Radiance</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Winter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Ice Knife, Rime's Binding Ice, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Glacial Spike, Sleet Storm</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Dream</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s85dc17c81e87651","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Fortitude","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can spend any number of sorcery points to roll a d4 for each point expended. You gain a number of temporary hit points equal to the total rolled + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s85e0152a85b502e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Devotion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you can't be Charmed while you are conscious.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"s85e8db74cc59e20","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persistent Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can regain all expended uses of Rage. After you regain uses of Rage in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, your Rage is so fierce that it now lasts for 10 minutes without you needing to do anything to extend it from round to round. Your Rage ends early if you have the Unconscious condition (not just the Incapacitated condition) or don Heavy armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"s8620054d6dc6993","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt an avian aspect, granting you physical traits such as the piercing eyes of a bird of prey, sharp nails, and wings sprouting from your back.</p><p>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. If you are not shifted, you have to end your flying movement on the ground.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, you no longer need to end your flying movement on the ground while not shifted.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8662b9efecb55e1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telepathic Speech","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can form a telepathic connection between your mind and the mind of another. As a Bonus Action, choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. You and the chosen creature can speak telepathically with each other while the two of you are within a number of miles of each other equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). To understand each other, you must both know at least one language.</p><p>The telepathic connection lasts for a number of minutes equal to your sorcerer level. It ends early if you are Incapacitated or die or if you use this ability to form a connection with a different creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8672a3694225bfe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Portent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. You roll three d20s for your Portent feature, rather than two.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s87170daaa56eee6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Sacred Weapon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to imbue one Melee weapon that you are holding with positive energy. For 10 minutes or until you use this feature again, you add your Charisma modifier to Attack Rolls you make with that weapon (minimum bonus of +1), and each time you hit with it, you cause it to deal its normal damage type or Radiant damage.</p><p>The weapon also emits Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light 20 feet beyond that.</p><p>You can end this effect early (no action required). This effect also ends if you aren't carrying the weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow-teal.webp","_id":"s875b428dd6225ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428352,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcery Points","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have 2 sorcery points, and you gain one additional point every time you level up, to a maximum of 20 at level 20. You can never have more sorcery points than shown on the table for your level. You regain all spent sorcery points when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.sorcerer.sorcery-points","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/runes-star-pentagon-orange.webp","_id":"s876f4c97b82810b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428363,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase your size to Large when you use your Formshift class feature and your Natural Weapons die is doubled for calculating your base weapon damage while you are shifted. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn't change.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/bull-horns-eyes-glowin-orange.webp","_id":"s8782ccda088efe4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blazing Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically transform into a creature of living flame. In this form, you have Resistance to piercing, bludgeoning, and slashing damage as well as Immunity to fire damage and poison.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature hits you with a melee attack from within 10 ft or touches you, it takes fire damage equal to half your sorcerer level. Additionally, you add your Charisma modifier to the damage of all the other features gained from this subclass that deal fire damage.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you have used this feature, you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8797dd234a36116","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artificer Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose the type of specialist you are, each of which is detailed at the end of the class's description. Your choice grants you features at 5th level and again at 9th and 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s87fb35cb9b2c1e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Instinctive Charm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an Attack Roll against you, you can use your Reaction to divert the attack, provided that another creature is within the attack's range. The attacker must make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker must target the creature that is closest to it, not including you or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target. On a successful save, you can't use this feature on the attacker again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>You must choose to use this feature before knowing whether the attack hits or misses. Creatures that can't be Charmed are Immune to this effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8863e688f848b02","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Order's Wrath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Enemies you designate for destruction wilt under the combined efforts of you and your allies. If you deal damage to a creature on your turn, you can curse that creature until the start of your next turn. When one of your allies hits the cursed creature with an attack, the target also takes 2d8 psychic damage. You can curse a creature in this way only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s887c436e8ed0916","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"s88df4aa92712010","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Call the Hunt","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The beast within you grows so powerful that you can spread its ferocity to others and gain resilience from them joining your hunt. When you enter your rage, you can choose a number of other willing creatures you can see within 30 feet of you equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of one creature).</p><p>You gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature that accepts this feature. Until the rage ends, the chosen creatures can each use the following benefit once on each of their turns: when the creature hits a target with an Attack Roll and deals damage to it, the creature can roll a d6 and gain a bonus to the damage equal to the number rolled.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s89310317173751a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Diamond Skin","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to harden specific areas of your body in response to physical trauma. When an effect makes you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, you can use your Reaction to halve the effect's damage against you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8931d50c96ed95a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inner Sun","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 1 to 10 Ki Points as an Action and bathe the area in a 30-foot Emanation in a blinding light. Each creature of your choice in the area has to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, a target takes 1d10 radiant damage per Ki Point spent and is Blinded until the end of your next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't Blinded.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s896a70a5764c83d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8987fc7572c17e3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mastery of Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use your familiarity with death to escape its grasp. When you are reduced to 0 hit points and don't die outright, you can expend 1 ki point (no action required) to have 1 hit point instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s89990a5dd5761fb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Life Link","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You create magical bond between your lifeforce and that of your Eidolon. When you or your Eidolon take damage that would reduce you to 0 hitpoints, you are reduced 1 hitpoint instead and the other takes the remainder of the damage.</p><p>The link has no effect on features that outright kill you when you are reduced to 0 hitpoints, such as the Disintegrate spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/debuff-energy-hold-green.webp","_id":"s89a3fa081fd1802","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Seasonal Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The radius of your Awakened Season increases to 60 feet. Additionally, you have the following spell prepared based on your chosen season. You can cast this spell once without expending a spell slot. You cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Power Word Fortify.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> Sunburst.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> Polar Ray.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s89ed0b064f735f4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Honorable Reputation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-peace-alliance.webp","_id":"s8a2faaf3b1e68bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically empower your bonded familiar for 10 minutes if it is within 60 feet of you. It gains the following benefits for the duration:</p><ul><li>Your bonded familiar grows to Huge size. If it lacks the room to become Huge, its size does not change.</li><li>Your bonded familiar's Strength and Constitution score are equal to your spellcasting ability score. If the latter is lower, your bonded familiar's stats do not change. It does not gain any hit points from this increase in Constitution, instead its current and maximum hit points increase by an amount equal to 5 x your Witch level.</li><li>Your bonded familiar has Advantage on Strength and Constitution Saving Throws.</li><li>The damage dice gained through the Battle Familiar feature are tripled.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature you cannot use it against until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8a95192b3de06f4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved War Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can cast a spell in place of two of your melee weapon attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8aa4a3865af1fb1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wanderer of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Survival skill and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for this skill.</p><p>Additionally, you gain one of the following benefits based on your chosen Wild Domain:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Wild Domain Feature</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>You are acclimatized to extreme heat and your Speed increases by 5 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>You and your bonded familiar cannot be Surprised unless you are Incapacitated.</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>You are acclimatized to extreme cold and you ignore 3 caused by ice and snow, magical or otherwise.</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, you add 30 feet to it.</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Stealth skill and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for this skill.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8ac217b04c5a7ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beguiling Twist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of the Feywild guards your mind. You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed or Frightened.</p><p>In addition, whenever you or a creature you can see within 120 feet of you succeeds on a Saving Throw against being Charmed or Frightened, you can use your Reaction to force a different creature you can see within 120 feet of you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. If the save fails, the target is Charmed or Frightened by you (your choice) for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a successful save.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8ac749873a8cb3c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Far Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You no longer need to breathe, and you gain Resistance to fire damage and cold damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8ad688ff50610ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flurry of Blows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 1 Ki Point to make two Unarmed Strikes as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-yellow-red.webp","_id":"s8b1999389a5c40d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Born to the Saddle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery as a rider becomes apparent. You have Advantage on Saving Throws made to avoid falling off your mount. If you fall off your mount and descend no more than 10 feet, you can land on your feet if you're not Incapacitated.</p><p>Finally, mounting or dismounting a creature costs you only 5 feet of movement, rather than half your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8b5603bdfd6e776","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expanded Element (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another element, but you can't choose the same element a third time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-smoke-pink.webp","_id":"s8b610c63f25fb75","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Anger of a Gentle Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to visit vengeance on someone who fells others. If you see a creature reduce another creature to 0 hit points, you can use your Reaction to grant yourself a bonus to all damage rolls against the aggressor until the end of your next turn. The bonus equals your monk level.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8bd1a4ba9a942d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Travel Along the Tree","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you activate your Rage and as a Bonus Action while your Rage is active, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p><p>In addition, once per Rage, you can increase the range of that teleport to 150 feet. When you do so, you can also bring up to six willing creatures who are within 10 feet of you. Each creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice within 10 feet of your destination space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8bdc6b696638af9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Amphibious","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can breathe air and water.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/amphibians/frog-water-teal.webp","_id":"s8c2ccb8458cccef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Benign Transporation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Bonus Action to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. Alternatively, you can choose a space within range that is occupied by a Small or Medium creature. If that creature is willing, you both teleport, swapping places.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest or you expend a 2+ spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8c805b26c1beae3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428376,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Urban Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar become Proficient in three skills out of the following: Deception, Insight, Investigation, Stealth, Persuasion, and Sleight of Hand. Both of you double your Proficiency for one of the chosen skills, this need not be the same skill. Both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for any of the chosen skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8cd276a59b0425c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empress of the Fathoms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of water allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of waves.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You ignore all water-based effects such as the Tsunami spell or a natural vortex.</li><li>You gain Immunity to cold damage.</li><li>Water flows from everywhere, including up from the ground and dropping as rain to form a vortex of writhing watery tentacles in a 60 feet radius around you that makes the area 3. You and any number of creatures of your choice in the area unaffected.</li><li>Any other creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your save DC or be Grappled and Restrained. It can make a Strength check as an Action on its turn to no longer be Grappled and Restrained.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8d0e80a63659a88","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mushroom Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following additional options for your Magic Mushrooms:</p><p><strong>Boom Shroom.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. They take force damage equal to 1d6 x your Proficiency on a failure, and half as much on a success.</p><p><strong>Madcap.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make an Intelligence Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Confused until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p><strong>Waxy Webber.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make an Strength Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Restrained until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p>Additionally, you regain one use of Magic Mushrooms when you roll Initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8d44cc3e0db4095","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master's Flourish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use a Blade Flourish option, you can roll a d6 and use it instead of expending a Bardic Inspiration die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8d6229b93d51e9a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Game of Caps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Magic Mushrooms are Invisible to anyone other than you and any number of creatures you designate when you initially create them.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move any circle of mushrooms to a different point you can see within 60 feet of its original position.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8de21e42e50dd7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Snap Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are ever ready to spring into action. If you take the Attack action on your first turn of a combat, you can make one additional ranged weapon attack as part of that action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e16d4cd6af0572","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raven's Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Raven Mother grants you a protective blessing. You gain Advantage on death Saving Throws, Immunity to the Frightened condition, and Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e2ee34436b377f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Circle Forms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While in a Wild Shape form, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Lunar Blessing.</strong> Your attacks in a Wild Shape form count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li><li><strong>Increased Toughness.</strong> You can add your Wisdom modifier to your Constitution Saving Throws.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e6b8ed72da9922","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Coils","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Spectral coils start appearing around you when you enter your rage. While you are raging, your reach with Unarmed Strikes increases by 5 ft and you ignore all size restrictions and Immunities for attempting grapples.</p><p>Once per turn, if you successfully hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike while raging, you can attempt to Grapple it.</p><p>You can use your Bonus Action to force a creature you Grappled in this manner to make a STR Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 8 + your Proficiency + your STR modifier. On a failure, the creature takes force damage equal to your Proficiency + your STR modifier + your rage bonus damage and is Restrained until the end of your next turn. On a success, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't Restrained.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e78144cf2046ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Naturally Stealthy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attempt to hide even if you are obscured only by a creature that is at least one size larger than you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"s8e9571ef6676829","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hands-to-Mouth","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you spend overtime crafting and have to make a Constitution Saving Throw to not suffer a level of Exhaustion, you make that Saving Throw with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-aura-energy.webp","_id":"s8ea8064771203d1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Words of Creation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered two of the Words of Creation: the words of life and death. You therefore always have the Power Word Heal and Power Word Kill spells prepared. When you cast either spell, you can target a second creature with it if that creature is within 10 feet of the first target. You can cast either spell once without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to cast these spells this way when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/scream-wail-shout-teal.webp","_id":"s8f2051e810bf9f2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alter Memories","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to make a creature unaware of your magical influence on it. When you cast an enchantment spell to charm one or more creatures, you can alter one creature's understanding so that it remains unaware of being Charmed.</p><p>Additionally, once before the spell expires, you can use your action to try to make the chosen creature forget some of the time it spent Charmed. The creature must succeed on an Intelligence Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC or lose a number of hours of its memories equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1). You can make the creature forget less time, and the amount of time can't exceed the duration of your enchantment spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f61f4f067001c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inevitable Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Sanctified Mark, you can declare a creature known to you as the target, ignoring all range, sight, and cover restrictions. If the target is on another plane of existence, you learn which one.</p><p>Additionally, you cannot have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against the the target of Sanctified Mark.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f6d3aa5e33ecaf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Forbidden Studies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficient in the Medicine skill. If you are already Proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p><p>Additionally, you can target a friendly dying creature with Shocking Grasp to resuscitate it. If you hit, the attack does not count as a critical hit, but the target still suffers one Death Saving Throw failure. It then regains hit points equal to half the lightning damage done. This feature cannot target creatures that have already incurred two Death Saving Throw failures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f8bad3de02be41","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primeval Awareness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ranger lore allows you to establish a powerful link to beasts and to the land around you.</p><p>You have an innate ability to communicate with beasts, and they recognize you as a kindred spirit. Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas to a beast as an Action, and can read its basic mood and intent. You learn its emotional state, whether it is affected by magic of any sort, its short-term needs (such as food or safety), and actions you can take (if any) to persuade it to not attack.</p><p>You cannot use this ability against a creature that you have attacked within the past 10 minutes.</p><p>Additionally, you can attune your senses to determine if any of your favored enemies lurk nearby. By spending 1 uninterrupted minute in Concentration (as if you were concentrating on a spell), you can sense whether any of your favored enemies are present within 5 miles of you. This feature reveals which of your favored enemies are present, their numbers, and the creatures' general direction and distance (in miles) from you.</p><p>If there are multiple groups of your favored enemies within range, you learn this information for each group.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-slit-pink.webp","_id":"s8f9467b10e64bb4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Sacrifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take a Short Rest and use your Arcane Recovery class feature, you can spend a number of hit dice up to equal to your Proficiency modifier.</p><p>The number of hit dice spent in this manner is added to the total level of spell slots that you can recover with Arcane Recovery.</p><p>Additionally, when a creature of at least CR 1/8 afflicted with the Lacerated condition from one of your spells dies within 120 feet of you, you regain one hit die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8fcbf280803d75b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elf Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the elvish sword, greatsword, longbow, and shortbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/bows/shortbow-recurve-yellow.webp","_id":"s8ff977395028af9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Healing Light","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel celestial energy to heal wounds. You have a pool of d6s that you spend to fuel this healing. The number of dice in the pool equals 1 + your warlock level.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can heal one creature you can see within 60 feet of you, spending dice from the pool. The maximum number of dice you can spend at once equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of one die). Roll the dice you spend, add them together, and restore a number of hit points equal to the total.</p><p>Your pool regains all expended dice when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8ffb5475251ae37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Witchcraft","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through arcane study and the guidance of your bonded familiar, you learn special occult practices and abilities. You gain four witchcraft options of your choice. When you finish a Long Rest you can replace one witchcraft you know with another one.</p><p><strong>Amelioration.</strong> As an Action, you touch a creature that is Blinded, Deafened, Poisoned, or is afflicted with a disease and magically alleviate its affliction. The target does not suffer the effects of your choice of one of these conditions until the start of your next turn. This does not remove the effects from the target and has no effect on them if they are reapplied during this time.</p><p><strong>Cackle.</strong> As an Action, you magically disrupt the ability to recover of one creature that can hear you within 60 feet. Until the start of your next turn, the target makes Saving Throws against ongoing effects on it with Disadvantage.</p><p><strong>Evil Eye.</strong> As an Action, you can curse a creature that you can see within 60 feet. The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it subtracts 1d4 from the result of all D20 Tests it makes until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Familiar Focus.</strong> As an Action, you can perceive through your bonded familiar's senses in addition to your own. You can end this effect again as an Action. Additionally, you can cast any spell or use any witchcraft option from your bonded familiar's space.</p><p><strong>Kettle Chant.</strong> When you make a crafting check using alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit, you add half your spellcasting ability modifier (rounded down).</p><p><strong>Mind Fog.</strong> As an Action, you can befuddle the mind of a creature you can see within 60 feet and that is currently concentrating. The target immedidately has to make a Concentration Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 10 + half your Witch level (rounded up) + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Minor Prophecy.</strong> Your gift for divination allows you to foresee minor events. When a creature you can see within 60 feet succeeds on or fails a D20 Test, you can use your Reaction to turn the roll on the D20 into a 9 or 11 (your choice). You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Witch Spittle.</strong> As an Action, you touch a creature and rub spit laced with a minor healing enchantment over its injuries. The target regains hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. If the target is your bonded familiar, it regains additional hit points equal to your Witch level. A creature cannot benefit from this effect again until it has finished a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s901ef0784a2070f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Coordination","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take an additional action and Bonus Action on your turn.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short Rest or you spend a spell slot of 4th level or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9032055ddbf4952","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rage of the Gods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you activate your Rage, you can assume the form of a divine warrior. This form lasts for 1 minute or until you drop to 0 Hit Points. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>While in this form, you gain the benefits below.</p><ul><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant damage.</li><li><strong>Revivification.</strong> When a creature within 30 feet of you would drop to 0 Hit Points, you can take a Reaction to expend a use of your Rage to instead change the target's Hit Points to a number equal to your Barbarian level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s904e5a75de4082b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirits from Beyond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While holding a Spellcasting Focus, you can take a Bonus Action to expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration and call forth the powers of a spirit. Roll the Bardic Inspiration die and refer to the Spirits from Beyond table to determine the spirit you channel, then choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself as the spirit's target. The spirit immediately takes effect; if a spirit's effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals your Bard spell save DC.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Spirits from Beyond</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Bardic Insp. Die</th><th scope=\"col\">Spirit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Beloved. The target regains Hit Points equal to one roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Sharpshooter. The target takes Force damage equal to one roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Avenger. Until the end of your next turn, any creature that hits the target with a melee attack roll takes Force damage equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Renegade. The target can immediately take a Reaction to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Fortune Teller. The target has Advantage on D20 Tests until the start of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Wayfarer. The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Bard level. While it has these Temporary Hit Points, the target's Speed increases by 10 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Trickster. The target makes a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target takes Psychic damage equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die and has the Charmed condition until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Shade. The target gains the Invisible condition until the end of its next turn or until the target makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell. When the invisibility ends, each creature in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take Necrotic damage equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Arsonist. The target makes a Dexterity Saving Throw, taking Fire damage equal to four rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die on a failed save or half as much on a successful one.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Coward. The target and each creature of your choice in a 30-foot Emanation originating from the target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or have the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn. While Frightened, a creature's Speed is halved, and it can take either an Action or a Bonus Action, not both.</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Brute. Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot Emanation originating from the target makes a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, a creature takes Thunder damage equal to three rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die and has the Prone condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Controlled Channeling. You determine the spirit's effect by choosing one of the other rows in this table.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9061d0eaf247879","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor of Hexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when a creature hits you with an attack, that creature has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it is subject to the effects of the Bane spell until the start of its next turn (no Concentration required). The effect applies to the triggering attack roll, possibly causing it to miss.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s90932960d7f4097","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Prey","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can focus your ire on one foe, increasing the harm you inflict on it. Once per turn, you can designate one creature you can see as the target of this feature (no action required). The first time each turn that you hit that target with a weapon attack, it takes an extra 1d6 damage from the weapon. This damage increases to 2d6 when your reach 11th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s90a0b3cead52a26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Cunning Action class feature, you can also choose to teleport 30 ft to an unoccupied space that you can see. You can choose to do so immediately after or before applying the effect of Cunning Action. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s90db7fab852a7e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insightful Negotiator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Insight and Persuasion skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp","_id":"s90ed77d602daa83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Star Map","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've created a star chart as part of your heavenly studies. It is a Tiny object and can serve as a spellcasting focus for your druid spells. You determine its form by rolling on the Star Map table or by choosing one.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Star Map</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Map Form</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>A scroll covered with depictions of constellations</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>A stone tablet with fine holes drilled through it</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>A speckled owlbear hide, tooled with raised marks</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>A collection of maps bound in an ebony cover</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>A crystal that projects starry patterns when placed before a light</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Glass disks that depict constellations</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>While holding this map, you have these benefits:</p><ul><li>You know the Guidance cantrip.</li><li>You have the Guiding Bolt spell prepared. It counts as a druid spell for you, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can have prepared.</li><li>You can cast Guiding Bolt without expending a spell slot. You can do so a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>If you lose the map, you can perform a 1-hour ceremony to magically create a replacement. This ceremony can be performed during a Short or a Long Rest, and it destroys the previous map.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s90f3753d5807a25","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your familiar learns all Witch cantrips you know and can cast them without material components. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus and spell save DC for these cantrips.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s915b60121130f94","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189562,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hour of Reaping","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to unsettle or terrify those around you as an Action, for your soul has been touched by the shadow of death. When you take this action, each creature within 30 feet of you that can see you must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><p>You can also this feature when you gain temporary hit points through Touch of Death (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9184fc23d50a849","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Negative Energy Manipulation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a pool of deathly energy represented by a number of points equal to twice your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier.</p><p>When you roll damage for a necromancy spell or an undead you control, you can deal additional necrotic damage by spending points from the pool, up to its current maximum.</p><p>When a creature of at least CR 1/8 dies within 60 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to harvest part of its remaining life force, regaining a number of points equal to the creature's CR (minimum of 1). You cannot do so if the creature is an undead or construct.</p><p>You regain expended points equal to your Proficiency when you finish a Short Rest and all expended points when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91abe92a474ddbb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428378,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Phoenix Spark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The fiery energy within you grows restless and vengeful. In the face of defeat, it surges outward to preserve you in a fiery roar.</p><p>If you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can instead be reduced to 1 hit point, and each creature within 10 feet of you takes fire damage equal to half your sorcerer level + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>If you use this feature while under the effects of your Mantle of Flame, this feature instead deals fire damage equal to your sorcerer level + double your Charisma modifier, and your Mantle of Flame immediately ends.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91ad7e46d644e34","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have dedicated yourself to one of the following sacred roles of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Magician.</strong> You know one extra cantrip from the Druid spell list. In addition, your mystical connection to nature gives you a bonus to your Intelligence (Arcana or Nature) checks. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum bonus of +1).</li><li><strong>Warden.</strong> Trained for battle, you gain Proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-sproud-hands-dirt-green.webp","_id":"s91b762adbacaca5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Death from the Dark.</strong> Once per turn, when you hit a creature you are hidden from with your natural weapons, you deal additional damage equal to two rolls of your Natural Weapons die and the target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw.</li><li>The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target is Frightened until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Evasive Flight.</strong> When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half damage if you fail.</li><li>If you succeed on the Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to move up to half your Speed to an unoccupied space that you can see. If you are carrying an ally or otherwise moving them with you, they also automatically succeed on the Saving Throw and take no damage.</li><li>You don't benefit from this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</li><li><strong>Concussive Impact.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and hit the target, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target suffers an effect based on the distance you travelled as part of Primal Pounce. The listed effects are cumulative.</li><ul><li><strong>20 feet or more:</strong> The target is knocked Prone.</li><li><strong>40 feet or more:</strong> The target is Dazed until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>60 feet or more:</strong> The target is Stunned until the end of your next turn.</li></ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91c8753d0a25bfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earth Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91c915e9b356b7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nature's Sanctuary","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape and cause spectral trees and vines to appear in a 15-foot Cube on the ground within 120 feet of yourself. They last there for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition or die. You and your allies have Half Cover while in that area, and your allies gain the current Resistance of your Nature's Ward while there.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move the Cube up to 60 feet to ground within 120 feet of yourself.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/encase-creature-humanoid-hold.webp","_id":"s920a8243b202aa8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Armor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as shown below.</p><p><strong>Dreadnought.</strong> When you use your Giant Stature, your reach increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Large or Huge (your choice), and you have Advantage on Strength Checks and Strength Saving Throws for the duration.</p><p>When you hit a creature with your Force Demolisher, creatures within 10 ft of it also take 2d6 force damage. Additionally, the original target and every affected creature around it have to make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell save DC. On a failure, they are knocked Prone. A creature makes this Saving Throw only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Guardian.</strong> When a Huge or smaller creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to magically force it to make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you pull the creature up to 25 feet directly to an unoccupied space. If you pull the target to a space within 5 feet of you, you can make a melee weapon attack against it as part of this Reaction.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Infiltrator.</strong> Any creature that takes lightning damage from your Lightning Launcher glimmers with magical light until the start of your next turn. The glimmering creature sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius, and it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you, as the light jolts it if it attacks you. In addition, the next Attack Roll against it has Advantage, and if that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d12 lightning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-gorget-steel-purple.webp","_id":"s922105af30f1f76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Forms of Your Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The astral self is a translucent embodiment of the monk's soul. As a result, an astral self can reflect aspects of a monk's background, ideals, flaws, and bonds, and an astral self doesn't necessarily look anything like the monk. For example, the astral self of a lanky human might be reminiscent of a minotaur-the strength of which the monk feels within. Similarly, an orc monk might manifest gossamer arms and a delicate visage, representing the gentle beauty of the orc's soul. Each astral self is unique, and some of the monks of this monastic tradition are known more for the appearance of their astral self than for their physical appearance.</p><p>When choosing this path, consider the quirks that define your monk. Are you obsessed with something? Are you driven by justice or a selfish desire? Any of these motivations could manifest in the form of your astral self.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9223d375e32708b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Hate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The paladin, as well any fiends and undead within 10 feet of the paladin, gains a bonus to melee weapon damage rolls equal to the paladin's Charisma modifier (minimum of +1). A creature can benefit from this feature from only one paladin at a time.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s92345f3bc1da4f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor Model","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can customize your Arcane Armor. When you do so, choose one of the following armor models: Guardian or Infiltrator. The model you choose gives you special benefits while you wear it.</p><p>Each model includes a special weapon. When you attack with that weapon, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity, to the attack and damage rolls. If your armor has an enhancement bonus, it is added to these attack and damage rolls.</p><p>You can change the armor's model whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, provided you have armorsmith's tools in hand.</p><p><strong>Dreadnought.</strong> You design your armor to become a towering juggernaut in battle. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul><p><strong>Guardian.</strong> You design your armor to be in the front line of conflict. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul><p><strong>Infiltrator.</strong> You customize your armor for subtle undertakings. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/hand/gauntlet-armored-grey.webp","_id":"s9291ce5914a5f8b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Hardened Bark.</strong> When you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, that damage is reduced by an amount equal to half your Shifter level. This reduction applies before all other calculations.</li><li><strong>Dryadic Bond.</strong> You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</li><li>Additionally, you can form a ranged weapon from plant material as a Bonus Action. As part of an attack, you can automatically form ammunition for this weapon if it requires it. The ammunition disappears are hitting or missing. The weapon remains while it is within 100 feet of you and otherwise disappears. This weapon counts as a natural weapon for you and has a range of 90/360 feet.</li><li><strong>Defensive Spores.</strong> When a creature within 10 feet of you hits or misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to force it to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, the target is Poisoned for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the target can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s92aee650d216eaf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Eldritch Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional eldritch invocation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s92d1b8dbde45876","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warcry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When your allies are affected by your Inspiring Surge, you can choose to apply one of the following additional effects per ally:</p><ul><li>The target has Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage until the start of your next turn.</li><li>The target's Speed is doubled until the start of your next turn.</li><li>The target has Advantage on melee weapon Attack Rolls until the start of your next turn, but Attack Rolls against it also have Advantage for the duration.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s92dc04e7a63ac37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grim Satisfaction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever a creature fails a Saving Throw against one of your Witch spells or features, you and your bonded familiar gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch level (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s930cb6390b17bea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadowdance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you use your Cunning Action while in dim light or darkness, you can teleport up to 60 feet to a different unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness. You can apply the effects of your Cunning Action before or after you teleport. This does not count as movement for the purpose of Cunning Action: Aim.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s931c38fa87631e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of the Ravaged Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a pool of power fueled by your zealous fervor that replenishes when you finish a Long Rest. The pool has a number of points equal to five times your Cleric level. You cannot benefit from this feature while you are wearing armor.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you draw power from the pool to give yourself Temporary Hit Points, up to the maximum amount remaining in the pool.</p><p>You can also expend 5 points from the pool to remove the Charmed, Frightened or Poisoned conditions from yourself, those points do not also give Temporary Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93223780d429a4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Conquest Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Command</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hold Person, Spiritual Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Bestow Curse, Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Dominate Beast, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cloudkill, Dominate Person</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93229449df8aa1e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scornful Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Those who dare to strike you are psychically punished for their audacity. Whenever a creature hits you with an attack, that creature takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1) if you're not Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93414f799b8daba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Careful Eyes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You excel at picking out hidden enemies and other threats. You can take the Search action as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Perception, Investigation, or Survival skill (choose one).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s934852c5561b80e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elegant Courtier","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your discipline and attention to detail allow you to excel in social situations. Whenever you make a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p>Your self-control also causes you to gain Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws. If you already have this Proficiency, you instead gain Proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma Saving Throws (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93ab00924241ccd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As magic flows through your body, it causes physical traits of your dragon ancestors to emerge. Your hit point maximum increases by 3 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, parts of your skin are covered by a thin sheen of dragon-like scales. When you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/claws/claw-scaled-red.webp","_id":"s93b7b5103794f48","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fungal Infestation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spores gain the ability to infest a corpse and animate it. If a beast or a humanoid that is Small or Medium dies within 10 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to animate it, causing it to stand up immediately with 1 hit point. The creature uses the zombie stat block in the Monster Manual. It remains animate for 1 hour, after which time it collapses and dies.</p><p>In combat, the zombie's turn comes immediately after yours. It obeys your mental commands, and the only action it can take is the Attack action, making one melee attack.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93df11b70cc6e01","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have developed ways to hamper your foes when you use your Sneak Attack. When you deal Sneak Attack damage, you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects. Each effect has a die cost, which is the number of Sneak Attack damage dice you must forego to add the effect. You remove the die before rolling, and the effect occurs immediately after the attack's damage is dealt. For example, if you add the Lacerate effect, remove 1d6 from the Sneak Attack's damage before rolling.</p><p>If a Cunning Strike effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Dexterity or Strength modifier (your choice).</p><ul><li><strong>Distract (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Lacerate (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target is Lacerated for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the Lacerated target can repeat the save, ending the effect on on a success.</li><li><strong>Trip (Cost: 1d6).</strong> If the target is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or be knocked Prone.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-white-orange.webp","_id":"s9402ac383585e63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hound of Ill Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call forth a howling creature of darkness to harass your foes. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 3 sorcery points to magically summon a hound of ill omen to target one creature you can see within 120 feet of you. The hound uses the dire wolf's statistics (see the Monster Manual or appendix C in the Player's Handbook), with the following changes:</p><ul><li>The hound is size Medium, not Large, and it counts as a monstrosity, not a beast.</li><li>It appears with a number of temporary hit points equal to half your sorcerer level.</li><li>It can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3. The hound takes 5 force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.</li><li>At the start of its turn, the hound automatically knows its target's location. If the target was hidden, it is no longer hidden from the hound.</li></ul><p>The hound appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of the target. Roll initiative for the hound. On its turn, it can move only toward its target by the most direct route, and it can use its action only to attack its target. The hound can make Opportunity Attacks, but only against its target. Additionally, while the hound is within 5 feet of the target, the target has Disadvantage on Saving Throws against any spell you cast. The hound disappears if it is reduced to 0 hit points, if its target is reduced to 0 hit points, or after 5 minutes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s94045224099c32c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Chaos","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell with a spell slot, you can create an effect of your choice from the Wild Magic Surge table, provided the effect casts a spell or restores all your expended Sorcery Points.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish 1d4 Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s940474497b6e1a6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arms of the Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of your ki allows you to summon a portion of your astral self. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 ki point to summon the arms of your astral self. Alternatively, you can spend this ki point as part of the same Bonus Action you used for another Monk feature. When you do so, each creature of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or take force damage equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die. At 11th level, the damage of this feature increases to three rolls of your Martial Arts die.</p><p>For 10 minutes, these spectral arms hover near your shoulders or surround your arms (your choice). You determine the arms' appearance, and they vanish early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>While the spectral arms are present, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You can use your Wisdom modifier in place of your Strength modifier when making strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</li><li>You can use the spectral arms to make Unarmed Strikes.</li><li>When you make an Unarmed Strike with the arms on your turn, your reach for it is 5 feet greater than normal.</li><li>The Unarmed Strikes you make with the arms can use your Wisdom modifier in place of your Strength or Dexterity modifier for the attack and damage rolls, and their damage type is force.</li><li>When you use Deflect Attack, you add your Wisdom modifier to both the amount of damage you reduce and the amount of damage you deal.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s941851b3dc5ef79","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rakish Audacity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your confidence propels you into battle. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Charisma modifier.</p><p>You also gain an additional way to use your Sneak Attack; you don't need Advantage on your Attack Roll to use Sneak Attack against a creature if it is within your melee reach, no other creatures are within 5 feet of you, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s944b1e0eb8d7898","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Appetite for Destruction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your destructive acts fuel further expressions of devastation. If you reduce a creature to 0 hit points, you can use your Reaction to immediately make one weapon attack or cast a cantrip.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9485d82620b2ccc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Arts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your practice of martial arts gives you mastery of combat styles that use your Unarmed Strike and Monk weapons, which are the following:</p><ul><li>Simple Melee Weapons</li><li>Martial Melee Weapons that have the Light property</li></ul><p>You gain the following benefits while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield.</p><ul><li><strong>Bonus Unarmed Strike.</strong> You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Martial Arts Die.</strong> You can roll 1d6 in place of the normal damage of your Unarmed Strike or Monk weapons. This die changes as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Features table.</li><li><strong>Dexterous Attacks.</strong> You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. In addition, when you use the Grapple or Shove option of your Unarmed Strike, you can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier to determine the save DC.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"s948f8de52a4adc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pact Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your arcane research and the magic bestowed on you by your patron have given you facility with spells. The information below details how you use those rules with Warlock spells, which appear on the Warlock spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two Warlock cantrips of your choice. Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Warlock cantrip of your choice.</p><p>When you reach Warlock levels 4 and 10, you learn another Warlock cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Warlock Features table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Warlock Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your warlock spells of levels 1–5. The table also shows the level of those slots, all of which are the same level. You regain all expended Pact Magic spell slots when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>For example, when you're a level 5 Warlock, you have two level 3 spell slots. To cast the level 1 spell Witch Bolt, you must spend one of those slots, and you cast it as a level 3 spell.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose two level 1 Warlock spells.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Warlock levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Warlock Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Warlock spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level no higher than what's shown in the table's Slot Level column for your level. When you reach level 6, for example, you learn a new Warlock spell, which can be of levels 1–3.</p><p>If another Warlock feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Warlock spells for you.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Warlock spell of an eligible level.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (your choice) is the spellcasting ability for your Warlock spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a spellcasting focus for your warlock spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/blood-spurt-spray-red.webp","_id":"s94f776149198c90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your draconic ancestry gives you special abilities. Choose a type of dragon from the table below. The type you choose influences your breath weapon and your damage Resistance.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Ancestry</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Dragon</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td><td>15 ft. cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td><td>15 ft. cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td><td>15 ft. cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td><td>15 ft. cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-fire-breath-orange.webp","_id":"s950c1dbe8468c61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a number of superiority dice equal to half your maximum (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s95542b9051682fb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to perceive the auras of other creatures.</p><p>As an Action, select a creature that you can see. That creature makes a Wisdom Saving Throw, though it has no knowledge that you forced it to attempt this Saving Throw. On a failed save, you learn if the creature shares any aspects of its alignment with you, its current hit points, and its current attitude and intentions toward you or one other creature, object, or location of your choice. In addition, for the next 24 hours or until you use this ability again, you can use an Action to determine the creature's distance and direction from you.</p><p>If a creature succeeds on its Saving Throw against this ability, you cannot use this ability against that creature again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9555ebb6a46b628","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189516,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stout Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"s95a938a8976779b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unyielding Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Wisdom Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96046d6778b3864","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action: Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional way to use your Cunning Action: carefully aiming your next attack. As a Bonus Action, you give yourself Advantage on your next Attack Roll on the current turn. You can use this Bonus Action only if you haven't moved during this turn, and after you use the Bonus Action, your Speed is 0 until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/projectile-spiral-gray.webp","_id":"s962ef3d3efeb3aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96747a7853f7497","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Ambition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion checks. Additionally, you do not expend a use of your Channel Divinity on Reject Failure if the D20 test does not succeed after the reroll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96799c835198d9f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Remarkable Athlete","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</p><p>You gain Proficiency in either the Athletics or Acrobatics skill. If you are already proficient in the chosen skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s969e04b7fb3ed8f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guarded Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The psionic energy flowing through you has bolstered your mind. You have Resistance to psychic damage. Moreover, if you start your turn Charmed or Frightened, you can expend a Psionic Energy die and end every effect on yourself subjecting you to those conditions.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s969f8f117c341fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Signature Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered certain techniques to the point that they have become second nature. Choose two maneuvers that you know. When you use one of these two maneuvers, you can roll a d8 and use it instead of expending a Combat Superiority Die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96e331596596736","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cosmic Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can consult your Star Map for omens. When you do so, roll a die. Until you finish your next Long Rest, you gain access to a special Reaction based on whether you rolled an even or an odd number on the die:</p><ul><li><strong>Weal (even).</strong> Whenever a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is about to make an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to roll a d6 and add the number rolled to the total.</li><li><strong>Woe (odd).</strong> Whenever a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is about to make an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to roll a d6 and subtract the number rolled from the total.</li></ul><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9702c2455cbe591","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Climb Speed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/settlement/city-wall.webp","_id":"s9710dbd4ca70105","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (9th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 9th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-face-blue.webp","_id":"s97220a698724c77","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Countercharm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use musical notes or words of power to disrupt mind-influencing effects. If you or a creature within 30 feet of you fails a Saving Throw against an effect that applies the Charmed or Frightened condition, you can take a Reaction to cause the save to be rerolled, and the new roll has Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you or a creature within 30 feet of you fails a Saving Throw against an effect that applies the Charmed or Frightened condition"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/scream-wail-shout-teal.webp","_id":"s9724a44a097b256","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stay the Cycle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An a Reaction when you activate the effect of a Lunar Phase, your familiar can prevent you from entering the next one in the cycle if it is within 120 feet of you.</p><p>Your bonded familiar can use this feature twice and it regains all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9762659ebe8977d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Illusory Reality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned the secret of weaving shadow magic into your illusions to give them a semireality. When you cast an illusion spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose one inanimate, nonmagical object that is part of the illusion and make that object real. You can do this on your turn as a Bonus Action while the spell is ongoing. The object remains real for 1 minute. For example, you can create an illusion of a bridge over a chasm and then make it real long enough for your allies to cross.</p><p>The object can't deal damage or otherwise directly harm anyone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s977ac750a78c7d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Slash","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spend 1 ki point to channel ki into your attacks you augment your soul knives to inflict devastating psionic attacks.</p><p>Whenever you hit a creature with one of the attacks granted by your Flurry of Blows and that attack inflicts psychic damage, you can impose one of the following effects on the target:</p><p><strong>Life Drain.</strong> You gain temporary hit points equal to half the damage your attack deals.</p><p><strong>Invoke Terror.</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or become Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Invoke Wrath.</strong> The target suffers Disadvantage on all Attack Rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Astral Slide.</strong> You teleport the target up to 10 feet to a destination you can see.</p><p><strong>Synaptic Overload.</strong> The target has to make an Intelligence Saving Throw or take double damage the next time it takes psychic damage from you before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s97bc9da14462789","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428351,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Disciplines","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The elemental disciplines are presented in alphabetical order. If a discipline requires a level, you must be the level in this class to learn the discipline.</p><h5>Breath of Winter</h5><p>You can spend 6 ki points to cast Cone of Cold.</p><h5>Clench of the North Wind</h5><p>You can spend 3 ki points to cast Rime's Binding Ice.</p><h5>Elemental Attunement</h5><p>You can use your action to briefly control elemental forces within 30 feet of you, causing one of the following effects of your choice:</p><ul><li>Create a harmless, instantaneous sensory effect related to air, earth, fire, or water, such as a shower of sparks, a puff of wind, a spray of light mist, or a gentle rumbling of stone.</li><li>Instantaneously light or snuff out a candle, a torch, or a small campfire.</li><li>Chill or warm up to 1 pound of nonliving material for up to 1 hour.</li><li>Cause earth, fire, water, or mist that can fit within a 1-foot cube to shape itself into a crude form you designate for 1 minute.</li></ul><h5>Eternal Mountain Defense</h5><p>You can spend 5 ki points to cast Stoneskin, targeting yourself.</p><h5>Fangs of the Fire Snake</h5><p>When you use the Attack action on your turn, you can spend 1 ki point to cause tendrils of flame to stretch out from your fists and feet. Your reach with your Unarmed Strikes increases by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. A hit with such an attack deals fire damage instead of bludgeoning damage. If you spend 1 additional ki point when you use this feature, all Unarmed Strikes until the start of your next turn also deal an additional 1d6 fire damage.</p><h5>Fist of Four Thunders</h5><p>You can spend 2 ki points to cast Thunderwave.</p><h5>Unbroken Air</h5><p>You can create a blast of compressed air that strikes like a mighty fist. As an Action, you can spend 2 ki points and choose a creature within 30 feet of you. That creature must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d10 bludgeoning damage, plus an extra 1d10 bludgeoning damage for each additional ki point you spend, and you can push the creature up to 20 feet away from you and knock it Prone. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and you don't push it or knock it Prone.</p><h5>Flames of the Phoenix</h5><p>You can spend 4 ki points to cast Fireball.</p><h5>Gong of the Summit</h5><p>You can spend 3 ki points to cast Shatter.</p><h5>Hand of Ore</h5><p>You can spend 2 ki points to cast Maximilian's Earthen Grasp.</p><h5>Mist Stance</h5><p>You can spend 4 ki points to cast Gaseous Form, targeting yourself.</p><h5>Ride the Wind</h5><p>You can spend 4 ki points to cast Fly, targeting yourself.</p><h5>River of Hungry Flame</h5><p>You can spend 5 ki points to cast Wall of Fire.</p><h5>Rush of the Gale Spirits</h5><p>You can spend 2 ki points to cast Gust of Wind.</p><h5>Shape the Flowing River</h5><p>As an Action, you can spend 1 ki point to choose an area of ice or water no larger than 30 feet on a side within 120 feet of you. You can change water to ice within the area and vice versa, and you can reshape ice in the area in any manner you choose. You can raise or lower the ice's elevation, create or fill in a trench, erect or flatten a wall, or form a pillar. The extent of any such changes can't exceed half the area's largest dimension. For example, if you affect a 30-foot square, you can create a pillar up to 15 feet high. raise or lower the square's elevation by up to 15 feet, dig a trench up to 15 feet deep, and so on. You can't shape the ice to trap or injure a creature in the area.</p><h5>Sweeping Cinder Strike</h5><p>You can spend 2 ki points to cast Burning Hands.</p><h5>Water Whip</h5><p>You can spend 2 ki points as an Action to create a whip of water that shoves and pulls a creature to unbalance it. A creature that you can see that is within 30 feet of you must make a Dexterity Saving Throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d10 bludgeoning damage, plus an extra 1d10 bludgeoning damage for each additional ki point you spend, and you can either knock it Prone or pull it up to 25 feet closer to you. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and you don't pull it or knock it Prone.</p><h5>Wave of Rolling Earth</h5><p>You can spend 6 ki points to cast Wall of Stone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s981fa6081ea5830","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428351,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s985d0e46a0b3324","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise (Level 9)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Expertise in two of your Skill Proficiencies of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"s9875556ae604260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Protective Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you forge between people helps them protect each other. When a creature affected by your Bonds of Solidarity feature is about to take damage, a second bonded creature within 30 feet of the first can use its Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the first creature. The second creature then takes all the damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s98e21a1b7b4d043","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Aquatic Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas with aquatic beasts.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/fish/fish-marlin-swordfight-blue.webp","_id":"s98e75b592cae475","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aegis of Rime","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to cold damage.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that deals cold damage, you form a protective layer of magical ice on yourself.</p><p>While under this effect, the first time you take damage, that damage is reduced by an amount equal to your sorcerer level + your Charisma modifier. The effect then ends on you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s98edc0ab3623034","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Calm Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed or Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/meditation-chi-focus-blue.webp","_id":"s9910f30e6f74086","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn maneuvers that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice.</p><p><strong>Maneuvers.</strong> You learn three maneuvers of your choice, which are listed under \"Maneuvers\" below. Many maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. You can use only one maneuver per attack.</p><p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice at 7th, 10th, and 15th level. Each time you learn new maneuvers, you can also replace one maneuver you know with a different one.</p><p><strong>Superiority Dice.</strong> You have four superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a superiority die (no action required).</p><p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level and one more at 15th level.</p><p><strong>Saving Throws.</strong> Some of your maneuvers require your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects. The Saving Throw DC is calculated as follows:</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Maneuver save DC</strong> = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier + your Dexterity modifier</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s991a04320cbd2fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189497,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes of Night","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can see through the deepest gloom. You have darkvision out to a range of 300 feet. In that radius, you can see in dim light as if it were bright light and in darkness as if it were dim light.</p><p>As an Action, you can magically share the darkvision of this feature with willing creatures you can see within 10 feet of you, up to a number of creatures equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one creature). The shared darkvision lasts for 1 hour. Once you share it, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of any level to share it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s997fad18990d02c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Healing Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mystical touch can heal wounds. You have a pool of magical healing power that replenishes when you take a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of hit points equal to your monk level × 5.</p><p>As an Action, you can touch a creature and draw power from the pool to restore a number of hit points to that creature, up to the maximum amount remaining in the pool.</p><p>Instead of healing the creature, you can expend 5 hit points from your pool of healing to cure the target of one disease or neutralize one poison affecting it. You can cure multiple diseases and neutralize multiple poisons with a single use of Healing Hands, expending hit points separately for each one.</p><p>When you use your Flurry of Blows, you can replace one of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of this feature.</p><p>This feature has no effect on undead and constructs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9986ac2f79f59ec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with calligrapher's tools and enchanter's supplies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"s9995ad141a5ea78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428380,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brute Force","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're able to strike with your weapons with especially brutal force. Whenever you hit with a weapon that you're proficient with and deal damage, the weapon's damage increases by an amount based on your level in this class, as shown on the Brute Bonus Damage table. You can also add the same die to the roll if you make a Strength (Athletics) check.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Brute Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Increase</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>1d4</td></tr><tr><td>10th</td><td>1d6</td></tr><tr><td>16th</td><td>1d8</td></tr><tr><td>20th</td><td>1d10</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s99a63c6063ef72c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ancestral Protectors","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Spectral warriors appear when you enter your rage. While you're raging, the first creature you hit with an attack on your turn becomes the target of the warriors, which hinder its attacks. Until the start of your next turn, that target has Disadvantage on any Attack Roll that isn't against you, and when the target hits a creature other than you with an attack, that creature has Resistance to the damage dealt by the attack. The effect on the target ends early if your rage ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"s99e085aef7c3a87","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428321,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Martyr","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can make your echo throw itself in front of an attack directed at another creature that you can see. Before the Attack Roll is made, you can use your Reaction to teleport the echo to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the targeted creature. The Attack Roll that triggered the Reaction is instead made against your echo.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or you spend a use of your Second Wind (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9a031ee43bddc31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enhanced Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond with your wildfire spirit enhances your destructive and restorative spells. Whenever you cast a spell that deals fire damage or restores hit points while your wildfire spirit is summoned, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus equal to the number rolled to one damage or healing roll of the spell.</p><p>In addition, when you cast a spell with a range other than self, the spell can originate from you or your wildfire spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9a216ee9b59dbe4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel divine fury into your weapon strikes. While you're raging, the first creature you hit on each of your turns with a weapon attack takes extra damage equal to 1d6 + half your barbarian level. The extra damage is necrotic or radiant; you choose the type of damage each time damage is dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9a2f7a7b0c5cd0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428323,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Preparation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9af755d70280db1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telekinetic Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Telekinesis spell prepared. With this feature, you can cast it without a spell slot or components, and your spellcasting ability for it is Intelligence. On each of your turns while you maintain Concentration on it, including the turn when you cast it, you can make one attack with a weapon as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so in this way again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9af97ea1bdfa795","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You no longer have to end your flying movement on the ground when you are shifted.</p><p>Additionally, you gain blindsight with a range of 20 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9b5cdafb7100510","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Falconian Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Light cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the Shield of Faith spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can also cast the Magic Weapon spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. WIS or CHA is your spellcasting ability for these spells (your choice). You can also cast them using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s9c7b6990807e326","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rock Solid","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill. You count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, and lift.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/construct-stone.webp","_id":"s9ca81df3708acd3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Formshift Damage to all Saving Throws. You do not gain this bonus if you're unconscious.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/spirit-fear-energy-pink.webp","_id":"s9ce2b8fa7f2e352","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189538,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the forces of nature grants you Blindsight with a range of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-shadow-red.webp","_id":"s9d0fb7198ab718d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision from your race, its range increases by 60 feet.</p><p>You are also adept at evading creatures that rely on darkvision. While in darkness, you are Invisible to any creature that relies on darkvision to see you in that darkness.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d34e75c56041d4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ambush Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You excel at leading ambushes and acting first in a fight.</p><p>You are proficient in Initiative. In addition, the first creature you hit during the first round of a combat becomes easier for you and others to strike; Attack Rolls against that target have Advantage until the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d40a9be5ffc5df","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Projected Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature that you can see within 30 feet of yourself takes damage, you can take a Reaction to cause your Arcane Ward to absorb that damage. If this damage reduces the ward to 0 Hit Points, the warded creature takes any remaining damage. If that creature has any Resistances or Vulnerabilities, apply them before reducing the ward's Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d6246a637c1b8b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aquatic Affinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, it instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>Additionally the distance you can move your water orb increases to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d6351d207bdb86","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Passionate Temper","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Persuasion or Intimidation skill (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"s9de2a636a131ef1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Wayfarer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Survival skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-forest-gray.webp","_id":"s9e594af933f7841","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Leading Evasion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and you take only half damage if you fail. If any creatures within 5 feet of you are making the same Dexterity Saving Throw, you can share this benefit with them for that save.</p><p>You can't use this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9e66a7657c01095","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Radiant Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are so suffused with righteous might that all your melee weapon strikes carry divine power with them. Whenever you hit a creature with a melee weapon, the creature takes an extra 1d10 radiant damage. The damage increases by 1d10 if the target is an undead or a fiend.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-gold-holy.webp","_id":"s9e971275fbbe263","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hexblade's Curse","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to place a baleful curse on someone. As a Bonus Action, choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The target is cursed for 1 minute. The curse ends early if the target dies, you die, or you are Incapacitated. Until the curse ends, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You gain a bonus to damage rolls against the cursed target. The bonus equals your Proficiency bonus.</li><li>Any Attack Roll you make against the cursed target is a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.</li><li>If the cursed target dies, you regain hit points equal to your warlock level + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 hit point).</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded up). You can regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also expend a Pact Magic slot to regain a number of expended uses up to half the slots spell level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9f2be8fd23c82a2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Defy Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can give yourself vitality when you cheat death or when you help someone else cheat it. You can regain hit points equal to 1d8 + your Warlock level when you succeed on a death Saving Throw or when you stabilize a creature with Spare the Dying.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9f75bf0af888cff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avenging Angel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become an avatar of vengeance. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You sprout spectral wings on your back, have a Fly Speed of 60 feet, and can hover.</li><li>If an enemy creature within your Aura of Protection damages you or your allies, it is automatically affected by your Vow of Enmity (no action required). This does not consume a use of your Channel Divinity.</li><li>If an enemy creature starts its turn in your Aura of Protection or enters it for the first time on a turn, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or become Frightened for 1 minute. If the creature is under the effect of your Vow of Enmity, it has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9f84f209c55cfc8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blade Flourish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to perform impressive displays of martial prowess and speed.</p><p>Whenever you take the Attack action on your turn, your Speed increases by 10 feet until the end of the turn, and if a weapon attack that you make as part of this action hits a creature, you can use one of the following Blade Flourish options of your choice. You can use only one Blade Flourish option per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9fae4884f84a079","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serpent's Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet and Blindsight with a range of 10 feet. If you already possess either sense, its range increases by the same amount.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9fc7aadfa6f596c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Surge (Level 18)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two allies within 60 feet of you, rather than one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9ff141756390cb0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vanguard","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The number of uses of your Second Wind feature increases by two, and the number of uses for your Indomitable feature increases by one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-aura-energy.webp","_id":"sa045f510698bb74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ignite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to start fires with a touch. As an Action, you can magically ignite a flammable object you touch with your hand—an object such as a torch, a piece of tinder, or the hem of drapes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa058c85010772d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Cantrips","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Booming Blade and Green-Flame Blade cantrips.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa05ab79a06d99d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Vow of Enmity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to utter a vow of enmity against a creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against the creature for 1 minute or until you use this feature again.</p><p>If the creature drops to 0 Hit Points before the vow ends, you can transfer the vow to a different creature within 30 feet of yourself (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa0688f5161ed25a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nymph Stride","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You ignore 3 caused by plants, including those of magical nature like the Entangle spell. You are still subject to any of their other effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-dashing-blue.webp","_id":"sa07d177fc3c352d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Tethering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The psychic damage from your Brand of Castigation increases to twice your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of 2). Additionally, a branded creature can't take the Dash action, and if it attempts to teleport or to leave its current plane by any means, it takes 4d6 psychic damage and must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the attempt to teleport or leave the plane fails.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/debuff-chains-red.webp","_id":"sa0ac6ad96780a73","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Elemental Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All features of your Elemental Might with an area of effect have their radius increased to 20 feet. Additionally, its element-specific benefits improve in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Air.</strong> Your movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks and you can move through the spaces of other creatures unimpeded.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> Every creature that fails its Saving Throw against your Elemental Might is knocked Prone.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> The critical range of your attacks increases by 1. Your critical hits deal an additional 2d8 fire damage.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> Every creature that fails its Saving Throw against your Elemental Might has its Speed halved until the start your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa0e5730cb0171be","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undying Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hold your breath indefinitely, and you don't require food, water, or sleep, although you still require rest to reduce Exhaustion and still benefit from finishing short and Long Rests. You are also Immune to diseases and poison.</p><p>In addition, you age at a slower rate. For every 10 years that pass, your body ages only 1 year, and you are Immune to being magically aged.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa0f3688cb5c7f78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"True Hide in Plain Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may choose to take the Hide action and may stay hidden even when the conditions normally wouldn't allow you to, such as when you are in direct line of sight of a creature or you are standing in bright light. If you do so, you take a -5 penalty to your Dexterity (Stealth) check to hide. Depending on the circumstances, the DM may impose this penalty multiple times.</p><p>This feature does not allow you to bypass the conditions for hiding against creatures that perceive you with senses other than mundane sight or are able to perceive the true form of a shapechanger.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa10c97a16fbfa28","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered the art of weaving spellcasting and weapon use into a single harmonious act. When you use your action to cast a bard spell, you can make one weapon attack as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa13f9910bdba04e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You regain all uses of Fighting Spirit when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1591047417567a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's Resistance to your spells. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, that creature has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1990275fbd05b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Conjuration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are concentrating on a conjuration spell, your Concentration can't be broken as a result of taking damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1aecd55e8b3443","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Embodiment of the Law","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become remarkably adept at channeling magical energy to compel others.</p><p>If you cast a spell of the enchantment school using a spell slot of 1st level or higher, you can change the spell's casting time to 1 Bonus Action for this casting, provided the spell's casting time is normally 1 action.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1fa9a489f74f45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class. These spells depend on the damage type of your chosen ancestry, as shown in the tables below. The spells count as sorcerer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Acid Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Create Or Destroy Water, Tasha's Caustic Brew, Darkvision, Melf's Acid Arrow</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Corrosion, Hunger of Hadar</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Vitriolic Sphere, Watery Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Acid Pit, Passwall</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Cold Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Grease, Rime's Binding Ice, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm, Slow</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Hold Monster</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Fire Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Hellish Rebuke, Heat Metal, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Fireball, Flame Stride</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fire Shield, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Flame Strike, Immolation</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Lightning Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Gift of Alacrity, Witch Bolt, Mirror Image, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Haste, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Freedom of Movement, Storm Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Far Step, Mislead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Necrotic Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Hex, Shadow Ray, Blindness/Deafness, Infirmity</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Bestow Curse, Dark Orb</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Shadow of Moil</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Enervation, Negative Energy Flood</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Poison Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Command, Ray of Sickness, Protection from Poison, Ray of Enfeeblement</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Stinking Cloud, Tongues</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Dominate Beast, Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cloudkill, Contagion</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Radiant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Bless, Cure Wounds, Lesser Restoration, Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Daylight, Mass Healing Word</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Banishment, Guardian of Faith</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mass Cure Wounds, Circle of Power</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa20b8a0c7bc987e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428364,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primeval Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting when you choose this circle, you can call upon the primeval creature whose spirit is bound to you. As an Action, you can expend one use of your Wild Shape feature to summon your primeval companion, rather than assuming a beast form. The companion appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of you.</p><p>The primeval companion is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See this creature's game statistics in the Primeval Companion stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. You can determine the cosmetic appearance of the companion; for example, your companion may evoke ancient predators like raptors or saber-toothed tigers, or it might be more inclined for defense, appearing as an armored ankylosaurus or a wooly rhino. These choices have no effect on the companion's game statistics.</p><p>The companion obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own. If you are small enough to ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can any of its actions during your turn or immediately after.</p><p>The companion remains until it is reduced to 0 hit points or until you die, at which point the companion vanishes. If you use this feature to summon the companion again and you already have a companion present, the first companion immediately vanishes. Anything the companion was wearing or carrying is left behind when the companion vanishes.</p><p>You can also channel your magic through your primeval companion. When you cast a spell with a range other than self, the spell can originate from you or your primeval companion.</p><p>In addition, if the primeval companion is affected by a spell you cast that allows creatures to make a Saving Throw against its effects, the primeval companion has Advantage on its Saving Throw. If the primeval companion would normally take half damage on a successful save against this spell, the companion instead takes no damage on a successful save and half damage with no additional effects on a failed save.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa228f9cb04e0453","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your intensity in battle can shield you and help you strike true. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can give yourself Advantage on weapon Attack Rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain temporary hit points equal to your fighter level + Wisdom modifier.</p><p>You can use this feature three times. You regain one use when you finish a Short Rest and all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa2431571982bb7a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grim Psychometry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a supernatural talent for discerning the secrets surrounding mysterious relics or places touched by evil. You can use your hemocraft ability score for History checks and whenever you make a History check to recall information about the sinister or tragic history of an object you are touching or your current location, you have Advantage on the check. At the DM's discretion, a suitably high roll might cause your character to experience brief visions of the past connected to the object or location.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/hand-eye-fire-blue.webp","_id":"sa26554c9efec68d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gnome Tinkerer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with artisan's tools (tinker's tools). Using those tools, you can spend 1 hour and 10 gp worth of materials to construct a Tiny clockwork device (AC 5, 1 hp).</p><p>The device ceases to function after 24 hours (unless you spend 1 hour repairing it to keep the device functioning), or when you use your action to dismantle it; at that time, you can reclaim the materials used to create it. You can have up to three such devices active at a time. When you create a device, choose one of the following options or suggest an idea of your own to your DM.</p><ul><li><strong>Clockwork Toy.</strong> This toy is a clockwork animal, monster, or person, such as a frog, mouse, bird, dragon, or soldier. When placed on the ground, the toy moves 5 feet across the ground on each of your turns in a random direction. It makes noises as appropriate to the creature it represents.</li><li><strong>Fire Starter.</strong> The device produces a miniature flame, which you can use to light a candle, torch, or campfire. Using the device requires your action.</li><li><strong>Music Box.</strong> When opened, this music box plays a single song at a moderate volume. The box stops playing when it reaches the song's end or when it is closed.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/claw-mechanical.webp","_id":"sa26df4ccae9b2be","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sa2992bb36b54128","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Portent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you choose this school, glimpses of the future begin to press in on your awareness. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, roll two d20s and record the numbers rolled. You can replace any Attack Roll, Saving Throw, or Ability Check made by you or a creature that you can see with one of these foretelling rolls. You must choose to do so before the roll, and you can replace a roll in this way only once per turn.</p><p>Each foretelling roll can be used only once. When you finish a Long Rest, you lose any unused foretelling rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa2a1b85732095ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Consult the Spirits","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to consult with your ancestral spirits. When you do so, you cast the Augury or Clairvoyance spell, without using a spell slot or material components. Rather than creating a spherical sensor, this use of Clairvoyance invisibly summons one of your ancestral spirits to the chosen location. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells.</p><p>After you cast either spell in this way, you can't use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-shadow-blue.webp","_id":"sa2c828eba52e26f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Stalker's Rake.</strong> You can Hide as a Bonus Action. If you hit a creature with your natural weapons while hidden, it has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw against your Clawed Aspect. Additionally, creatures Lacerated by you cannot make Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Big Game Hunter.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and your attack hits, you can also attempt to Climb onto a Bigger Creature as per the Additional Combat Actions as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Disembowel.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can force it to make the Saving Throw against your Clawed Aspect again, ignoring the usual per-turn limit. Once per turn, if the Prone creature is already Lacerated, it takes the damage from the condition immediately after the attack if it fails the Saving Throw.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa2e44009aa88a8f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serene Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You make Wisdom Saving Throws with Advantage and when you use Self-Restoration, you can also remove the Confused condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa319cb71cc1cadc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Primeval Guardian Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, and it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Primeval Guardian Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Entangle</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Enhance Ability</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Animals</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Giant Insect</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa335d718d711180","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raging Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of the storm you channel grows mightier, lashing out at your foes. The radius of your aura grows to 20 ft and your aura gains an additional effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa33f70cf844053e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells from the Wizard spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa34de43b6875826","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Athletics, Intimidation, Nature, or Perception.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"sa35c23323e5ddb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428346,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Assassinate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are at your deadliest when you get the drop on your enemies. You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against any creature that hasn't taken a turn in the combat yet. When you use your Sneak Attack against a creature on the first turn of combat that hasn't acted yet or that you are hidden, the number of d6s that you roll as part of your Sneak Attack's damage increases by an amount equal to your Proficiency.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa363fb5995bf3df","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bard College","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You delve into the advanced techniques of a bard college of your choice from the list of available colleges. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sa3708d95815e525","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pyromancy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Pyromancy Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Faerie Fire, Flaming Sphere, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Melf's Minute Meteors, Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Elemental Bane, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Flame Strike, Immolation</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3c564ef6e88919","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Versatile Trickster","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Cunning Strike, you can instead choose a creature other than the original target of your attack that you can see within 5 ft of your mage hand.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3d25fc3f5f5821","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hurricane Queen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of air allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of storms.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You ignore all wind-based effects such as the Whirlwind spell or even a natural tornado.</li><li>You gain Immunity to lightning damage.</li><li>You are surrounded by a 60 foot radius aura of stormlike winds of such intensity that they render ranged weapon attacks against you completely impossible. You and any number of creatures of your choice in the area are unaffected.</li><li>Any other creature is Deafened while in this area, must spend 4 feet for every 1 foot of movement while in it, and has to succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your save DC at the start of its turn or when it enters the area for the first time or be knocked Prone or hurled 20 feet away in a direction that you choose.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3da9c15358b5a6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Starry Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape feature to take on a starry form, rather than transforming into a beast.</p><p>While in your starry form, you retain your game statistics, but your body becomes luminous; your joints glimmer like stars, and glowing lines connect them as on a star chart. This form sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. The form lasts for 10 minutes. It ends early if you dismiss it (no action required), are Incapacitated, die, or use this feature again.</p><p>Whenever you assume your starry form, choose which of the following constellations glimmers on your body; your choice gives you certain benefits while in the form:</p><p><strong>Archer.</strong> A constellation of an archer appears on you. When you activate this form, and as a Bonus Action on your subsequent turns while it lasts, you can make a ranged spell attack, hurling a luminous arrow that targets one creature within 60 feet of you. On a hit, the attack deals radiant damage equal to 1d8 + your Wisdom modifier.</p><p><strong>Chalice.</strong> A constellation of a life-giving goblet appears on you. Whenever you cast a spell using a spell slot that restores hit points to a creature, you or another creature within 30 feet of you can regain hit points equal to 1d8 + your Wisdom modifier.</p><p><strong>Dragon.</strong> A constellation of a wise dragon appears on you. When you make an Intelligence or a Wisdom check or a Constitution Saving Throw to maintain Concentration on a spell, you can treat a roll of 9 or lower on the d20 as a 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa43371d92af727a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hollow Warden Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Ranger level specified in the Hollow Warden Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hollow Warden Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Wrathful Smite</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Spike Growth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Guardian of Nature</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Sanguine Vortex</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa47f69c9694d3b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heroic Warrior","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>10th-level fighter Champion feature (replaces Champion's Reflexes)</p><p>The thrill of battle drives you toward victory. During combat, you can give yourself Heroic Inspiration whenever you start your turn without it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa4e48ecb25cfd9d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortified Position","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're a master at forming well-defended emplacements using Eldritch Cannon:</p><ul><li>You and your allies have half cover while within 10 feet of a cannon you create with Eldritch Cannon, as a result of a shimmering field of magical protection that the cannon emits.</li><li>You can now have two cannons at the same time. You can create two with the same action (but not the same spell slot), and you can activate both of them with the same Bonus Action. You determine whether the cannons are identical to each other or different. You can't create a third cannon while you have two.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/artillery/cannon-banded.webp","_id":"sa4ea7fbddc32020","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Path of the Kensei","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your special martial arts training leads you to master the use of certain weapons. This path also includes instruction in the deft strokes of calligraphy or painting. You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Kensei Weapons.</strong> Choose two weapons that do not have the special or heavy properties. You are proficient in these weapons and they count as monk weapons for you.</p><p>Whenever you make an unarmed attack, you can attack with one of these weapons instead if you are currently wielding them.</p><p>You can choose two additional weapons when you reach the levels 6, 11, and 17 in this class, following the same criteria.</p><p><strong>Way of the Brush.</strong> You gain Proficiency with your choice of calligrapher's supplies or painter's supplies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa4f0fc8757e530b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strength before Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you drop to 0 Hit Points and don't die outright, you can instead drop to 1 Hit Point and immediately move up to your Speed and make a weapon attack.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa519ee00c0d0b38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Disciple","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel draconic power to magnify your presence and imbue your Unarmed Strikes with the essence of a dragon's breath. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Draconic Presence.</strong> If you fail a Charisma (Intimidation) or Charisma (Persuasion) check, you can use your Reaction to reroll the check, as you tap into the mighty presence of dragons. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</li><li><strong>Draconic Strike.</strong> When you damage a target with an Unarmed Strike, you can change the damage type to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison.</li><li><strong>Tongue of Dragons.</strong> You learn to speak, read, and write Draconic or one other language of your choice.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa547612b4947189","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428350,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Plane Charter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa55bda2f0d0a508","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Waxing and Waning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain greater control over the phases of your lunar magic. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 sorcery point to change your lunar phase for a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa596b1382940dff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nightwalker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to adopt a shadowy form as a Bonus Action for 10 minutes. While in this form, Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you, you gain the Spiderclimb trait, and you double your Speed if you start your turn in an area of dim light or darkness.</p><p>You can use this feature once and must finish a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa5ab0954b560d27","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (Level 18)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa5dd7d57c33058a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of the Crown","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tenets of the Oath of the Crown are often set by the sovereign to which their oath is sworn, but generally emphasize the following tenets.</p><p><strong>Law.</strong> The law is paramount. It is the mortar that holds the stones of civilization together, and it must be respected.</p><p><strong>Loyalty.</strong> Your word is your bond. Without loyalty, oaths and laws are meaningless.</p><p><strong>Courage.</strong> You must be willing to do what needs to be done for the sake of order, even in the face of overwhelming odds. If you don't act, then who will?</p><p><strong>Responsibility.</strong> You must deal with the consequences of your actions, and you are responsible for fulfilling your duties and obligations.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa6112b1c2b42d79","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monster Slayer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Monster Slayer Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Monster Slayer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Protection from Evil and Good</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Magic Circle</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Hold Monster</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa652481d274653f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>By studying the magic of the planes, coming into contact with an extraplanar entity, or other circumstances you have acquired the ability to call forth a magical entity called an Eidolon.</p><p>To summon your Eidolon, you have to spend 10 minutes performing a magical ritual. Upon completion, your Eidolon appears in an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of you.</p><p>When the Eidolon drops to 0 hit points, it disappears, leaving behind no physical form. If your Eidolon is more than 1000 feet away from you or you die, it also disappears. You can also dismiss your Eidolon as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Your Eidolon can understand and speak all languages you speak. While it is on the same plane of existence as you, you can communicate with your Eidolon telepathically.</p><p>Additionally, as an Action, you can see through your Eidolon's eyes and hear what it hears until you end the effect (no action required), gaining the benefits of any special senses that the Eidolon has. During this time, you are deaf and blind with regard to your own senses.</p><p>Your Eidolon acts independently of you, but it always obeys your commands. In combat, it rolls its own initiative and acts on its own turn.</p><p>When you acquire this feature, you choose a template for your Eidolon that determines it's base statistics. Your options are: aquatic, avian, biped, quadruped, serpentine, and tauric. Your Eidolon shares your mental ability scores and all Saving Throw proficiencies.</p><p>Additionally, your Eidolon learns two skills of your choice.</p><p>If you have a bonus to spell save DC, you also apply this bonus to your Eidolon's Attack Rolls, damage rolls, and armor class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":10,"units":"minute"},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-giant-forest-blue.webp","_id":"sa670ed5800f8c1d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Combat Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your wit to turn the tide of battle. A creature that has a Bardic Inspiration die from you can use it for one of the following effects.</p><ul><li><strong>Defence.</strong> When the creature is hit by an Attack Roll, that creature can use its Reaction to roll the Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to its AC against that attack, potentially causing the attack to miss. If the attack still hits, the target takes half damage from it.</li><li><strong>Offence.</strong> Immediately after the creature hits a target with an Attack Roll, the creature can roll the Bardic Inspiration die twice and add the number rolled to the attack's damage against the target.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa676e516b16c5f4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Overwhelming Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The size of your weapon's damage die increases by 2 steps.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/shield-damaged-broken-orange.webp","_id":"sa6976669c68e353","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wholeness of Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to heal yourself. As an Action, you can regain hit points equal to three times your monk level. You must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"sa6b428116d6391d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Evolution Feats","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>In your study of planar lore, you have unearthed ways to augment your Eidolon, changing its form or otherwise imbuing it with new abilities.</p><p>You gain two evolution feats of your choice. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page. When you gain certain summoner levels, you gain additional evolution feats of your choice, as shown in the Evolution Feats column of the Summoner table.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the evolution feats you know and replace it with another evolution feat that you could learn at that level.</p><p>If an evolution feat has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the evolution feat at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/bat-giant-tattered-purple.webp","_id":"sa7e13ddb7fcca26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189548,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Second Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a limited well of physical and mental stamina that you can draw on. As a Bonus Action, you can use it to regain Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Fighter level.</p><p>You can use this feature twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain more uses of this feature, as shown in the Second Wind column of the Fighter Features table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.second-wind","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"heal","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["1d10 + @classes.fighter.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"sa86851d9575db76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428341,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hold the Line","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are not incapacitated, Attack Rolls against allies that benefit from your Formation Fighting cannot have Advantage. Additionally, you and all allies under the effect of your Formation Fighting add your Leadership ability modifier to Saving Throws and Ability Checks against being knocked prone, pushed, or otherwise forced to move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa880bd8c51bc72f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Cantrip","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the Light cantrip if you don't already know it. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of cleric cantrips you know.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/vines-thorned-glow-green.webp","_id":"sa8a21c84cad2ad8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Share Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell targeting yourself, you can also affect your Primal Companion beast with the spell if the beast is within 30 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa8a80ec305aba1b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Dreadful Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you focus your negative emotion into a lance of magical menace. Choose one creature you can see within 60 ft of you that can also you. The creature has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls and contested Ability Checks against you for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa8b7083ef2f658e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead. Moreover, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sa92ed49afaec609","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Air Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict bludgeoning or lightning damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa95b056ee2d2d7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know how to strike subtly and exploit a foe's distraction. Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack if you have Advantage on the Attack Roll. The attack must use a finesse or a ranged weapon.</p><p>You don't need Advantage on the Attack Roll if another enemy of the target is within 5 feet of it, that enemy isn't Incapacitated, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll.</p><p>The amount of the extra damage increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Sneak Attack column of the Rogue table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-arcane-pink.webp","_id":"sa9b39cb85f54721","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by an additional 10 feet. Additionally, whenever you finish a Short Rest, your Exhaustion level, if any, decreases by 1.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-bladed-boots-fire.webp","_id":"sa9d39945ba0ea1a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage caused by your Gathered Swarm counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saa2c4f209dcae1b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Formulas","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The number of mutagens you can concoct when you finish a rest, and the number of formulas you know, increases as you gain levels in the blood hunter class, as shown on the Mutagencraft table above. Additionally, when you learn a new mutagen formula, you can replace one formula you already know with a new mutagen formula. You choose four mutagen formulas to learn from the Optional Features page, and you can concoct one mutagen when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saa32867703f797d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant's Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned how to imbue yourself with the might of giants. As a Bonus Action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn't change.</li><li>You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</li><li>Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike can deal an extra 1d6 damage to a target on a hit.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saa7d008ddb89ae5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Amphibious","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can breathe air and water.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/amphibians/frog-water-teal.webp","_id":"saac746f96e7a00f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dervish Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing light or no armor and using no shield, you can use a Bonus Action to enter the Dervish Dance for 1 minute, gaining the benefits below. It ends early if you are Incapacitated and if you don medium or heavy armor or a shield. You can also end it early (no action required).</p><ul><li>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>On each of your turns, you can give all your melee weapon attacks the benefits of the Flurry or Cleave mastery (your choice). These do not limit your use of other masteries on your attacks, but you cannot use the same mastery twice on the same attack.</li><li>You have advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</li><li>Your AC increases by 1 + half your Proficiency (rounded down).</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Additionally, you can expend a use of your Second Wind to use it again (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sab219fe55acf636","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frozen Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you cast a Ranger spell using a Spell Slot, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier + half your Ranger level (rounded down). If the spell already gives you temporary hit points, they stack with the ones granted by this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sab284c75d5b1b76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can supernaturally inspire others through words, music, or dance. This inspiration is represented by your Bardic Inspiration die, which is a d6.</p><ul><li><strong>Using Bardic Inspiration.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can inspire another creature within 60 feet of yourself who can see or hear you. That creature gains one of your Bardic Inspiration dice. A creature can have only one Bardic Inspiration die at a time. Once within the next hour when the creature fails a D20 Test, the creature can roll the Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning the failure into a success. A Bardic Inspiration die is expended when it's rolled.</li><li><strong>Number of Uses.</strong> You can confer a Bardic Inspiration die a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). You regain one die when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li><li><strong>At Higher Levels.</strong> Your Bardic Inspiration die changes when you reach certain Bard levels, as shown in the Bardic Die column of the Bard Features table. The die becomes a d8 at level 5, a d10 at level 10, and a d12 at level 15.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"max(1, @abilities.cha.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"@scale.bard.inspiration","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sab3287e49ae0b88","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bastion of Law","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can tap into the grand equation of existence to imbue a creature with a shimmering shield of order. As an Action, you can expend 1 to 5 sorcery points to create a magical ward around yourself or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The ward lasts until you finish a Long Rest or until you use this feature again.</p><p>The ward is represented by a number of d8s equal to the number of sorcery points spent to create it. When the warded creature takes damage, it can expend a number of those dice, roll them, and reduce the damage taken by the total rolled on those dice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sab38deda268ec8b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Evolution Feat (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional evolution feat for which you meet the prequisites.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sab3ef56c3b4f09c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beauty's Refuge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mere presence is enough to inspire hope and determination in others. When you complete a Short or a Long Rest, up to 6 allies of your choice gain temporary hit points equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) plus twice your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sabd39ba8749f6ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Languages","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can speak, read, and write two additional languages.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sabed504386cf8a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Intimidating Shout","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you force all hostile creatures within 60 feet that can hear you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, a target deals half damage on its weapon attacks that hit until the start of your next turn.</p><p>This feature has no effect against creatures that are Immune to the Frightened condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac172492e94cff5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bruiser's Arsenal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in martial weapons, medium armor, shields, as well as the Intimidation skill. If you are already proficient in Intimidation, you gain expertise in it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac234d4a1541613","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fang and Claw","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal your choice of piercing or slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your fangs or claws to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blood-slash-foam-red.webp","_id":"sac4fc20a9da2d69","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of the Crown Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Command, Compelled Duel</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Warding Bond, Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Aura of Vitality, Spirit Guardians</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment, Guardian of Faith</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Circle of Power, Geas</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac78de7bdad211f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with armorsmith's tools. If you already have this Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"sacdfa3483dc424a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428319,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speech of the Woods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to converse with beasts and many fey.</p><p>You learn to speak, read, and write Sylvan. In addition, beasts can understand your speech, and you gain the ability to decipher their noises and motions. Most beasts lack the intelligence to convey or understand sophisticated concepts, but a friendly beast could relay what it has seen or heard in the recent past. This ability doesn't grant you friendship with beasts, though you can combine this ability with gifts to curry favor with them as you would with any nonplayer character.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sace2c5ddde26b00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428339,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against spells.</p><p>Furthermore, you have Resistance against the damage of spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sad810c925edec50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Throw Wide the Gates","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Gate spell without expending a spell slot and without a material component. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sad894e59390ed53","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Treacherous Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in deception or stealth. Additionally, you can use your Lay on Hands to target creature that cannot see you, that is not aware you are hostile to it or that is under some other effect that makes it non-hostile to you, e.g. the Charmed condition.</p><p>The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failure, the creature takes necrotic damage equal to the number of points spent from the pool. On a success, the creature takes half as much damage. You then regain hit points equal to the damage dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sade26850b951508","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Wit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your keen ability to assess tactical situations allows you to act quickly in battle. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Intelligence modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sae0a551f307ca2b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428379,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"sae2d30434ee83d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (8th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 8th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-face-black.webp","_id":"sae3e092917d4bdc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Constricting Grasp","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill. You can choose to grapple a creature with your coils instead of your hands. If you do so, you can attempt and maintain a grapple even when your hands are occupied, but your Speed is also reduced to 0 while you maintain the grapple. Any creature that is the same size or smaller than you has Disadvantage on skill checks to try and escape this grapple on subsequent turns. Any creature that is a smaller size than you is also restrained while Grappled in this manner.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/tentacles/tentacles-thing-green.webp","_id":"sae5a76cc5896cfc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to your astral self is complete, allowing you to unleash its full potential. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 3 ki points to summon the arms, visage, and body of your astral self and awaken it for 10 minutes. Alternatively, you can spend these ki points as part of the same Bonus Action you used for another Monk feature. This awakening ends early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>The cost is reduced by 1 each if you have currently summoned your astral arms and your astral visage.</p><p>While your astral self is awakened, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Armor of the Spirit.</strong> You gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class.</p><p><strong>Astral Barrage.</strong> Whenever you use the Extra Attack feature to attack twice, you can instead attack three times if all the attacks are made with your astral arms.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saea91c4ea3c9f4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Writhing Tide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can condense part of your swarm into a focused mass that lifts you up. As a Bonus Action, you gain a Fly Speed of 10 feet and can hover. This effect lasts for 1 minute or until you are Incapacitated.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saeababe4446ced1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonds of Solidarity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can forge an empowering bond among people who are at peace with one another. As an Action, you choose a number of willing creatures within 30 feet of you (this can include yourself) equal to your Proficiency bonus. You create a magical bond among them for 10 minutes or until you use this feature again. While any bonded creature is within 30 feet of another, the creature can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw it makes. Each creature can add the d4 no more than once per turn.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also spend a level 2+ spell slot to regain a use.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saeb45d29f84b253","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shielding Aurora","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke the Seeker's power to protect you from harm. As a Bonus Action, you create a whirling aurora of brilliant energy that swirls around you. Until the end of your next turn, you gain Resistance to all damage, and if a hostile creature ends its turn within 10 feet of you, it takes radiant damage equal to your warlock level + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf1b60e62c89718","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Constitution Saving Throws against Exhaustion made as a result of a forced march.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-bladed-boots-fire.webp","_id":"saf3489cc28bce78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire's Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to direct your inner fire to lash out at attackers. When you are hit by a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to make the attacker take fire damage equal to your kineticist level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf564c11626dbd1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Path","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose a path that shapes the nature of your rage from the list of available paths. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th levels.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/projectile-wave-arrow.webp","_id":"saf691dfa94217f0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Henotic Ascendence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the realm of the divine permanently changes you. You gain Resistance to the damage type you chose for the Harm effect of your Channel Divine Energy class feature. For every 10 years that pass, your body only ages 1 year. Additionally, the dice from your pool change to d10s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf85c72db580980","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189572,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Projection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spirit can become untethered from your physical form. As an Action, you can project your spirit from your body. The body you leave behind is Unconscious and in a state of suspended animation.</p><p>Your spirit resembles your mortal form in almost every way, replicating your game statistics but not your possessions. Any damage or other effects that apply to your spirit or physical body affects the other. Your spirit can remain outside your body for up to 1 hour or until your Concentration is broken (as if concentrating on a spell). When your projection ends, your spirit returns to your body or your body magically teleports to your spirit's space (your choice).</p><p>While projecting your spirit, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your spirit and body gain Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>When you cast a spell of the conjuration or necromancy school, the spell doesn't require verbal or somatic components or material components that lack a gold cost.</li><li>You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover. You can move through creatures and objects as if they were 3, but you take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.</li><li>While you are using your Form of Dread, once during each of your turns when you deal necrotic damage to a creature, you regain hit points equal to half the amount of necrotic damage dealt.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf9006feb1fb5da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanctuary Vessel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter your Genie's Vessel via the Bottled Respite feature, you can now choose up to five willing creatures that you can see within 30 feet of you, and the chosen creatures are drawn into the vessel with you.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can eject any number of creatures from the vessel, and everyone is ejected if you leave or die or if the vessel is destroyed.</p><p>In addition, anyone (including you) who remains within the vessel for at least 10 minutes gains the benefit of finishing a Short Rest, and anyone can add your Proficiency bonus to the number of hit points they regain if they spend any Hit Dice as part of a Short Rest there.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf901105d1b1725","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vicious Fangs","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal piercing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your fangs to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/fangs-teeth-bite.webp","_id":"safa118133b260b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Divine Spark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you point your Holy Symbol at another creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself and focus divine energy at it. Roll 2d8 and add your Cleric level and your Wisdom modifier. You either restore Hit Points to the creature equal to that total or force the creature to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the creature takes Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice) equal to that total. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage (round down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"2d8 + @abilities.wid.mod","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-glow-spiral-yellow.webp","_id":"safb9c3b277eecdb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unbreakable Majesty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can assume a magically majestic presence for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition. For the duration, whenever any creature hits you with an Attack Roll for the first time on a turn, the attacker must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or the attack misses instead, as the creature recoils from your majesty.</p><p>Once you assume this majestic presence, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saff54ed1f5973ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Step of the Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action. Alternatively, you can expend 1 Ki Point to take both the Disengage and Dash actions as a Bonus Action, and your jump distance is doubled for the turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/air-wave-gust-blue.webp","_id":"sb07514d85b9fda3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Delve and Climb","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage-orange.webp","_id":"sb0815eafaa92345","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Skirmisher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are difficult to pin down during a fight. You can move up to half your Speed as a Reaction when an enemy ends its turn within 10 feet of you. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb0a28bfbd523da7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fast Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can do one of the following.</p><ul><li><strong>Sleight of Hand.</strong> Make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check to pick a lock or disarm a trap with Thieves' Tools or to pick a pocket.</li><li><strong>Use an Object.</strong> Take the Utilize action, or take the Magic action to use a magic item that requires that action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/theft-pickpocket-bribery-brown.webp","_id":"sb0ab82498eeb1b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serpent's Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Blindsight range increases by 10 feet. No attack from within your Blindsight range has Advantage against you as long as you are not Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb0d80787b3ab046","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Hunter's Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you can take a Reaction to give yourself Resistance to that damage and any other damage of the same type until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/reptiles/serpent-horned-green.webp","_id":"sb134dcfe3ad1418","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Breath Weapon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to exhale destructive energy. Your draconic ancestry determines size, shape, and damage of the exhalation. Every creature in the area of a effect needs to make a Saving Throw against a DC of 8 + your CON, INT, or CHA modifier (your choice) + your Proficiency. The damage equals 4d6 on a failed save, and have as much on a successful one. The damage increases by 1d6 at levels 6, 11, and 16.</p><p>After you use your breath weapon, you can't use it again until you complete a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["(4+floor(((@details.level)-1)/5))d6",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/beam-jet-stream-trails-orange.webp","_id":"sb1d26b9c9e7e359","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Warding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Ancient magic lies so heavily upon you that it forms an eldritch ward. You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you have Resistance to damage from spells.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb1f3afe904f932e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189518,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire Lord","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of fire allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of flame.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You shed bright light in a 60 feet radius and dim light in a radius of 30 feet beyond that.</li><li>You gain Immunity to fire damage.</li><li>Creatures in the bright light have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against infusions that include the fire element.</li><li>You radiate intense heat in a 10 feet radius around you. Any creature of your choice that enters that radius for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, takes half your kinetic shape damage.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb204971135e4dfd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wings Unfurled","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Step of the Wind, you can unfurl spectral draconic wings from your back that vanish at the end of your turn. While the wings exist, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. While you have no uses available, you can spend 3 ki points to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb2199b9d1b2c3f6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supreme Sneak","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Stealth checks and you do not lose the benefits of being Hidden as long as you end your turn behind at least three-quarters cover or heavily obscured.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"sb21d4b6ad232844","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Icy Glare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself deals damage to you or forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to force the creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the target takes 4d8 cold damage and its Speed is reduced 0 until the start of your next turn. On a success, it takes half as much damage and its Speed isn't reduced. This damage ignores Resistance.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb22271a5e206eed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of the Forge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the forge grants you special abilities:</p><ul><li>You gain Resistance to fire damage.</li><li>While wearing heavy armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb23f779e9f58e8a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Glamour","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your fey qualities give you a supernatural charm. As a result, whenever you make a Charisma check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p>In addition, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Performance, or Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb26e5d4011c0f34","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Arcane Jolt and steel defender become more powerful:</p><ul><li>The extra damage and the healing of your Arcane Jolt both increase to 4d6.</li><li>Your steel defender gains a +2 bonus to Armor Class.</li><li>Whenever your steel defender uses its Deflect Attack, the attacker takes force damage equal to 1d4 + your Intelligence modifier.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-stone-earth-gray.webp","_id":"sb28e0377603a62e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see when you use your Action Surge. You can teleport before or after the additional action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb2a329ddee01456","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bovine Brawn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage-orange.webp","_id":"sb2ae266c4a3e92f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Accursed Magicks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to blend hemocraft and profane magic together, using one pool of dark power to feed the other. You gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p><p>Additionally, you can expend uses of your Blood Maledict to cast Warlock spells and Pact Magic spell slots to use Blood Curses as per the table below. This feature allows you to cast Pact Magic spells at a lower level than you currently have access to, but not higher. If you use a Blood Curse by expending a Pact Magic spell slot, any excess uses generated are regained instead. If you amplify a Blood Curse used in this manner, you do not roll separately for the hit point cost and gain, they nullify each other at a 1:1 ratio.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Accursed Magick Conversion</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Pact Magic Spell Slot</th><th scope=\"col\">Blood Maledict Cost/Regain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>1 use</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>1 use + hit point cost for amplifying 1 blood curse</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>2 uses</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>2 uses + hit point cost for amplifying 2 blood curses</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb2e42c02e4deb80","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Intimidating Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter a frenzy, you also adopt a menacing presence that frightens foes around you. Any hostile creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of you while you are in a frenzy or enters that area for the first time on a turn and can see or hear you, must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be Frightened of you until the start of its next turn.</p><p>If a creature's Saving Throw is successful, it is Immune to your Intimidating Presence for the next 24 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"sb33decaa7fc6b03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Irresistible Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Otto's Irresistible Dance spell prepared. You can cast it without expending a spell slot. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of the feature by expending four uses of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb38ad9789586f07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiotic Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are in Symbiosis, you can gain a bonus to your AC and Saving Throws equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb397dc9f6c4b857","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warping Implosion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unleash your aberrant power as a space-warping anomaly. As a Bonus Action, you can teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 120 feet of you. Immediately after you disappear, each creature within 30 feet of the space you left must make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 4d10 force damage and is pulled straight toward the space you left, ending in an unoccupied space as close to your former space as possible. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pulled.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb3ae5d117b90763","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Conquest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You constantly emanate a menacing aura while you're not Incapacitated. The aura extends 10 feet from you in every direction, but not through total cover.</p><p>Any creature of your choice that starts its turn in the aura takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier. If that creature is Frightened, this damage is doubled. Additionally, any creature in the aura that is Frightened, has its Speed reduced to 0.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb3ca5f429d385e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to fight with your Spiritual Weapon like a seamless unit, using it to attack as well as defend.</p><p>When a creature you can see hits you with an Attack Roll while your Spiritual Weapon is within 5 ft of you, you can use your Reaction to gain a +5 bonus to AC against that attack, potentially causing it to miss you.</p><p>If the attack misses, you can make one weapon attack or melee spell attack with your Spiritual Weapon against the attacker as part of this Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb3d4fb186ee8080","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Aquatic Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas with aquatic beasts.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/fish/fish-marlin-swordfight-blue.webp","_id":"sb3e4dc48f273caa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a plantlike aspect, granting you physical traits such as floral skin color, twiglike fingers, and leafs or flowers sprouting from your hair.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb415a2dc52265db","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Siphon Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>One of the things that contributes the most to the reputation Shadowborn have among other races, is their ability to harness residual life energy from the dead. For this reason, Shadowborn are very conscious of when they use this ability.</p><p>As an Action, you can siphon energy from a creature within 5 ft of you that has died within the last 24 hours. If you do so, you can spend hit dice as if you had taken a rest. You cannot use this feature more than once on the same creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"target has died within the last 24 hours and has not been targeted by this feature before"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":5,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hands-cloud-light-pink.webp","_id":"sb48602422e0c615","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Misty Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can slip in and out of the Feywild to move in a blink of an eye: you can cast Misty Step without expending a spell slot. You can do so a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, whenever you cast Misty Step, you can bring along one willing creature you can see within 5 feet of you. That creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice within 5 feet of your destination space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb4f02dbb64a554f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infectious Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you successfully inspire someone, the power of your eloquence can now spread to someone else. When a creature within 60 feet of you adds one of your Bardic Inspiration dice to its Ability Check, Attack Roll, or Saving Throw and the roll succeeds, you can use your Reaction to encourage a different creature (other than yourself) that can hear you within 60 feet of you, giving it a Bardic Inspiration die without expending any of your Bardic Inspiration uses.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). You regain one use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb4f562f79d0b184","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Arcana","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a draconic patron from the following table. Each patron is associated with a damage type.</p><p>Every time you gain access to a new spell level on your Dragon Expanded Spells table, including this one, you can replace one of the spells listed for that spell level with another spell of the same level that deals damage of the chosen type. You can change your choice for one spell learned in this manner whenever you gain another level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, you can change the damage type of any of your cantrips to the chosen type above when you cast them.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Patron</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Draconic Patron</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Jabberwock</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Night</td><td>Force</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Shadow</td><td>Necrotic</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>Sylvan</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5036d24c2f634d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428372,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to make your very presence a soothing balm. As an Action, you can move up to your Speed, without provoking Opportunity Attacks, and when you move within 5 feet of any other creature during this action, you can restore a number of hit points to that creature equal to 2d6 + your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1 hit point). A creature can receive this healing only once whenever you take this action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb50e7cb1b209c1a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rooted Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to twist and turn the ground beneath you. While you are in your guardian form, the ground within 30 feet of you is 3 for your enemies.</p><p>Additionally, you cannot be moved forcibly or knocked Prone while in your guardian form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5239199341275d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Skill Versatility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in 3 extra skills of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp","_id":"sb5823659d5727d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you aren't wearing any armor, your base Armor Class equals 10 plus your Constitution and Wisdom modifiers. You can use a Shield and still gain this benefit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"sb582f6f2f4330d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sb5acc9e1622e102","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your control of the air streams around you to help you dodge or otherwise ward off certain area effects, like the explosion of a fireball or a dragon's breath.</p><p>When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half damage if you fail.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5f1f5ff592d023","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Enveloping Winds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can surround yourself with a whirling torrent of air or a static field of crackling lightning, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier and all ranged weapon attacks against you are made with Disadvantage. Additionally, any gas, vapor, or fog that can be dispersed by a strong wind has no effect on you.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb60ce40cc90de31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Movement improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling during the move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/wave-water-teal.webp","_id":"sb61d4d6e0255132","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jack of All Trades","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can add half your Proficiency bonus, rounded down, to any Ability Check you make that doesn't already include your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-steel.webp","_id":"sb64cb4020280dde","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Guide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to control the weather in your vicinity. You and your companions do not suffer the effects of bad weather. Additionally, your travel speed is doubled if you are using a naval vessel for Overland Travel. Said vessel is likewise protected from bad weather effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb67601f51b9d146","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When your bonded familiar hits a creature you can see within 60 feet of you with a weapon attack on its turn, you can use your Reaction to expend a Spell Slot of 1st level or higher. The target creature takes damage of the type gained through your Familiar Bonus Damage equal to 1d8 per level of the spell slot.</p><p>Additionally, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or suffer one of the following effects until the end of your bonded familiar's next turn, based on your chosen Wild Domain:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Familiar Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>Target is Blinded.</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>Attack Rolls against the target have Advantage and any healing it receives is halved.</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>Target is Dazed.</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>Target is Restrained.</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>Target is knocked Prone and moved to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of its original position.</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>Attack Rolls against the target have Advantage. You or any of your allies regain hit points equal to your Witch level + your spellcasting ability modifier if they reduce the target to 0 hit points.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb68f29ee5339aa2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Litany of Purgation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature is affected by your Inspiring Surge, it can immediately repeat a Saving Throw against one on-going effect on it that normally allows for repeated Saving Throws at the end of its turn. If it spends an additional hit die, it can make this Saving Throw with Advantage. The target does not regain additional hitpoints from spending this additional hit die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb692ff9c2a174dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Elemental Shielding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and any allies within your Aura of Protection have Resistance to the damage type associated with the oath patron you have chosen for your Elemental Smite and make any Saving Throw related to them with Advantage: Cold (Marid), Fire (Efreeti), Lightning (Djinni), Poison (Dao).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb69d3c14273a333","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to psychic damage. When you have to make a Wisdom Saving Throw, you can make an Intelligence Saving Throw instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb6af855e8f9168e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb6e081f3d629834","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Atlas","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Adventurer's Atlas improves, gaining the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Safe Haven.</strong> When a map holder would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright, that creature can destroy its map. The creature's Hit Points instead change to a number equal to twice your Artificer level, and the creature is teleported to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you or another map holder of its choice.</p><p><strong>Unerring Path.</strong> If you are one of the map holders for your Adventurer's Atlas, you can cast Find the Path without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without needing spell components. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-eye-brown.webp","_id":"sb6f017bf59d8eac","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Action Surge (two uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Action Surge twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sb6f2ec274890a50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Imbuing Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can touch one nonmagical weapon and spend 2 sorcery points to imbue it with magic for 1 minute. For the duration, the weapon is considered magical for the purpose of overcoming Immunity and Resistance to nonmagical attacks.</p><p>For each additional 2 sorcery points you spend, you can give the weapon a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls and damage rolls (up to +3), stacking with existing bonuses on the weapon, up to a maximum of +5 for the Attack Roll bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"object"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"touch"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"sb6fc3232fe26134","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Falconian Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the battleaxe, longsword, aven javelin, and longbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/hand-grip-sword-white-brown.webp","_id":"sb709a7d24376674","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dreadful Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can augment your weapon strikes with mind-scarring magic, drawn from the gloomy hollows of the Feywild. When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d4 psychic damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn.</p><p>The extra damage increases to 2d4 when you reach 11th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb743d141f1dec8b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Powerful Build","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, and lift.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sb74e0b016affe8c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Exalted Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your presence on the field of battle is an inspiration to those dedicated to your cause. You can use your Bonus Action to gain the following benefits for 1 hour:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>You gain a Heroic Inspiration at the start of every one of your turns if you do not currently have one. Alternatively, you can give a Heroic Inspiration to one ally you can see within 30 ft of you and who does not already have one. You can do so even if you already have a Heroic Inspiration yourself.</li><li>All allies within 30 ft of you have Advantage on Wisdom Saving Throws.</li></ul><p>This effect ends early if you are Incapacitated or die. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb74e820889918d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Convergent Future","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can peer through possible futures and magically pull one of them into events around you, ensuring a particular outcome. When you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to ignore the die roll and decide whether the number rolled is the minimum needed to succeed or one less than that number (your choice).</p><p>The first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a Long Rest, you take 1d12 necrotic damage for each level (or CR if the creature has no levels) the target creature has. Each time you use this feature again before finishing a Long Rest, the damage increases by 1d12 per level/CR. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb7715b7ce6effc7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark One's Own Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on your patron to alter fate in your favor. When you make an Ability Check or a Saving Throw, you can use this feature to add a d10 to your roll. You can do so after seeing the initial roll but before any of the roll's effects occur.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/unholy/demon-fanged-horned-yellow.webp","_id":"sb79979b97ad2d25","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Magical Cunning feature, you regain all your expended Pact Magic spell slots and the use of your 6th and 7th level Mystic Arcanum spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/orb-ball-purple.webp","_id":"sb7b9aca50007ead","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189552,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Favored Enemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have significant experience studying, tracking, hunting, and even talking to a certain type of enemy commonly encountered in the wilds.</p><p>Choose a creature type. You gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with weapon attacks or ranger spells that use a weapon or piece of ammunition as a material component against the chosen type.</p><p>Additionally, you have Advantage on Wisdom and Intelligence checks that pertain to your favored enemies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp","_id":"sb7cdfd6efa61e76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Witchcraft","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your knowledge of your craft deepens. You learn two additional Witchcraft options. Additionally, you can select two Witchcraft options you know, which improve as described below:</p><p><strong>Amelioration.</strong> You can also use this feature on targets with the Confused, Dazed, Exhausted, Incapacitated, Paralyzed, and Stunned conditions.</p><p><strong>Cackle.</strong> You affect all creatures of your choice that can hear you within 60 feet.</p><p><strong>Evil Eye.</strong> You can use this feature as an Action or Bonus Action, but only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Familiar Focus.</strong> As an Action, you can switch positions with your bonded familiar if you can see it.</p><p><strong>Kettle Chant.</strong> The bonus to the listed crafting checks is now equal to your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Mind Fog.</strong> If the target fails the Concentration Saving Throw, it takes psychic damage equal to half your Witch level + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Minor Prophecy.</strong> You gain 1 additional use of this feature. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Witch Spittle.</strong> The healing from this feature is doubled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb7d8ff11bc29718","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189562,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Verdant Reprisal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Enemies affected by your Protector's Mark have Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you while they are within 30 feet of you.</p><p>Additionally, if an affected enemy attacks a creature other than you while within that range, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed and make a weapon attack against that enemy. If you are mounted, your mount moves up to its own Speed instead. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1) and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a spell slot of 2nd level or higher to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb8aaf56bf1c6851","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Great Stature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll.</p><p>Moreover, the extra damage you deal with your Giant's Might feature increases to 1d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb8dd8ec23c64586","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189504,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb8f1d4f090dd835","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Chivy (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw or use its Reaction to move as far from you as it can, taking the safest route.</li><li><strong>Stupefy (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target must make an Intelligence Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes before the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb92e59d65ede7bc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Sanctified Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast the Hunter's Mark spell or transfer its effect to a new target, you can transform the spell into a Sanctified Mark as part of the same Bonus Action. The effect persists while this casting of Hunter's Mark is active, including when you select a new target. Sanctified Mark retains all the usual effects of Hunter's Mark in addition to the following:</p><ul><li>The target of this effect cannot benefit from Invisibility against you. And the range of any Locate X spell you cast to track the creature is doubled.</li><li>When you hit the target with a weapon attack, you can choose to change the damage type of your weapon and Sanctified Mark to radiant or necrotic.</li><li>The spell does not count towards your Concentration limit, though you still have to roll Concentration Saving Throws as normal. If you fail a Concentration Saving Throws, you lose Concentration on all spells you are concentrating on.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb939251ac1d184c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Nature's Wrath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to conjure spectral vines around nearby creatures. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 15 feet of yourself must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw or have the Restrained condition for 1 minute. A Restrained creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb94025f378a5099","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Vengeance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tenets of the Oath of Vengeance vary by paladin, but all the tenets revolve around punishing wrongdoers by any means necessary. Paladins who uphold these tenets are willing to sacrifice even their own righteousness to mete out justice upon those who do evil, so the paladins are often neutral or lawful neutral in alignment. The core principles of the tenets are brutally simple.</p><p><strong>Fight the Greater Evil.</strong> Faced with a choice of fighting my sworn foes or combating a lesser evil, I choose the greater evil.</p><p><strong>No Mercy for the Wicked.</strong> Ordinary foes might win my mercy, but my sworn enemies do not.</p><p><strong>By Any Means Necessary.</strong> My qualms can't get in the way of exterminating my foes.</p><p><strong>Restitution.</strong> If my foes wreak ruin on the world, it is because I failed to stop them. I must help those harmed by their misdeeds.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb94aa8575527741","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transport","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and up to 5 creatures of your choosing that you can see are grasped by tentacles that emerge from the portal. A second portal opens at a point of your choice within 100 miles that you have visited in the past 24 hours, depositing you and your chosen allies there.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb97f8cc1bfffec4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Branches of the Tree","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever a creature you can see starts its turn within 30 feet of you while your Rage is active, you can take a Reaction to summon spectral branches of the World Tree around it. The target must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC 8 plus your Strength modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or be teleported to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of yourself or in the nearest unoccupied space you can see. After the target teleports, you can reduce its Speed to 0 until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba4f0fbbb86ca3d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Walker in Dreams","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of the Feywild grants you the ability to travel mentally or physically through dreamlands.</p><p>When you finish a Short Rest, you can cast one of the following spells, without expending a spell slot or requiring material components: Dream (with you as the messenger), Scrying, or Teleportation Circle.</p><p>This use of Teleportation Circle is special. Rather than opening a portal to a permanent Teleportation Circle, it opens a portal to the last location where you finished a Long Rest on your current plane of existence. If you haven't taken a Long Rest on your current plane, the spell fails but isn't wasted.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba559b4ef6f3428","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earthen Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/strike-fist-stone-light.webp","_id":"sba6e14912e10302","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weaver of Weal and Woe","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Bane and Fortune's Favor spells prepared.</p><p>When you cast Bane, its range increases to 60 feet and you can cast Fortune's Favor without providing the material component. You can cast Fortune's Favor in this manner three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba6ee75c8a08414","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage or it fails its Saving Throw against such a spell, it also suffers the Lacerated condition for 1 minute. If the spell natively causes them to become Lacerated, the damage they take from the condition increases by an amount equal to your Proficiency.</p><p>At the end of their turns, they can make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC to end the condition.</p><p>They do not make this Saving Throw if the spell triggering this effect is still affecting them and allows for repeat Saving Throws on subsequent turns. In such a case, the Lacerated condition instead ends when they succeed on the repeat Saving Throw for that spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbab90d2155b33cf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Treachery Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Charm Person, Expeditious Retreat</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Invisibility, Mirror Image</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Gaseous Form, Haste</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Confusion, Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Dominate Person, Passwall</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbabeee008dfbf5d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tongue of the Sun and Moon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to touch the ki of other minds so that you understand all spoken languages. Moreover, any creature that can understand a language can understand what you say.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/day-night-sunset-sunrise.webp","_id":"sbaca8edae4137b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Saint of the Currents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to poison and disease and you can walk on water as per the Water Walk spell.</p><p>Additionally, all your water-based spells and your Channel Divinity: Cleaning Current have their area of affect doubled and you can choose to exempt a number of creatures equal to your WIS modifier from their effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb3afb62e9eba9c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can conduct a magical ritual that wards off those that would do you and your companions harm. You have to spend 8 hours during downtime before a rest to prepare the ritual. You and your companions do not suffer a random combat encounter during the night. If a combat encounter happens through different circumstances, none of you can be Surprised and are automatically woken at the start of combat.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb5a5c12a4cdf03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your scholarly efforts bear fruit. While studying magic, you also specialized in an academic field of study. Choose one of the following skills: Arcana, History, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, or Religion. Your gain Proficiency in the chosen skill. If you are already proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-embossed-spiral-purple-white.webp","_id":"sbb6f987ee930d3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Piercing Thorns","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your command of primal magic allows you to enhance your attacks with thorns. Once during each of your turns, you can deal an additional 1d6 piercing damage to one creature you hit with a weapon attack. This damage increases to 2d6 when your reach 11th level in this class.</p><p>If your weapon counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage, this damage does as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb91c9824283b10","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Create Thrall","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to infect a humanoid's mind with the alien magic of your patron. You can use your action to touch an Incapacitated humanoid. That creature is then Charmed by you until a Remove Curse spell is cast on it, the Charmed condition is removed from it, or you use this feature again.</p><p>You can communicate telepathically with the Charmed creature as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb997c0613b9100","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fool's Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Jesters seem to have a knack for pulling themselves out of tight situations, transforming what looks like sure failure into an embarrassing but effective success.</p><p>You can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration after you fail an Ability Check, fail a Saving Throw, or miss with an Attack Roll. Roll a Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to your attack, Saving Throw, or Ability Check, using the new result in place of the failed one.</p><p>If using this ability grants you a success on the attack, Saving Throw, or Ability Check, note the number you rolled on the Bardic Inspiration die. The DM can then apply that result as a penalty to an attack or check you make, and you cannot use this ability again until you suffer this drawback. When the DM invokes this penalty, describe an embarrassing gaffe or mistake you make as part of the affected die roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb9c761c299e2b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sigils of Warding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add Glyph of Warding to your spellbook and it doesn't count against the number of prepared spells for you. You can replace the material component of the spell with a use of one of your runes.</p><p>Additionally, you can also choose objects you or someone else is wearing as valid targets for the spell. If you do so, you cannot choose the Spell Glyph option of the spell.</p><p>You can place only one glyph in this manner and if you place a new one in this manner, the first one disappears.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast Glyph of Warding, you can choose a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier. The chosen creatures are exempt from the Glyph's effect when it is triggered.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbbb2a7f787b57e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Archer Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn magical theory or some of the secrets of nature—typical for practitioners of this elven martial tradition. You choose to gain Proficiency in either the Arcana or the Nature skill, and you choose to learn either the Prestidigitation or the Druidcraft cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbc316684ef0dce1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kiss of the Spider Queen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the Spider Queen's malevolence into a deadly kiss. As an Action, you touch a creature within your reach. The target takes 12d10 poison or psychic damage (your choice), or half as much on a successful Constitution save. A creature Charmed by you has Disadvantage on its Saving Throw. After you use this ability, you cannot cast it again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbc4518b5c150bf4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamystic Arts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to blend your mastery of body and mind with your mystic arts to modify your spells and Unarmed Attacks; you gain two Metamystic options of your choice from the list below. You use the chosen options to temporarily modify one spell you cast, with additional benefits to your Unarmed Attacks as described. To use an option, you must spend the number of Ki Points that it costs. You can use only one Metamystic option on a spell and subsequent Unarmed Attacks this turn.</p><p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest you can replace one metamystic art you know with another one. </p><h5>Distant Arts</h5><p>When you cast a spell on your turn that has a range of 30 feet or greater, you can spend 1 Ki point to also give that same range to your Unarmed Attacks this turn.</p><h5>Empowered Arts</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend a number of Ki points up to your Wisdom modifier to reroll a number of damage dice equal to the number of Ki points expended. You can then reroll the weapon damage die on a number of Unarmed Attacks you make this turn, up to the number of Ki points expended. You must use the new rolls.</p><h5>Swift Arts</h5><p>When you use your Flurry of Blows, you can spend 2 Ki points to cast one of your Sorcerer cantrips that has a cast time of an Action in place of one of the attacks.</p><h5>Twinned Arts</h5><p>When you cast a spell that targets only one creature and doesn't have a range of self, you can spend a number of Ki points equal to the spell's level to target a second creature in range with the same spell (1 Ki point if the spell is a cantrip). You can spend up to 4 additional Ki points. For each additiona Ki point expended, one of your Unarmed Attacks this turn can target a second creature within their reach, using the original attack and damage roll.</p><p>To be eligible, a spell must be incapable of targeting more than one creature at the spell's current level. For example, Magic Missile and Scorching Ray aren't eligible, but Ray of Frost and Chromatic Orb are.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbc994d09631f665","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Farseer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The range of your Minor Prophecy increases to 120 feet and you can turn the roll on the D20 into a 7 or 13 (your choice).</p><p>When you roll Initiative, you regain one use of Minor Prophecy.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbcc3a7fd5427b65","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knightly Valor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You cannot be Frightened or Charmed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbcc3a91c6e71e28","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Friendly Fungi","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The radius of your mushroom circles increases to 20 feet and when you activate your Magic Mushrooms, you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your spellcasting ability modifier from the effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbcd94f9ffc182b2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189565,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Training in War and Song (Bladesinging)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with light armor, and you gain Proficiency with one type of one-handed melee weapon of your choice.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Performance skill if you don't already have it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbcdc4e6463cd0b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blaze of Glory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can delay death for an instant to perform a final heroic act.</p><p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points by an attacker you can see, even if you would be killed outright, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed toward the attacker and make one melee weapon attack against it, as long as the movement brings it within your reach. You make this attack with Advantage. If the attack hits, the creature takes an extra 5d10 fire damage and an extra 5d10 damage of the weapon's type. You then fall Unconscious and begin making death Saving Throws as normal, or you die if the damage you took would have killed you outright.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbd0793ab7d99439","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell-Storing Item","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch one Simple or Martial weapon or one item that you can use as a Spellcasting Focus, and you store a spell in it, choosing a level 1, 2, or 3 Artificer spell that has a casting time of an action and doesn't require a Material component that is consumed by the spell (you needn't have the spell prepared).</p><p>While holding the object, a creature can take a Magic action to produce the spell's effect from it, using your spellcasting ability modifier. If the spell requires Concentration, the creature must concentrate. Once a creature has used the object to produce the spell's effect, the object can't be used this way again until the start of the creature's next turn.</p><p>The spell stays in the object until it's been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum of twice) or until you use this feature again to store a spell in an object.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/beam-impact-purple.webp","_id":"sbd0bcf4c7837fbd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Brutal Strike (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The extra damage of your Brutal Strike increases to 2d10. In addition, you can use two different Brutal Strike effects whenever you use your Brutal Strike feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"sbd6ba36dc81eb82","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Protection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you or a friendly creature within 10 feet of you must make a Saving Throw, the creature gains a bonus to the Saving Throw equal to your Charisma modifier (with a minimum bonus of +1). You must be conscious to grant this bonus.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-tornado-wall-blue.webp","_id":"sbd95984cf49c04d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have dedicated yourself to one of the following sacred roles of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Protector.</strong> Trained for battle, you gain Proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Heavy armor.</li><li><strong>Thaumaturge.</strong> You know one extra cantrip from the Cleric spell list. In addition, your mystical connection to the divine gives you a bonus to your Intelligence (Arcana or Religion) checks. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/barrier-shield-winged-cross.webp","_id":"sbdbf292578b65bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189482,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a Warlock spell that deals damage, you can change its damage type to Psychic. In addition, when you cast a Warlock spell that is an Enchantment or Illusion, you can do so without Verbal or Somatic components.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbdc411717f6f897","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428369,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d10s. They turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe36163682e24f6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Demiurgic Colossus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The primordial power of your rage intensifies. When you rage, your reach now increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Huge, and you can now use your Mighty Impel to move creatures that are Large or smaller.</p><p>In addition, the extra damage dealt by your Elemental Cleaver feature increases to 2d6.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe401a609fe8b3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Protective Canopy.</strong> While you are shifted, your reach increases by 10 feet and allies within 10 feet of you have half-cover.</li><li><strong>Blinding Beauty.</strong> As an Action, you can force every creature of your choice within 30 feet of you that you can see and that can see you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, a target is Blinded for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the target can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success. Once a creature has succeeded on the Saving Throw, it is Immune to this feature for the next 24 hours.</li><li>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 4th Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li><li><strong>Aggressive Effluvia.</strong> Hostile creatures that start their turn within 30 feet of you or enter that space for the first time on a turn, take necrotic damage equal to double your Formshift Damage. Creatures that are Poisoned or have hit points equal to half or less of their maximum, take double damage from this feature. If you are Unconscious or dead, this effect disappears after 1d4 days.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe45610f2baa952","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189540,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. This energy is represented by your Psionic Energy dice, which are each a d6. You have a number of these dice equal to twice your Proficiency bonus, and they fuel various psionic powers you have, which are detailed below.</p><p>Some of your powers expend the Psionic Energy die they use, as specified in a power's description, and you can't use a power if it requires you to use a die when your dice are all expended. You regain all your expended Psionic Energy dice when you finish a Long Rest. In addition, as a Bonus Action, you can regain one expended Psionic Energy die, but you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach certain levels in this class, the size of your Psionic Energy dice increases: at 5th level (d8), 11th level (d10), and 17th level (d12).</p><p>The powers below use your Psionic Energy dice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe60e483033c4f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aegis of Faith","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any creature that currently has temporary hitpoints from your Armor of Faith, is also considered to be under the effect of the Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe891463e622c16","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to read the barriers between the planes, making it easier for you to draw forth more powerful creatures. When you expend a spell slot to cast a conjuration or necromancy spell that summons creatures, the spell counts as a number of spell levels lower for you for the purposes of which level of spell slot it requires. This reduction is equal to half your proficiency (rounded down). Further, it determines when you can learn these spells and also affects spells cast at a higher level. This feature cannot reduce the level of a spell below 1st.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe8efbe018757dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystical Connection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You now have the ability to nudge which spirits of Spirits from Beyond you channel. Whenever you roll on the Spirits from Beyond table, you can roll the die twice and choose which of the two effects to bestow. If you roll the same number on both dice, you can ignore the number and choose any effect on the table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbedb1ad3b25ca72","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Right Tool for the Job","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to produce exactly the tool you need: with thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand, you can magically create one set of artisan's tools in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. This creation requires 1 hour of uninterrupted work, which can coincide with a Short or a Long Rest. Though the product of magic, the tools are nonmagical, and they vanish when you use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/construction-carpentry-hammer.webp","_id":"sbee2a6e3c681f52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stroke of Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a marvelous knack for succeeding when you need to. If you fail a D20 Test, you can turn the roll into a 20.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sbef2c4f2fb640ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bestial Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The feral power within you increases, causing the natural weapons of your Form of the Beast to count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>You can also alter your form to help you adapt to your surroundings. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you finish your next Short or a Long Rest:</p><ul><li>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you can breathe underwater.</li><li>You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed, and you can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an Ability Check.</li><li>When you jump, you can make a Strength (Athletics) check and extend your jump by a number of feet equal to the check's total. You can make this special check only once per turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbf0a5c7390bad23","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hardened Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed and Frightened, and you have a bonus to Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma Saving Throws equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"sbf4faf374f00a36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Devastating Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you score a critical hit with a weapon attack, you gain a bonus to that weapon's damage roll equal to your level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbf840d16ac68edb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Menacing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Intimidation skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/water-elemental-blue-teeth.webp","_id":"sbf8b03d5a1876ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sentinel Raven","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the service of a spirit sent by the Raven Mother to watch over you. The spirit assumes the form and game statistics of a raven, and it always obeys your commands, which you can give telepathically while it is within 100 feet of you.</p><p>While the raven is perched on your shoulder, you gain darkvision with a range of 30 feet and a bonus to your passive Wisdom (Perception) score and to Wisdom (Perception) checks. The bonus equals your Charisma modifier. While perched on your shoulder, the raven can't be targeted by any attack or other harmful effect; only you can cast spells on it; it can't take damage; and it is Incapacitated.</p><p>You can see through the raven's eyes and hear what it hears while it is within 100 feet of you. In combat, you roll initiative for the raven and control how it acts. If it is slain by a creature, you gain Advantage on all Attack Rolls against the killer for the next 24 hours.</p><p>The raven doesn't require sleep. While it is within 100 feet of you, it can awaken you from sleep as a Bonus Action. The raven vanishes when it dies, if you die, or if the two of you are separated by more than 5 miles.</p><p>At the end of a Short or a Long Rest, you can call the raven back to you—no matter where it is or whether it died—and it reappears within 5 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbfd8f00b75ca694","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428370,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channeler","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to contact spirits beyond the grave, letting their power and knowledge flow through you. You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Guiding Whispers.</strong> You know the Guidance cantrip. It has a range of 60 feet when you cast it.</li><li><strong>Spiritual Focus.</strong> You employ tools that aid you in channeling spirits. You gain a Gaming Set (Playing Cards). You have Proficiency with this Gaming Set, and you can use the cards or one of the following items as a Spellcasting Focus for your Bard spells: Arcane Focus (Crystal or Orb), Candle, or Ink Pen.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0111e095ef9301","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Empowerment","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of a lunar phase saturates your being. Whenever you choose a lunar phase to affect your magic, you also gain the following benefit associated with that phase:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon:</strong> You shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. In addition, you and creatures of your choice have Advantage on Saving Throws while within the bright light you shed.</li><li><strong>New Moon:</strong> You have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. In addition, while you are in dim light or darkness, Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you.</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon:</strong> You have Resistance to necrotic and radiant damage</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc080541007a5440","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189546,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twilight Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The twilight that you summon offers a protective embrace: you and your allies have half cover while in the sphere created by your Twilight Sanctuary.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0acd15ad39bb04","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Initiate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Arcana skill, and you gain two cantrips of your choice from the wizard spell list. For you, these cantrips count as cleric cantrips.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you gain access to a new spell level of your domain spells, including at this level, you can exchange one domain spell from that spell level for another spell from the wizard spell list.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0d5582b0f1351e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strong Jaws","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill. You can grapple creatures using your jaws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-long-red.webp","_id":"sc157f7f1c5b5c0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Divine Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can open your awareness to detect Celestials, Fiends, and Undead. For the next 10 minutes or until you have the Incapacitated condition, you know the location of any creature of those types within 60 feet of yourself, and you know its creature type. Within the same radius, you also detect the presence of any place or object that has been consecrated or desecrated, as with the Hallow spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp","_id":"sc15b2e29cb546ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ascendant Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The maximum number of Profane Augmentations that can be grafted to your companion increases to three and the maximum for ability scores and AC conferred by the grafted body part increases to 22.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc175d895e4a26b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Profane Recuperation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you spend a Hit Die to regain hit points, you add your Hemocraft modifier to the roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc17b2c5636a6046","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Emissary of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in persuasion. Additionally, when you use your Lay on Hands, you can spend 5 points from the pool to cast the sanctuary spell on the target without components and a spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc17c36a918cde93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Siphon Shadows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to necrotic damage. When you are subject to necrotic damage from any source except cantrips, you are instead healed for half the amount of the damage you would have taken.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hand-claw-glow-orange.webp","_id":"sc1938e54b349dea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tentacles slam into your foes. Pick up to 5 creatures that you can see within 30 ft. of the portal. Those creatures must make Dexterity Saving Throws against your Warlock spell save DC. Creatures that fail their Saving Throws take 10d6 bludgeoning damage and are Restrained for 1 minute. Creatures that succeed take half the bludgeoning damage and are not Restrained. On its turn, a Restrained creature can use its action to attempt Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your Warlock spell save DC to end its Restrained condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc1fbb342a261c4a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metakinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You further evolve your ability to twist your chosen elements to your needs. You gain access to three of the following Metakinesis options of your choice, all of which modify your kinetic shape.</p><p>You can only use one Metakinesis option with your kinetic shape, unless otherwise noted.</p><h5>Careful Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that forces other creatures to make a Saving Throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the shape's full force. To do so, you spend 1 kinesis point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its Saving Throws against the blast and takes no damage if it would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Distant Kinesis</h5><p>When you use a kinetic shape, you can spend 1 kinesis point to double its range.</p><h5>Empowered Kinesis</h5><p>When you roll damage for your kinetic shape, you can spend 1 kinesis point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p><p>You can use Empowered Kinesis even if you have already used a different Metakinesis option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Extended Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that makes it last more than 1 round, you can spend 1 kinesis point to double its duration, to a maximum duration of 24 hours.</p><h5>Heightened Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that forces a creature to make a Saving Throw to resist its effects, you can spend 2 kinesis points to give one target of the shape Disadvantage on all its Saving Throws made against the effect.</p><h5>Twinned Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that doesn't have a range of self and is incapable of targeting more than one creature, you can spend 3 kinesis points to have it target a second creature within range as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-beam-pink.webp","_id":"sc1ff24bde46d74b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Glory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tenets of the Oath of Glory drive a paladin to attempt heroics that might one day shine in legend.</p><p><strong>Actions over Words.</strong> Strive to be known by glorious deeds, not words.</p><p><strong>Challenges Are but Tests.</strong> Face hardships with courage, and encourage your allies to face them with you.</p><p><strong>Hone the Body.</strong> Like raw stone, your body must be worked so its potential can be realized.</p><p><strong>Discipline the Soul.</strong> You must marshal the discipline to overcome failings within yourself that threaten to dim the glory of you and your friends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc210089bd3cc9f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Consuming Fervor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to channel your zeal into unchecked ferocity.</p><p>When you roll fire or radiant damage, you can use your Channel Divinity to deal maximum damage instead of rolling.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc21b8a103cfd34d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Concerted Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your allies form a more effective fighting force. When you use the attack action on your turn, an ally of your choice within 60 feet that can see or hear you can use its Reaction to make a weapon attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-strike-triple-blue.webp","_id":"sc22900edf9d8cbc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Truth-seeker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are proficient in your choice of three of the following skills: Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Medicine, and Religion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-slit-orange.webp","_id":"sc234464b7198e0d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mixed Heritage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose the single strongest influence of your parentage from the following:</p><p>Human: You gain Proficiency in one skill</p><p>High Elf: You gain the Cantrip racial trait.</p><p>Wood Elf: You gain the Mask of the Wild racial and Fleet of foot racial traits.</p><p>Dark Elf: Your gain the Dark Elf Spellcasting trait, excluding Healing Spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/group.webp","_id":"sc24af6e44516499","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Domain Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed on the Fate Domain Spells table. See the Divine Domain class feature for how domain spells work.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fate Domain Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cleric Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Domain Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Dissonant Whispers, Heroism, See Invisibility, Fortune's Favor</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Beacon of Hope, Clairvoyance</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Death Ward, Divination</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Commune, Geas</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc275dbd855d0de8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unleash the Kraken","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call upon your patron for aid. As an Action, you open a portal at a point you can see within 30 ft. of you and choose one of the following effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc276693283ddb21","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Searing Vengeance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or an ally within 60 feet of you is about to make a Death Saving Throw, you can unleash radiant energy to save the creature. The creature regains Hit Points equal to half its Hit Point maximum and can end the Prone condition on itself. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of the creature takes Radiant damage equal to 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier, and each has the Blinded condition until the end of the current turn.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc27e414a3d7e00f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crescent Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can harness your connection to Vaeraustraee to emulate her warrior aspect, entering the Cresent Dance. To do so, you can't be wearing medium or heavy armor or using a shield. It graces you with supernatural speed, agility, and focus.</p><p>You can use a Bonus Action to start the Crescent Dance, which lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you don medium or heavy armor or a shield. You can also dismiss the Crescent Dance at any time you choose (no action required).</p><p>While your Crescent Dance is active, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You gain a bonus to your AC equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</li><li>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</li><li>You gain a bonus to any Constitution Saving Throws you make to maintain Concentration on a spell. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</li><li>If you currently have a Spiritual Weapon summoned via the spell of the same name and you move on your turn, you can move your Spiritual Weapon the same distance.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice. You regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc2866fe5a1e6eee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Zealous Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to channel divine power to inspire zealotry in others. As a Bonus Action, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you that can hear you gain Advantage on Attack Rolls and Saving Throws until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. If you've run out of uses of this feature, you can expend one use of your Rage, choosing to activate this feature instead of Rage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc28949054466b8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Action Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use it again. Starting at 17th level, you can use it twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.action-surge","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sc290e756fbc497a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428341,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Breaker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you restore hit points to an ally with a spell of 1st level or higher, you can also end one spell of your choice on that creature. The level of the spell you end must be equal to or lower than the level of the spell slot you use to cast the healing spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc3bdbb9386b00e0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Destructive Wrath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to wield the power of the storm with unchecked ferocity.</p><p>When you roll lightning or thunder damage, you can use your Channel Divinity to deal maximum damage, instead of rolling.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc3cd4e575887985","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silvertongued","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Persuasion, Intimidation, and Deception skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/mouth-smile-deception-purple.webp","_id":"sc3e2d40cf72043e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warded Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar have Immunity to the Confused condition and Resistance to psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc415ee731c64ac8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Healer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The healing spells you cast on others heal you as well. When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that restores hit points to a creature other than you, you regain hit points equal to 2 × the spell's level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"sc476c4b4a25794c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blackguard's Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to slip away from your foes. Immediately after you are hit by an attack, you can use your Reaction to turn Invisible and teleport up to 60 feet to a spot you can see. You remain Invisible until the end of your next turn or until you attack, deal damage, or force a creature to make a Saving Throw. Once you use this feature, you must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc4899a5dc6e8570","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Tinkering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to invest a spark of magic into mundane objects. To use this ability, you must have thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand. You then touch a Tiny nonmagical object as an Action and give it one of the following magical properties of your choice:</p><ul><li>The object sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet.</li><li>Whenever tapped by a creature, the object emits a recorded message that can be heard up to 10 feet away. You utter the message when you bestow this property on the object, and the recording can be no more than 6 seconds long.</li><li>The object continuously emits your choice of an odor or a nonverbal sound (wind, waves, chirping, or the like). The chosen phenomenon is perceivable up to 10 feet away.</li><li>A static visual effect appears on one of the object's surfaces. This effect can be a picture, up to 25 words of text, lines and shapes, or a mixture of these elements, as you like.</li></ul><p>The chosen property lasts indefinitely. As an Action, you can touch the object and end the property early.</p><p>You can bestow magic on multiple objects, touching one object each time you use this feature, though a single object can only bear one property at a time. The maximum number of objects you can affect with this feature at one time is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one object). If you try to exceed your maximum, the oldest property immediately ends, and then the new property applies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"you must have thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"object"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"touch"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/runes-etched-steel-blade.webp","_id":"sc4ab9d21ff73fed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189463,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Inspiring Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Leadership ability modifier to the number of hitpoints targets regain from your Inspiring Surge.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sc4afdcf80417163","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lightning Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to lightning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/fist-unarmed-strike-blue-green.webp","_id":"sc4c7f23c73a2171","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bulwark of Force","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can shield yourself and others with telekinetic force. As a Bonus Action, you can choose creatures, which can include you, that you can see within 30 feet of you, up to a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one creature). Each of the chosen creatures is protected by half cover for 1 minute or until you're Incapacitated.</p><p>Once you take this Bonus Action, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc52442b0cff1dc9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Cunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use up to two Cunning Strike effects when you deal Sneak Attack damage, paying the die cost for each effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-blood-red.webp","_id":"sc53693eac3becf5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellguard Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you see a creature within your reach casting a spell with Verbal, Somatic, or Material components, you can take a Reaction to make a melee attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike against that creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc540a51d762a301","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable (two uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Indomitable twice between Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"sc577d957cfc3779","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to inspire your allies to draw on their hidden reserves and keep fighting. As a Bonus Action, choose a number of allies equal to half your Proficiency (rounded up) within 60 feet that can see or hear you and aren't incapacitated. A target can immediately spend a hit die as if it had taken a rest, gaining hit points as normal.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"sc63374d0b16f5d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspired Ferocity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally that is currently affected by your Warcry lands a critical hit, it deals additional damage equal to half your warlord level (rounded down) + your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc63b46a858b9408","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189561,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Sorcerer level specified in the Arcane Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Arcane Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Detect Magic, Magic Missile, Misty Step, Nystul's Magic Aura</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Counterspell, Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Arcane Eye, Spell Turning</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Circle of Power, Spell Mantle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc647b581c6039f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189547,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weapon Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn a ritual that creates a magical bond between yourself and one weapon. You perform the ritual over the course of 1 hour, which can be done during a Short Rest. The weapon must be within your reach throughout the ritual, at the conclusion of which you touch the weapon and forge the bond.</p><p>Once you have bonded a weapon to yourself, you can't be Disarmed of that weapon unless you are Incapacitated. If it is on the same plane of existence, you can summon that weapon as a Bonus Action on your turn, causing it to teleport instantly to your hand.</p><p>You can have up to two bonded weapons, but can summon only one at a time with your Bonus Action. If you attempt to bond with a third weapon, you must break the bond with one of the other two.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc676ad8ce6a9d72","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Bone-Chilling Cold","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to inflict your enemies with a deep, biting cold that cripples their ability to fight or cast spells.</p><p>As an Action, you present your holy symbol and choose a number of creatures up to equal to your Proficiency you can see within 30 feet of you. Each affected creature has to make a CON Saving Throw. Any creature affected by your Winter's Touch class feature has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw.</p><p>On a failure, their movement Speed is halved and they have Disadvantage on Ability Checks and Attack Rolls for 1 minute. If the creature attempts to cast a spell with a casting time of 1 action, roll a d20. On an 11 or higher, the creature completes the spell as normal. On a 10 or lower, the spell is lost. At the end of their turn, they can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success.</p><p>This feature has no effect on creatures that are Immune to cold damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc67ef40bbc51f51","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428337,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summon Wildfire Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can summon the primal spirit bound to your soul. As an Action, you can expend one use of your Wild Shape feature to summon your wildfire spirit, rather than assuming a beast form.</p><p>The spirit appears in an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you. Each creature within 10 feet of the spirit (other than you) when it appears must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take 2d6 fire damage.</p><p>The spirit is friendly to you and your companions and obeys your commands. See this creature's game statistics in the Wildfire Spirit stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. You determine the spirit's appearance. Some spirits take the form of a humanoid figure made of gnarled branches covered in flame, while others look like beasts wreathed in fire.</p><p>In combat, the spirit obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, the spirit acts on its own.</p><p>The spirit manifests for 1 hour, until it is reduced to 0 hit points, until you use this feature to summon the spirit again, or until you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc6a9aa825ce2202","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Third Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to increase your powers of perception. When you do so, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you take a Short or a Long Rest. You can't use the feature again until you finish a rest.</p><p><strong>Darkvision.</strong> You can see normally in darkness, both magical and non-magical, to a distance of 120 feet.</p><p><strong>Greater Comprehension.</strong> You can read any language.</p><p><strong>Truesight.</strong> You gain truesight, to a distance of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc6e217b52807db1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Uncanny Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to halve the attack's damage against you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"sc6f677ce9ce653b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Tranquility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Sanctuary spell prepared.</p><p>As a Reaction when you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you is targeted by an attack or other harmful effect, you can cast Sanctuary without expending a spell slot, and you adopt a presence of tranquility for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. During this time, you can cast Sanctuary again as a Reaction without expending a spell slot.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc714791132a12c6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beauty's Elegance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two out of the follwing skills: in Deception, Performance, and Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc73a924062c3d11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of Corrosion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blood curse can infuse a creature's body with terrible toxins. You gain the Blood Curse of Corrosion for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["2 * @attributes.prof","acid"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/dissolve-arm-flesh.webp","_id":"sc766f29b1c93354","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Curse Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to master blood curses. You gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature. In addition, your blood curses can target any creature, whether it has blood or not.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc79a5a4b2368bd5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428327,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Well-placed Shots","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you score a critical hit with a ranged weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice (and only the weapon's own damage dice) again and add the result to the total.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/target-bullseye-archer-orange.webp","_id":"sc80c59549418096","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indestructible Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You partake some of the true secrets of the Undying. On your turn, you can use a Bonus Action to regain hit points equal to half your maximum hit points. Additionally, if you put a severed body part of yours back in place when you use this feature, the part reattaches.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc817fc07d4690c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189554,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Arcana","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Arcana checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8204a91cee418f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Reinforcements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The royal courts of the Feywild have blessed you with the assistance of fey beings: you know Summon Fey. It doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know, and you can cast it without a material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require Concentration. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc84566a1040912a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Scrivener","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The gold and time you must spend to make a spell scroll are halved if you use your Wizardly Quill.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can create one or more spell scrolls with a combined spell level of no more than your Proficiency. You do not have to make a skill check or provide any spell slots, gold, or time for these scrolls and the resulting scrolls automatically have the masterwork property. All other rules for creating spell scrolls apply normally.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc852102618d5c26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Alacrity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emanate an aura that fills you and your companions with supernatural speed, allowing you to race across a battlefield in formation. Your Speed increases by 10 feet. In addition, if you aren't Incapacitated, the Speed of any ally who starts their turn within 10 feet of you increases by 10 feet until the end of that turn.</p><p>When you reach 18th level in this class, the range of the aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc863f57ab259d75","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Favored by the Gods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Divine power guards your destiny. If you fail a Saving Throw or miss with an Attack Roll, you can roll 2d4 and add it to the total, possibly changing the outcome. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you use 2 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8ad6436a2864de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summoner's Call","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to call your Eidolon to your side. It appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you that you can see.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8d86088ad2548f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiosis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to meld with your Eidolon's essence, two creatures merged as one, fighting in perfect unison.</p><p>As an Action, when you are within 5 feet of your Eidolon, you can merge forms with it, entering Symbiosis. The resulting form can be that of your Eidolon, your own, or something in-between.</p><p>In this form, you gain all your Eidolon's features and evolution feats, and you choose whether to use your own or your Eidolon's stats for each ability score and armor class. You gain your Eidolon's hitpoints as temporary hitpoints. All features and effects that normally affect your Eidolon's hitpoints affect these temporary hitpoints as well. If these temporary hitpoints reach 0, your Eidolon disappears and you lose the benefits of Symbiosis and revert to your normal form. You can also relinquish the Symbiosis and split up into a summoner and Eidolon as an Action.</p><p>You also retain all of your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the Eidolon.</p><p>You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them. And you can use any special senses available to your Eidolon and you.</p><p>When you transform, you choose whether your equipment merges into the new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal. The DM determines whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the form's shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change shape or size to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must merge into your new form. Equipment that merges has no effect in that state.</p><p>While in this form, you can cast all summoner spells as a Bonus Action. Summoner class features that normally require you to be separate entities to work, allow you to target a different beneficiary instead, treating it as the summoner. In the case of Twin Eidolon, you instead completely duplicate your merged form for the duration and it receives all benefits from equipment that you are wearing and currently using in that form as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8f004fad8b9b17","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Treachery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emanate an aura of discord, which gives you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Cull the Herd.</strong> You have Advantage on melee Attack Rolls against any creature that has one or more of its allies within 5 feet of it.</p><p><strong>Treacherous Strike.</strong> If a creature within 5 feet of you misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to force the attacker to reroll that attack against a creature of your choice that is also within 5 feet of the attacker. The ability fails and is wasted if the attacker is Immune to being Charmed.</p><p>You can use this ability three times. You regain one expended use on a Short Rest and all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc913837d9cf0dd5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Hunter Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You commit to an order of blood hunters whose philosophy will guide you throughout your life: the Order of the Ghostslayer, the Order of the Lycan, the Order of the Mutant, or the Order of the Profane Soul, each of which is detailed at the end of the class description. Your choice grants you features at 7th level and again at 11th, 15th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc928f2354684678","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reliable Talent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make an Ability Check that uses one of your skill or tool proficiencies, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/target-bullseye-arrow-glowing.webp","_id":"sc933f37d5439894","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thought Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means unless you allow it. You also have Resistance to psychic damage, and whenever a creature deals psychic damage to you, that creature takes the same amount of damage that you do.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc98e2c96c52f437","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Harfolk Hardiness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you can choose to use your Reaction to shrug off the blow. Roll a d12 + your CON modifier. And substract the result from the damage taken. You can't use this feature again until you have finished a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you take damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d12 + @abilities.con.mod","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp","_id":"sc9f996923346e1c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Flexibility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can grant your allies attacks as per the Concerted Strike class feature even when you use your action for something other than the attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/gaming/chess-knight-white.webp","_id":"sca08fc78d455291","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reanimated Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Using Tinker's Tools or another type of Artisan's Tools with which you have Proficient, you can take a Magic action to create a Reanimated Companion (see the stat block) through the power of necromancy and science. The companion manifests in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. You determine the companion's appearance; your choices don't affect the companion's game statistics.</p><p>The companion is Friendly to you and your allies and obeys you. It lasts until you finish a Long Rest or until you take a Magic action to dismiss it early, at which point it harmlessly collapses into a pile of viscera. It immediately drops to 0 Hit Points and dies if you die.</p><p>Once you create a companion, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest or expend a spell slot to create one. You can have only one companion at a time and can't create one while your companion is present.</p><ul><li><strong>The Companion in Combat.</strong> The Reanimated Companion shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the companion's.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sca3f87ade40dcd8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mob Rule","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use your Cunning Strike feature, you learn the following new way to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Bully (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or all Attack Rolls against it have Advantage until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Cow (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you.</li></ul><p>Additionally, you can reduce the die cost of any of your Cunning Strike options by 1 (to a minimum of 0) while none of your target's allies are within 5 feet of it and at least 1 of your allies is within their melee reach. You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scaac03fbfa05f3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sacred Oath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You swear the oath that binds you as a paladin forever. Up to this time you have been in a preparatory stage, committed to the path but not yet sworn to it. Now you choose from the list of available oaths.</p><p>Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 15th, and 20th level. Those features include oath spells and the Channel Divinity feature.</p><p><strong>Oath Spells.</strong> Each oath has a list of associated spells. You gain access to these spells at the levels specified in the oath description. Once you gain access to an oath spell, you always have it prepared. Oath spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.</p><p>If you gain an oath spell that doesn't appear on the paladin spell list, the spell is nonetheless a paladin spell for you.</p><div><strong>Breaking Your Oath</strong><p>A paladin tries to hold to the highest standards of conduct, but even the most virtuous paladin is fallible. Sometimes the right path proves too demanding, sometimes a situation calls for the lesser of two evils, and sometimes the heat of emotion causes a paladin to transgress his or her oath.</p><p>A paladin who has broken a vow typically seeks absolution from a cleric who shares his or her faith or from another paladin of the same order. The paladin might spend an all-night vigil in prayer as a sign of penitence, or undertake a fast or similar act of self-denial. After a rite of confession and forgiveness, the paladin starts fresh.</p><p>If a paladin willfully violates his or her oath and shows no sign of repentance, the consequences can be more serious. At the DM's discretion, an impenitent paladin might be forced to abandon this class and adopt another, or perhaps to take the Oathbreaker paladin option that appears in the Dungeon Master's Guide.</p></div","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp","_id":"scb235d27fa36a14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189517,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d12.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"scb48f3a01a334e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tools of the Trade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Tool Proficiency.</strong> You gain proficiency with Calligrapher's Supplies and Cartographer's Tools. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of Artisan's Tools of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).</p><p><strong>Scroll Crafting.</strong> When you craft a Spell Scroll, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/plate-steel-grey.webp","_id":"scb54de336f6ceee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428319,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of the Voracious","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on the Saving Throw for your bloodlust while in hybrid form. Additionally, your Brand of Castigation can now bind a foe to your hunter's ferocity. While in your hybrid form, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against a creature branded by you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scb5bcc1e7cec8ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d10s. At 18th level, they turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scb614e94f6117b6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428345,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Paladin level specified in the Genie Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of the Noble Genie Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Chromatic Orb, Elementalism, Thunderous Smite</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Mirror Image, Phantasmal Force</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fly, Gaseous Form</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Conjure Minor Elementals, Summon Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Banishing Smite, Contact Other Plane</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scba1cd6334c88ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>By choice or circumstance, you possess the ability to shift into an animal-like form that outfits you with heightened senses, swiftness, and primal ferocity in battle. You shift forms as a Bonus Action. While shifted, you gain the following benefits as long as you aren't wearing armor heavier than light or a shield:</p><ul><li>You have Advantage on Perception checks.</li><li>Your Speed is doubled.</li><li>When you make a melee weapon attack with your natural weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll. This bonus increases as you level.</li></ul><p>If you are able to cast spells, you can't cast them or concentrate on them while shifted.</p><p>Your Formshift lasts for an amount of hours equal to your shifter level. It ends early if you fall Unconscious or you are Incapacitated. You can also end your Formshift as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You can Formshift a number of times shown for your Shifter level in the Formshifts column of the Shifter Features table. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>You choose whether your equipment falls to the ground in your space, merges into your shifted form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it is practical for your shifted form to wear a piece of equipment, based on your shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that your shifted form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with it. Equipment that merges with your shifted form has no effect until you leave Formshift.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"@scale.shifter.formshifts","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/beast-horned-scaled-glowing-orange.webp","_id":"scba5372efaa0ccf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earth Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move across 3 made of earth or stone without expending extra movement.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/projectile-stone-landslide.webp","_id":"scbae19767704ab4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mortal Bulwark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You manifest a spark of divine power in defense of the mortal realms. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You gain truesight with a range of 120 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, and fiends.</li><li>When you hit a creature with an Attack Roll and deal damage to it, you can also force it to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature is magically banished to its native plane of existence if it's currently not there. On a successful save, the creature can't be banished by this feature for 24 hours.</li></ul><p>Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scbc7ce26c04ea97","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Avenger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your supernatural focus helps you close off a foe's retreat. When you hit a creature with an Opportunity Attacks, you can reduce the creature's Speed to 0 until the end of the current turn. You can then move up to half your Speed as part of the same Reaction. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scbcae26b0839bec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Uncanny Metabolism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can regain all expended Ki Points. When you do so, roll your Martial Arts die, and regain a number of Hit Points equal to your Monk level plus the number rolled.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you roll initiative"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.monk.martial-arts + @classes.monk.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"scbe9a26550d26e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189510,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes in the Dark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hide even when in plain view, as long as you are in an area of dim light or darkness. Additionally, you can see normally in darkness, both magical and non-magical, to a distance of 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scbf46c8d9f944a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trickster's Transposition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you take the Bonus Action to create or move the illusion of your Invoke Duplicity, you can teleport, swapping places with the illusion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scc6c65be9f61504","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Watcher at the Threshold","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to necrotic and radiant damage. In addition, while you aren't Incapacitated, any ally within 30 feet of you has Advantage on death Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scca90829b3b7d85","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Outmaneuver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>After initiative has been rolled, but before the first turn of combat, you and all allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you can move up to your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. This feature has no effect if you're incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sccb05f6f0379162","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Conquering Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to exude a terrifying presence. As an Action, you force each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, a creature becomes Frightened of you for 1 minute. The Frightened creature can repeat this Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scd18454ea037859","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Halo of Spores","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are surrounded by invisible, necrotic spores that are harmless until you unleash them on a creature nearby. When a creature you can see moves into a space within 10 feet of you or starts its turn there, you can use your Reaction to deal 1d4 necrotic damage to that creature unless it succeeds on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. The necrotic damage increases to 1d6 at 6th level, 1d8 at 10th level, and 1d10 at 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scd4ea36af5e2e8f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Protector of the Prime Material","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar are always under the effects of a Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast Banishment on a creature that has the Magic Resistance trait and is not native to the Prime Material Plane, you ignore the effects of that trait.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scd713748ec18f4d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189567,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you fail a Saving Throw, you can add half your Fighter level (rounded down) to it, possibly turning it into a success.</p><p>You can use this feature twice between Long Rests starting at 13th level and three times between Long Rests starting at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you fail a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.indomitable","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"floor(@classes.fighter.levels/2)","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"scda9c4e67d71089","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428341,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Controlled Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you roll on the Wild Magic table, you can roll the die twice and choose which of the two effects to unleash. If you roll the same number on both dice, you can ignore the number and choose any effect on the table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scdd579e6c8f7202","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grasping Tentacles","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the spell Evard's Black Tentacles. It counts as a warlock spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of spells you know. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Whenever you cast this spell, your patron's magic bolsters you, granting you a number of temporary hit points equal to your warlock level. Moreover, damage can't break your Concentration on this spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scdfed3d6d8c261f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Darkness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain strength from darkness. As a Bonus Action, you fade into the shadows. You regain hit points equal to your cleric level and gain Resistance to all damage for one minute. In addition, while this duration lasts you can use a Bonus Action to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is in dim light or darkness. It ends early if you become Incapacitated or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you use this feature you cannot use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce5b8730ce86d93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The night has taught you to be vigilant. As an Action, you give one creature you touch (including possibly yourself) Advantage on the next initiative roll the creature makes. This benefit ends immediately after the roll or if you use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce6764c673e46eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of the Spellguard","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A paladin who swears this oath ensure that villains who misuse magic are brought to justice.</p><ul><li>Protect the innocent from wicked mages.</li><li>Prevent magic from falling into villains' hands.</li><li>Protect mages who use magic honorably.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce7366b663113ee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Deflection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you can take a Reaction to reduce the attack's total damage against you. The reduction equals 1d10 plus your Intelligence modifier and Wizard level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce86123515771d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428378,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contingency Plans","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As long as you are not incapacitated, you and allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you cannot be Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scedc3cbc9b21c5e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warding Flare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature that you can see within 30 feet of yourself makes an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll, causing light to flare before it hits or misses.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scedc6c5f3fdf4b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roving Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed isn't reduced to 0 by using Cunning Action: Aim.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scf4f0d6beb3ed11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Abjuration Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Abjuration school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Abjuration school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scf5e167a3efd2d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428376,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a feline aspect, granting you physical traits such as the vertical pupils, sharp nails, and elongated canines.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>Additionally, once per turn when you hit a creature with your natural weapons, you can force the target to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failure, the target is Lacerated. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Creatures who cannot bleed are Immune to this feature.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, any laceration inflicted with your natural weapons deals damage equal to thrice your Proficiency, rather than twice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scf8924c2b516ac1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kinetic Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you form the energy of your element into a weapon-like shape of your choice, which lasts until you are incapacitated or dismiss it as a Bonus Action. You cannot use this shape if you have already used your kinetic blast this turn.</p><p>As an Action, you can make a melee spell attack with this shape against a target of your choice within 5 ft of you, dealing your kinetic shape die + your CHA modifier + your Proficiency modifier damage of your chosen element's type.</p><p>Additionally, your ability to defend yourself with this shape grants you a +1 bonus to your AC while maintaining it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":5,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"msak","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.kineticist.kinetic-shape + @abilities.cha.mod + @attributes.prof",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-flanged-lightning.webp","_id":"scf8bd9d1c7b559a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fanatical Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine power that fuels your rage can protect you. If you fail a Saving Throw while you're raging, you can reroll it and take the highest. You can use this ability only once per rage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scfbc12e1d5e49f8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189474,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scfe462e6aae4955","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to create a perfect visual illusion of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The illusion is intangible and doesn't occupy its space. It lasts for 1 minute, but it ends early if you dismiss it (no action required) or have the Incapacitated condition. The illusion is animated and mimics your expressions and gestures. While it persists, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Cast Spells.</strong> You can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses.</li><li><strong>Distract.</strong> When both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.</li><li><strong>Move.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is within 120 feet of yourself.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scff8882b9483d98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Champion Challenge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you issue a challenge that compels other creatures to do battle with you. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, a creature can't willingly move more than 30 feet away from you. This effect ends on the creature if you are Incapacitated or die or if the creature is more than 30 feet away from you.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down). And you regain one expended use on a Short Rest and all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd058d855bc5224e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ghost Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can phase partially into the realm of the dead, becoming like a ghost. As a Bonus Action, you assume a spectral form. While in this form, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed, you can hover, and Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you. You can also move through creatures and objects as if they were 3, but you take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.</p><p>You stay in this form for 10 minutes or until you end it as a Bonus Action. To use this feature again, you must finish a Long Rest or destroy one of your soul trinkets as part of the Bonus Action you use to activate Ghost Walk.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd09d3a11541e25d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Fateweavers Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Fateweavers Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Silvery Barbs, Augury, Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Clairvoyance, Counterspell</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Divination, Spell Turning</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dream, Scrying</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd09ec9057830b58","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vanish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the Hide action as a Bonus Action on your turn. Also, you can't be tracked by nonmagical means, unless you choose to leave a trail.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"sd0b3a52cb0bf6b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189522,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wildfire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to fire damage and when you cast a spell that deals fire damage, you can choose any creature you can see within 120 ft of you that is currently affected by your Heart of Fire feature as the point of origin. If you do so, the effect of Heart of Fire ends on it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd0c68922d2b604e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Spirit Totem safeguards the beasts and fey that you call forth with your magic. When a beast or fey that you summoned or created with a spell ends its turn in your Spirit Totem aura, that creature regains a number of hit points equal to half your druid level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd0e5d52d8230f68","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your command of sword magic grows stronger, allowing you to harness it for protection.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can grant an aegis to yourself or one allied creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The aegis is a dim, gray aura of earth magic that protects the target. Any bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage the target takes is reduced by half your sorcerer level (rounded down). This effect lasts for 1 minute or until you use it again.</p><p>In addition, when a creature you can see within 60 feet of you hits the protected target (which can be you) with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of the attacker. You can then make one melee weapon attack against the attacker. If that attack hits, it deals an extra 1d10 force damage. This extra damage increases to 2d10 at 11th level and 3d10 at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd1377270f202175","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Ultimate Mercy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of life energy opens the door to the ultimate mercy. As an Action, you can touch the corpse of a creature that died within the past 24 hours and expend 5 ki points. The creature then returns to life, regaining a number of hit points equal to 4d10 + your Wisdom modifier. If the creature died while subject to any of the following conditions, it revives with them removed: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, and Stunned.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd180f04465c35c6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reaper","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The cleric learns one necromancy cantrip of his or her choice from any spell list. When the cleric reduces a creature to 0 hit points with an effect that deals necrotic damage, it regains hit points equal to 1d6 + half its cleric level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd18faf4b974725c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undead Thralls","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Animate Dead and Summon Undead spells prepared and they do not count against the number of your prepared spells. When you cast Animate Dead, you can target one additional corpse or pile of bones, creating another zombie or skeleton, as appropriate.</p><p>Any undead creature you control has the following additional benefits:</p><ul><li>The creature's hit point maximum is increased by an amount equal to your wizard level.</li><li>The creature adds your Proficiency bonus to its weapon damage rolls.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd1eebb34901fd3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Vengeance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The authority with which you speak your Vow of Enmity gives you greater power over your foe. When a creature under the effect of your Vow of Enmity makes an attack, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature if it is within range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd21ef701cc64cab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your link to the divine allows you to learn spells from the cleric class. When your Spellcasting feature lets you learn or replace a sorcerer cantrip or a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose the new spell from the cleric spell list or the sorcerer spell list. You must otherwise obey all the restrictions for selecting the spell, and it becomes a sorcerer spell for you.</p><p>In addition, you learn two additional 1st-level spells of your choice from the cleric spell list. These spells count as sorcerer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>When you reach 3rd level, 5th, 7th, and 9th level in this class, you also learn two additional spells of 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th level of your choice from the cleric spell, respectively.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd235111dc99487e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strongheart Toughness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-red-blue.webp","_id":"sd262d520edac090","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonded Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you cast a spell on yourself, you can choose to cast the spell on your Eidolon instead if you can see it within 60 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd28b6b318ab9383","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of the Sea","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your tie to the sea grants you the ability to breathe underwater, and you have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd2a428056281a9d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visage of the Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can summon the visage of your astral self. As a Bonus Action, or as part of the Bonus Action you take to activate Arms of the Astral Self, you can spend 1 ki point to summon this visage for 10 minutes. It vanishes early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>The spectral visage covers your face like a helmet or mask. You determine its appearance.</p><p>While the spectral visage is present, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Astral Sight.</strong> You can see normally in darkness, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet.</p><p><strong>Wisdom of the Spirit.</strong> You have Advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.</p><p><strong>Word of the Spirit.</strong> When you speak, you can direct your words to a creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you, making it so only that creature can hear you. Alternatively, you can amplify your voice so that all creatures within 600 feet can hear you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd2fb56f0adac3d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiotic Entity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel magic into your spores. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape feature to awaken those spores, rather than transforming into a beast form, and you gain 4 temporary hit points for each level you have in this class. While this feature is active, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>When you deal your Halo of Spores damage, roll the damage die a second time and add it to the total.</li><li>Your weapon attacks and spells deal additional damage equal to your Halo of Spores to creatures within the area of effect of your Halo of Spores.</li></ul><p>These benefits last for 10 minutes, until you lose all these temporary hit points, or until you use your Wild Shape again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd33db84c7e9ce6d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428340,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your magical energy by drawning from the essence of the planes. Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your summoner level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 3rd level or higher.</p><p>For example, if you're a 4th-level summoner, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots.</p><p>You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd373c9323fa3b68","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Supremacy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use feature type=WM, you may choose from any mastery rather than only the ones available for your weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/maneuver-greatsword-yellow.webp","_id":"sd3a801153ab3497","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ashborn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"sd3df90abcc654b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Rebuke the Violent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to rebuke those who use violence. Immediately after an attacker within 30 feet of you deals damage with an attack against a creature other than you, you can use your Reaction to force the attacker to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, the attacker takes radiant damage equal to the damage it just dealt. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd3f5f53cb983f2c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"sd40b46cb52b4459","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Finest Hour","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Leadership can temporarily inspire your companions to transcend their limits. On your turn, choose an ally within 60 feet that can see or hear you and isn't incapacitated. That ally gains an additional turn immediately after your current one.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have completed a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-weapons-orange.webp","_id":"sd4110bda12da744","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189559,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Harmonious Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to weave the energies of all your chosen elements together seamlessly.</p><p>Your Elemental Defense subclass features are no longer exclusive and you can choose to activate any number of them with the same Bonus Action (dismissing them still requires no action on your part).</p><p>If your chosen elements grant you access to different formulas to calculate your AC, you must still decide which one to use when you activate your Elemental Defense.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-flaming-pentagon-teal-purple.webp","_id":"sd413cf9dd341422","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stalker's Prowess","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your hemocraft modifier to Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd43a580bcaebaad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sneaky","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the stealth skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-dashing-blue.webp","_id":"sd47f9e3e2722536","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Doom Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, your or your bonded familiar can touch a creature you can see and weave a protective charm that wards against ill luck for 1 hour. The target cannot have Disadvantage on any D20 Tests. You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd48d63fc04df00c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise (Level 6)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two more of your proficiencies (in skills or with thieves' tools) to gain the benefit of Expertise.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"sd49144ed2592ec0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cloak of Shadows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action while entirely within Dim Light or Darkness, you can expend 3 Ki Points to shroud yourself with shadows for 1 minute, until you have the Incapacitated condition, or until you end your turn in Bright Light. While shrouded by these shadows, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Invisibility.</strong> You have the Invisible condition.</li><li><strong>Partially Incorporeal.</strong> You can move through occupied spaces as if they were 3. If you end your turn in such a space, you are shunted to the last unoccupied space you were in.</li><li><strong>Shadow Flurry.</strong> You can use your Flurry of Blows without expending any Ki Points. When you use your Improved Shadow Step, you can use Flurry of Blows as part of the same Bonus Action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd495beb992f6176","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189513,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pact Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You augment your combat techniques with the ability to cast spells. See chapter 10 of the Player's Handbook for the general rules of spellcasting and chapter 11 of the Player's Handbook for the warlock spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You learn two cantrips of your choice from the Warlock spell list. You learn an additional warlock cantrip of your choice at 10th level, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Blood Hunter Features table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Blood Hunter Features table shows how many spell slots you have. The table also shows what the level of those slots is; all of your spell slots are the same level. To cast one of your warlock spells of 1st level or higher, you must expend a spell slot. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>For example, when you are 8th level, you have two 2nd-level spell slots. To cast the 1st-level spell Witch Bolt, you must spend one of those slots, and you cast it as a 2nd-level spell.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature.</p><p>You know three 1st-level spells of your choice from the Warlock spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Blood Hunter levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Blood Hunter Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Warlock spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level no higher than what's shown in the table's Slot Level column for your level. When you reach level 7, for example, you learn a new Warlock spell, which can be of levels 1–2.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Blood Hunter level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Warlock spell of an eligible level.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Your chosen Hemocraft ability (Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma) is your spellcasting ability for your Warlock spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a Spellcasting Focus for your Warlock spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/blood-spurt-spray-red.webp","_id":"sd4d8014a1c216d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The might of the elements flows through you. You gain one of the following options of your choice:</p><p><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> You add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip.</p><p><strong>Primal Strike.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll using a weapon or a natural weapon of your Wild Shape, you can cause the target to take an additional 1d8 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-glow-spiral-teal.webp","_id":"sd580de50ffb3738","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Guided Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature within 30 feet of you misses with an Attack Roll, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity and give that roll a +10 bonus, potentially causing it to hit. When you use this feature to benefit another creature's Attack Roll, you must take a Reaction to do so.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd594a8a325d3bc6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are hit by an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to halve the attack's damage against yourself (round down) and force the attacker to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker takes damage equal to 4d10 plus your Charisma modifier; the damage type is that associated with your genie patron as per your Aura of Elemental Shielding. On a successful save, the attacker takes half as much damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd59b88940a24c29","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Athlete","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage-orange.webp","_id":"sd5a791b64faf80a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189577,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Naturally Stealthy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attempt to hide even if you are obscured only by a creature that is at least one size larger than you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"sd5b2ff27b07cba2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189581,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bulwark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally within 60 feet of you fails a Saving Throw, you can expend a use of your Indomitable class feature as a Reaction to grant its benefit to that ally.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd5e34829b3b7471","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast one of the level 1+ spells that you have prepared from your Circle Spells feature without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a Long Rest before you do so again.</p><p>In addition, when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your Druid level (round up), and none of them can be level 6+. For example, if you're a level 6 Druid, you can recover up to three levels' worth of spell slots. You can recover a level 3 spell slot, a level 2 and a level 1 spell slot, or three level 1 spell slots. Once you recover spell slots with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"sd5f265aa8365407","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thief's Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-beam-purple.webp","_id":"sd62c9b99731cda1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Apex Predator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your experience and skill allow you to hunt and fight any creature as effectively as your chosen foes, given a little time to prepare. When you finish a Long Rest, you can exchange any of your chosen favorite enemies and replace them with a different one.</p><p>Additionally, your critical range against your favorite enemies increases by 1 and if you land a critical hit with a weapon attack, you add your ranger level to the damage roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-beast-eyes-green.webp","_id":"sd63bb241b7b7ff7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.</p><p>For example, if you're a 4th-level wizard, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots.</p><p>You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/explosion-lava-stone-green.webp","_id":"sd678d7e6ab30dc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infiltration Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unfailingly create false identities for yourself. You must spend seven days and 25 gp to establish the history, profession, and affiliations for an identity. You can't establish an identity that belongs to someone else. For example, you might acquire appropriate clothing, letters of introduction, and official-looking certification to establish yourself as a member of a trading house from a remote city so you can insinuate yourself into the company of other wealthy merchants.</p><p>Thereafter, if you adopt the new identity as a disguise, other creatures believe you to be that person until given an obvious reason not to.</p><p>You also gain the ability to unerringly mimic another person's speech, writing, and behavior. You must spend at least three hours studying these three components of the person's behavior, listening to speech, examining handwriting, and observing mannerism.</p><p>Your ruse is indiscernible to the casual observer. If a wary creature suspects something is amiss, you have Advantage on any Charisma (Deception) check you make to avoid detection.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd67b611461e6e8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the Help action as a Bonus Action. Additionally, when you use the Help action to aid an ally in attacking a creature, the target of that attack can be within 60 feet of you, rather than within 5 feet of you, if the target can see or hear you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd67ca0671c41a53","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drunkard's Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always seem to get a lucky bounce at the right moment. When you make an Ability Check, an Attack Roll, or a Saving Throw and have Disadvantage on the roll, you can spend 2 ki points to cancel the Disadvantage for that roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd687f1dcfd7b1fd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While using Wild Shape, you can cast spells in Beast form, except for any spell that has a Material component with a cost specified or that consumes its Material component.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"sd6a25e09b703919","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Creative Crescendo","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Performance of Creation feature, you can create more than one item at once. The number of items equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of two items). If you create an item that would exceed that number, you choose which of the previously created items disappears. Only one of these items can be of the maximum size you can create; the rest must be Small or Tiny.</p><p>You are no longer limited by gp value when creating items with Performance of Creation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6d9c7677be9ca0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Strength","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You count as one size larger for the purpose of grappling, shoving, and carrying. Additionally, when you make a Strength check, Strength Saving Throw, or Constitution Saving Throw, you add your Wisdom modifier to it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6f4bbc50704d74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undeniable Ambition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Also add your Wisdom modifier to the D20 test when you use Reject Failure. If you fail the D20 test, you can choose to use Reject Failure again immediately without a Reaction, rerolling again and taking the highest result. You can only do so once per initial use of Reject Failure.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd732b897ab74347","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Silent Flight.</strong> While flying, you can hide as a Bonus Action and your wings cause no sound when you move while flying. If you attack while hidden, the benefits of being hidden persist against the target of your attack until the end of your turn.</li><li><strong>On Swift Wings.</strong> When you move, you can choose a creature that is within 5 ft and at least one size smaller than you and move the creature with you until the end of the current turn. The creature's movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Deadly Talons.</strong> The critical range with your natural weapons increases by 1. When you critically hit with your natural weapons, you roll your weapon damage dice two additional times and add them to the damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd741883c7d40eb0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189539,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Sundering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your strikes expose a fragment of your foe's essence, leaving them vulnerable to your Crimson Rite feature.</p><p>Whenever you hit a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you roll an additional hemocraft die when determining the extra damage from the rite.</p><p>Additionally, if a branded creature has the Incorporeal Movement trait or a similar feature, it can't move through creatures or objects while branded and it cannot benefit from being Invisible.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd7777955c3ebd44","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to cast spells. The information below details how you use those rules with Cleric spells, which appear on the Cleric spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know three cantrips of your choice from the Cleric spell list.</p><p>Whenever you gain a Rogue level, you can replace one of your cantrips, with another Cleric cantrip of your choice.</p><p>When you reach Rogue level 10, you learn another Cleric cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Inquisitor Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of 1st+ Level.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 Cleric spells.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Rogue levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Inquisitor Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Cleric spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the Inquisitor Spellcasting table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Rogue, your list of prepared spells can include five Cleric spells of level 1 or 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Rogue level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Cleric spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for your Cleric spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use a Holy Symbol as a Spellcasting Focus for your Cleric spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"sd7f00d85c1e8117","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428361,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast's Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion can attack twice instead of once whenever it takes the Attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd7fbf7e92050461","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189523,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd864850e0c3cf4e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428450,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflect Energy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Wou can now use your Deflect Attacks feature against attacks that deal any damage type, not just Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/barrier-shield-dome-deflect-blue.webp","_id":"sd8c6f97491acfc4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 19)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd8d3f00672b6a11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428450,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Whispers of the Dead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Echoes of those who have died cling to you. Whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can choose one skill or tool Proficiency that you lack and gain it, as a ghostly presence shares its knowledge with you. You lose this Proficiency when you use this feature to choose a different Proficiency that you lack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd90b980c7ac6935","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable (three uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Indomitable three times between Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"sd91ff0fddc63ac6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Advanced Artifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Magic Item Savant.</strong> You can now attune to up to five magic items at once.</p><p><strong>Refreshed Genius.</strong> When you finish a Short Rest, you regain one expended use of your Flash of Genius feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hands-humanoid-yellow.webp","_id":"sd921a8233d96715","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to cold, fire, lightning, and thunder damage. When you use Elemental Might, you gain Immunity to the damage type of the chosen element.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd939da99acf9d8a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189489,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Vengeance Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Bane, Hunter's Mark</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hold Person, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Haste, Protection from Energy</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment, Dimension Door</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Hold Monster, Scrying</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd96b9c76a4ed25a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Secrets","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned secrets from various magical traditions. Whenever you reach a Bard level (including this level) and the Prepared Spells number in the Bard Features table increases, you can choose any of your new prepared spells from the Bard, Cleric, Druid, and Wizard spell lists, and the chosen spells count as Bard spells for you (see a class's section for its spell list). In addition, whenever you replace a spell prepared for this class, you can replace it with a spell from those lists.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"sd9da1e208e5d966","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stalker's Flurry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to attack with such unexpected speed that you can turn a miss into another strike. Once on each of your turns when you miss with a weapon attack, you can make another weapon attack as part of the same action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda0ed6c9f206356","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following Channel Divinity options. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how Channel Divinity works.</p><p><strong>Watcher's Will.</strong> You can use your Channel Divinity to invest your presence with the warding power of your faith. As an Action, you can choose a number of creatures you can see within 30 feet of you, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). For 1 minute, you and the chosen creatures have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-smoke-yellow.webp","_id":"sda1957570f52e78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428357,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you spend a Spell Slot to cast a spell of 1st level or higher that requires a spell attack roll, you can use your Sneak Attack on it, adhering to all other conditions as usual. If you do so, the damage die of your Sneak Attack increases to a d8 and its damage type to that of the spell.</p><p>Additionally, the cost of any Cunning Strike you use with such a spell is reduced by a number of dice equal to half the spell's level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda3a08af1773cb7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Spell selection is part of what defines a wizard and their individual fields of expertise. When creating your Psionics wizard, consider spells that are thematically appropriate for that tradition. Psionics as a theme generally includes spells that do the following:</p><ul><li>contact or manipulate minds</li><li>allow the caster to perceive distant locations or planes</li><li>alter perception</li><li>move objects and creatures</li><li>teleport</li><li>deal psychic or force damage</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda5533c22a7dc74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knightly Vigilance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can't be Surprised while you are conscious. Additionally, you add your Wisdom modifier to your Initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda8909441bb1493","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Awareness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can open your awareness to the presence of concentrated magic. Until the end of your next turn, you know the location of any spell or magic item within 60 feet of you that isn't behind total cover. When you sense a spell, you learn which school of magic it belongs to.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda8f1df86ba87ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428322,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Toughness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-red-blue.webp","_id":"sdadd087a3c5ccfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Knowledge of the Ages","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to tap into a divine well of knowledge. As an Action, you choose one skill or tool. You have Proficiency with the chosen skill or tool until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdaf67ed051bb431","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of the Forge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to imbue magic into a weapon or armor. At the end of a Long Rest, you can touch one object that is a suit of armor or a simple or martial weapon. Until the end of your next Long Rest or until you die, the object becomes a magic item, granting a +1 bonus to AC if it's armor or a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls if it's a weapon. These bonuses increases +2 once you reach level 11 in this class. This bonus is subject to the enhancement bonus limit from items.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdaf69f15c106317","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Duck and Cover","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you have half or three-quarters cover and you aren't incapacitated, your cover is instead considered one step better.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-eyes-green.webp","_id":"sdb33820dd57e03f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Furious Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, as part of a melee weapon attack, you can move up to your Speed in a straight line towards a target of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/charge.webp","_id":"sdb339ac76b3c7de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Full of Stars","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While in your Starry Form, you become partially incorporeal, giving you Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdb661dbfbe0d868","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bend Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to twist fate using your wild magic. When another creature you can see makes an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction and spend 1 sorcery points to roll 1d4 and apply the number rolled as a bonus or penalty (your choice) to the creature's roll. You can do so after the creature rolls but before any effects of the roll occur.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdb7322957b5ce24","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hydrokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Shape Water cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdb8e1e64d08eb2b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Laestrygonian Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the warhammer, longsword, maul, and greatsword.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/hammers/hammer-double-steel-embossed.webp","_id":"sdb93f5fdbf23144","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Shift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks when you use your Second Wind feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"sdb9a5b7301d495e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189495,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Light as Air","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use your Reaction when you fall to reduce any falling damage you take by an amount equal to five times your kineticist level.</p><p>Additionally, your standing and running jumps use Charisma instead of Strength to determine the distance you cover.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdc10d412add8480","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legendary Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you fail a Saving Throw, you can succeed instead. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when your Eidolon fails a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":3,"max":3,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/barrier-shield-dome-deflect-teal.webp","_id":"sdc3a232ee798e98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189557,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Currents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level higher it fails a Save against such a spell, you can move the affected creature up to 5 x your Proficiency feet to an unoccupied square of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdc4bbf2fc348bca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428365,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Confounding Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Charm (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to succeed on a Wisddom Saving Throw or become Charmed by you for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns to end the effect.</li><li><strong>Confuse (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target has to succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or become Confused until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdd590ea4d0afbb4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189535,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master of navigating the natural world, and you react with swift and decisive action when attacked. This grants you the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You ignore 3.</li><li>You have Advantage on initiative rolls.</li><li>On your first turn during combat, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that have not yet acted.</li></ul><p>In addition, you are skilled at navigating the wilderness. You gain the following benefits when traveling for an hour or more:</p><ul><li>Difficult terrain doesn't slow your group's travel.</li><li>Your group can't become lost except by magical means.</li><li>When performing a task during the Travelling Phase of Overland Travel, you may additionally perform the Lookout task or assist with it.</li><li>If you are traveling alone, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.</li><li>When you forage, you find twice as much food as you normally would.</li><li>While tracking other creatures, you also learn their exact number, their sizes, and how long ago they passed through the area.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sdd5d336312f624a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transmutation Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Transmutation school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Transmutation school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdd7fd3c7de547c1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428378,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unfailing Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your inspiring words are so persuasive that others feel driven to succeed. When a creature adds one of your Bardic Inspiration dice to its Ability Check, Attack Roll, or Saving Throw and the roll fails, the creature can keep the Bardic Inspiration die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdd9411706c940e6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Chronal Shift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically exert limited control over the flow of time around a creature. As a Reaction, after you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can force the creature to reroll. You make this decision after you see whether the roll succeeds or fails. The target must use the result of the second roll.</p><p>You can use this ability a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier, and you regain any expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdd97d8b91192954","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428379,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Detect Portal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to magically sense the presence of a planar portal. As an Action, you detect the distance and direction to the closest planar portal within 1 mile of you.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>See the \"Planar Travel\" section in chapter 2 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for examples of planar portals.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdda488f049a8a20","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with woodcarver's tools. If you already have this Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"sdda8e1e4e986eb7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428319,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fungal Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The fungal spores in your body alter you: you can't be Blinded, Deafened, Frightened, or Poisoned, and any critical hit against you counts as a normal hit instead, unless you're Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sddc303a1048216c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189492,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you present your Holy Symbol and censure extraplanar creatures. Each celestial, elemental, fey, and fiend of your choice within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. If the creature fails its save, it has the Frightened and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute. For that duration, it tries to move as far from you as it can on its turns. This effect ends early on the creature if it takes any damage, if you have the Incapacitated condition, or if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sddc4fe33efdec85","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Apotheosis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use one Metamagic option on each of your turns without spending Sorcery Points on it and your Spell Save DC is increased by 2 rather than 1.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sddd15516e2c6daa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Talent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one feat of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/thumbsup-approval-like.webp","_id":"sde3859a58e0b7df","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crafty Negotiator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp","_id":"sde609b88129742d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flurry of Healing and Harm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now mete out a flurry of comfort and hurt. When you use Flurry of Blows, you can now replace each of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of your Hand of Healing, without spending ki points for the healing.</p><p>In addition, when you make an Unarmed Strike with Flurry of Blows, you can use Hand of Harm with that strike without spending the ki point for Hand of Harm. You can still use Hand of Harm only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sde63cf7d3f43434","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to cast spells. See the Player's Handbook for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you  use those rules as a Way of the Mystic Arts.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two cantrips of your choice from the Sorcerer spell list. Whenever you gain a Monk level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the Sorcerer spell list.</p><p>When you reach Monk level 10, you learn another Sorcerer cantrip of your choice, as shown in this subclass' progression table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Way of the Mystic Arts Spellcasting table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose three level 1 spells from the Sorcerer spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Mystic Arts Spellcasting table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the Sorcerer spell list until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 7 Monk, your list of prepared spells can include five Sorcerer spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Monk level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Sorcerer spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for your Sorcerer spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a Spellcasting Focus for your Sorcerer spells.</p><p><strong>Multiclassing.</strong> If you multiclass and have the Spellcasting feature from more than one class, add one third of your Monk levels (round down) to determine your available spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"sde80d6eb7778818","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428348,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Words of Terror","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to infuse innocent-seeming words with an insidious magic that can inspire terror.</p><p>If you speak to a humanoid alone for at least 1 minute, you can attempt to seed paranoia in its mind. At the end of the conversation, the target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or be Frightened of you or another creature of your choice. The target is Frightened in this way for 1 hour, until it is attacked or damaged, or until it witnesses its allies being attacked or damaged.</p><p>If the target succeeds on its Saving Throw, the target has no hint that you tried to frighten it.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a use of your Bardic Inspiration to use it again (no Action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sde9749fb67b618f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tandem Footwork","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration if you don't have the Incapacitated condition. When you do so, roll your Bardic Inspiration die; you and each ally within 30 feet of you who can see or hear you gains a bonus to Initiative equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdeeb9fed9663ba4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Saint of Forge and Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blessed affinity with fire and metal becomes more powerful:</p><ul><li>You gain Immunity to fire damage.</li><li>You can now use your Blessing of the Forge feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdf843d60817beb4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hooves","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your hooves to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/modfiy-luck-fortune-gray.webp","_id":"sdf87c6a21d99fc3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extraordinary Acrobatics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces on your turn without falling during the move and you can use your Dexterity in place of your Strength to determine the distance of your jumps.</p><p>In addition, once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with an attempt to Climb onto a Bigger Creature, as per the Additional Combat Actions. You can attempt and maintain this special grapple even when you don't have a free hand.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdf8cd07d7a735dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Mysticism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your study of the supernatural gives you a limited ability to use magic. You can cast Detect Magic as a ritual. You can cast Protection from Evil and Good on yourself as a Bonus Action and without expending a Spell Slot, but you cannot cast it again with this feature until you finish a Long Rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells.</p><p>In addition, you gain the ability to speak three of the following languages of your choice: Abyssal, Celestial, Deep Speech, Draconic, Giant, Primordial, Sylvan, or Umbral.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdf8f7f906181394","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Ambusher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master the art of the ambush. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p>At the start of your first turn of each combat, your Speed increases by 10 feet, which lasts until the end of that turn. If you take the Attack action on that turn, you can make one additional weapon attack as part of that action. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's damage type.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdfa95fad165277f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drunken Technique","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to twist and turn quickly as part of your Flurry of Blows. Whenever you use Flurry of Blows, you gain the benefit of the Disengage action, and your Speed increases by 10 feet until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdfe92eae0c886f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428349,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"sdffb84e648b71a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oathbreaker Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oathbreaker spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oathbreaker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Hellish Rebuke, Inflict Wounds</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Crown of Madness, Darkness</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Animate Dead, Bestow Curse</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Blight, Confusion</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Contagion, Dominate Person</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se009df69486aca3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flyby","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You don't provoke Opportunity Attacks when you fly out of an enemy's reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/birds-flock-fly-yellow.webp","_id":"se00a0eb1e7f0864","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twin Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While your spellbook's spectral mind is manifested, it can concentrate for you on any spell you cast through the spellbook or on a scroll that has been placed inside of it. If the spectral mind disappears, that spells ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se03d6ba00332b99","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Cleansing Current","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to summon a current of magical water to cleanse allies and wash away your foes.</p><p>The current rushes from your position in a line 15 ft wide and 30 ft long. You can end one disease or poison currently affecting any of your allies in the area of effect. If an ally is afflicted by multiple such effects, you choose which one to remove.</p><p>All hostile creatures in the area of effect have to make a STR Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, they are pushed 10 ft away from you in a straight line and knocked Prone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se04389b7bd7931c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428336,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature five times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"se044f3f1181043e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189480,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Physician's Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can administer even greater cures with a touch, and if you feel it's necessary, you can use your knowledge to cause harm.</p><p>When you use Hand of Healing, you can also end one of the following conditions on the creature you heal or remove one disease affecting them: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, or Stunned.</p><p>When you use Hand of Harm on a creature, you can also force that creature to make a Constitution Saving Throw or have the Poisoned condition until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0484a7b6da9123","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Turn the Tide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can bolster injured creatures with your Channel Divinity. Each creature of your choice that can hear you within 30 feet of you regains hit points equal to 1d6 + half your Proficiency bonus (rounded down) + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1).</p><p>If an creature has half its hit points or less, the healing it receives from this feature is doubled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se04f9c22abe2cda","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428354,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword Sage's Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Arcane Aegis to protect an ally, you can choose up to three creatures to gain its benefits. (You are a valid target as well).</p><p>Additionally, when you have no Reaction remaining and a creature triggers the Reaction attack from your Arcane Aegis feature, you can spend 2 sorcery points to use the attack without a Reaction. You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0a055202dd9862","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infectious Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with your natural weapons while you are raging, the beast within you can curse your target with rabid fury. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Constitution modifier + your Proficiency bonus) or suffer one of the following effects (your choice):</p><ul><li>The target must use its Reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of your choice that you can see.</li><li>The target takes 2d12 psychic damage.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0ad1df72f06200","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Breaker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Counterspell and Dispel Magic spells prepared and they don't count against your number of prepared spells. In addition, you can cast Dispel Magic as a Bonus Action, and you can add your Proficiency Bonus to the Ability Checks of both spells.</p><p>When you cast either spell with a spell slot, that slot isn't expended if the spell fails to stop a spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0bab40727792ae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189569,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental School","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A kineticist chooses one primary element on which to focus. This element determines how she accesses the raw power of the Ethereal Plane, and grants you features at 1st level and again at 6th, 10th, 15th, and 20th level.</p><p>Regardless of your chosen element, you use your Charisma modifier when setting Attack Rolls and determining the Saving Throw DC of your abilities.</p><p><b>Spell save DC</b> = 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier</p><p><b>Spell attack modifier</b> = your Proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier</p><p><strong>The Elements, intertwined.</strong> Unlike other classes, the kineticist can mix and match her subclass features, provided she has access to multiple different elements through her Expanded Element class feature.</p><p>If so, she can choose from the subclass features available to any of her schools at the appropriate level. For example, if a kineticist picked air as her school at 1st level and then fire at 6th, she can choose her subclass feature at 7th level from either school.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/elements-air-earth-fire-water.webp","_id":"se0bbdb0e181919f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unwavering Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can menace your foes, foiling their attacks and punishing them for harming others. When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can mark the creature until the end of your next turn. This effect ends early if you are Incapacitated or you die, or if someone else marks the creature.</p><p>While it is within 5 feet of you, a creature marked by you has Disadvantage on any Attack Roll that doesn't target you.</p><p>In addition, if a creature marked by you deals damage to anyone other than you, you can make a special melee weapon attack against the marked creature as a Bonus Action on your next turn. You have Advantage on the Attack Roll, and if it hits, the attack's weapon deals extra damage to the target equal to half your fighter level.</p><p>Regardless of the number of creatures you mark, you can make this special attack a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0d0bf34420a774","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"se0d5412e033ede4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189468,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sylvan Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your creature type is both humanoid and fey.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/fae-fairy-winged-glowing-green.webp","_id":"se1900c90efc4e95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thirst for Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Arcana skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hand-claw-glow-orange.webp","_id":"se1b883803400894","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expansive Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The benefits of your Bonds of Solidarity and Protective Bond features now work when the creatures are within 60 feet of each other. Moreover, when a creature uses Protective Bond to take someone else's damage, the creature has Resistance to that damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se1c03de6dbe1711","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Unarmed Strikes count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se22dc1885a25fcd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189476,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can weave fey magic into a song or dance to fill others with vigor. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of Bardic Inspiration, rolling a Bardic Inspiration die. When you do so, choose a number of other creatures within 60 feet of yourself, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). Each of those creatures gains a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to two times the number rolled on the Bardic Inspiration die, and then each can use its Reaction to move up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se22ffcc07f2109a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expert Crafter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"se25ac26c8cfd686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189582,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rallying Cry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to inspire your allies to fight on past their injuries.</p><p>When you use your Second Wind feature, you can choose up to three creatures within 60 feet of you that are allied with you. Each one regains hit points equal to your fighter level plus twice your Proficiency, provided that the creature can see or hear you.</p><p>If a creature is healed for more hit points than they are missing, they regain the difference as temporary hit points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se25bda9c437b913","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189503,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Titanic Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The primeval companion can grow to Large size if you so choose, and when you summon it, you can grant it either a Climb Speed, Swim Speed, Fly Speed or Burrow Speed equal to its Speed.</p><p>In turn, the primeval companion lends you some of its terrifying might. Once per turn while your primeval companion is summoned, when you hit a creature with an attack or deal damage to a creature you can see with a spell you cast, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC; on a failure, the creature is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se26e5bd27a0bad3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mutagencraft","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to master forbidden alchemical formulas—known as mutagens—that can temporarily alter your mental and physical abilities.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you consume a mutagen, whose effects last until you finish a Short or a Long Rest unless otherwise specified.</p><p>Mutagens are designed for the specific biology of the character who concocted them, and your mutagens have no effect on other creatures. They are also unstable by nature, losing their potency over time and becoming inert if not used before you finish your next Short or a Long Rest.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Mutagencraft</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Blood Hunter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Mutagens Created</th><th scope=\"col\">Formulas Known</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>1</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>2</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>11th</td><td>2</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>15th</td><td>3</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>18th</td><td>3</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se272cd1fb435cea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The guardian spirits that aid you can provide supernatural protection to those you defend. If you are raging and another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to reduce that damage by 2d6.</p><p>When you reach certain levels in this class, you can reduce the damage by more: by 3d6 at 10th level and by 4d6 at 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you are raging and another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["20","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-blades-teal.webp","_id":"se2c2626039f036c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Disciple of Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your healing spells are more effective. Whenever you use a spell of 1st level or higher to restore hit points to a creature, the creature regains additional hit points equal to 2 × the spell's level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-teal.webp","_id":"se2d8c60fdad912c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guided Precision","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, whenever you cast a spell from your Plane Charter Spells list or hit a creature affected by your Faerie Fire with an attack roll, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell or attack.</p><p>In addition, taking damage can't cause you to lose Concentration on Faerie Fire.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"whenever you cast a spell from your Cartographer Spells list or hit a creature affected by your Faerie Fire with an attack roll"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"@abilities.int.mod","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-strike-triple-blue.webp","_id":"se2d925c4c84a37e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Performance of Creation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can channel the magic of the Song of Creation to create one nonmagical item of your choice in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of you. The item must appear on a surface or in a liquid that can support it. The gp value of the item can't be more than 20 times your bard level, and the item must be Medium or smaller. The item glimmers softly, and a creature can faintly hear music when touching it. The created item disappears after a number of hours equal to your Proficiency bonus. For examples of items you can create, see the equipment chapter of the 5.</p><p>Once you create an item with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 2nd level or higher to use this feature again. You can have only one item created by this feature at a time; if you use this action and already have an item from this feature, the first one immediately vanishes.</p><p>The size of the item you can create with this feature increases by one size category when you reach 6th level (Large) and 14th level (Huge).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se2e64ae9b6e9a67","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428324,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raised by the Steppe","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are proficient in your choice of two of the following skills or tools: Herbalism Kit, Leatherworker's Tools, Nature, Perception, or Survival.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/tree-oak.webp","_id":"se3011da877b6857","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hybrid Transformation Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered your inner predator. You can use your Hybrid Transformation feature an unlimited number of times, and your hybrid form lasts until you revert to your normal form, fall Unconscious, or die.</p><p>You also gain the Blood Curse of the Howl for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se313cbbe42514e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one eldritch invocation available to the warlock class. You cannot select an invocation for which you do not meet all prerequisites, including certain class features available only to the warlock class. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can replace the invocation you know with another invocation that you could learn at that level. You use your levels in this class in place of warlock levels to determine whether you meet the prerequisites.</p><p>If an invocation allows you to cast a spell, you must have access to the appropriate spell level, even if the invocation does not require you to expend a spell slot to cast it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se373931707db386","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scout's Swiftness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can roll a Combat Superiority Die without expending it and add it to your initiative.</p><p>Additionally, when initiative is rolled but before the first round of combat, you can expend a Combat Superiority Die to move up to your Speed and make a single weapon attack. If it hits, you add your Combat Superiority Die to the damage roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se39bc378f4a7ca2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of Winter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master the cold element, to the point that you grow stronger as your foes succumb to the touch of ice and frost:</p><ul><li>You gain Immunity to cold damage.</li><li>At the start of every one of your turns, you gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature within 30 feet of you that is affected by your Winter's Touch class feature or your Bone-Chilling Cold Channel Divinity. If a creature is affected by both, you double the temporary hit points gained for that creature. These temporary hit points last for 1 hour and do not stack with temporary hit points applied in this manner on subsequent rounds.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se3c44fc5c01b6e0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Balm of the Summer Court","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become imbued with the blessings of the Summer Court. You are a font of energy that offers respite from injuries. You have a pool of fey energy represented by a number of d6s equal to your druid level.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 120 feet of you and spend a number of those dice equal to half your druid level or less. Roll the spent dice and add them together. The target regains a number of hit points equal to the total. The target also gains 1 temporary hit point per die spent.</p><p>You regain all expended dice when you finish a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Wildshape as an Action to regain a number of dice equal to half your Proficiency (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se401f363091c078","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428338,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bladesong","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke a secret elven magic called the Bladesong, provided you aren't wearing medium or heavy armor or using a shield. It graces you with supernatural speed, agility, and focus.</p><p>You can use a Bonus Action to start the Bladesong, which lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you don medium or heavy armor or a shield, or if you use two hands to make an attack with a weapon. You can also dismiss Bladesong at any time you choose (no action required).</p><p>While your bladesong is active, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You gain a bonus to your AC equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</li><li>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</li><li>You gain a bonus to any Constitution Saving Throws you make to maintain Concentration on a spell. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se41b59077303459","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"se41fd42039657a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189499,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Circle of Mortality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to manipulate the line between life and death. When you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell to a creature at 0 hit points, you instead use the highest number possible for each die.</p><p>In addition, you learn the Spare the Dying cantrip, which doesn't count against the number of cleric cantrips you know. For you, it has a range of 30 feet, and you can cast it as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se432d1f09cdce17","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unending Breath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hold your breath indefinitely while you're not incapacitated and exposed to air.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/air-smoke-casting.webp","_id":"se436047d4264827","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can spend 1 to 3 ki points to increase your Attack Roll by 2 for each of these ki points you spend, potentially turning the miss into a hit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/crosshair-triple-strike-orange.webp","_id":"se43a7e04afa3dc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twin Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to assume the shape of your Eidolon, adopting its Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, armor class, and hitpoints, and all its features and evolution feats.</p><p>You also retain all of your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the Eidolon.</p><p>You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them, provided that your new form is physically capable of doing so. You can't use any special senses you have (for example, darkvision) unless your new form also has that sense.</p><p>When you transform, you choose whether your equipment falls to the ground, merges into the new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal. The DM determines whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the form's shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change shape or size to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge into your new form. Equipment that merges has no effect in that state.</p><p>You can maintain this form up to 1 hour while concentrating (as if concentrating on a spell) and you cannot assume it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/spirit-undead-horned-blue.webp","_id":"se449c6d01688850","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel—or sometimes sacrifice—a part of your vital essence to curse and manipulate creatures through hemocraft magic. You know one blood curse of your choice. A list of the available blood curses can be found on the Optional Features page. You learn one additional blood curse of your choice at 3rd, 6th, 10th, 14th, and 18th level. Each time you learn a new blood curse, you can also choose one of the blood curses you know and replace it with another blood curse.</p><p>Each time you use your Blood Maledict feature, you choose which curse to invoke from the curses you know. While invoking a blood curse, but before it affects the target, you can choose to amplify the curse by taking necrotic damage equal to one roll of your hemocraft die. This damage can't be reduced in any way. An amplified curse gains an additional effect, noted in the curse's description. Creatures that do not have blood are Immune to blood curses unless you have amplified the curse.</p><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all uses on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"@scale.bloodhunter.blood-maledict","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.bloodhunter.hemocraft","necrotic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"se4ec083778d1719","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor of Faith","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can target yourself with your Inspiring Surge. When you affect a creature with your Inspiring Surge and the target regains hitpoints in excess of its hitpoint maximum, it gains the difference as temporary hitpoints.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se5447f3b1625652","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell-Breaking Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you hit a creature with your Spellguard Strike, you can cast Counterspell as part of the same Reaction.</p><p>Additionally, once per turn when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can cast Dispel Magic as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se56e16472b3767c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189521,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Evasion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can nimbly dodge out of the way of certain dangers. When you're subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail. You can't use this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/beam-red-orange.webp","_id":"se5c05267751ad98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428440,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warding Flare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can interpose divine light between yourself and an attacking enemy. When you are attacked by a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll, causing light to flare before the attacker before it hits or misses. An attacker that can't be Blinded is Immune to this feature.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se5f45173e1b21c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfect Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative and don't use Uncanny Metabolism, you regain expended Ki Points until you have 4 if you have 3 or fewer.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-shadow-blue.webp","_id":"se612e34e30e5ae4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189512,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Weapons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Even when not shifted, your form is permanently altered to include fangs, claws, or talons. When you make a melee weapon attack with these natural weapons, you roll a d6 and add your Strength or Dexterity modifier to the attack and damage roll (your choice).</p><p>This die changes as you gain shifter levels, as shown in the Natural Weapons column of the Shifter table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/claws/claw-talons-yellow-red.webp","_id":"se651f50e241358f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Adventurer's Atlas","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest while holding Cartographer's Tools, you can use that tool to create a set of magical maps by touching at least two creatures (one of whom can be yourself), up to a maximum number of creatures equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum of two creatures). Each target receives a magical map, which constantly updates to show the relative position of all the map holders but is illegible to all others. The maps last until you die or until you use this feature again, at which point any existing maps created by this feature immediately vanish.</p><p>While carrying the map, a target gains the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Awareness.</strong> The target adds 1d4 to its Initiative rolls.</p><p><strong>Positioning.</strong> The target knows the location of all other map holders that are on the same plane of existence as itself. When casting a spell or creating another effect that requires being able to see the effect's target, a map holder can target another map holder regardless of sight or cover, so long as the other map holder is still within the effect's range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d4","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-circle-white.webp","_id":"se65817ae601d488","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Invincible Conqueror","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to harness extraordinary martial prowess. As a Bonus Action, you can magically become an avatar of conquest, gaining the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make one additional attack as part of that action.</li><li>The damage of your Aura of Conquest and Scornful Rebuke is doubled.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se6afce7f33728db","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189520,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Lorist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain proficiency in Animal Handling, Insight, Medicine, Nature, Perception, or Survival. Additionally, you can use your Charisma in place of your Wisdom for any of these skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se6ba673ea2a4aea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silent Flight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Stealth skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/raptor-owl-flying-moon.webp","_id":"se6c0dc3e6229ced","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Adjust Density","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically alter the weight of one object or creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The object or creature must be Large or smaller. The target's weight is halved or doubled until the end of your next turn.</p><p>While the weight of a creature is halved by this effect, the creature's Speed increases by 10 feet, it can jump twice as far as normal, and it has Disadvantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws. While the weight of a creature is doubled by this effect, the creature's Speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it has Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</p><p>Upon reaching 10th level in this class, you can target an object or a creature that is Huge or smaller.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se6f9c111431d3f6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428379,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fleet of Foot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your base walking increases to 35 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-sandals-tan.webp","_id":"se71c04198c83af3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189580,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Phantasmal Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell that deals damage and is not an Illusion spell, you can change its school to Illusion and its damage type to psychic. If the spell requires a Saving Throw, that saving throw becomes a Wisdom saving throw.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se72dee873bdc00f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Instinctive Pounce","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As part of the Bonus Action you take to enter your rage, you can move up to half your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp","_id":"se7306b67e4cc93d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Join Fates","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through a ritual that lasts 10 minutes, you can touch two other creatures and temporarily tie their fates together. Whenever either creature makes an Ability Check or Saving Throw, the other also rolls and the original creature uses the average of the two rolls to determine the effect (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se740920efffd484","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenets of Redemption","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tenets of the Oath of Redemption hold a paladin to a high standard of peace and justice.</p><p><strong>Peace.</strong> Violence is a weapon of last resort. Diplomacy and understanding are the paths to long-lasting peace.</p><p><strong>Innocence.</strong> All people begin life in an innocent state, and it is their environment or the influence of dark forces that drives them to evil. By setting the proper example, and working to heal the wounds of a deeply flawed world, you can set anyone on a righteous path.</p><p><strong>Patience.</strong> Change takes time. Those who have walked the path of the wicked must be given reminders to keep them honest and true. Once you have planted the seed of righteousness in a creature, you must work day after day to allow that seed to survive and flourish.</p><p><strong>Wisdom.</strong> Your heart and mind must stay clear, for eventually you will be forced to admit defeat. While every creature can be redeemed, some are so far along the path of evil that you have no choice but to end their lives for the greater good. Any such action must be carefully weighed and the consequences fully understood, but once you have made the decision, follow through with it knowing your path is just.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se7b3a62f5b5098b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Warding Flare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You regain all expended uses of your Warding Flare when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, whenever you use Warding Flare, you can give the target of the triggering attack a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to 2d6 plus your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se7d4f2239de3f36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grasp of the Kraken","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call forth spectral tentacles that grab at your foes. As an Action, pick a point that you can see within 60 ft. of you. A horde of grasping tendrils appears at that point. Creatures of your choice within 10 ft. of that point must make a Strength Saving Throw against your Warlock spell save DC. Creatures that fail their Saving Throws are Grappled for 1 minute or until you use this ability again. The spectral tentacle's Strength (Athletics) bonus is equal to your Spell Attack Bonus and its reach is 10 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se80415cb5e56c42","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kenku Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Minor Illusion cantrip. When you reach 3rd level, you can cast the Expeditious Retreat spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. When you reach 5th level, you can also cast the Invisibility spell once per day; you must finish a Long Rest in order to cast the spell again using this trait. INT, WIS, or CHA is your spellcasting ability for these spells (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"se871e39cbb72ea6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Font of Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You now regain all your expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, you can expend a spell slot (no action required) to regain one expended use of Bardic Inspiration.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"se8811458f88af80","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Power of Many","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to choose a different creature you can see within 30 feet of it or you and that isn't already targeted by the same effect to make the same Saving Throw as well. The second creature is not subject to any effects from the Saving Throw and the first creature can use its roll instead of its own if it is higher.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se8bb490737ff5ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428335,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drake Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically summon the drake that is bound to you. It appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of you.</p><p>The drake is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See its game statistics in the accompanying Drake Companion stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. Whenever you summon the drake, choose a damage type listed in its Draconic Essence trait. You can determine the cosmetic characteristics of the drake, such as its color, its scale texture, or any visible effect of its Draconic Essence; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.</p><p>In combat, the drake obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own. If you are small enough to ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can any of its actions during your turn or immediately after.</p><p>The drake remains until it is reduced to 0 hit points, until you use this feature to summon the drake again, or until you die. Anything the drake was wearing or carrying is left behind when the drake vanishes.</p><p>Once you summon the drake, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher to summon it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se8c82887a6830f0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of Redemption Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Sanctuary, Sleep</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Calm Emotions, Hold Person</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Counterspell, Hypnotic Pattern</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Otiluke's Resilient Sphere, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Hold Monster, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se8f8f1d2d40e535","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428355,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowering Reserves","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Ability Check, you can spend 1 sorcery points to gain Advantage on the check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make an ability check"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-tornado-wall-blue.webp","_id":"se907efcd0d2b1ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gloom Stalker Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Gloom Stalker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Gloom Stalker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Disguise Self</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rope Trick</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se9582879cc1a067","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Armor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your metallurgical pursuits have led to you making armor a conduit for your magic. As an Action, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor, provided you have armorsmith's tools in hand.</p><p>You gain the following benefits while wearing this armor:</p><ul><li>If the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the arcane armor lacks this requirement for you.</li><li>You can use the arcane armor as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells.</li><li>The armor attaches to you and can't be removed against your will. It also expands to cover your entire body, although you can retract or deploy the helmet as a Bonus Action. The armor replaces any missing limbs, functioning identically to a limb it replaces.</li><li>You can doff or don the armor as an Action. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-gorget-steel.webp","_id":"se96ef844b53f421","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Devastation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spells deliver exceptional power. When you roll damage for a spell, you can reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se99a6c9b71da27f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Evocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of any wizard evocation spell you cast.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/explosion-mushroom-nuke-orange.webp","_id":"se9a6e28d65fb8e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a set of abilities that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice.</p><p><strong>Superiority Dice.</strong> You have four superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a superiority die (no action required). You gain another superiority die at 7th level and one more at 15th level.</p><p><strong>Using Superiority Dice.</strong> You can expend superiority dice to gain a number of different benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Scout's Knowledge.</strong> When you make a check that allows you to apply your Proficiency in Acrobatics, Athletics, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival, you can expend one superiority die to bolster the check. Add the number rolled on the superiority die to your check. You apply this bonus after making the check but before learning if it was successful.</li><li><strong>Precision Attack.</strong> When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can expend one Superiority Die, roll that die, and add it to the Attack Roll, potentially causing the attack to hit.</li><li><strong>Scout's Deflection.</strong> If you are hit by an attack while wearing light or medium armor, you can expend one superiority die as a Reaction, adding the number rolled to your AC. If the attack still hits, you take half damage from it.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se9ce329df8f1c5d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428344,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Item Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You achieve a profound understanding of how to use and make magic items:</p><ul><li>You can attune to up to four magic items at once.</li><li>If you craft a magic item with a rarity of common or uncommon, it takes you a quarter of the normal time, and it costs you half as much of the usual gold.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-seed-hands-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"se9d79f14c507654","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gale Stride","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Second Wind and Tactical Shift, you can move up to your full Speed instead. If you choose to not receive healing from Second Wind, you can activate it without a Bonus Action. You can do so only once on your turn.</p><p>Additionally, this movement allows you to move through the spaces of hostile creatures, treating them as 3.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se9e5a33742b8c23","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189500,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oath Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oath spells at the paladin levels listed in the Oath of the Watchers table. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how oath spells work.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oath of the Watchers Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Alarm, Detect Magic</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Moonbeam, See Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Counterspell, Nondetection</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Aura of Purity, Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Hold Monster, Scrying</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sea0dc25519ca17b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428357,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grand Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Eidolon becomes an absolutely monstrosity. A true thing of legend and terror. Your Eidolon's Strength or Dexterity (your choice) and Constitution increase by 4. And its maximum for those scores is now 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sea37cf3ea7f2cca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189550,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Arts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to draw on the power of the Shadowfell, gaining the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Darkness.</strong> You can expend 1 Ki Point to cast the Darkness spell without spell components. You can see within the spell's area when you cast it with this feature. While the spell persists, you can move its area of Darkness to a space within 60 feet of yourself at the start of each of your turns.</li><li><strong>Darkvision.</strong> You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet. If you already have Darkvision, its range increases by 60 feet.</li><li><strong>Shadowy Figments.</strong> You know the Minor Illusion spell. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.</li><li><strong>Silent Shadow.</strong> You can can expend 2 Ki Points to cast the Pass without Trace without spell components.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sea62c3b3e572c82","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428348,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of the moon suffuses you, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Improved Lunar Blessing.</strong> Once per turn, you can deal an extra 2d10 Radiant damage to a target you hit with a Wild Shape form's attack.</li><li><strong>Shared Moonlight.</strong> Whenever you use Moonlight Step, you can also teleport one willing creature. That creature must be within 10 feet of you, and you teleport it to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of your destination space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sea7154e00b650b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189490,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Pounce","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, as part of an attack with your natural weapons, you can move up to your Speed in a straight line towards a target of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp","_id":"seabe4cfd0a62972","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drake's Breath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can exhale a 30-foot cone of damaging breath or cause your drake to exhale it. Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice doesn't have to match your drake's Draconic Essence). Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>This damage increases to 10d6 when you reach 15th level in this class.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seacb5e813e1d32a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your natural weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"seb0e15a2efada02","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189537,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Acrobatics, Sleight of Hand, Stealth, or Performance.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"seba1100bb3e846d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189508,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battlefield Dancer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier. Additionally, you gain Proficiency in one martial melee weapon of your choice and you learn the Booming Blade and Green-Flame Blade cantrips.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sebb444de89bf090","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The storm grants you benefits even when your aura isn't active. The benefits are based on the environment you chose for your Storm Aura.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sebe7cd67a95e218","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189473,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Equine Build","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Provided you are willing, you can serve as a mount for other creatures that are at least one size smaller than you. When you climb, each foot of movement costs you 5 feet of movement instead and you have Disadvantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to climb.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/charge.webp","_id":"sebf8ffdadcc2f3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You draw on the strange and ancient horrors of the land for power. While you are Concentrating on a Ranger spell or are under the effect of a Ranger spell that you have cast, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Ancient Armor.</strong> You gain a bonus to your AC equal to your Wisdom modifier. Your body is wreathed in rotten bark or beastly bristles.</li><li><strong>Unnerving Aura.</strong> When an enemy starts its turn within a 10-foot Emanation originating from you, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn. The shadows lengthen around you, insects begin to crawl out of the ground, or carrion birds circle overhead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sebf90c3c8fc6d55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Queen's Servitor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to transform into the Spider Queen's most beloved servitor, a giant spider. As a Bonus Action, you turn into a spider until you turn back as a Bonus Action or you die. You gain a +2 bonus to AC. You gain 3 temporary hit points per Warlock level.You gain a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed and the Spiderclimb trait. Additionally, your Unarmed Attack turns into venomous bite. You are Proficient with this attack and it inflicts piercing and poison damage based on your level, as per the table below. You can use your choice of Strength or Dexterity to modify your bite attack's attack and damage rolls (you choose whether to add them to the poison or piercing damage). This attack benefits from all Warlock class features that affect a pact weapon.</p><p>While in spider form, you retain the ability to speak, but you cannot cast any spells except those from your Expanded Spell List, which do not require any material components in this form. The spider form doesn't break your Concentration or otherwise interfere with a spell you've already cast.</p><p>Your ability to handle objects is determined by the form's limbs rather than your own. In addition, you choose whether your equipment falls in your space, merges into your new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it's practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment based on the creature's size and shape. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with the form. Equipment that merges with the form has no effect while you're in that form.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Spider Form Bite Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Piercing Damage</th><th scope=\"col\">Poison Damage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>1d4</td><td>1d6</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>1d6</td><td>1d12</td></tr><tr><td>11th</td><td>1d8</td><td>2d12</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>1d10</td><td>3d12</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>You can use this feature twice and you regain all uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sec29513596d92c1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cutting Words","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use your wit to supernaturally distract, confuse, and otherwise sap the confidence and competence of others. When a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself makes a damage roll or succeeds on an Ability Check or Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration; roll your Bardic Inspiration die, and subtract the number rolled from the creature's roll, reducing the damage or potentially turning the success into a failure.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp","_id":"sec60d6f1cf2a234","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Horns & Hooves","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your unarmed attacks deal your choice of piercing or bludgeoning damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier. If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step if you use your hooves or horns to attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/bull-head-horns-glowing.webp","_id":"sec7273b8381219e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Invocations","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have unearthed Eldritch Invocations, pieces of forbidden knowledge that imbue you with an abiding magical ability or other lessons. You gain one invocation of your choice, such as Pact of the Tome. Invocations are described in the Optional Features page.</p><p><strong>Prerequisites.</strong> If an invocation has a prerequisite, you must meet it to learn that invocation. For example, if an invocation requires you to be a level 5+ Warlock, you can select the invocation once you reach Warlock level 5.</p><p><strong>Replacing and Gaining Invocations.</strong> Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your invocations with another one for which you qualify. You can't replace an invocation if it's a prerequisite for another invocation that you have.</p><p>When you gain certain Warlock levels, you gain more invocations of your choice, as shown in the Invocations column of the Warlock Features table.</p><p>You can't pick the same invocation more than once unless its description says otherwise.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-hand-glow-pink.webp","_id":"sec89d6fe2fecab7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Danger Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an uncanny sense of when things aren't as they should be, giving you an edge when you dodge perils. You have Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws unless you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp","_id":"sec9988bb86a4b61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spectral Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to move between planes enables you to slip through the planar boundaries to lessen the harm done to you during battle. When you take damage from an attack or an effect that requires you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to give yourself Resistance to all of that attack's damage on this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"secd7af061b07514","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Lord","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can empower yourself with dark forces and exude a corrupting presence. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You emanate an aura of magical gloom within 30 ft. This counts as dim light and sunlight cannot illuminate this area.</li><li>Enemy creatures have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against any of your features and spells, as well as those of undead and fiends while within the gloom.</li><li>When an enemy creature starts its turn in the gloom, it takes 10 necrotic damage. This damage is doubled if the creature is good-aligned. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sed1776bfe08ab74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with thieves' tools. You also gain Proficiency in Sleight of Hand and one additional skill of your choice. If you are already proficient with thieves' tools or in Sleight of Hand, choose another skill Proficiency for each Proficiency you already have.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"sed2229c761b6329","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428325,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alleyway Rituals","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following additional Cauldron Rituals:</p><p><strong>Beguiling Performance.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target performs a Perform check, it can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If the Perform check is successful, it treats the result of the roll as 1 step better.</p><p><strong>Drunkard's Luck.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target makes a Carouse check, it adds your spellcasting ability modifier to the result of the d20 roll.</p><p><strong>Eagle Eyes.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target performs a Guard check, it can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If the Guard check results in an encounter, the target cannot be surprised and adds your spellcasting ability modifier to its initiative roll.</p><p><strong>Gutter Remedies.</strong> When you perform an Attend check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If your Attend check is successful, you roll an additional d4 and add it to the result of the die on the result column.</p><p><strong>Magpie's Blessing.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target makes a Pickpocket check, it rolls 2d8 and adds them to the result of the die on the result column if the check was successful. If the check was a failure, it adds your spellcasting ability modifier to any checks made to evade the authorities.</p><p><strong>Twisted Fortune.</strong> Choose one creature. The target rolls 2d8 and adds them to the result of the die on the result column, regardless of whether the Gambling check was successful or not.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sed48bdb29975435","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189563,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchantment Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two Wizard spells from the Enchantment school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.</p><p>In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Enchantment school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sed7055f0251227b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428377,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadowy Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>WWhen a creature makes an Attack Roll against you, you can take a Reaction to impose Disadvantage on that roll. Whether the attack hits or misses, you can then teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sedd3951abd0d165","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189525,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rune Maven","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke each rune twice. When you finish a Short Rest, you now can regain two uses of one rune or one use of two different runes of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sedee7c7df120fde","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to peer at a creature and magically discern how best to hurt it. As an Action, choose one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. You immediately learn whether the creature has any damage Immunities, Resistances, or vulnerabilities and what they are. If the creature is hidden from divination magic, you sense that it has no damage Immunities, Resistances, or vulnerabilities.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seebbb8c3bba8a50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189526,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Harbinger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in intimidation. Additionally, the bonus damage of your Divine Smite also applies to good-aligned creatures. Additionally, if a feature or spell allows you to do radiant damage, you can cause it to deal necrotic damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seece49f4b15e22b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Paths of the Dead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of death allows you to tread the paths used by ghosts and other spirits. Using this feature, you can cast Etherealness. Once the spell ends, you can't cast it with this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seee2e60f89566fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189493,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells of the necromancy school from any spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sef56f9a13e5402d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Fortitude","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing no armor, your AC equals 10 + your Strength or your Spellcasting Ability modifier (your choice) + your Constitution modifier.</p><p>Your hit point maximum increases by 3 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sef64cd64653367f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428372,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aspect of the Wyrm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of your draconic spirit now radiates from you, warding your allies or inspiring fear in your enemies. As a Bonus Action, you can create an aura of draconic power that radiates 10 feet from you for 1 minute. For the duration, you gain one of the following effects of your choice:</p><ul><li><strong>Frightful Presence.</strong> When you create this aura, and as a Bonus Action on subsequent turns, you can choose a creature within the aura. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your ki save DC or become Frightened of you for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a successful save.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> Choose a damage type when you activate this aura: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. You and your allies within the aura have Resistance to that damage.</li></ul><p>Once you create this aura, you can't create it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend 3 ki points to create it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sefb3c2bd3c415b5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189515,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast any level 1+ spell from your Psionic Spells feature, you can cast it by expending a spell slot as normal or by spending a number of Sorcery Points equal to the spell's level. If you cast the spell using Sorcery Points, it requires no Verbal or Somatic components, and it requires no Material components unless they are consumed by the spell or have a cost specified in it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sefb4944d28c9df3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Majesty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Command spell prepared.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you cast Command without expending a spell slot, and you take on an unearthly appearance for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. During this time, you can cast Command as a Bonus Action without expending a spell slot.</p><p>Any creature Charmed by you automatically fails its Saving Throw against the Command you cast with this feature.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sefbe6a505b05a33","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189477,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infuse Item","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to imbue mundane items with certain magical infusions. The magic items you create with this feature are effectively prototypes of permanent items.</p><div><strong>Artificer Infusions</strong><p>Artificers have invented numerous magical infusions, extraordinary processes that rapidly create magic items. To many, artificers seem like wonderworkers, accomplishing in hours what others need weeks to complete.</p><p>The description of each of the following infusions details the type of item that can receive it, along with whether the resulting magic item requires attunement.</p><p>Some infusions specify a minimum artificer level. You can't learn such an infusion until you are at least that level.</p><p>Unless an infusion's description says otherwise, you can't learn an infusion more than once.</p></div<p><strong>Infusing an Item.</strong> Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch a nonmagical object and imbue it with one of your artificer infusions, turning it into a magic item. An infusion works on only certain kinds of objects, as specified in the infusion's description. If the item requires attunement, you can attune yourself to it the instant you infuse the item. If you decide to attune to the item later, you must do so using the normal process for attunement.</p><p>Your infusion remains in an item indefinitely, but when you die, the infusion vanishes after a number of days have passed equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 day). The infusion also vanishes if you give up your knowledge of the infusion for another one.</p><p>You can infuse more than one nonmagical object at the end of a Long Rest; the maximum number of objects appears in the Infused Items column of the Artificer table. You must touch each of the objects, and each of your infusions can be in only one object at a time. Moreover, no object can bear more than one of your infusions at a time. If you try to exceed your maximum number of infusions, the oldest infusion immediately ends, and then the new infusion applies.</p><p>If an infusion ends on an item that contains other things, like a bag of holding, its contents harmlessly appear in and around its space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-runed-glowing.webp","_id":"sefdc576e12839b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limited Wish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You entreat your patron to grant you a small wish. As an Action, you can speak your desire to your Genie's Vessel, requesting the effect of one spell that is 7th level or lower and has a casting time of 1 action. The spell can be from any class's spell list, and you don't need to meet the requirements in that spell, including costly components; the spell simply takes effect as part of this action.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sefea019e75b2ae7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189556,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Rebuke the Defiler","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to rebuke those who lash out at your in violence.</p><p>As a Reaction when a creature you can see within 30 feet of you inflicts damage, you force that creature to make a Wisdom save. On a failed Saving Throw, it takes psychic damage equal to the damage dealt. On a successful save, it takes half that damage.</p><p>If the creature made multiple attacks, select one attack to determine the damage dealt. If the creature used one or more effects that damaged multiple targets, choose the damage take by one of those targets from one of the effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf02b0f08cd95bfe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Veil Wardens Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Veil Wardens Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Detect Evil and Good, Protection from Evil and Good, Darkvision, Mental Barrier</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Intellect Fortress, Magic Circle</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Arcane Storm, Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Circle of Power, Planar Binding</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf050886a1c58b59","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Acolyte of Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one druid cantrip of your choice. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of cleric cantrips you know. You also gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Nature, or Survival.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you gain access to a new spell level of your domain spells, including at this level, you can exchange one domain spell from that spell level for another spell from the druid spell list.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf086491f19ac555","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428334,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Affinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry. Additionally, as an Action, you can spend 2 sorcery points to give yourself Immunity to that damage type for 1 hour.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-icecicles-salvo.webp","_id":"sf08cc71a2bedb7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189542,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Red Exultation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice) plus your Rogue level (minimum of 1 Temporary Hit Point). You also gain this benefit if someone else reduces an enemy within 10 feet of you to 0 Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf0b9d98ac30d825","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Origin","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a sorcerous origin, which describes the source of your innate magical power, from the list of available origins.</p><p>Your choice grants you features when you choose it at 3rd level and again at 6th, 14th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf0d7cd0bae0bdfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Consuming Flames","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your flames grow extraordinarily intense. You ignore Resistance to fire damage and treat Immunity to fire damage as Resistance instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf0f08fad454fe7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sf0f173d6fc4504e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189484,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ingenious Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Flash of Genius, you or a willing creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of yourself can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see as part of that same Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"sf101e82d91f1bba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Scourge of the Ancients","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Scourge of the Ancients feature, you can select two of the listed benefits instead of one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf11f18efe30cd31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infused Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Eidolon's Attacks are treated as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"sf1c33dd4f48db95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189549,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stormborn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Fly Speed equal to your current Speed whenever you are not underground or indoors, and gain Resistance to lighting and thunder damage.</p><p>Additionally, you regain all expended uses of your Wrath of the Storm subclass feature when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf1cbd9f75494821","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189487,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells from the Druid spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf1ceb3391f4c193","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tokens of the Departed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a life ends in your presence, you're able to snatch a token from the departing soul, a sliver of its life essence that takes physical form: when a creature you can see dies within 30 feet of you, you can open your free hand and cause a Tiny trinket to appear there, a soul trinket. The DM determines the trinket's form or has you roll on the Trinkets table in the Player's Handbook to generate it. You can have a maximum number of soul trinkets equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you can't create one while at your maximum.</p><p>You can use soul trinkets in the following ways:</p><ul><li>While a soul trinket is on your person, you have Advantage on death Saving Throws and Constitution Saving Throws, for your vitality is enhanced by the life essence within the object.</li><li>When you deal Sneak Attack damage on your turn, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets that's on your person and then immediately use Wails from the Grave, without expending a use of that feature.</li><li>As an Action, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets, no matter where it's located. When you do so, you can ask the spirit associated with the trinket one question. The spirit appears to you and answers in a language it knew in life. It's under no obligation to be truthful, and it answers as concisely as possible, eager to be free. The spirit knows only what it knew in life, as determined by the DM.</li></ul><p>You gain two soul trinkets when you gain this feature. You regain all soul trinkets whenever you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2036aba37cad04","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189534,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mapping Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Illuminated Cartography.</strong> You can cast Faerie Fire without expending a spell slot, outlining the affected creatures as if in ink. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Portal Jump.</strong> On your turn, you can spend an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down) to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of yourself or within 5 feet of a creature that is within 30 feet of you and holding one of your Adventurer's Atlas maps. You can't use this benefit if your Speed is 0.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"on your turn, spend an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down)"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"sf238d112425dc58","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189469,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Labyrinthine Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means, unless you allow it. You can present false thoughts by succeeding on a Charisma (Deception) check contested by the mind reader's Wisdom (Insight) check. You are also Immune to the Charmed condition.</p><p>Additionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates you are being truthful if you so choose, and you can't be compelled to tell the truth by magic.</p><p>If you fail a Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to reroll the Saving Throw and add your Intelligence modifier to it, even if it was already added, taking whichever result was higher.</p><p>You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf271066d423ecc6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189533,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Split Enchantment","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast an enchantment spell of 1st level or higher that targets only one creature, you can have it target a second creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2936b643154462","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189570,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telekinetic Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered new ways to use your telekinetic abilities, detailed below.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf295b041b7e1249","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"sf2a4a759dd718a6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dreadful Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The size of your Dreadful Presence increases to 30 feet. Creatures that fail their Saving Throw against your Unnerving Aura are also Frightened for the duration. When a creature Frightened in this manner is subject to the effect of A Feast for Crows, it deals maximum damage and ignores Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2b1c3a13132401","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189529,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swarming Dispersal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can discorporate into your swarm, avoiding danger. When you take damage, you can use your Reaction to give yourself Resistance to that damage. You vanish into your swarm and then teleport to an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you, where you reappear with the swarm.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2d9fa0aa0966f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (d12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2e9b9d8418bb8e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189498,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine energy coursing through you can empower healing spells. Whenever you or an ally within 5 feet of you rolls dice to determine the number of hit points a spell restores, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll any number of those dice once, provided you aren't Incapacitated. You can use this feature only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf334c7208cdf56c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Overflow","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A kineticist's body surges with energy from her chosen element whenever she spends kinesis points, causing her to glow with a nimbus of fire, weep water from her pores, or experience some other thematic effect.</p><p>When you have less than half your current maximum number of kinesis points, your Charisma bonus to damage on your kinetic shape is doubled. Additionally, you gain Resistance to one damage type corresponding to one of your chosen elements. You can change the chosen resistance to a different one corresponding to one of your chosen elements at the start of each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sf34739b438317ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189507,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inquisitor's Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Cunning Action: Aim, you can choose one creature you can see. You have Advantage on the first Attack Roll against that creature each turn for 1 minute instead. This effect ends early if you can no longer see the target, you are Incapacitated, you perform a hostile action against a different creature (such as an attack or forcing it to make a Saving Throw), or you use Inquisitor's Gaze on a different creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3528ba3c79629b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your allies have Resistance to radiant and necrotic damage while within your Aura of Protection.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf37dcc0160d4e9c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189519,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Innate Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An event in your past left an indelible mark on you, infusing you with simmering magic. As a Bonus Action, you can unleash that magic for 1 minute, during which you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>The spell save DC of your Sorcerer spells increases by 1.</li><li>You have Advantage on the Attack Rolls of Sorcerer spells you cast.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":2,"max":2,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-green.webp","_id":"sf3a3f6f76a89207","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avenger's Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in insight or intimidation. Additionally, the bonus damage of your Divine Smite also applies to any creature that is under the effect of your Vow of Enmity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3b79a2c84cd72f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428353,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alchemical Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell while you have alchemist's supplies on your person, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/mortar-powder-green.webp","_id":"sf3d12f0e27b0bf1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Secrets","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two spells of your choice from any class. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Wizard table, or a cantrip. The chosen spells count as wizard spells for you and don't count against the number of wizard spells you can prepare.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3db985c5543e66","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Archfamiliar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your occult bond with your familiar is at the height of its power, granting you the following benefits:</p><p><strong>Bonded Magic.</strong> Choose three Witch spells of 1st or 2nd level. You always have the chosen spells prepared. Your bonded familiar also learns these spells. Both of you can cast these spells without spell slots and without material components. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus and spell save DC for these spells.</p><p><strong>Life Ward.</strong> When either you or your bonded familiar drop to 0 hit points but aren't killed out right, you can change the affected target's hit points to a number equal to triple your Witch level. You cannot use this feature again until you have completed a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Longevity.</strong> The mystical powers coursing through you grant you an extended life span. For every nine years that pass, your body ages only one year.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3f231dc189acf0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189562,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Malevolence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Creatures that start their turn within 10 feet of you or enter it for the first time on a turn, take psychic damage equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice) and have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against the Frightened and Lacerated conditions while within the aura The aura is inactive while you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf419b455901d193","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master of navigating the natural world, and you react with swift and decisive action when attacked. This grants you the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You ignore 3.</li><li>You have Advantage on initiative rolls.</li><li>On your first turn during combat, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that have not yet acted.</li></ul><p>In addition, you are skilled at navigating the wilderness. You gain the following benefits when traveling for an hour or more:</p><ul><li>Difficult terrain doesn't slow your group's travel.</li><li>Your group can't become lost except by magical means.</li><li>When performing a task during the Travelling Phase of Overland Travel, you may additionally perform the Lookout task or assist with it.</li><li>If you are traveling alone, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.</li><li>When you forage, you find twice as much food as you normally would.</li><li>While tracking other creatures, you also learn their exact number, their sizes, and how long ago they passed through the area.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sf427bbe672ce3e2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Esoteric Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one feat of your choice. You ignore all race, class, and level prerequisites the feat normally has. You do not, however, gain any features that the feat might depend on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf43d5d97fd75605","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189571,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Mushrooms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you or your bonded familiar can cause enchanted mushrooms to spring up from the ground in a 10-feet circle around a point you can see within 60 feet.</p><p>The effect of the mushrooms depends on the type you choose from the options below, which you can activate as a Reaction when a creature steps into the area. Immediately afterwards, the mushrooms disappear.</p><p><strong>Fortifying Fungus.</strong> The triggering creature and all other creatures in the area gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch level.</p><p><strong>Nightcap.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, they fall asleep until the start of the triggering creature's next turn. An affected creature wakes up early if it takes damage or another creature uses an Action to shake it awake.</p><p><strong>Venomgill.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Poisoned until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p>You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf44699c9ad4b6fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189564,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflect Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an Attack Roll hits you and its damage includes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage, you can take a Reaction to reduce the attack's total damage against you. The reduction equals 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier and Monk level.</p><p>If you reduce the damage to 0, you can expend 1 Ki Point to redirect some of the attack's force. If you do so, choose a creature you can see within 5 feet of yourself if the attack was a melee attack or a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself that isn't behind Total Cover if the attack was a ranged attack. That creature must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or take damage equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die plus your Dexterity modifier. The damage is the same type dealt by the attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when an Attack Roll hits you and its damage includes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d10 + @abilities.dex.mod + @classes.monk.levels","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/arrow-flying-white-blue.webp","_id":"sf460753e0735e8d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189511,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to summon a spirit that assumes an animal form: as an Action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape feature to cast the Find Familiar spell, without material components.</p><p>When you cast the spell in this way, the familiar is a fey instead of a beast.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rabbit-movement-glowing-green.webp","_id":"sf46ae0da8633644","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189488,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sea Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once on your turn, you can move up to your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks and teleport your water orb to your position. You can do so before, during, or after this movement.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you can regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf47ac4e1f0ce0b8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with calligrapher's tools and enchanter's supplies, and you learn to speak, read, and write Giant.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"sf4a829fd1f805a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189575,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Experimental Elixir","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can magically produce a number of experimental elixirs equal to your Proficiency in empty flasks you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for each elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an Action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an Incapacitated creature.</p><p>Creating an experimental elixir requires you to have alchemist's supplies on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next Long Rest.</p><p>You can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your Action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Experimental Elixir</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Swiftness. The drinker's walking Speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every Attack Roll and Saving Throw they make for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Flight. The drinker gains a Fly Speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the Alter Self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/consumables/potions/bottle-bulb-corked-purple.webp","_id":"sf4fb6342360edec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189467,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bond to your drake reaches the pinnacle of its power. While your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Empowered Attack.</strong> The drake's Bite, Elemental Bolt, and Infused Strikes attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for its Draconic Essence (for a total of 2d6 extra damage).</li><li><strong>Draconic Might.</strong> The drake grows to Huge size. Its Strength and Constitution are increased by 4 and its Hit Points increase by an additional 2 for each of your levels in this class.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Breath.</strong> The size of your Drake's Breath increases to 60 feet and you regain its use on a Short Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf5011fe941085ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189524,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Impeccable Memory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all INT-checks to recall information about something.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/arrows-circling-pink.webp","_id":"sf50a9c8c89bff36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189576,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Tradition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an arcane tradition from the list of available traditions, shaping your practice of magic. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/orb-ice-glow.webp","_id":"sf51c02ad3e65cc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189568,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Elegance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make a Charisma (Deception, Intimidation, or Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf52c75ed54455e2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189483,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiotic Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws and Initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf5460b7b1ab37dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189551,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Path to the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to mark another creature's life force for termination.</p><p>As an Action, you choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of you, cursing it until the end of your next turn. The next time you or an ally of yours hits the cursed creature with an attack, the creature has vulnerability to all of that attack's damage, and then the curse ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf5925ae84f7de71","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428332,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heightened Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your hemocraft modifier to Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf596dc826fd04e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428328,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gift of the Sea","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a Swim Speed of 40 feet, and you can breathe underwater. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf5ba996298da091","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428371,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d8)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sf61942f11cd5deb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189475,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bladesinger Styles","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>From its inception as a martial and magical art, Bladesinging has been tied to the sword, more specifically the longsword. Yet many generations of study gave rise to various styles of Bladesinging based on the melee weapon employed. The techniques of these styles are passed from master to students in small schools, some of which have a building dedicated to instruction. Even the newest styles are hundreds of years old, but are still taught by their original creators due to the long lives of elves. Most schools of Bladesinging are in Evermeet or Evereska. One was started in Myth Drannor, but the city's destruction has scattered those students who survived.</p><p>Styles of Bladesinging are broadly categorized based on the type of weapon employed, and each is associated with a category of animal. Within that style are specializations named after specific animal types, based on the types of spells employed, the techniques of the master, and the particular weapon used. Bladesingers who apprentice to a master typically get a tattoo of their chosen style's animal. Some bladesingers learn multiple styles and bear many tattoos, wearing a warning on their skin of their deadly skills.</p><p><strong>Cat.</strong> Styles that employ a sword belong to this family. The lion style, the eldest, trains practitioners in the use of the longsword and doesn't favor any particular type of spells. Leopard style focuses on the shortsword and spells of illusion and stealth. Red tiger, a style just three centuries old, has its bladesingers using the scimitar in a whirling dance of defense from which they launch into sudden leaps and attacks.</p><p><strong>Bird.</strong> Styles that focus on the use of a hafted weapon, such as an axe or hammer, have been grouped together as bird styles, yet they vary wildly. All relatively new styles, they use weapons not typically favored by elves. Eagle-style bladesingers use small handaxes, and many maneuvers in the style focus on fluid ways to throw the weapon and draw a new one. Raven style uses a war pick, and spells associated with it grant the bladesinger more agility in combat.</p><p><strong>Snake.</strong> Practitioners of these styles use a flail, chain, or whip. Viper style uses a whip, despite its inelegance as a weapon, and has almost as long a history as the lion style. Its masters punctuate their bladesong with a stunningly rapid rhythm of whip cracks, which can keep many foes at bay and allow the bladesinger space to cast the cruel spells of poison and disease favored by the style.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf63a1668bf1bfc2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Elementalism cantrip and Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it. You only use the somatic component to cast this spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"sf68c28451364edc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189506,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Rage can keep you fighting despite grievous wounds. If you drop to 0 Hit Points while your Rage is active and don't die outright, you can make a DC 10 Constitution Saving Throw. If you succeed, your Hit Points instead change to a number equal to twice your Barbarian level.</p><p>Each time you use this feature after the first, the DC increases by 5. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, the DC resets to 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sf68d9c6e9c5d8af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If your total for a Strength check or Strength Saving Throw is less than your Strength score, you can use that score in place of the total.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-yellow-red.webp","_id":"sf6d352b2e4c7ed9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189472,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Searing Flesh","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can superheat your body to extreme temperatures, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier and any creature that touches you or hits you with a melee attack from within 10 feet of you takes fire damage equal to your Charisma modifier.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf71a70b2c702deb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to temporarily grow and take on the appearance of a treelike person, covered with leaves and bark. As a Bonus Action, you assume this guardian form, which lasts until you end it as a Bonus Action or until you are Incapacitated.</p><p>You undergo the following changes while in your guardian form:</p><ul><li>Your size becomes Large, unless you were larger.</li><li>Your reach increases by 5 feet.</li><li>You gain a number of temporary hit points at the start of each of your turns. The number equals half your ranger level. When the form ends, you lose any temporary hit points you have from it.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice and you regain all expended uses on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf737b7d2e2586fb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Corona of Light","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you cause yourself to emit an aura of sunlight that lasts for 1 minute or until you dismiss it (no action required). You emit Bright Light in a 60-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. Your enemies in the Bright Light have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your Radiance of the Dawn and any spell that deals Fire or Radiant damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf7877d3b941ff26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a particular style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take the same Fighting Style option more than once, even if you get to choose again.</p><h5>Archery</h5><p>You gain a +2 bonus to Attack Rolls you make with ranged weapons.</p><h5>Close Quarters Shooter</h5><p>When making a ranged weapon attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. You have a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls on ranged weapon attacks.</p><h5>Defense</h5><p>While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Dueling</h5><p>When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon.</p><h5>Great Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.</p><h5>Mariner</h5><p>As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a Swim Speed and a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Protection</h5><p>When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. You must be wielding a shield.</p><h5>Two-Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.</p><h5>Superior Technique</h5><p>You learn one maneuver of your choice from among those available to the fighter archetype. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).</p><p>You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach level 10, the size of this die increases to a d8.</p><h5>Blind Fighting</h5><p>You have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</p><h5>Interception</h5><p>When a creature you can see hits a target, other than you, within 5 feet of you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by 1d10 + your Proficiency bonus (to a minimum of 0 damage). You must be wielding a shield or a simple or martial weapon to use this Reaction.</p><h5>Thrown Weapon Fighting</h5><p>You can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.</p><p>In addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll.</p><h5>Unarmed Fighting</h5><p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-daggers-orange.webp","_id":"sf7a22ed51e22c6a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428326,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (Level 18)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf7a2dd066594911","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Aura","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your guardian form emanates a magical aura that fortifies your injured allies. When any ally starts their turn within 30 feet of your guardian form, that ally regains a number of hit points equal to half your ranger level. This aura has no effect on undead and constructs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf7a39a81a1cb4d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Truesight to a distance of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf7c67c2451fca4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189566,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steppe Skirmisher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you move at least 30 feet in a straight line right before attacking a creature and you hit it with melee weapon attack, that target must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be knocked Prone. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.</p><p>You can move up to half your Speed as a Reaction when an enemy ends its turn within 10 feet of you after moving towards you and you are not already within 5 feet of a different enemy. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when an enemy ends its turn within 10 feet of you after moving towards you and you are not already within 5 feet of a different enemy"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-axe-red.webp","_id":"sf8059f24c2f1a46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strange Metabolism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your body begins to adapt to toxins and venoms, ignoring their corrupting effects. You gain Resistance to damage from poison and diseases. At the end of each of your turns, you can end one disease or poison affecting you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf828ef4d529b30a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189481,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mage Hand Legerdemain","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Mage Hand, you can cast it as a Bonus Action, and you can make the spectral hand Invisible. You can control the hand as a Bonus Action, and through it, you can make Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf86ff0c418b18b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189530,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Profane Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can harvest body parts from slain creatures and graft them onto your companion to give it new capabilities. You use your Medicine in place of the usual skill for harvesting each creature type. However, the attempt only succeeds if you meet the DC for a pristine ingredient.</p><p>You can graft or remove body parts to your companion as part of completing a Short or Long Rest. The maximum number of grafted body parts is two and you cannot choose the same creature type more than once. You automatically preserve any body parts that aren't currently grafted, though you need a method of storing and carrying them to bring them with you.</p><p>Your companion gains the ability associated with each grafted body part as per the list below.</p><ul><li><strong>Aberration.</strong> Your companion's Intelligence is replaced with that of the aberration, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, it gains a new ability, which it can use in place of its slam attack: Psychic Rend: 60 ft range, Intelligence Saving Throw: DC equals your spell save DC. Failure: 1d6 + the aberration's proficiency + your companion's Intelligence modifier psychic damage.</li><li><strong>Beast.</strong> Your companion's Strength or Dexterity (your choice) is replaced with that of the beast, up to a maximum of 20, and your companion can use its Dexterity in place of its Strength for melee damage rolls with its slam. Additionally, your companion gains any special movement type of the harvested creature, equal to its own Speed.</li><li><strong>Construct.</strong> Your companion's AC is replaced with that of the harvested creature, up to a maximum of 20.</li><li><strong>Dragon.</strong> Your companion gains a breath weapon which it can use as an Action. The damage type and shape of the breath weapon is the same as that of the dragon. The size of the breath weapon is 30 feet if it is a cone and 5 x 60 feet if it is a line. The damage is equal to that of your companion's death burst feature + the Proficiency of the dragon.</li><li>Once has used its breath weapon, you have to roll a d6 at the start of each of your turns. On a roll of 5 or 6, it regains its use of this feature.</li><li><strong>Elemental.</strong> Your companion gains a damage Resistance based on the elemental's Immunity. If the elemental has multiple Immunities, you choose which one to use. Additionally, your companion deals bonus damage of the same type equal to the elemental's Proficiency when it hits with its slam attack.</li><li><strong>Fey.</strong> Your companion's alignment and its Charisma is replaced with that of the fey, up to a maximum of 20. Your companion also gains its own personality, based on that of the fey, and may act on its own when not currently ordered to do something.</li><li>Additionally, if your companion has to make a Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, it adds half the fey's Proficiency (rounded down). This augmentation is exclusive with those gained from fiends.</li><li><strong>Fiend.</strong> Your companion's alignment and two Ability Scores of your choice are replaced with those of the fiend. Your companion also gains its own personality, based on that of the fiend, and may act on its own when not currently ordered to do something.</li><li>Additionally, your companion regenerates hit points equal to the fiend's Proficiency at the start of each of its turn, unless it has taken radiant damage since its last turn. This augmentation is exclusive with those gained from fey.</li><li><strong>Giant.</strong> Your companion's Strength is replaced with that of the giant, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, your companion's size changes to Large and it has advantage on Strength checks and Strength Saving Throws. When your companion hits with its slam attack, it deals additional damage of the same type equal to the giant's Proficiency.</li><li><strong>Ooze.</strong> Your companion's Constitution is replaced with that of the ooze, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, its current and maximum hit points increase by four times the ooze's Proficiency and it can spend 5 feet of its movement to remove the Grappled or Restrained condition from itself.</li><li><strong>Plant.</strong> Your companion's current and maximum hit points increase by double the plant's Proficiency. Additionally, the reach of its slam attack increases by 10 feet. Once per turn, a creature hit by your companion's slam attack has to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it is Grappled by your companion. Any creature that starts its turn Grappled in this manner, takes bludgeoning damage equal to the plant's Proficiency.</li><li><strong>Undead.</strong> As part of the Bonus Action used to command it, you can tell your companion to exude an aura of necrotic energy. When you do so, you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier from the effect. On subsequent turns, you can deactivate the aura the same way.</li><li>The size of the aura is 10 feet, but increases to 20 feet if the undead's CR was 10 or higher, and to 30 feet if its CR was 20 or higher.</li><li>Any creature that ends its turn in the aura or enters it for the first time on a turn, takes necrotic damage equal to the undead's proficiency.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf879dd81e926df2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Inspiring Smite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you deal damage to a creature with your Divine Smite feature, you can use your Channel Divinity as a Bonus Action and distribute temporary hit points to creatures of your choice within 30 feet of you, which can include you. The total number of temporary hit points equals 2d8 + your level in this class, divided among the chosen creatures however you like.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf880de4a8aeccb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428356,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Knight Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with Heavy Armor and do not suffer Disadvantage on Stealth checks caused by Heavy Armor.</p><p>Additionally, you have Advantage on Saving Throws and Ability Checks against being dismounted.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8bce828ca0e647","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428359,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mountain Born","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your are acclimatized to cold regions as per the DMG. You also have Resistance to cold damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-vulcano.webp","_id":"sf919f8ec54a4412","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189578,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ancient Fortitude","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the endurance of the ancient forests. Your hit point maximum and current hit points increase by 2 per ranger level when you assume your guardian form. This increase lasts until you leave the form; your hit point maximum then returns to normal, but your current hit points remain the same, unless they must decrease to abide by your hit point maximum.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf97832e3af23e21","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189527,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Training in War and Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Performance skill and one of the following: elvish sword, greatsword, rapier, scimitar, shortsword.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf993ff563c0ec7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in light and medium armor as well as the battleaxe, warhammer, light crossbow, and heavy crossbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/hammers/hammer-double-engraved-green.webp","_id":"sf9bd1595c5e6b5e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189579,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fathomless Plunge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically open temporary conduits to watery destinations. As an Action, you can teleport yourself and up to five other willing creatures that you can see within 30 feet of you. Amid a whirl of tentacles, you all vanish and then reappear in a body of water (pond size or larger) you've seen in the same plane of existence as you or within 30 feet of it, each of you appearing in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of the others.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf9cb3386f1bcfd3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189555,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessings of Knowledge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two languages of your choice. You also become proficient in your choice of two of the following skills: Arcana, History, Nature, or Religion.</p><p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses either of those skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfa66fa698952a3e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428333,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Momentary Stasis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically force a Large or smaller creature you can see within 60 feet of you to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. Unless the Saving Throw is a success, the creature is encased in a field of magical energy until the end of your next turn or until the creature takes any damage. While encased in this way, the creature is Paralyzed and has a Speed of 0. This feature ignores Immunity to the Paralyzed condition.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfaa5036d275d50f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dagger in the Dark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are in dim light or darkness, you can reduce the cost of any feature that uses your Sneak Attack dice by 1 (to a minimum of 0). You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfad8e41f31f2ff0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189536,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Brutal Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed new ways to attack furiously. The following effects are now among your Brutal Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Staggering Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a CON Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes, and it can't take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Sundering Blow.</strong> Before the start of your next turn, the next Attack Roll made by another creature against the target gains a +5 bonus to the roll. If the attack hits, the attacker can maximize up to two of its damage dice. An Attack Roll can gain only one Sundering Blow bonus.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"sfb0522939ceadce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189471,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Summoner","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beasts and fey that you conjure are more resilient than normal. Any beast or fey summoned or created by a spell that you cast gains the following benefits:</p><ul><li>The creature appears with more hit points than normal: 2 extra hit points per Hit Die it has.</li><li>The damage from its natural weapons is considered magical for the purpose of overcoming Immunity and Resistance to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfb4aa5f4db9b133","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189491,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Holy Arms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Sanctified Strike cantrip if you do not know it already. Additionally, you can cast Sanctified Strike in place of one attack when you take the attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfb4be65b33b2154","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189560,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Reanimated Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion attacks twice instead of once when you command it to take the Attack action. In addition, you can give it two out of the following benefits. You can change your choice each time you complete a Short or Long Rest.</p><ul><li>Your companion gains Proficiency in Strength or Dexterity Saving Throws (your choice).</li><li>Your companion's Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>Your companion's current and maximum hit points increase by an amount equal to your Artificer level.</li><li>You can cast spells is if you were in your companion's space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfb7600f7c0deb00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189470,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Radiant Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An ally affected by your Channel Divinity: Radiant Defense also has Resistance against the damage of the triggering attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfba99d38c004469","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189486,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death Dealer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Envenom (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or become Poisoned for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of every one of its turns, ending the effect on a success. You must have a Poisoner's Kit on your person to use this effect. Alternatively, you can apply a poison that you currently have on your person. If you do so, the save DC of the poison changes to your Cunning Strike save DC if it is normally lower.</li><li><strong>Silence (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or be unable to speak or produce sound with its voice until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfbb7b0e14af49d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189531,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tipsy Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move in sudden, swaying ways. You gain the following benefits.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfbd1d692dd85075","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189514,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack (3)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack four times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sfbe1a0dae61d9a3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Channeling","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to channel spirits improves. You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Power from Beyond.</strong> Once per turn, when you cast a Bard spell that deals damage or restores Hit Points, roll a d6. You gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls or to the total Hit Points the spell restores equal to the number rolled.</li><li><strong>Spiritual Manifestation.</strong> You always have the Spirit Guardians spell prepared. You can cast the spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so the spirits also guard against worldly threats. When cast in this way, you and allies within the spell's Emanation have Half Cover. Once you modify the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfc1f5c06a65dae5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189478,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You ignore Resistance to psychic and force damage, and you treat Immunity to them as Resistance instead. Additionally, you double your Proficiency for Intelligence Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfca2d30272a4426","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189573,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Shots","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to infuse projectiles with magic. Whenever you make a ranged weapon attack with a nonmagical weapon, you can make it magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you make a ranged weapon attack, you can change the damage type to any other damage type of your choice except bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfca4ac5a7bf321e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189496,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Confound (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you until the start of your next turn while any of your allies are within reach of its attacks.</li><li><strong>Instigate (Cost: 3d6).</strong> An ally of your choice within 60 feet of you can use its Reaction to make a weapon attack against the same target, provided it is within reach.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcb77e0ff0a425d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189532,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Endurance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 hit point instead. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"sfcc48d403b52403","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamagic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Because your magic flows from within, you can alter your spells to suit your needs; you gain two Metamagic options of your choice from the list below. You use the chosen options to temporarily modify spells you cast. To use an option, you must spend the number of Sorcery Points that it costs.</p><p>You can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it unless otherwise noted in one of those options.</p><p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest you can replace one metamagic you know with another one. You gain two more options at Sorcerer level 10 and two more at Sorcerer level 17.</p><h5>Careful Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that forces other creatures to make a Saving Throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the spell's full force. To do so, you spend 1 sorcery point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their Saving Throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Distant Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a range of 5 feet or greater, you can spend 1 sorcery point to double the range of the spell.</p><p>When you cast a spell that has a range of touch, you can spend 1 sorcery point to make the range of the spell 30 feet.</p><h5>Empowered Spell</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p><p>You can use Empowered Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Extended Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, you can spend 1 sorcery point to double its duration, to a maximum duration of 24 hours.</p><p>If the affected spell requires Concentration, you have Advantage on any Saving Throw you make to maintain that Concentration.</p><h5>Heightened Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that forces a creature to make a Saving Throw to resist its effects, you can spend 2 sorcery points to give one target of the spell Disadvantage on all its Saving Throws made against the spell.</p><h5>Maximized Spell</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 2 sorcery points and choose a number damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You maximize the rolled result for the chosen dice.</p><p>You can use Maximized Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Quickened Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a casting time of an Action, you can spend 2 Sorcery Points to change the casting time to a Bonus Action for this casting. You can't modify a spell in this way if you've already cast a level 1+ spell on the current turn, nor can you cast a level 1+ spell on this turn after modifying a spell in this way.</p><h5>Seeking Spell</h5><p>If you make an Attack Roll for a spell and miss, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll the d20, and you must use the new roll.</p><p>You can use Seeking Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Subtle Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to cast it without any somatic, verbal and material components, unless that material component has a cost or is consumed by the spell.</p><h5>Twinned Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that targets only one creature and doesn't have a range of self, you can spend a number of sorcery points equal to the spell's level to target a second creature in range with the same spell (1 sorcery point if the spell is a cantrip).</p><p>To be eligible, a spell must be incapable of targeting more than one creature at the spell's current level. For example, Magic Missile and Scorching Ray aren't eligible, but Ray of Frost and Chromatic Orb are.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-colllecting-energy-green.webp","_id":"sfcd507fc5acccb2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189541,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Misty Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast Misty Step as a Reaction in response to taking damage.</p><p>In addition, the following effects are now among your Steps of the Fey options.</p><p><strong>Disappearing Step.</strong> You have the Invisible condition until the start of your next turn or until immediately after you make an Attack Roll, deal damage, or cast a spell.</p><p><strong>Dreadful Step.</strong> Creatures within 5 feet of the space you left or the space you appear in (your choice) must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take 2d10 Psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcea2a52a05504c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189553,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Striding Giant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of earth allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of the mountain.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>Your size changes the huge and you gain temporary hit points equal to three times your kineticist level.</li><li>You are Immune to the Charmed, Exhausted, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, and Poisoned conditions.</li><li>You ignore all earth-based effects such as the Erupting Earth spell or even a natural earthquake.</li><li>When you move for the first time on your turn, your steps shake the earth. All creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you have to make a Strength Saving Throw against your save DC or be knocked Prone.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcf15dfa3f9d027","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Event Horizon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically emit a powerful field of gravitational energy that tugs at other creatures for up to 1 minute or until your Concentration ends (as if you were concentrating on a spell). For the duration, whenever a creature hostile to you starts its turn within 60 feet of you, it must make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, it takes 4d10 + Intelligence modifier force damage, and its Speed is reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage, and every foot it moves this turn costs 2 extra feet of movement.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest or until you expend a spell slot of 5th level or higher to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcfbab7fe41f6fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189574,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Shroud of Water","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you can surround yourself with a shroud of water, ice, or both that protects you from harm, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While this effect is active and you are not wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 12 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfd26d8e9d502a80","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189509,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shield of Ineffable Darkness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke the power of darkness to punish anyone fool enough to harm you. As a Reaction when a creature you can see damages you, that creature has to make a CON Saving Throw or become Blinded until the end of your next turn.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain one use when you finish a Short Rest and all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfd2fa9f48b6e83a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unearthly Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to overcome grievous injuries. As a Bonus Action, you can regain a number of hit points equal to half your hit point maximum.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you use 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfd4c7811a31a2a3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189544,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shifting Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to enter a liquid state while moving.</p><p>When you move on your turn, you take only half damage from Opportunity Attacks, and you can move through any enemy's space but can't willingly end your move there.</p><p>On your turn, you can move through any space that is at least 3 inches in diameter and do so without squeezing. When you stop moving, the regular squeezing rules apply if you're in a space one size smaller than you. You can't willingly stop in a space smaller than that, and if you're forced to do so, you immediately flow to the nearest space that can fit you, back along the path of your movement.</p><p>If you start your turn with the Grappled and/or Restrained condition, you can spend half your Speed to immediately end those effects on you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfd59c254cd75f38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189543,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steady Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your aim becomes deadly. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can take careful aim at a creature you can see that is within range of a ranged weapon you're wielding. Until the end of this turn, your ranged attacks with that weapon gain two benefits against the target:</p><ul><li>The attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover.</li><li>On each hit, the weapon deals additional damage to the target equal to 2 + half your fighter level.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature three times. You regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Additionally, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to regain one use.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfdaf3b3748525ae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189505,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monster Slayer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose three creature types, except humanoids. Whenever you use Monster's Bane, you can expend up to two dice instead of just one, adding both to the roll. Both dice are expended as normal. If the target of your attack has one of your chosen creature types, you deal maximum damage with all combat superiority dice you expended, instead of rolling them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfdc67e691fc69ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189502,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Winter Wanderer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Ranger level specified in the Winter Wanderer Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Winter Wanderer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rime's Binding Ice</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fortify</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Ice Storm</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cone of Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfdf0ce441a56e36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189528,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Veteran Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you give your Bonus Action or Reaction to an ally, you can target two allies instead of one. You can do so only once per turn. </p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sfdf5e33fe897c2e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189558,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul Knife","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your psionic energy to manifest blades that disrupt your foes' minds.</p><p>Your Unarmed Strikes deal your choice of psychic, piercing, slashing, or bludgeoning damage each time you hit.</p><p>In addition, you can expend a Ki Point to increase the reach of your Unarmed Strikes by 30 feet until the end of your current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfe67b57bfcb1b4c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428351,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flash of Genius","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails an ability check or a saving throw, you can take a Reaction to add a bonus to the roll, potentially causing it to succeed. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p>You can take this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails an Ability Check or a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sfeb057e0d1f9fb6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428318,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Shadow Spawn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you envelope yourself in a coat of shadows for 1 minute. For the duration, you gain Advantage on all Dexterity (Stealth) checks while you are in dim light or darkness. This benefit lasts for one minute or until you are Incapacitated. It is also suppressed until the end of your next turn if you are in bright light or you take radiant damage.</p><p>If you damage a creature that cannot see you with a spell or an attack while this effect is active on you, you can choose to deal maximum damage. You can do so only once per use of this Channel Divinity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfec0f0a602d9540","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428331,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dampen Elements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature within 30 feet of you takes acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, you can use your Reaction to grant Resistance to the creature against that instance of the damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfec800babec61ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189485,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Nature, or Perception. You can choose to gain Proficiency with thieves' tools in place of one skill choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"sff0d372ba6fe7ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189501,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to psychic damage, and you have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed or Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sff5b3ec8f91af5c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189545,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses your Proficiency with a tool.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-backing-steel.webp","_id":"sff5ca00338b4cd3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189464,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Reject Failure","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you fail a D20 Test, you can use your Reaction to reroll it and take the higher result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sff67214ab24429e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777218428330,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Castigation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you can channel hemocraft magic to sear an arcane brand into that creature (no action required). You always know the direction to the branded creature as long as it's on the same plane as you. Further, each time a branded creature deals damage to you or forces you to make a Saving Throw, it takes psychic damage equal to your Hemocraft modifier.</p><p>Your brand lasts until you dismiss it or until you use this feature to apply a brand to another creature. Your brand can be dispelled with Dispel Magic, and is treated as a spell with a level equal to half your blood hunter level (maximum 9th level).</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest - or until you spend a use of your Blood Maledict to regain it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["max(1, @abilities.int.mod, @abilities.wis.mod)","psychic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-hook-white-red.webp","_id":"sff8f0c1d1c097c7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777217189479,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
